}
satisfies 
    \be{
    \mathbb{E}\bcls{ Z_{\ell,j}^{T_n^i}(u)^4}\leq C_\star.
    } (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:06.326447+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0060c9dc48adb5ee3a4139371f833940d7f621773f7b564020714fa22ac9d605","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 14 of arXiv:2607.06242, 'Exponential mixing and Freidlin--Wentzell large deviation principle for Markov cocycles'] Under Assumption \ref{a.050201}, for $m$-a.e. $\sigma\in\Sigma$, the family of stationary measures $\{\mu_{\sigma}^{\eps}\}_{\eps\in(0,1]}$ satisfies the large deviation upper bound
      \begin{align*}
          \limsup_{\eps\to0}\eps\ln\mu_{\sigma}^{\eps}(F)
          \leq -\inf_{u\in F}E_{\Ac(\sigma)}(u),
          \qquad \text{for any closed } F\subset H .
      \end{align*}
      If the attractor of the limit system \eqref{e.080301} is a random point, then the large deviation lower bound also holds:
      \begin{align*}
          \liminf_{\eps\to0}\eps\ln\mu_{\sigma}^{\eps}(G)
          \geq -\inf_{u\in G}E_{\Ac(\sigma)}(u),
          \qquad \text{for any open } G\subset H .
      \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:53:10.211096+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_00625f799596e567e4e9088e47d98e731f14be4b675bc4ea0d0efcd57398a55d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop HTR of arXiv:2608.29018, 'Sharp Restricted Isometry Thresholds for\\ Global Minima of Rank-Restricted Matrix LASSO'] Fix $k\ge2$ and $r_{\star}\ge1$, and let $t\coloneqq k/r_{\star}$.
Suppose $A\in\operatorname{rip}(\delta,k)$ with $\delta<\delta_{\mathrm{sharp}}(t)$. For
$\sigma\in\mathbb{R}^{d}$, the quantities $\mathsf{H}$ and $\mathsf{T}$ defined in \defref{HTD}
satisfy
\begin{equation}
\mathsf{H}\le\rho_{\delta,t}\,\mathsf{T}+\tau_{\delta,t}\,\normtwo{A\sigma}
\end{equation}
where $\rho_{\delta,t}$ and $\tau_{\delta,t}$ are defined in ((eq:rhotau of the paper)). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:37:51.457844+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_006374dab13050d4618ca9cee059bdd7e47e6c0cd6b0a0b5564f3cccca2022df","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 32 of arXiv:2604.03777, 'Equilibrium fluctuations for a multi-species particle system with long jumps'] Let $\gamma >0$, $0 \leq s \leq t \leq T$, $n \in \mathbb{N}_+$ and $ \widehat{b}_n \in \mathbb{R}$. Denote $C_{\alpha,\beta}:=8 \chi(\rho_{\alpha}) \chi(\rho_{\beta})$. For $1 \leq \ell_n \leq L_n$, it holds
		\begin{align*}
			\mathbb{E}_{\nu_{\rho}} \Bigg[ \Bigg\{ \widehat{b}_n \int_s^t \dd r \sum_{x}   \nabla H ( \tfrac{ \lfloor x - r v_n \rfloor }{n}  )    \big[   \Psi_{x, \ell_n}^{\alpha,\beta}(\eta_r^n) - \Psi_{x,L_n}^{\alpha,\beta}(\eta_r^n)  \big]  \Bigg\}^{2} \Bigg] \leq C_{\alpha,\beta} (t-s)^{2} n \frac{(\widehat{b}_n)^2}{\ell_n} \| \nabla H \|^{2}_{2,n}.
		\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:13:18.536584+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0072906a73c197a3988979d34c8efcff0a7415d3b7692407f4d8af50aa1a90cf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2608.30668, 'Recurrence and capacity of stable branching random walks'] \begin{equation*}{
\lim_{ R \to +\infty } \sup_{\lVert x \rVert, \lVert y \rVert \geq  R } \left\vert\frac{g_A(x,y)}{g_{\theta}(x,y)}-1\right\vert \to 0,
}\end{equation*}
where we recall that \(g_{\theta}(x,y)=g_{\theta}(y-x)\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.093314+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0074c7bc22ee03402e16890f0a31471d2c6b15d4512281989386bd588c7cec93","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop manytoone-lebesgue of arXiv:2411.12717, 'Excursion theory for Markov processes indexed by Lévy trees'] Under $\mathbb{N}_{x,r}^\bullet$ and  $\mathbf{N}_{x,r}^\bullet$, conditionally on $(\rho_U,\eta_U, \overline{W}_U)$, the
processes $(\rho,\overline{W})^{U,\leftarrow}$ and  $(\rho,\overline{W})^{U,\rightarrow}$ are independent and their 
 respective   conditional laws are as follows:
\begin{itemize}
\item the process $(\rho,\overline{W})^{U,\leftarrow}$ is distributed as  $(\eta, \overline{W})$ under $\mathbb{P}_{\eta_U, \rho_U,\overline{W}_U}^\dagger$; 
\item the process $(\rho,\overline{W})^{U,\rightarrow}$ is distributed as  $(\rho, \overline{W})$ under $\mathbb{P}_{\rho_U,\overline{W}_U}^\dagger$.
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

