{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:19:56.668871+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0166e1d290e5d09382b982771d6943739975ccd352c879696e8cf2d67e28311e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 6 of arXiv:2608.30875, 'A Decomposition Theorem for Topological Semi-small Maps'] A continuous proper surjection $ f: X \longrightarrow Y$ between path-connected, locally compact, Hausdorff spaces $X$ and $Y$ is called an \textbf{almost covering map}
     if 
     \begin{enumerate}
     	\item there exists a nowhere closed dense set $R \subset Y$ such that the restriction $f \vert_{f^{-1}(Y \setminus R)} : f^{-1}(Y \setminus R) \longrightarrow
     	Y \setminus R$ is a finite covering map, and
     	\item there is a finite decomposition $R=\bigsqcup_{\beta}T_{\beta}$ such that the restriction $f \vert_{f^{-1}(T_{\beta})}:f^{-1}(T_{\beta}) \longrightarrow T_{\beta}$ is a fiber bundle for each $\beta$.
     \end{enumerate}
     The set $Y \setminus R$ is called the regular set of the almost covering map $f$, and the set $R$ is referred to as a fibered set of the map $f$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:06:21.750255+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_016fb8a25623178fdcd2522b9a39a8c10d86eb76922e53a65c110ed0aa9dc221","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 40 of arXiv:2607.21374, 'Local structure at the maximum and sharp persistence asymptotics of rough fractional Brown'] For every finite \(T\subset(0,\infty)\cap\mathbb D\), there is a function
\(\omega_T(\delta)\downarrow0\) such that, uniformly over finite positive
constraint sets \(P\supset T\) and finite
\(N\subset[-\delta,0)\cap\mathbb D\),
\begin{equation}
  d_{\mathrm{BL}}\left(
    \mathcal L(G_T\mid A_P\cap A_N),
    \mathcal L(G_T\mid A_P)
  \right)
  \leq\omega_T(\delta).

\end{equation}
Here \(d_{\mathrm{BL}}\) is formed from the bounded metric
\begin{equation*}
  d_T(x,y):=1\wedge\sum_{t\in T}|x_t-y_t|
\end{equation*}
on \(\mathbb R^T\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.514074+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0195ca7628527b56c51de827afe7356b4bc93a14176716cbad76c7764c8c5029","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop poc of arXiv:2411.11759, 'Milstein-type schemes for McKean--Vlasov SDEs driven by Brownian motion and Poisson random'] If Assumptions \mbox{\normalfont  (asum:ic of the paper)} to \mbox{\normalfont  (asum:con of the paper)}    are satisfied, then the rate of convergence of the interacting particle system (equation eq:int of the paper) to the non-interacting particle system (equation eq:non-int of the paper)  is given~by
		\begin{align*}
			\sup_{i\in\{1,\ldots,N\}}\,\,\sup_{ t\in[0,T]}E|x_t^i-x_t^{i, N}|^2\leq K
			\begin{cases}
				N^{-1/2}, & \mbox{ if }  d <4,
				\\
				N^{-1/2}\ \log_2 N, & \mbox{ if } d=4,
				\\
				N^{-2/d}  &  \mbox{ if }d>4,
			\end{cases}
		\end{align*}
		where $K>0$ is a constant independent of $N$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.425795+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_01a01e2ee1645520d1550b334c4f906e213b3c124ca667f95791694c84656258","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 169 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Under the conditions of Proposition~\ref{Proposition_hex_hole_offcrit}, $\tilde{\boldsymbol{\mu}}$ has exactly two bands and $q^-(z)$ factorizes as:
