{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:47:04.925156+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_01e5813dae3c9bcb27392499dc0e99f704c18378d2316177642e7aacfc9a76f3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:local CLT of arXiv:2412.02160, 'A functional central limit theorem for weighted occupancy processes of the Karlin model'] Fix $\epsilon\in(0,1)$. Then, there exists $C>0$ such that
