{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.022633+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_01edfb8b0750e16bd8d9dba46efba614a5f880743b0d24a1bb39bbee23e3e71d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 8 of arXiv:2606.31528, 'Well-posedness and stationary distribution of free stochastic differential equations'] Assume the hypotheses of Theorem~\ref{thm:stationary}. Let $\mu$ be the stationary distribution for the solution $\{U_t\}_{t\geq 0}.$ Then for every $ f \in C_c^3(\mathbb{R}) $, there exist constants $ C_f, C >0$, independent of $ t $, such that 
