{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.895084+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_02bb3356d4b245e4528fcb813f53b9da101272659298f6c81d1acd6db255a9f4","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def: cocycle property of arXiv:2411.06861, 'Quenched invariance principle for random walks in random environments admitting a cycle de'] A random field $\Psi\colon \Omega \times \mathbb{Z}^{d} \to \mathbb{R}$ satisfies the \emph{cocycle property} if for $\mathbb{P}$-a.e.\ $\omega$

  \begin{align}

    \Psi(\omega, y) - \Psi(\omega,x)
    \;=\;
    \Psi(\tau_{x}\omega, y-x),
    \qquad \forall\, x, y \in \mathbb{Z}^{d}.
  \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:07.299601+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_02c4b49a0baff5efdf368ea314b51d021e8b022e8717c3479d32c3f80abaca20","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2606.23383, 'Near-Lipschitz stability of the Kim--Milman flow map'] For any probability measure $\mu$ with $\mom(\mu) \defeq (\int \|x\|^2\,\mu(\!\dd x))^{1/2} < \infty$ and any $t > 0$,
    \begin{align*}
        \FI(q_t^\mu\mmid \gamma)
        &\le e^{-2t}\,\mom^2(\mu) + \frac{e^{-4t}}{1-e^{-2t}}\,d\,.
    \end{align*}
    In particular, if $\mom(\mu) \le \sqrt d$,
    \begin{align*}
        \FI(q_t^\mu\mmid \gamma)
        &\le \frac{de^{-2t}}{1-e^{-2t}}\,.
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:58:01.570141+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_02cb0eafe10f58f608c9294dccdc752bbe8f3e76231baf38b14297ba912bd661","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 6 of arXiv:2608.27307, '2608.27307'] Under the assumptions of Theorem~\ref{thm:opt_ll}, let $E_*$ be a regular right edge in the sense of Definition~\ref{def:reg_r_edge}, the following statements hold.
