{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.229823+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_031add61fc009ee056b5c7a8e9f6dc3af26f669e8b9309c07621221a249c5d28","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] Let $\varepsilon>0$ and $n\in \N$. For all $M \in \N_0$, $i \in \lbr \varepsilon^{-1}\rbr$, and $z>0$, we define the events 
