{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.548279+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_05bb3c161f8c96d7759cf30ce4fbcd8a39a693707fc66137e9709417d9994065","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:kolmo of arXiv:2412.03366, 'Regularity of Weighted Tensorized Fractional Brownian Fields and associated function space'] Let $\alpha \in [0,1]$ be fixed. Assume that $\{X_{(x_1,x_2)}\}_{(x_1,x_2) \in \mathbb{R}^2}$ is a stochastic field for which there exist some constants $\beta, \eta, c, R>0$ such that 
   \begin{equation}  \mathbb{E}[|\Delta  X_{(h_1,h_2);(x_1,x_2)}|^\eta] \leq c \left(\max\{|h_1|,|h_2| \}^{1-\alpha}\min\{|h_1|,|h_2| \}^{1+\alpha}\right)^{1+\beta}
    \end{equation}
    for all $(x_1,x_2)\in \mathbb{R}^2$ and $(h_1,h_2) \in \mathbb{R}^2$ with $|h_1| < R$ and $|h_2|<R$. Then, there exists a version $\{\widetilde{X}_{(x_1,x_2)}\}_{(x_1,x_2) \in \mathbb{R}^2}$ of $\{X_{(x_1,x_2)}\}_{(x_1,x_2) \in \mathbb{R}^2}$ such that, for every $\gamma \in [0,\frac{\beta}{\eta})$ and for every bounded intervals $I,J$ of $\mathbb{R}$, for all $\omega \in \Omega$, there exists a finite constant $C(\omega)>0$ such that
    \begin{equation}
        |\Delta  \widetilde{X}_{(h_1,h_2);(x_1,x_2)}| \leq C(\omega)\left(\max\{|h_1|,|h_2| \}^{1-\alpha}\min\{|h_1|,|h_2| \}^{1+\alpha}\right)^\gamma
    \end{equation}
for every $x_1 \in I$, $x_2 \in J$ and $h_1, h_2 \in \mathbb{R}$ with $x_1+h_1 \in I$ and $x_2 + h_2 \in J$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-09T06:55:03+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_05beb096fdd08a18f563ae4bf3faa09c649950447d455aaac2d6eef17efbe131","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 32 of arXiv:2507.06186, '2507.06186'] For every $\ka>0$,
