{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:30:14.227799+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_05d89d15070d258d02d7d4cb4a197ae7788f1d638985e69803aea1f54d61608c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma C(a) definition of arXiv:2608.23202, 'Locally finite Fixed points of Branching Brownian Motion'] Let $f, \phi, u_\phi$ be as in Proposition (Bramson-psi-estimate-for-one-sided-f of the paper). Then, for $\alpha>0$ and $z= \alpha t+o(t)$,
