{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.212373+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_05d93081f3dbed8c965b7853c2db5d7ec6727e5118fd1c79a820ddd60c103924","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def: nets of arXiv:2512.06640, 'Existence and sharpness of the phase transition for the frog model on transitive graphs'] Let $V_0 \subseteq V$. We say $V_0$ is \textbf{$a$-separated} if $d_G(x, y) \ge a$ for all $x, y \in V_0$. For $b\geq 1,$ we say that $V_{0}$ forms an \textbf{$(a, b)$-group net} of $G$ if the auxiliary graph $ G_{0}:= (V_{0},E_{0}),$ where
\begin{align*}
	E_0 := \big\{ \{x, y\}: x,y \in V_0, \, d_G(x, y) \le 4b \big\},
\end{align*}
satisfies that $p^{\mathrm{site}}_c(G_0) \le 3/4$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:33:11.958610+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_05da51cd22f8016cbb798f4fed2f31116c3e475976ddd17ac45d945aa2a5ede2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Problem The rank-constrained Gaussian maximum of arXiv:2607.14087, 'Stochastic Domination of Gaussian Maxima: A Resolution of the Weak Simplex Conjecture'] \label[problem]{prob:rank-constrained}
Fix integers $m\geq3$ and $1\leq d<m-1$, and fix $\lambda>0$.  Determine
\[
  \max\left\{
    \mathbb E\exp\!\left(\lambda\max_{1\leq i\leq m}\xi_i\right):
    \xi\sim\mathcal N(0,G),\ G\text{ a correlation matrix},\ \rank G\leq d
  \right\},
\]
and characterize all maximizing covariance matrices.  In particular, determine
whether the maximizing configuration depends on $\lambda$. (Stated as a problem by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.419010+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_05deba9afe0451e9610406d49818f6148aab35dc02f160194c040d17f7a6be13","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn eq: restriction of a set to a closed ball of arXiv:2412.08236, 'Aging and sub-aging for Bouchaud trap models on resistance metric spaces'] [{The local Hausdorff metric $\lHausdMet{S}{\rho_{S}}$}]
  For $A \in \mathcal{C}(S)$ and $r>0$,
  we write 
  \begin{equation}  
    A^{(r)} 
    \coloneqq 
    \closure(A \cap B_{d^{S}}(\rho, r)), 
  \end{equation}
  where we recall that $\closure(\cdot)$ denotes the closure of a set.
  We then define, for $A,B \in \mathcal{C}(S)$,
  \begin{equation}
    \lHausdMet{S}{\rho_{S}} (A, B) 
    \coloneqq 
    \int_{0}^{\infty} e^{-r} \bigl( 1 \wedge d_{H}^{S}(A^{(r)}, B^{(r)}) \bigr)\, dr.
  \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.973015+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_05fde3d05ec646014b27b6681b7711d4cafd6d79be3879da9fbd3f090c4f0301","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:defTripleNorm of arXiv:2411.07157, 'Rough differential equations in the flow approach'] For every $N\geqslant1$, $\tau\in\mathcal{T}_*$ and $\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau} \in {\mcb{C}}[\tau]$, and  $\mu\in(0,1]$, set
    \begin{equs}        K^{\otimes 1+\mathfrak{s}(\tau)}_{N,\mu}\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^\tau(t,s^\tau)\eqdef \big(K_{N,\mu}\otimes\dots\otimes K_{N,\mu}\big)*\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^\tau(t,s^\tau)\,.
    \end{equs}
We then endow $\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^\tau$ with the norm
    \begin{equs}       \nnorm{\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^\tau}_{N,\mu} \eqdef \norm{K^{\otimes1+\mathfrak{s}(\tau)}_{N,\mu}\text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^\tau}_{L^\infty_tL^1_{s^\tau}((-\infty,1]\times\R^{\mathfrak{s}(\tau)})}\equiv \sup_{t\leqslant1}\int_{\R^{\mathfrak{s}(\tau)}} |K^{\otimes1+\mathfrak{s}(\tau)}_{N,\mu} \text{$\mathfrak{z}$}^{\tau}(t,s^\tau)|\mathrm{d} s^\tau\,.\textcolor{white}{blabl}
    \end{equs}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.974564+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_05fe0c30879270e6789b5d6e2b985c5c8014bb9a1750e7b0acdc3a1b3d37ecae","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2606.11142, 'Strong invariance principles for diffusions, Markov chains and their perturbations.'] Assume that conditions A1, A2, A3, A4 hold. Let $\mathbb{T}_n = \{t_1, \dots, t_n\}$, $\mathbb{T}_m = \{\tau_1, \dots, \tau_m\}$ be a micro and macro grids respectively, and $n = m^l$ for some $l > \frac{1}{\min(\gamma_2/2,\alpha_2,\beta)}$. Then, there exists a probability space supporting versions of the diffusion process $X_t$ and the Markov chain $Y_t$, and constants $C_1, C_2 > 0$ such that for every $1/2 < \alpha < 1$:
\begin{equation*}
\mathbb{P} \left( \sup_{t \in [0,1]} |X_t - Y_t| \ge 2m^{\alpha-1} + 2K_1m^{-1} \right) \le C_1 m \Delta^{(n)} + 4md \exp\left(-\frac{m^{2\alpha-1}}{2C_2 d}\right),
\end{equation*}
where $K_1$ is the upper bound for the norm of the drift and $Y_t$ is the linear interpolation of the Markov chain. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.245801+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_05fe82bd0d3fb4b115a1424d931dbf6a44de58c8e1889f4e1fbf2737f54bf832","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 71 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] Fix some $\ell \in \N$. 
