{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:01:48.571277+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0653e9538816d57f28300ab9238a290c7d96c6e60b9e6afcae2f27a36669b766","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:sig_vol_Fourier_laplace of arXiv:2606.29622, 'Affine Structure of the Brownian Signature'] Let $\bm{\sigma} \in \TA[2]$ with $\deg(\bm{\sigma}) = N$ satisfy either the assumption  (equation eq:martingality_condition of the paper) {or $\rho = 0$ and $\bm{\sigma}^{{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{1}}}^{\otimes N}} \neq 0$}. Suppose that $u, v \in \mathbb{C}$ are such that 
