{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.578257+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0675b93472e6008e1c922aa507ebf76cb280eda9af511256a94ef9e1991d48a7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 46 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d\geq 2$ and $G=(V,E)\subset H=(V',E')$ be two subgraphs of $\mathbb Z^d$. For every $\beta\geq 0$, and every $x,y \in V'$,
