{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.969641+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_06dc79b1447218b27d152272e36a13a3676d5e4c8d899ce083f9afd0cbfe82c2","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[0 3 of arXiv:2606.10058, 'Mean First Passage Times and Fundamental Tensors of Higher Order Markov Chains'] For an $m$th order tensor ${\cal A}=[a_{i_1i_2\ldots i_m}] \in \mathbb R^{u \times u \times n \times \cdots \times n}$, the diagonal tensor obtained from $\cal A$, denoted by ${\cal A}_d=[a^{[d]}_{i_1i_2\ldots i_m}]$, is defined as: for any $1 \le i_1, i_2 \le u$ and $1 \le i_3, \ldots, i_m \le n$, 
$$a^{[d]}_{i_1i_2i_3\ldots i_m}=a_{i_1i_2i_3\ldots i_m}\delta_{i_1i_2}=\left\{\begin{array}{cl}
a_{i_1i_1i_3\ldots i_m}, & i_1=i_2;\\
0, & {\rm otherwise}.
\end{array}\right.$$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.413374+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_06dcc14fee0a811704d48198e080f0b9911e028e0ff800de8265ae1708622afa","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:qRacah_ensemble of arXiv:2507.22011, 'Random Lozenge Waterfall:\\Dimensional Collapse of Gibbs Measures'] The $q$-Racah ensemble
	$\mathfrak{R}^{qR(N)}_{M,\alpha,\beta,\gamma,\delta}$
	depending on the parameters satisfying (equation eq:qRacah_parameters_nonnegative of the paper),
	is a probability measure on $N$-tuples of particles $(x_1<\ldots<x_N )$ in $\{0,1,\ldots,M \}$,
	with probability weights given by
	\begin{equation}

		\mathfrak{R}^{qR(N)}_{M,\alpha,\beta,\gamma,\delta}(x_1,\ldots,x_N )=
		\frac{1}{Z(N,M,\alpha,\beta,\gamma,\delta)}
		\prod_{1\le i<j\le N}\left( \mu(x_i)-\mu(x_j) \right)^2
		\prod_{i=1}^{N}w^{qR}(x_i).
	\end{equation}
	Here $Z(N,M,\alpha,\beta,\gamma,\delta)$ is the normalization constant ensuring that the total probability is~$1$. The condition $M \ge N-1$ in (equation eq:qRacah_parameters_nonnegative of the paper) is required so that $N$ particles can fit into $\{0,1,\ldots, M \}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:26:02.477324+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_06e72eb7e0733d5b9c6cd9cef5d3fd9cf0b806ab6acf4ea97713a9c7949c866e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem convexbifurcation of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] After some arbitrarily $C^\infty$-small perturbation of $\xi$, there exists finitely many times $0 < t_1 < \dots < t_N < 1$ such that 
    \begin{itemize}
        \item If $t \neq t_i$, then $S_t$ is $\xi$-convex ,
        \item At $t=t_i$, a pair of parallel closed characteristics of $\xi|_{S_t}$ is born or dies.
    \end{itemize}
    Moreover, when a pair of characteristics is born (in forwards time), a $\flat$ annulus appears between them, and when a pair of characteristics dies, a $\sharp$ annulus disappears between them (see \zcref{fig:birthdeath}). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.355068+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_06e84e2f417e6966609a72c9e90e252a32309b45eb7cfb712f5acd51bb4a05f5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2511.09280, 'Random Walk conditioned to stay above a non-flat floor: curvature effects'] There are \(n_0\geq 1\), \(c>0\) such that for any \(n\geq n_0\),
