{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.726578+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_07bcf2301cd785a2d1a9ebe3333f3d9b14dce360609de6f3d387f3d8e7a72caf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma operators_with_M of arXiv:2411.17653, 'Exclusion processes with non-reversible boundary: hydrodynamics and large deviations'] Fix a path $\pi(t,dx)=\rho_t(x)\;dx$ in $ {\mathcal{D}}([0,T],\mathscr{M}_{ac})$. Assume $ {\rho}$  {to satisfy the same hypothesis as in Lemma (decomposition_lemma of the paper).} Then, there exists an $M\in L^2(\sigma(\rho)^{-1})$ satisfying 
