{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:44.956017+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_08b2c07d00081954d96141cdb8ea8bce05fabbc8a01561d01fd79290097662db","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 of arXiv:2606.25501, 'An RDT based approach to large deviations of Wishart and Wigner matrices spectral edges'] Consider large $n\in\mN$  and let $A_{ij}\sim \cN(0,1)$ be the independent elements of $A\in\mR^{n\times n}$. For a real scalar $c_3\geq 0$ set
