{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:31:49.912139+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a3d6abefee0cf9df70be4163711cabec61f7946593e041bcd027e8faa002dbc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lm:ProbEstimate of arXiv:2608.27828, 'Scaling limit of the 3D abelian Yang--Mills Langevin dynamics'] Let $T>0$, $p \geq 2$, and $0<\kappa<1$ sufficiently small. Then, for any $\tilde\kappa\in (0,\kappa)$,
\begin{align}

 \E\sup_{t\in [0,T]}\|\tilde \Psi^\varepsilon(t)\|^p_{\CC^{-1/2-\kappa}_\varepsilon} & \le C_{p,T}  \;,
 \\

  \E \sup_{t\in [0,T]} \norm{  \varepsilon^{4}\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}_\varepsilon^* (\mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}_\varepsilon\tilde\Psi^\varepsilon )^3 (t)}^p_{\CC^{-3/2-2\kappa}_\varepsilon}
