\end{equation}
in the Le Donne--Z\"ust signature tree. Every point of the endpoint geodesic is therefore attained by a prefix of the original parametrised path. The geodesic trace and its order are independent of the auxiliary Euclidean norm.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:09.856704+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a4134d4921c1491d4d1f853f6a0cca7b784f43a4b25d28b70efabf5b8ea9f0d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2605.20115, 'Moment bounds on correctors for the degenerate random conductance model'] Suppose that $1\le p_0< p_1 \le \infty$, $C,C_0\ge1$, and $g,h\in L^{p_0}\cap L^{p_1}(\ZZ^d)$ are non-negative. Assume that on any ball $B$, there exist $g_{B,0},g_{B,1}\ge0$  such that
    \begin{gather}
        g\le g_{B,0}+g_{B,1}, \quad g_{B,1}\le g+g_{B,0}\quad  \text{ on } B;\nonumber\\
        \Big(\fint_B|g_{B,0}|^{p_0}\Big)^{\frac1{p_0}} \le C\Big(\fint_{C_0B}|h|^{p_0}\Big)^{\frac1{p_0}};\\
        \Big(\fint_{\frac1{C_0}B}|g_{B,1}|^{p_1}\Big)^{\frac1{p_1}} \le C\Big(\fint_{B}|g_{B,1}|^{p_0}\Big)^{\frac1{p_0}}.
    \end{gather}
    Then for all $q\in(p_0,p_1)$,
    \begin{equation}
        \int_{\ZZ^d} |g|^q\lesssim_{p_0,p_1,q,C,C_0}\int_{\ZZ^d} |h|^q. 
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:44:28.001856+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0a49576e8091a2fcb4548197f7d970dcd400a26deb1c368a57fe91419df6f117","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 4 of arXiv:2607.13308, 'No infinite clusters at criticality for two-dimensional dependent percolation under abstra'] Under~\eqref{h2},~\eqref{h3}, and~\eqref{h4}, there exists $\uc{c:fsc}>0$ such that, if
