{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.102593+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0ae6f4cddcde1f32f0454d7ef301f355296a4c200d70118d9246f7d79d1f1d37","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lem:pathcounting of arXiv:2411.13030, 'Classification of the limit shape for 1+1-dimensional FPP'] Given integers  $M \ge k \ge 1$, let $S(M,k)$  be the number of distinct $k$-tuples $(a_1,...,a_k)$ of integers whose absolute values sum up to $M$. We then have that
