{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.705956+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0ae8ace0ee353261a460f44fb387759ad4b53d6b202e710571be47c2374422d6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem rep1 of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] There exists a constant $c > 0$ such that, if $k$ is large enough, for any $i,j \in \mathbb N$ with $i<j$, $n \geq k$ and $x,\widetilde{x} \in {\rm D}_n$ such that $x \in {\rm B}^-[\widetilde{x};j-1]$ and $\overline{{\rm B}^+[\widetilde{x};j]}\subseteq {\rm D}_n$, we have that	
