{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:36:04.989859+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0b51292cce831b02f307fc479cff7e9ee2add7a4723d77d22f93b6f25f966000","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 of arXiv:2604.00882, 'On some extensions of generalized counting processes'] The solution ${p}_k^\nu(t)$, for $k = 0, 1, \dots$ and $t \ge 0$, of \eqref{(3.1)-(3.2)}, with $\Lambda<\lambda^2$, is given by
	\begin{equation}

		{p}_k^\nu(t) = \lambda^{2k} t^{2k\nu} E_{\nu, 2k\nu+1}^{k+1, k+1}(p_1 t^\nu, p_2 t^\nu) + \lambda^{2k+1} t^{(2k+1)\nu} E_{\nu, (2k+1)\nu+1}^{k+1, k+1}(p_1 t^\nu, p_2 t^\nu),
	\end{equation}
	where
	\begin{equation}
	p_1 = -\lambda + \sqrt{\lambda^2 - \Lambda}, \quad p_2 = -\lambda - \sqrt{\lambda^2 - \Lambda},
	\end{equation}
	and the multivariate Mittag-Leffler function is defined in \eqref{multML}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.056897+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0b57a38fe3409937fba587da416af2f857ebabb4db93c08e0c466e3a31d9c7e1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 28 of arXiv:2606.16636, 'Free energy of non-convex multi-species spin glasses with centered Ising spins'] Let $t>0$ and $q\in\mcl Q_{\upa,c}^\D$ for some $c>0$. There is a constant $b>0$ such that
