{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:43:00.039786+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0cca192143b39d246baad89234891da7026a83d89dae34913c2bf87f97a93329","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 6 of arXiv:2609.00743, '$L_p$ Brunn-Minkowski inequality for the eigenvalue of generalized Monge-Ampère equation'] There exists $u\in C^{2,\alpha}(\bar{\Omega})\cap C^\infty(\Omega)$ which is a solution to \eqref{general MA} for $\lambda=\underline{\lambda}_{n+k+1}$, where
