{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:42:16.236156+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0ec7cb8b7e0919b22824cda34498a8de2bea32619bbabdc001fcea5952981a25","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem prop:uniform-time-averaged-w1 of arXiv:2607.00149, '\bf Uniform-in-time Propagation-of-Chaos for\\ Stein Variational Gradient Descent'] Let Assumption~(ass:w1-normalized-matern of the paper) hold.  Recall the constant $c_0$ from Lemma~(lem:finite-time-w1 of the paper). Let $$\gamma := (3(1+7d/6+2\nu))^{-1}.$$ Then, there exists a finite constant $C>0$ such that, for any $\delta>0$ and all sufficiently large $N$,
