{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:06.329311+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_0f784ab78f5d44f8471b96112d185995b8c44880bc9d30083bab99c638e1c6c6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 11 of arXiv:2607.06428, 'Impact of spinning on the early-warning signs in non-Markovian stochastic systems'] Let $H\in(0,1)$, $\sigma>0$, $\tau\ge0$ and $(x_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be a solution to \eqref{eq:fast system simplified} that satisfies \nameref{S1}. Then, we get that
