{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.377166+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_103e5af22a599e4cda4c9b93efe211a5a9f43b4d7b001af4a0e1602bf62aba3f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:fsecondorder of arXiv:2412.01995, 'Exciting games and Monge-Amp\`{e}re equations'] Suppose $x^0 \in \partial \Delta$ with $x^0_1=\dotso=x^0_k=0$, $x^0_{k+1},\dotso,x^0_d >0$, and $\sum_{j=k+1}^d x_j^0<1$. Taking $r= (1-\sum_{i=k+1}^d x^0_i)/{(2d)}$,  there exist two positive constants $c_1(x^0)$, $c_2(x^0)$ such that for any $x_1,\dotso, x_k \in (0,r)$,
