 For every $(\kappa,R)\in (0, +\infty)\times[0, +\infty)$, there exists $\lambda_0>0$ such that {if $\mathbf{(S_{\kappa,R,\lambda})}$ holds with $\lambda\le \lambda_0$}, then for every  $\varepsilon>0$,  there exists a functional $\Upsilon$ defined on $\ER^d\times{\cal C}((-\infty,0],\ER^d)$ such that for every $0\le s\le t$, $\P$-$a.s.$, 
