{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.606205+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1133f8e6b5ea97e162fab22a986ccedad6192181d7ad0b95dee7dca14c4011a9","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2606.03079, 'Mean Field Limits for Stochastic, Underdamped Reactive Langevin Dynamics Models'] For $x \in \mathbb{R}^{d}$, let $G(x)$ denote a standard positive mollifier and $G_{\eta}(x)=\eta^{-d} G(x / \eta)$. That is, $G(x)$ is a smooth function on $\mathbb{R}^{d}$ satisfying the following four requirements
