{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.059851+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_118b16a701c34e8bb395e244021d06f12018e1d78cf6896a1194150c19c6f984","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 8 (Finite second-order tensor estimate) of arXiv:2606.16662, '2606.16662'] Let \(A,B,C,E\) be finite sets and set
\[
        \Lfin=2+|A|+|B|+|C|+|E|.
\]
Let \((g_a)_{a\in A}\) and \((h_b)_{b\in B}\) be independent standard real Gaussian families.  For a deterministic tensor \(H=(H_{a,b,c,e})\), define the random matrix
\begin{equation}
        Z_{e,c}=\sum_{a\in A}\sum_{b\in B}H_{a,b,c,e}g_ah_b .
\end{equation}
Define the four-cut norm
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
\mathfrak R_4(H):=\max\bigl\{&
  \|H\|_{\ell^2_{a,b,c}\to\ell^2_e},
  \ \|H\|_{\ell^2_{a,b,e}\to\ell^2_c},\\
 &\|H\|_{\ell^2_{a,c}\to\ell^2_{b,e}},
  \ \|H\|_{\ell^2_{b,c}\to\ell^2_{a,e}}
\bigr\}.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
Then, for every \(p\ge2\),
\begin{equation}
        \bigl\|\|Z\|_{\ell^2_c\to\ell^2_e}\bigr\|_{L^p(\Omega)}
        \le C\bigl(p+\log\Lfin\bigr)\mathfrak R_4(H),
\end{equation}
where \(C\) is an absolute constant.  The same bound holds for complex Gaussian families after realification and, after the order-two decoupling in Lemma~\ref{lem:local-normal-form}, for arbitrary finite centered quadratic Gaussian chaoses.  It is also stable under the finite sign, real-Fourier and auxiliary-coordinate patterns produced there: each pattern is estimated separately, and a bounded enlargement of the Gaussian legs or a finite sum of pattern bounds changes only the implicit constant.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:42.304367+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_11a07a4f1faeb54a1588f92131bec61dbbb052be944039140efdd919703a6169","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 53 (Backwards-time propagation of test functions in $d \geq 3$) of arXiv:2510.22155, 'Random walks in space-time random media in all spatial dimensions: the full subcritical fl'] Let $d\ge 3$. Assume $\x_N=(x^1_N,x^2_N)$ is any sequence such that $N^{-1/2}x_N^1 \to x_1$ and $x^1_N-x^2_N$ converges to $y\in I$ (\textit{without} any normalization), and consider the same setting as Assumption \ref{ass:SRI}. 
      Consider smooth bounded functions $\phi_1, ..., \phi_m : \mathbb R^d\to \mathbb R$ with globally bounded and continuous first and second partial derivatives, and consider $f^1,..., f^m : I\to \mathbb R$ continuous of exponential decay at infinity. Then \begin{align} 
    \lim_{N\to\infty}\notag  \Ebbnn &\bigg[\sum_{0\leq r_1 < \ldots < r_m \leq Nt} \prod_{\ell =1}^m f^{\ell}(   R^1_{r_{\ell}}-   R^2_{r_{\ell}})\phi_{\ell}(N^{-1/2} (R^1_{r_\ell}-   s_N r_\ell))\bigg] \\&=  \phi_1 (x_1) \cdots \phi_m(x_1) \sum_{0\le r_1 < ...< r_m<\infty } \; \mathbf E^{\boldsymbol b_{\mathrm{dif}}}_y \big[ f^1(X_{r_1}) \cdots f^m(X_{r_m}) ].\end{align}
    The claim remains true if we replace $(f^1,...,f^m)$ on the left side by some sequence $(f^1_N,...,f^m_N)$ equicontinuous and converging uniformly on compact sets as $N\to\infty$ to some $(f^1,...,f^m)$, as long as $\sup_{N} |f^j_N|$ decays exponentially fast at infinity for $j=1,...,m$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:42.305970+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_11a25cb4e4b1b09d6e009881a809c97a06acd4dbe0b3c03377eea4701753b8a9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 70 (Martingale tightness bound) of arXiv:2510.22155, 'Random walks in space-time random media in all spatial dimensions: the full subcritical fl'] Fix $q\ge 1$ and 
