{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:23:27.755754+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_11f602707edba296f1c085db5a953ba793910b1e135c3a50a976e39306278d33","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:absolute-compensators-paper of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] Fix \(d\in\mathfrak D_{\xi,n}^{\mathrm{osc}}\), and write \(m=m_{\xi,d}\). Define
\[
\mathfrak C^{\mathrm{pre}}_{\xi,d,n}
=
\sum_{\ell=0}^{m-1}
\sum_{I\in\mathcal D_\ell^\circ}
\sum_{\substack{J\in\mathcal D_{\ell+1}^\circ\\J\subset I}}
\lvert D_{J,n}\rvert,
\]
and
\[
\mathfrak C^{\mathrm{post}}_{\xi,d,n,L}
=
\sum_{\ell=m}^{L-1}
\sum_{I\in\mathcal D_\ell^\circ}
\sum_{\substack{J\in\mathcal D_{\ell+1}^\circ\\J\subset I}}
\lvert D_{J,n}\rvert.
\]
Set
\[
\mathfrak C^{\mathrm{pre}}_{\xi,n}
=
\sum_{d\in\mathfrak D_{\xi,n}^{\mathrm{osc}}}
\mathfrak C^{\mathrm{pre}}_{\xi,d,n},
\qquad
\mathfrak C^{\mathrm{post}}_{\xi,n,L}
=
\sum_{d\in\mathfrak D_{\xi,n}^{\mathrm{osc}}}
\mathfrak C^{\mathrm{post}}_{\xi,d,n,L}.
\]
When the limit exists, set \(\mathfrak C^{\mathrm{post}}_{\xi,n}=\lim_{L\to\infty}\mathfrak C^{\mathrm{post}}_{\xi,n,L}\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:12:19.518788+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_12072082a705b32baf7f42a41753b5f4c1a2da31fd93368ad1256a1907d7db76","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 (Samuels' conjecture) of arXiv:2608.18392, 'On Samuels' Conjecture'] For every integer $n\geq1$, ordered mean vector $0\leq\mu_1\leq\cdots\leq\mu_n$, and $\lambda>\sum_{i=1}^n\mu_i$,
\begin{equation}
c(\bm{\mu},\lambda)
=
\min_{1\leq i\leq n} q_i(\bm{\mu},\lambda)
=
\min_{1\leq i\leq n} \prod_{j=i}^n \left( 1- \frac{\mu_j}{ \lambda-\sum_{k=1}^{i-1}\mu_k } \right).

\end{equation}
The bound is sharp and is attained. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:43:18.803020+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_12080dc10b73ecf28320a571b594054bf39fc23053a5fc02741661ba6ea4b3f3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conj GW:vertex of arXiv:2609.02409, 'Membranes and Maps'] For $n\in\{1,\ldots,5\}$ and curve class $\beta = [C_1]+\cdots+[C_n]$, the equivariant Gromov--Witten theory of $Z_n$ is given by
    \begin{equation}

       \GWargs{Z_n}{\mathsf{T}}{\beta} 
       =
       \hat{\mathsf{A}}_{\mathsf{T}}\bigl( \overline{M}_{0}(Z_n,\beta) \bigr) \,,
    \end{equation}
