{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:01:15.327740+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_122950a677988d9388878c89440f4dc39de32c446f35765c99c37bbc7fe568f3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 2 of arXiv:2608.30357, 'Mean convergence for Banach space-valued random elements indexed in measure spaces'] Let $p \in (0, \infty)$ and assume
 $\{K_n : n \ge 1\}$ is a family of compact subsets of $\cX$. A collection $\{X^n_s : s\in S_n, n \ge 1\}$ of $\cX$-valued random elements is \textit{$(\nu_n)$-compactly uniformly $p$-th order integrable w.r.t. $\{K_n\}$} (or $(\nu_n)$-$\CUI(p)$ w.r.t. $\{K_n\}$, for short) if:
	\begin{enumerate}[\rm (a)]
		\item the map $(\omega, s) \mapsto X^n_s(\omega)$ is $\cF \otimes \cS_n/\cB(\cX)$-measurable for every $n \ge 1$,

		\item  the following convergence holds:
		\begin{align}
			\lim_{n \to \infty} \bE\int_{S_n} \lt\|X^n_s\rt\|^p \1_{\{X^n_s \notin K_n\}} \nu_n(\od s)  =0.
		\end{align}
	\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

