{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:44:39.744951+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_128d16dc0c9717a008d56b9d25442a5310df1d287ac75a90a2bb96ecae7b113b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2608.29872, 'Local Laws and Outlier Eigenvalues for Spiked Separable Covariance Matrices'] Suppose the assumptions \eqref{eq_ratio}, \eqref{assm3}, and \eqref{assm_gap} hold. Then
there exists sufficiently small constant $\wt c>0$ such that the following estimates hold:
\begin{itemize}
