{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.577170+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_156fbdb367c2a4376537b258e6dea92a4fb0f472a675bbc40e4d5b6bd4f29cef","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 13 of arXiv:2606.14812, 'Joint convergence in Wiener chaos via transport hierarchy and Malliavin covariances'] Let $p\geq 2$ and let $(X_N=I_p(f_N), N\geq 1)$ with $f_N\in H^{\odot p}$ 
		for all $N\geq 1$. Assume that $(X_N, N\geq 1)$ satisfies \eqref{c1}. 
		Let $Y_N=I_q(g_N)$ with $q=ap$ for some integer $a\geq 1$. Assume that
		\begin{equation*}
			(Y_N, Y_{1,N}, \ldots, Y_{a-1,N}) \xrightarrow[N\to\infty]{(d)} 
			(Y, Y_1, \ldots, Y_{a-1}),
		\end{equation*}
		and that there exists $\rho_a\in\mathbb{R}$ such that
		\begin{equation*}
			\mathbf{E}[Y_{a,N}] \xrightarrow[N\to\infty]{} \rho_a.
