{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.777583+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_16424a63d12daba461e5dd087a805eb6c9930dff797c06c2384a46ed7af8410c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Coro Feller-Full of arXiv:2411.19543, 'Feller property and convergence for semigroups of time-changed processes'] Assume that $F=X$. Then we have the following:
