{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:42:47.765183+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_16e27359252ce20abfa574316242ce7779e8d306cec2d75b4a173137e037e5a5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 9 (Martingale structure) of arXiv:2604.12797, 'A free boundary problem for the mean-field limit of diffusing particles with nonlinear bou'] For any $\phi \in C^1(\R)$, the limit points of $(Z^{n,\phi})_{n\geq 1}$ are continuous processes. Moreover, let $\psi_{\varepsilon}$ be the probability density function of a reflected
