{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:20:55.532216+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_182744132a8187d3d6f31195e499a196f34317590071a2a6ba52f27d7f889e5f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm Main Theorem of arXiv:2411.07671, 'Long Time Behavior of General Markov Additive Processes'] Let $(\xi,\Theta),\mathbb{P})$ be a MAP such that Assumptions 1,2,3, and 4 are satisfied. Then, we have
\begin{enumerate}[label=(\roman*)]
