{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:32:18.868323+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_184b76f3c60ce45b40483e73aec19bca24b65d05aa0a0be9197c7f69b356172a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 76 of arXiv:2609.03875, 'Measure theory without infinities'] Let $\eta_1$ and $\eta_2$ be $\mf R$-valued maps, $\mu_1 = \mf F\eta_1$, and $\mu_2 = \mf F\eta_2$.
