        \lim_{N\to\infty}\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{N} \mathrm{Tr}\left(\kappa_r^{\mathcal{B}_N}\bigl(V_N^{\epsilon(1)}b_{1,N},\ldots,V_N^{\epsilon(n)}b_{n,N}\bigr)\right)\right]=(-1)^{m-1}C_{m-1}.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.745358+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1997a0051736b62d85d5f63dd491560a46551c430cf3409b0315c5b7f4275407","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:energy-admissible-vector-law of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] The dyadic vector-weight law is called \emph{energy-admissible} if
