{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:34:09.925837+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1afdd57e29dd23ea2e7c0530555c2a3d1f79f8b9cdeb976f355f16e609de6fc4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 24 of arXiv:2603.27433, 'The $k$-cycle shuffling with repeated cards'] Let $l\ge 2$ be a fixed integer, $(n_N)_{N\ge 1},(m_N)_{N\ge 1},(k_N)_{N\ge 1}$, and $(t_N)_{N\ge 1}$ be sequences of positive integers that satisfy the following:
\begin{enumerate}
\item $n_N=m_N\cdot l$ for all $N\ge 1$.
\item $\lim_{N\rightarrow\infty}m_N=\infty$.
\item $k_N\ge 2$ for all $N\ge 1$, and $\lim_{N\rightarrow\infty}\frac{k_N\log n_N}{n_N}=0$.
\item $t_N=\frac{n_N}{k_N}(\log n_N+c)$ for all $N\ge 1$, where $c\in\R$ is an absolute constant.
\end{enumerate}
Then, we have
$$\lim_{N\rightarrow\infty}d_{TV}(\sim_{l}\backslash P_{n_N,k_N}^{*t_N},\sim_{l}\backslash U_{\S_{n_N}})=d_{TV}(\Pois(l+\exp(-c)),\Pois(l)).$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:51:52.060193+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1afdeca72894eceb3e15e3ccd92dd393d3968e4b70655c47dd796d58cb385e6d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition classiquedecomposition of arXiv:2607.14792, 'On the degree distribution of large tentacular Bienaymé--Galton--Watson trees'] Let $(X_i)_{i \geq 1}$ and $(Y_i)_{i \geq 1}$ be the i.i.d. increments of $W$ and $W'$, respectively. We define $(\widehat{X}_i)_{i \geq 1}$ as the sequence obtained from $(X_i)_{i \geq 1}$ by removing all steps equal to $-1$. 
     Let $f : \mathbb{R}^{n-k_n} \to \mathbb{R}_+ $ be a measurable and stable by cyclic permutation function.
     Then, we have the following equality:
     \begin{align*}
   & \mathbb{E}\left[ f\left( (\widehat{X}_i)_{1\leq i \leq n-k_n}\right) \1_{ W_n=-1, \ W_i \geq 0 \, \forall i \in [\![1,n-1]\!], \ |\{i \in [\![1,n]\!] : X_{i}=-1\}|=k_n  }\right] \\ & \qquad = \frac{1}{n}\binom{n}{k_n}\mu(0)^{k_n}\left(1-\mu(0) \right)^{n-k_n}  \mathbb{E}\left[ f\left( (Y_i)_{1\leq i \leq n-k_n}\right) \1_{W'_{n-k_n}=k_n-1} \right].
   \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:34:45.634932+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1affbcf3422b96a627d02e7dba004c5f278d4f0490808d14e94566d1c134e03d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:AsympSimplexD1 of arXiv:2609.01825, 'On everywhere locally soluble varieties \\ in families over toric bases'] Let $f \colon \mathbb R^s \to \mathbb R$ be given by $f(\vec t) = \prod_{i=1}^s (t_i + 1)^{\ell_i}$ for any $\vec \ell \in \mathbb R^s$. Let $C \in \mathbb R_{\geq 0}$, $\vec c \in \mathbb R_{>0}^m$, $\vec x \in \mathbb R^s$ and $W \in \mathbb R^{s \times m}$ be a matrix such that $W \vec t + \vec x \in \mathbb R_{\geq 0}^s$ for all $\vec t \in C \Delta^m$. Then uniformly in all $C \geq 0$, we have
	\begin{multline*}
		\int_{C \Delta^m} \exp\Bigl(-\sum_{i=1}^m c_i t_i \Bigr) f(W \vec t + \vec x) \,\mathrm d\vec t = \frac{ f(\vec x)}{c_1 \cdots c_m}\\
		+ O_{W, \vec c}\Bigl( \mathrm e^{-\min_i c_i C} (C+1)^{m-1} \max_{\vec t \in C \Delta^m} |f(W \vec t + \vec x)| \Bigr)\\
		+ O_{W, \vec c}\biggl( \int_{C \Delta^m} \exp\Bigl(-\sum_{i=1}^m c_i t_i \Bigr) \tilde f(W \vec t + \vec x) \,\mathrm d\vec t \biggr),
	\end{multline*}
	where $\tilde f(\vec t) = f(\vec t) (\min_i t_i + 1)^{-1}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:45:27.885376+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1b0ae9492dfffdd83d8f460e08aab0e950183cc94c03bdf34cade4a5fb23af2f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Weg of arXiv:2607.02367, 'Flux solutions for stochastic chemical systems with sources and sinks'] The following statements hold for mass action systems. 
\begin{enumerate} 
