{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.976532+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1b6236e3efdac312889ae4d6a0ca287372af5b96155047527a1eeccece50c764","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 16 of arXiv:2606.11271, '\LARGE The $K$-th nearest neighbor random walk on a Poisson point process gets trapped'] For any $\varepsilon >0$, $R\in \N^*$ and $n\in \N$, $X_n$ is called an $(\varepsilon,R)$-nice point if there exists $u \in \Z^d$ such that
