\]
and $C_n(s)$ is the leading tail coefficient of $f_n(s,\cdot)$ from
Lemma~(lem:kernel-asymp of the paper)(iii). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.864893+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1c88b634c0dfe193f04e75dde6398cb3868227a050980c4a2fc8f5efc24f6e4a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 19 of arXiv:2506.10856, 'The space of multifurcating ranked tree shapes: enumeration, lattice structure, and Markov'] The tree $\ddot{T}_N$ with the maximum backwards degree in $\mathcal{MT}_N$ is the multifurcating tree with the following properties 
\begin{enumerate}
    \item It has $K=\lfloor \frac{N-2}{2} \rfloor+1$ internal nodes.
    \item Each of the $\lfloor \frac{N-2}{2} \rfloor$ non-root internal nodes subtend distinct cherries descending from the root.
    \item The rest of the $L=2 + (N \text{ mod } 2)$ tips are leaves descending from the root.
\end{enumerate}
