{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.712216+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1c8fec3cd40adf769c25da01112b63778087083070e6286fe1848260c766447c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition defn_Mm of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] We define $m(z)\equiv m_N(z)$ as the unique solution to 
