{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:49.288968+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1ccda063301a6069b48b921d7bcdc7616255a432b6da11b0868dd842ee4ad0f3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 7 of arXiv:2606.23099, 'Path-dependent Affine Processes'] Let $X$ be an affine process on $S$ satisfying the full-support condition, Condition \ref{cond:full support_inhom} and Assumption~\ref{LG-Condition}.
    Then, there exist $b^0: [0,T]  \to \R^d$,\ $a^0 : [0,T] \to \R^{d \times d}$ and $b^i: [0,T] \to \ccM([0,T],\R^d)$, $a^i : [0,T] \to \ccM([0,T],\R^{d\times d})$, $i=1,\dots,d$, such that
    \begin{align}
        b(t,x_{[0,t]}) & = b^0(t) + \sum_{i=1}^d  b^i(t) \cdot x^i_{[0,t]}, \\

        a(t,x_{[0,t]}) & = a^0(t) + \sum_{i=1}^d  a^i(t) \cdot x^i_{[0,t]},
    \end{align}
    for all $(t,x) \in \ccC_T(S)$. Moreover, the functions $\phi$ and $\psi$ satisfy the following generalized Riccati equations
    \begin{align}
        \phi'(t,T,\mu) & = -\psi(t,T,\mu) b^0(t) - \frac{1}{2} \psi(t,T,\mu) a^0(t) \psi(t,T,\mu)^\top, \quad dt\text{-a.e. on } t \in [0,T],                   \\

        \psi(t,T,\mu)  & = \mu([t,T]) + \int_{t}^{T} \psi(s,T,\mu)B(s,\Ind_{[t,s]}) + \frac{1}{2} A(s,\Ind_{[t,s]}, \psi(s,T,\mu)) \, ds, \quad t \in (0,T],
    \end{align}
    with $\phi(T,T,\mu)=0$ and $\Psi(T,T,\mu)=\mu$,
    where $\psi$ is given by Assumption~\ref{ass:sm-diff-Psi} and $\phi'(t,T,\mu)$ denotes a Lebesgue density of $\phi$.
    Furthermore,
    \begin{align}
        \begin{split}
            \Psi(t,T,\mu) \cdot X_{[0,t]} & = \Psi(0,T,\mu) \cdot X_{[0,0]} + \int_{0}^{t} \psi(s,T,\mu) \, dX(s)                                                                                             \\
                                          & \quad - \int_{0}^{t} \sum_{i = 1}^{d} \psi(s,T,\mu) ( b^i(s) \cdot X^i_{[0,s]}) + \frac{1}{2} \psi(s,T,\mu) ( a^i(s) \cdot X^i_{[0,s]}) \psi(s,T,\mu)^\top \, ds,
        \end{split}
    \end{align}
    with
    \begin{equation*}
        \Psi(0,T,\mu)(\{0\}) = \mu([0,T]) + \int_{0}^{T} \psi(s,T,\mu)B(s,\Ind_{[0,s]}) + \frac{1}{2} A(s,\Ind_{[0,s]}, \psi(s,T,\mu)) \, ds.
    \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.770093+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1ccdfc26e2def180a59086c25e6325a761e40871b7e7ee61ebf15b41c70f7017","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 34 of arXiv:2603.24616, 'Pinning in non-critical half-space geometric last passage percolation'] Fix $q \in (0,1)$, $c \in [0,1)$ and put $p = \frac{q}{1-q}$, $\sigma = \sqrt{p(1+p)}$. In addition, fix $\epsilon$, $\eta$, $M^{\mathrm{bot}}$, $M^{\mathrm{side}}$, $A^{\mathrm{sep}}$, $A^{\mathrm{gap}}\in (0, \infty)$, $\Delta^{\mathrm{gap}}  \in (0,1/2)$, and $k \in \mathbb{N}$. There exist $W_1 \in \mathbb{N}$ and $\delta > 0 $, depending on all previously listed constants, such that the following holds for all $n \geq W_1$. If we assume:
