{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:34:09.925284+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1d70cd0d0623b2f36e488d5800b94e049092ff3ee0079110a22d8f31fffaaeee","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 17 of arXiv:2603.27433, 'The $k$-cycle shuffling with repeated cards'] Let $P_{n,k}$ be the random permutation in $\S_n$ given by
\begin{equation}
P_{n,k}:=\begin{cases}
(i_1\ldots i_k) & \text{with probability }\frac{k}{n(n-1)\cdots(n-k+1)}\\
\text{otherwise} & \text{with probability zero}\end{cases}.
\end{equation}
Moreover, for any $t\ge 1$, let $P_{n,k}^{*t}$ be the $t$-fold convolution of $P_{n,k}$. If $k$ is even and $t$ is odd, we view $P_{n,k}^{*t}$ as a random variable in $\A_n^c$; otherwise, we view $P_{n,k}^{*t}$ as a random variable in $\A_n$. Given $n=ml$ with $l\ge 2$, the random variable $\sim_l\backslash P_{n,k}^{*t}\in\sim_l\backslash\S_n$ is induced from \Cref{defi: quotient of space} in the obvious way.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.858300+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1d736838681dfcba5cc1d29c82fab30ca97874f014804c1b8c3575f49fac2651","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:supp_lmeasx of arXiv:2606.11951, 'On Skorokhod Problems for Reflected and Singular Stochastic Heat Equations'] The set $\mathcal{G}_0 \coloneqq \{z \in \mathrm{HC} \mid z_a=0\}$ is a measurable set of full measure w.r.t.\ $\mu^{(a)}$ and $\var{\sigma^{(a)}}$, (where we identify $\mathcal{G}_0$ with its canonical embedding into $[C_0]$,) but it is not closed as a subset of $(C_0, \| \cdot \|_{\infty})$. Identifying the considered measures with their restrictions to $\mathcal{B}(L)\cap [C_0]$ or $\mathcal{B}(C_0,\|\cdot\|_{\infty})$ (see Remark (rem:embeddings_and_measurability of the paper)), it holds that
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathrm{supp} \, \mu^{(a)} = \mathrm{supp} \var{\sigma^{(a)}} = \{z \in C_0 \mid z_a=0\},
    \end{equation*}
    where the support is defined w.r.t.\ the topology on $C_0$ induced by $\| \cdot \|_{\infty}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.385748+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1d746bd2d89af3dfacacbbb177670933b2f9c2bc1e036e78dbcb5cd3d43c9b5b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:global_clt_intro of arXiv:2507.10531, 'Quantitative central limit theorems for exponential random graphs'] Define
