{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:35:57.242091+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1dbab63f062c0fac8b15d03ffda5d14c292f6843bf4d89d31a3413a327307571","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem teoScaleFnUV of arXiv:2604.08889, 'Matrix Representations for Scale Functions of Spectrally Negative Lévy Processes with Rati'] Let $X$ be a L\'evy process as in (equation eqnXTrajectories of the paper), with $\sigma>0$ and $d\in \mathbb{R}$. 
Consider $\bm{G}: = \bm{C}^- + \bm{D}^{-+}\bm{\Psi}$ which, under the block structure given below in (equation eq:params_ubv of the paper)-(equation eq:params_ubv1 of the paper), takes the explicit form $\bm{G} = \begin{pmatrix} -a & \bm{b} \\ \bm{t} & \bm{T} \end{pmatrix}$. Define $\bm{\nu}:=(\Phi_q \bm{I}-\bm{T})^{-1}\bm{t}$ and $\bm{V}:=\binom{1}{\bm{\nu}}$. Let $\bm{e}_1^-:=(1,0,\dots,0)^\intercal\in\mathbb{R}^{p+1}$ be the first canonical basis vector.
Then, for any $x\geq 0$ and $q\geq 0$ such that $\psi'(\Phi_q)>0$ we have
\begin{equation}
W^{(q)}(x) = \frac{1}{\psi'(\Phi_q)}\Big(e^{\Phi_q x} - (\bm{e}_1^-)^\intercal\,e^{\bm{G}x}\,\bm{V}\Big), \qquad x \ge 0.
\end{equation}
The matrix $\bm{\Psi}$ can be 
recovered from the pair $(a,\bm{b})$ via
\begin{equation}
\bm{\Psi} = \frac{1}{\omega_{\lambda+q}}\begin{pmatrix}\omega_{\lambda+q} - a & \quad \bm{b}\end{pmatrix},
\end{equation}
where $\omega_{\lambda+q} := \big(\sqrt{d^2 + 2\sigma^2 (\lambda+q)} + d\big)\sigma^{-2}$, $\eta_{\lambda+q} := \big(\sqrt{d^2 + 2\sigma^2 (\lambda+q)} - d\big)\sigma^{-2}$, and $(a,\bm b)$ are a solution to the system of equations
\begin{equation}
\sigma^2a^2-2da-2(\lambda+q)+\sigma^2\bm b\bm t=0,
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
\sigma^2\bm{b}\left(\big(a-2d\sigma^{-2}\big)\bm I-\bm{T}\right) =2\lambda\bm{\alpha}.
\end{equation}
Finally, such a pair can be obtained as the limit of the recursive equations
\begin{equation}
\bm{b}_n = \Big( \frac{2\lambda}{\sigma^2}\,\bm{\alpha} + (\omega_{\lambda+q}-a_{n-1})\bm{b}_{n-1} \Big) \big(\eta_{\lambda+q}\bm{I} - \bm{T}\big)^{-1}, \qquad n \ge 1,
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
a_n = \omega_{\lambda+q} - \frac{\sigma^2}{2\sqrt{d^2+2\sigma^2(\lambda+q)}}\Big((\omega_{\lambda+q} - a_{n-1})^2 + \bm{b}_n\bm{t}\Big), \qquad n \ge 1,
\end{equation}
with $a_0=\omega_{\lambda+q}$, $\bm{b}_0=\bm{0}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

