 \bigg| \int_{\amsmathbb R} f(x)\dd(\mu^{\textnormal{I}}-\mu^{\textnormal{II}})(x)\bigg|\leq M \cdot |\!|f|\!|_{\frac{1}{2}} \cdot \sqrt{|\!|\boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\textnormal{I}}- \boldsymbol{\Theta}^{\textnormal{II}}|\!|_{\infty}}.
 \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:49:06.293292+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1de3eeb605ca6165ed24391250ed41b7acf6998a902c06e661703927b67ed34d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem teo:2 of arXiv:2601.00291, 'The probability of connection between two vertices cannot be monotone with the distance fo'] For every $d \geqslant 2$, there exists a critical value $\lambda_c(\mathbb{Z}^d) \in (0,\infty)$ such that
\begin{enumerate}
    \item[a)] If $\lambda > \lambda_c$, then $\mathbb{P}_{\lambda}\left(o\longleftrightarrow \vec{e}\, \right) > \mathbb{P}_{\lambda}\left(o\longleftrightarrow t\vec{e}\, \right)$ for all $t\in (0,1)$.
    \item[b)] If $0 < \lambda < \lambda_c$, then there exists
    $t = t(\lambda) \in (0,1)$ such that $\mathbb{P}_{\lambda}\left(o\longleftrightarrow \vec{e}\, \right) < \mathbb{P}_{\lambda}\left(o\longleftrightarrow t\vec{e}\, \right)$.
\end{enumerate}
Where $\vec e = (1,0,\ldots,0)\in\mathbb{Z}^d$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:41:28.174983+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1dfb312bc798180c9a913c1973fd963ad1ead3962462f9b5b33131bb590f37d9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary C_TP_sizes of arXiv:2510.26724, 'Sharp Fuss-Catalan thresholds in graph bootstrap percolation'] Let $W$ be a witness graph of order $\sigma$ and cost $\kappa$, 
