{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.903575+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1ed84d44c6977dd61b3acdedc1c1d36035fae2e914bbdd2644f6862f3fcb968f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 57 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] The measure $\mu$ has a density which is given, if $\sqrt{2 \theta \kappa}\leq \pi$, by
\begin{equation}
 \mu(x)= \left\{\begin{array}{lll}
