{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:30.963379+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1f01212deaf094b39b82d86edfe6d38e931b2b4a50bec66b516cc029fd7a9263","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 24 of arXiv:2608.12291, 'When should one stop the most exciting game?\\ {\tiny Sequential Inference for win-marting'] For every $\mathcal{I}=[t_1,t_2]\subset[0,\infty)$ and $\mathcal{J}=[\underline{a},\overline{a}]\subset(0,1)$ it holds that
