Note that this order of quantifiers corresponds to the limit \eqref{e:control.problems.limiting.regime}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.529869+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1f4d13c8e3afab5d5195d02a77dc532e006d81cff27f01908f1bc0035b39f26d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary eq:approximately-sparse-rate of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[corollary]{cor:sharp-approximately-sparse}
Under the hypotheses of (prop:sharp-profile-energy of the paper), let
\(1\le k_N\le N\), \(k_N=o(N)\), and for \(\rho>0\) put
\[
 \mathcal A_N(k_N,\rho)
 =\left\{x\in\mathbb S^{N-1}(1):
 \text{some \(S\subset[N]\), \(\left\lvertS\right\rvert\le k_N\), satisfies }
 \norm{x_{S^c}}_2\le\rho\right\}.
\]
Then, for every \(a>0\),
\begin{equation}
 \lim_{\rho\downarrow0}\limsup_{N\to\infty}\frac1N\log
 \mathbb P\left\{
 \sup_{x\in\mathcal A_N(k_N,\rho)}
 \left\lverth_N^J(x)\right\rvert\ge a\right\}
 \le-\frac{a^2}{2}.
\end{equation}
The same conclusion holds in the standard symmetric-coordinate model
whenever that field satisfies \(({\rm PT})_p\); the orbit-coordinate
joint MGF bound is sufficient.","status":"unverified"}

