{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:44:39.744018+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1f856c589e790e3edb9e6b5f4e0fc0e32eb6aae225ae32dcc0d5a08886b393ad","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2608.29872, 'Local Laws and Outlier Eigenvalues for Spiked Separable Covariance Matrices'] The densities $\rho_{c}$, $\rho_{1c}$, and $\rho_{2c}$ share the same support on $(0,\infty)$, which is a union of intervals. For $\al=1,2$,
