{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.756336+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_1f9a9aafad76f301e102b2d33ae593ca749be62dd71b0216108e17d5a4455d61","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:centered-capped-arrays-paper of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] For \(d\in\mathfrak D_{\xi,n}^{\mathrm{osc}}\), 
set \(m=m_{\xi,d}\).
Define the stopped centered capped prefix array by
\[
\widehat F^{\mathrm{pre,cap}}_{\xi,d,n}
=
\sum_{\ell=0}^{m-1}
\mathbf 1_{\{\tau_n>\ell\}}
\sum_{I\in\mathcal D_\ell^\circ}
\sum_{\substack{J\in\mathcal D_{\ell+1}^\circ\\J\subset I}}
X_{J,n}^{\mathrm{cap}}(\xi,d,\ell).
\]
For \(L>m\), define the stopped centered capped post-bin partial sum by
\[
\widehat F^{\mathrm{post,cap}}_{\xi,d,n,L}
=
\sum_{\ell=m}^{L-1}
\mathbf 1_{\{\tau_n>\ell\}}
\sum_{I\in\mathcal D_\ell^\circ}
\sum_{\substack{J\in\mathcal D_{\ell+1}^\circ\\J\subset I}}
X_{J,n}^{\mathrm{cap}}(\xi,d,\ell).
\]
The corresponding unstopped arrays \(F^{\mathrm{pre,cap}}_{\xi,d,n}\) and \(F^{\mathrm{post,cap}}_{\xi,d,n,L}\) are obtained by removing the factors \(\mathbf 1_{\{\tau_n>\ell\}}\).","status":"unverified"}

