{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.687519+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2007f5ecacf9cd5f5b8a77cdc49c0b16e8524588a269a51390054ac8e9c5b82c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor concentration_meso of arXiv:2510.18856, 'Evolution of recursive trees with limited memory'] Fix $\beta \in (0,1)$. For any $\epsilon,\delta>0$ and $T < T_\beta = 2(1-\beta)^{-1}$ there exist constants $C=C(\delta,T)>0$ and $\xi=\xi(\epsilon)>0$ such that
