{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.141555+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_21a7d507b4d5a9954cc7f89607feb41dabb1c5849b6161e217a69270e6ab2e41","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem lem:8 of arXiv:2510.13572, 'Coalescence in Markov chains'] \mbox{\hfil}
\begin{letlist}
\item
We have that $1\in K(P)$ if and only if $P\in\mathcal{P}_S$ is aperiodic. 
In this case, $k(\mu_{\text{\rm ind}})=1$.
\item
If $P\in\mathcal{P}_S$ has period $d$, then the coalescence classes of $\mu_{\text{\rm ind}}$
