{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:29:14.938300+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2245166929d567097b82ffd326cba4417a813592a36bab271a262f95b265b5f3","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop.HomoResolvent of arXiv:2606.13442, 'Scaling limit of additive functionals for reversible non-gradient exclusion process: criti'] There exists a constant $C(d,c_{-},c_{+},\mathbf{r},\rho)$ such that for any $\lambda>0$, the following estimate holds:
