{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.723108+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_22454504a8fdf162aa5485e582a1b478edec2802febd52d4898f537e43b4fa0b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition lem.COR1 of arXiv:2411.19145, 'On the intersection of critical percolation clusters and other tree-like random graphs'] Assume that $\mathcal G$ satisfies~(equation Halpha of the paper), for some $\alpha\in(d/2,d)$. 
There exist positive constants $C_0$ and $\kappa$, such that for any $r,R\ge 1$ and  $\rho>0$, satisfying 
\begin{equation}
\rho \cdot r^{2\alpha - d} \ge C_0\cdot \log R, 
\end{equation}
and any $L\ge 1$, one has 
$$\mathbb P(|\mathcal C_0^R(r,\rho)|>L)\le \exp\big(-\kappa \rho^{2(1-\frac{\alpha}{d})}\cdot L^{\frac{2\alpha}{d} -1}\big).
$$","status":"unverified"}

