{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:39:11.666440+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_22dcc9c9f7c2ebf3b3adef1a4da8b6ca00c88462212d5a3db616411198aafc32","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 (Khinchin's LIL) of arXiv:2608.04644, 'Khinchin's and Chung's Laws of the Iterated Logarithm at Time Zero for the Linear Stochast'] \textcolor{black}{Suppose  Condition~\ref{hypo} holds and that  $H<1$. Then, for every fixed} $x\in\RR^d$,
