{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:31:20.863777+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2314f622115bf7a17944fe6b411da62f1997ccd48d71edb445ff8a4f4b4c3988","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2506.10856, 'The space of multifurcating ranked tree shapes: enumeration, lattice structure, and Markov'] Let $t$ be a valid length $K\geq 2$ vector. Then given $K_0(t)$, the values $K_1(t)$ can take are: 
