{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.778143+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_23fcacc1b5273a3c35a9a779070b08ec9adff55a2d70f84e3a00bdfb03e5e125","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2 of arXiv:2603.25615, 'Fourier dimension of Mandelbrot cascades on planar curves'] Suppose that $1\leq q<p < q_{\max}$. If $1 < p/q \leq 2$, for any $1 \leq j \leq n $ and  $I \in \Q_j$, we have

    \begin{equation}
    \E(Y_{j,n }(q,I)^{p/q}) \leq \frac{b^{-2\tau(\frac{p}{2})+\frac{p\tau(q)}{q}}}{1-b^{-\tau(p)+\frac{p\tau(q)}{q}}}\,.    
    \end{equation}
    If $2^k < p/q \leq 2^{k+1}$ for some $k \geq 1$, for any $1 \leq j \leq n$ and $I \in \Q_j$, then 
    \begin{equation}
    \E(Y_{j,n}(q,I)^{p/q}) \leq \left({1-b^{-\tau(2q)+2\tau(q)}} \right)^{-2^{k+1}}.
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.083227+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2402662ab64c3aa961e9c83e412ac4d592ef66cbbcd35a44dc99dfdbde9af1b6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition BoundedExpectedN of arXiv:2411.12522, 'Canonical insurance models: stochastic equations and comparison theorems'] For  $i,j \in \mathcal{Z}$, $i \neq j$,  $ T \in  [0,\infty)$, and $n \in \mathbb{N}$, it holds that 
