{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.246292+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2410db0e7de7833007757bc5d44dedc96312d1e0e7532d91185030e39d7d96e6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition of arXiv:2604.23981, 'Accelerating sampling via asymptotic relaxation enhancing flows'] Suppose $v$ is relaxation enhancing in $\mathcal{Y}\subset L^2(\pi)$. Suppose that $q_0$ satisfies Assumption (ass:warmstart of the paper) with $q_0-1\in \mathcal{Y}$. Then, for any given $B>0$ and $t>0$, there is $A_0$, whenever $A>A_0$, one has
