{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.616123+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2436c5a8bbed19fa64f7f3d06e6f322122c7a8d70dc1d98d16c6d871017c6a8e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 14 (Swapping the local time for GFF) of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] Given two naturals $n>k\ge1$, a real $t>0$ and a function $f\in\Cloc^+$, define
\begin{equation}

U_{n,k}(f):=E^\varrho\biggl(\,\prod_{x\in\BbbL_n}\texte^{-f(\theta_n(x),\sqrt{L_t(x)}-m_n,\,\sqrt{L_t(x)}-\sqrt{L_t(x\cdot)}\,)\,1_{\MM_{n,k}(\sqrt{L_t},\,x)}}\biggr)
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}

V_{n,k}(f):=E^\varrho\otimes \wt E\biggl(\,\prod_{x\in\BbbL_n}\texte^{-f(\theta_{n-k}(z),\sqrt{L_t(z)}+h(x)-h(z)-m_n,\,h(x)-h(x\cdot)\,)\,1_{\MM_{n,k}(h,x)\cap \BB_{n,k}(x)}}\biggr),
\end{equation}
where we put $z:=\frakm^k(x)$ to reduce clutter and with the same convention set
 \begin{equation}

\BB_{n,k}(x):=\Bigl\{m_k+k^{1/3}\le m_n-\sqrt{L_t(z)}\le m_k+k^{2/3}\Bigr\}.
\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}

\lim_{k\to\infty}\limsup_{n\to\infty}\bigl|U_{n,k}(f)-V_{n,k}(f)\bigr|=0
\end{equation}
holds for all $t>0$ and all $f\in\Cloc^{+}$. Moreover, 
\begin{equation}

\lim_{\ell\to\infty}
\limsup_{k \to \infty} \limsup_{n \to \infty} 
P^\varrho\otimes\wt P\biggl(\,\sum_{x\in\BbbL_n}1_{\MM_{n,k}(h,x)\cap \BB_{n,k}(x)}1_{\{\sqrt{L_t(z)}+h(x)-h(z)>m_n-\lambda\}}>\ell\biggr)=0
\end{equation}
holds for all $t>0$ and all~$\lambda>0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.730506+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_24416213fed974fd6c6b462c3248227c2f5574ab86623907f67c2453b5ad340e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:mu-doublePrime of arXiv:2412.09290, 'Asymptotics of Harish-Chandra transform and infinitesimal freeness'] Let $\Psi, \Phi, \mathrm{T}$ be infinitely differentiable functions at $0$ and
  consider the sequences $(c_n)_{n \in \mathbb{N}}, (c'_n)_{n \in \mathbb{N}},
  (c''_n)_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$, where for every $n \in \mathbb{N}$
  \[ c_n := \frac{\Psi^{(n)} (0)}{(n - 1) !}, \text{\quad} c'_n :=
     \frac{\Phi^{(n)} (0)}{(n - 1) !} \text{\quad and\quad} c''_n := 2
     \frac{\mathrm{T}^{(n)} (0)}{(n - 1) !} . \]
  Then for the sequence $(\ensuremath{\boldsymbol{\mu}}''_k)_{k \in \mathbb{N}}$ defined by
  ((Ss of the paper)), for every $k \in \mathbb{N}$,  we have
  \[ \ensuremath{\boldsymbol{\mu}}''_k = \frac{1}{2} \left( \sum_{\pi \in \ensuremath{\operatorname{NC}} (k)}
     \sum_{V \in \pi} c''_{|V|} \prod_{\underset{W \neq V}{W \in \pi}} c_{|W|}
     + \sum_{\pi \in \ensuremath{\operatorname{NC}} (k)} \sum_{\underset{W \neq V}{V, W \in \pi}}
     c'_{|V|} c'_{|W|} \prod_{\underset{U \neq V, W}{U \in \pi}} c_{|U|}
     \right) . \]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:40.975667+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2445e5e79680da42bb4d548a5f527ad8d3fc7e64e38bc5ab01860816ac4ec9ac","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem prop_4 of arXiv:2412.03774, '{ Refining Concentration for \\Gaussian Quadratic Chaos with\\ Applications in Sonar and C'] Let $m\geq1$ be an integer, $0<b<1$, $\|A\|_{m+1}$ be Schatten norm of order $m+1$ for a symmetric matrix $A$ and $r(A)$ be the rank of $A$. Then  
 \begin{eqnarray}

\Pr(\boldsymbol{\Delta}>t)\leq e^{\Lambda_m(t, b)},
\end{eqnarray} 
 where\footnote{The function $\Lambda(t,a)$ in ((en_exp of the paper)) and the functions $\Lambda_m(t,b)$ in ((Lambda_m of the paper)) are not related. }
 \begin{eqnarray}

\Lambda_m(t, b)=\frac{r(A)}{2}\sum_{k=2}^m \frac{b^k}{k}-\kappa_m(b)\min\bigg\{\frac{t^{1+\frac{1}{m}}}{\|A\|_{m+1}^{1+\frac{1}{m}}}, \frac{t}{\|A\|} \bigg\} 
\end{eqnarray}
and 
\begin{eqnarray}

\kappa_m(b)=\frac{m}{2(m+1)}\min\bigg\{\frac{1}{\big((m+1)\theta_m(b)\big)^{\frac{1}{m}}}, b\bigg\}
\end{eqnarray}
with $\theta_m(b)$ as defined in ((theta_func of the paper)).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.571994+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_244b54fd90f467d5ba3a34cf873d9ee60bb9a3f4c2cf36fc655a0509b5870eae","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 11 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d>4$. There exist $c,C>0$ such that, for every $n\geq 1$,
