{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.474884+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_24553b00ba47f1f52a1728e66f4d5249a2a1209d9e235a58a3de737eff9f494a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:joint-K-subg of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[lemma]{lem:remainder-tight}
Suppose, without requiring independence, that the coefficient vector
satisfies the joint linear-form estimate
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb E\exp\left\{\sum_{I\in[N]^p}t_IJ_I\right\}
 \le\exp\left\{\frac{K^2}{2}\sum_{I\in[N]^p}t_I^2\right\},
 \qquad t\in\mathbb R^{N^p}.
\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb E\sup_{x\in\mathbb S^{N-1}(1)}\left\lvertR_N(x)\right\rvert\le C_{p,K}
\end{equation}
uniformly in \(N\).  Consequently, there is \(M=M(p,K)\) such that
\begin{equation}
 \inf_N\mathbb P\left(\left\lVertR_N\right\rVert_\infty\le M\right)\ge\frac12.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

