{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:42:08.471455+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_24cc51bda6e1c1795c22405af8488392bb182b28c74b32069db755f060bb933c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq83 of arXiv:2511.19391, 'Central limit theorem for supercritical Crump-Mode-Jagers processes counted with non-indiv'] Define the sub-$\sigma$-algebras $(\mathcal{A}^{(n)})_{n \geq 0}$ of $\mathcal{F}$ by letting, for each $n \in \mathbb{N}_{0}$,
