{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:39:41.406047+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2500aab84ad920a0328d476bb9778a11f4b6c9f50a0cf31dc62bd31a445792bc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 12 of arXiv:2604.06516, 'From stochastic individual-based models to free-boundary Hamilton-Jacobi equations'] For any $t>0$ and for any closed $A\subset\mathbb{D}[0,t]$, 
