{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.581634+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_268bc6d5af1508e327f18d74b6f3e98291645982f60f9cfa6526a8c15a428b13","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Maximum principle-Lemma of arXiv:2605.16963, 'Stochastic Euler Equations with Pseudo-differential Noise: Continuous and Discontinuous Pe'] Assume  $\upvartheta:\mathbb R\to\mathbb R$ satisfies, for some $C>0$, $|\upvartheta(x)|\leq C |x|$ for $x\in\mathbb R.$
