{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.095808+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_26afc21f83212bae6ffbdf0b1916d1e0bdb3afff51300533adbb3cfc356950ec","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lemma:convergenceL of arXiv:2411.12717, 'Excursion theory for Markov processes indexed by Lévy trees'] Fix $r\geq 0$. Under $\mathbf{N}_{x,r}$ and for every $\varepsilon>0$, let  $ {\textbf{\emph{m}}} ( \widetilde{H}  , \varepsilon )$ be the number of connected components of $\mathcal{T}_{\widetilde{H}}\setminus\{ 0 \}$ having  at least a point  at distance  $\varepsilon$ from the root $p_{\widetilde{H}}(0)$.  Then the following convergence holds 
