{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:07:56.711765+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_27a302f5e74234099d4faaaf9c98cb523c77ae4802384b3af762497edbf2070e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition p:for_back_SDE of arXiv:2411.04773, 'Meeting of squared Bessel flow lines and application to the skew Brownian motion'] With probability 1, for all quadruples $\left(s, r, t, x\right) \in {\mathbb Q}^4$ with $t>s\ge 0$:

