{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:56:14.270986+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_27bf0c8b97912ec9753a81c97999154031f26f28046f558d160728f44dd71c08","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop pc of arXiv:2412.09535, 'Local limit theorem for joint subgraph counts'] Suppose $p = a/b$ where $a$ and $b$ are relatively prime positive integers. Then a positive integer $n \geq 3$ is $p$-PC if and only if
\begin{cond}
\item  If $2 \mid b$, $\nu_2(n) \geq 3\nu_2(b)$ or $\nu_2(n-1) \geq 3\nu_2(b) + 1$;
\item  If $3 \mid b$, $\max\set{\nu_3(n),\nu_3(n-1)} \geq 3\nu_3(b) + 1$;
\item  For every prime $q > 3$, $\max\set{\nu_q(n),\nu_q(n-1)} \geq 3\nu_q(b)$.
\end{cond} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.586390+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_27d093762187f8a681f6bc84d7a2cc8e43a115db0a46e1a505d60feeffc79ece","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm EVI_1_dim of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] Let $\mathsf{P},\mathsf{P}^* \in \mathcal P_{s,1}(\Gamma)$.  For $\mathsf{P}_t:= \mathsf{gap}^{-1}(\mathsf S^{gap}_t \mathsf{gap}(\mathsf{P}))$ the integral form EVI holds 
