{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:42:08.465685+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2800e192ace7c08a8e3920436a9e9becfff817af81404778b1a2f6d39e3289b4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem eq:LT1-Palm of arXiv:2511.15893, 'On a Class of Dynamical Poisson-Voronoi Tessellations'] Consider the motion model with speed $v=1$. Under the Palm probability measure $\mathbb{P}^0_{\mathcal V }$, the Laplace transform of the inter-handover time $T$ is given by,
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{E}^0_{\mathcal V }\left[e^{-\rho T}\right] = 2\pi \lambda^{\frac 5 2}
\int_{(\mathbb{R}^+)^5} e^{-\rho (\hat s_1-\hat s)}
 e^{-2\lambda \vert U^{\hat s_1}_{\hat h_1}\cup U^{\hat s}_{\hat h}\vert}
 {\rm d}t_3\, {\rm d} h_3\, {\rm d} t_2\, {\rm d} h_2\, {\rm d} h_1, 

