         Then, $\pi \in \mathcal{T}_{bc}\deln{\mathbb{W}^d, \mathbb{W}^d}$.
        \item If $\pi$ is induced by a bicausal Monge map $T$, then $\rho$ is $\mathcal{O}^d$-valued and there exists a strong solution to (equation eqn:extendedbrowniansde of the paper). 
    \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:02:08.152327+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_28bf75cf218c50efcc8a1850735a17a120926af187f5022233c9af398e026512","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 57 of arXiv:2608.27630, 'Oriented planar maps and \\ annular mating of trees'] For every $\delta>0$,
