{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:06.329067+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_28c533613ce413124bca4f3dc0c1b4a96cb770917000c9905ce63dd9d2743d5d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 8 of arXiv:2607.06428, 'Impact of spinning on the early-warning signs in non-Markovian stochastic systems'] A fractional Brownian motion (fBm) $\left(\mathbf{W}^{H}_t\right)_{t\geq 0}\subset \R^n$ with Hurst index $H\in(0,1)$ is a centered Gaussian process with covariance 
\begin{equation}

\left(\E \left[\mathbf{W}^H_t \left(\mathbf{W}^H_s\right)^\textnormal{T}\right]\right)_{j_1,j_2\in\{1,\dots,n\}}=\frac{1}{2} (t^{2H} +s^{2H} -|t-s|^{2H}) \delta_{j_1,j_2},
 \end{equation}
for $\delta$ that indicates the Kronecker delta. Specifically, the fBm in $\R^n$ is composed by i.i.d. scalar fBms with Hurst index $H$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.288066+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_28c793f4813a0626bd5a9f7ea4d6e14fb6f15dae49f46814478dc1066d6005cb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem th:max_fluct of arXiv:2604.21142, 'Gaussian fluctuations for Internal DLA on cylinders'] Let $(A(t))_{t\geq 0}$ denote an IDLA process on the cylinder ${\ensuremath{\mathbb G}} _N$ starting from $A(0) = R_0$. For every $\n > 0$ and every $m \geq 1$ there exists a constant $C = C(\n, m) < \infty$ such that, with
	\[ T^\sharp \coloneqq N \sqrt{\t_{mix}} \,(\log N)^2\,, \qquad \Delta_N \coloneqq C \max\!\left\{\, \log N,\; \sqrt{\frac{T \wedge T^\sharp}{N}\,\Big( \log N + \log_+\!\big( T/N \big) \Big)} \,\right\}\,, \]
we have
	\begin{equation}
	{\ensuremath{\mathbb P}}  \Big( R_{\lfloor T/N - \Delta_N \rfloor}
	\subseteq A(T) \subseteq R_{T/N +  \Delta_N } \Big) \geq 1-N^{-\n}
	\end{equation}
uniformly over integer $T$ with $1 \leq T \leq N^m$, for every $N$ large enough. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.377058+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_28c985894ffb88d4ed7079b257d31732b1502e5091fe2c2befd88c2f76f6cbea","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:secondorder of arXiv:2412.01995, 'Exciting games and Monge-Amp\`{e}re equations'] Suppose $C>10$ and denote $\iota=\frac{1}{4e^{C+10}}$. Then we have 
