{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.238549+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_28eec02842d3f7dce88c778776e4229b050f42c0274ee798c567b690766bf749","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 43 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] Fix initial data $\hfix_0 \in \UC$ and $\hfixp_0 \in \UCp$ such that
\begin{equation}
\hfix_0(x) = \hfixp_0(x)
\end{equation} for all $x\in \R$, where with a slight abuse of notation, we extend $\hfixp$ periodically from $\mathbb{T}$ to $\R$. 
Fix some $a\in \R$. 

Then there exist constants $c,C>0$, and a coupling $\mathbf{P}$ between the periodic KPZ fixed point $\hfixp$ and the KPZ fixed point $\hfix$, started from $\hfixp_0$ and $\hfix_0$, respectively, such that 
\begin{equation}
    \mathcal{A}_{\varepsilon} := \left\{ \hfixp\big(\hfixp_0;y,\varepsilon\big) = \hfix(\hfix_0;y,\varepsilon) \ \forall y \in \Big[a-\frac{1}{4},a+\frac{1}{4}\Big] \cap  \textup{ext}_{\varepsilon}(\hfix_0)\right\}
\end{equation}
satisfies for all $\varepsilon>0$
\begin{equation}
\mathbf{P}\left( \mathcal{A}_{\varepsilon} \right) \geq 1- C\exp(-c\varepsilon^{-1/2}) .
\end{equation} Moreover, we get that for all $y\in \mathbb{T}\setminus\textup{supp}(\hfix_0)$ 
\begin{equation}
   \lim_{\varepsilon \rightarrow 0} \hfix\big(\hfix_0;y,\varepsilon\big) =  \lim_{\varepsilon \rightarrow 0} \hfixp\big(\hfixp_0;y,\varepsilon\big) = -\infty ,
\end{equation} in the sense of almost sure convergence in supremum-norm of the function in $y$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:36:23.124233+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_28f59ddc38174a3d625d12029cb198c0bcdad6ff359f0075e4deaefef25ff3ae","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lemmadistance of arXiv:2506.18207, 'Cartan's Path Development, the Logarithmic Signature and a Conjecture of Lyons-Sidorova'] If $\theta\in C^1([0,T])$, then for any $\epsilon\in(0,\frac{\pi}{2})$, there exists a $\lambda_0>0$ such that $\forall\lambda>\lambda_0$, it holds that
$$
\sup_{s\in[0,t]}|\alpha_s-\beta_s|\leq c_{\theta,t}\frac{1-e^{-2\lambda\sin(\epsilon t)}}{2\lambda\sin{\epsilon}},\quad t\in[0,T],
$$
where $c_{\theta,t}:=\sup_{s\in[0,t]}|\dot{\theta}_s|$ and $\alpha_s$, $\beta_s$ are obtained by the following equations
\begin{equation}\left\{
\begin{array}{lllll}
\dot{\alpha}_s=-2\lambda\sin(\alpha_s)-\dot{\theta}_s\\
\dot{\beta}_s=-2\lambda\sin(\beta_s)\\
\alpha_0=\beta_0\in[-\frac{\pi}{2}+\epsilon,\frac{\pi}{2}-\epsilon].
\end{array}
\right.\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:52:47.244979+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_29070aa7cd7ad505a162772a263514902082cbcd022bdd26243ce0b7777f2287","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 (the map is a contraction) of arXiv:2609.01093, 'Ideal MHD below the classical well-posedness threshold'] With $T_*$ chosen by \eqref{eq:Tstar}, the map $\mathcal M$ satisfies
