{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.831552+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2b874720ecc5f9c3c951d17300f2107ac286dbb2be56ef7ee1fa9ce260d1628b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:extFLE of arXiv:2608.05089, 'Correlation decay in area-tilted line ensembles'] For $\mathbf{x}, \mathbf{y} \in \mathbb{A}_+^n$ and functions
$\mathbf{f}, \mathbf{g}: (\ell,r) \to \mathbb{A}_+^n$ with $\mathbf{f} \prec \mathbf{g}$ and $\bm{\lambda} : (\ell,r) \to \mathbb{R}^n$,
let  $\mathcal{L}^{\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y},\bm{\lambda}}_{n,\ell,r,\mathbf{f},\mathbf{g}}$ denote the probability measure
with the following Radon--Nikodym derivative relative to the
Brownian bridge measure $\mathcal{B}^{\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}}_{n,\ell,r}$:
\begin{equation}
    \frac{d\mathcal{L}^{\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y},\bm{\lambda}}_{n,\ell,r,\mathbf{f},\mathbf{g}}}{d\mathcal{B}^{\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}}_{n,\ell,r}}(\mathbf{X}_n)
    \propto \Exp{-2 \sum_{i=1}^n \int_\ell^r \lambda^i(t) X^i_n(t) \,dt}
    \ind{\mathbf{X}_n(t) \in \mathbb{A}_+^n \text{ for all } t \in [\ell,r]}
    \mathbf{1}_{\{\mathbf{f} \prec \mathbf{X}_n \prec \mathbf{g}\}}.
\end{equation}
Note that to recover the geometrically increasing area tilts, we should
take $\bm{\lambda}(t) \equiv (1,\lambda,\lambda^2,\dotsb,\lambda^{n-1})$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-09-07T12:18:08.279088+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2b8ca9da5796df078534339d8c0121dac0032ee4773170358c77cbbb674505de","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2505.20799, 'A note on the improved sparse Hanson-Wright inequalities'] Let $\xi$ be a random variable such that for $r\ge r_{0}$
