{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:42:55.322481+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2d3399131690a0b9ab320d2bffdced2b85f3b0c0c7cdf473e4ef99d8b0ce7fad","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 42 (Domination, strictness and attainment) of arXiv:2609.02398, '\textbf{Convex Order Comparisons for Sub-Gamma Random Variables}'] Let $\sigma, \alpha > 0$. Every $X \in \SG(\sigma^2,\alpha)$ satisfies
