{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:35:04.166593+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2d711caac7dc309386d16b2585bbbaf54c4f0c74ba89a2df3103cbfd4d537f60","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thLIL2 of arXiv:2608.30848, '\huge \bf Limit Laws of the Iterated Logarithm Under Sub-linear Expectations'] Assume ((eqLILmomentcondition1 of the paper)), ((eqLILmeanzerocondition of the paper)), ((eqLILmomentcondition2 of the paper)), ((eqLILmomentcondition3 of the paper)), and condition (CC) holds for the family of probability measures $\mathscr{P}$. Then
 \begin{description}
