such that the following boundedness estimates hold for all $\nu \in (0,1)$:

\begin{align*}
&\int_0^T \|(S_{\text{{\tiny $1,\!\delta,\!\nu$}}}(\tilde{z},\tilde{g}))'(t)\|_{L^2(\Omega)}^2dt
+\sup_{0 \le t \le T} \Phi_\nu ((S_{\text{{\tiny $1,\!\delta,\!\nu$}}}(\tilde{z},\tilde{g}))(t))\\
&\hspace*{3cm}+\nu^2 \int_0^T \|(S_{\text{{\tiny $1,\!\delta,\!\nu$}}}(\tilde{z},\tilde{g}))(t)\|_{H^2(\Omega)}^2 dt \le C_5.
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.589788+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2ecfd397fec6bd8da7651bb4b2bc1bb2180778606f70e75f10965c12c383f162","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:Fourier-isometry of arXiv:2606.02003, 'Higher-Order Multifractional Stable Motion:\\ Definition and Fundamental Properties'] Let $M_\alpha$ be a real S$\alpha$S random measure on $\mathbb{R}$
with Lebesgue control measure, and $\widetilde{M}_\alpha$ a complex
isotropic S$\alpha$S random measure on $\mathbb{R}$ with Lebesgue
control measure. For $f \in L^\alpha(\mathbb{R})$ with Fourier transform
$\widehat{f} \in L^\alpha(\mathbb{R},\mathbb{C})$:
\begin{equation}

\int_\mathbb{R} f(u)\,dM_\alpha(u)
\;\overset{d}{=}\;
\mathrm{Re}\int_\mathbb{R}
C_\alpha\,
\widehat{f}(\xi)\,
e^{-i\pi(1-1/\alpha)\,\mathrm{sign}(\xi)/2}
\,d\widetilde{M}_\alpha(\xi),
\end{equation}
where the constant $C_\alpha$ is chosen so that
$\|C_\alpha \widehat{f}\|_{L^\alpha} = \|f\|_{L^\alpha}$.
Its explicit value is
\begin{equation}

C_\alpha
:= \left[\frac{(2\pi)^{1-\alpha}}{c_\alpha}\right]^{1/\alpha}
= \left[\frac{(2\pi)^{1-\alpha}\,\sqrt{\pi}\,
\Gamma\!\left(\frac{\alpha}{2}+1\right)}
{\Gamma\!\left(\frac{\alpha+1}{2}\right)}\right]^{1/\alpha},
\end{equation}
consistent with the normalization of $\widetilde{M}_\alpha$ in Definition~(def:complex-SaS of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.232395+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2ed1c0856ec2860fe29402c526106cf1175eb0585eb4a62e95cae4ca24353827","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 37 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] Recall the definition of the periodic LPP landscape $\LLpeps$ with respect to the periodic last passage percolation $(T_{u,v}^{\per})_{u,v\in \Z^2}$ from \eqref{def:periodicLPPSheet}. Let $\tilde{\omega}=2^{\frac{3}{2}}(1+\sqrt{\rho})^{-\frac{1}{2}}\rho^{\frac{1}{4}}$. Then 
