{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:09:23.967462+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_2f54bc441d76766e4867066c25d9d3d2f60b69c2cc1d2a4e855987bed9a31203","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2607.22416, 'A multi-player optimal stopping game based on a spider Brownian bridge'] Suppose $\sG_i$ and $\sL_i$ are as above for $i=1,2$.
