{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:32:18.854807+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3013089afebb8b21030f9b3fb81f8c6bfdad2bb8ab38fbfd583b528bde326efa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 1 of arXiv:2609.03875, 'Measure theory without infinities'] Let $\mathcal Q$ be a $\delta$-ring. Then the following statements hold:
