{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.651901+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_30efd266e610125c9a5d08c230c30c9863cd31d156ad2d584225c34a4007cbfc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem_maximum_hitting_time_of_0 of arXiv:2411.13964, 'Long-time analysis of a pair of on-lattice and continuous run-and-tumble particles with ja'] Let $\tau = \inf \left\{ t \ge 0 : X_D(t) = (0, *^0_{(1, -1)} ) \right\}$. There exists $C > 0$ such that
