{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.587495+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_310dccc45ad15af6b9fb10a2f70c0c8e77c978f1365573c946f086bf882fe2f7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem finite_energy_approx of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] For $\mathsf{P}\in  \mathcal P_{s,1}(\Gamma)$ with  $\mathcal F_{\beta}({P})<\infty$  there exists a sequence $\mathsf{P}^n\in \mathcal P_{s,1}(\Gamma)$ with $\mathcal{W}^{int}(\mathsf{P}^n)\leq \mathcal{W}^{int}(\mathsf{P})+1/n$, $\mathcal E(\mathsf{P}^n)\leq \mathcal E(\mathsf{P})+1/n$ and 
    \begin{align}
        \int \sum_{x\in \xi\cap \Lambda_1}\left\lvertx^+-x\right\rvert^p\mathsf{P}^n(d\xi)<\infty.
    \end{align}
    Furthermore, $\mathsf{P}^n\xrightarrow{n\to \infty}\mathsf{P}$  w.r.t. $\mathcal T_{\mathcal L}$ (in particular weakly) and for $n\in \IN$ there exists $q_n>0$  such that the measure $\mathsf{P}^n$ is concentrated on the set \begin{align}
        \Gamma_{q_n}=\{\xi\in \Gamma: \varphi(x-y)\leq q_n,1/q_n\leq \left\lvertx-y\right\rvert \text{ for any two distinct }x,y\in \xi \}.
    \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:10.192735+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_310e8ca19634cf90b7391277ea05abfbcf0daaf20b6a75aa650d4d9629f58550","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 of arXiv:2605.03851, 'The Relay Random Tree:\\A stochastic geometry approach of multihop relay in an urban visib'] \textbf{Blockage.}

    For $\landsc$ a landscape and $(x, y)\in \Half$ a point, we call (first) blocking building of $(x, y)$ in $\landsc$ the following quantity when it is well defined:
    \[\tau(x, y, \landsc) = (x_b, y_b) := \underset{\substack{(a, b) \in \landsc \\a>x}}{\text{argmax}} \frac{b-y}{a-x}.\]
    When the blocking building of $(x, y)$ is well defined, we further introduce its blockage angle as:
    \[\theta(x, y, \landsc): = \arctan\left(\frac{y_b - y}{x_b-x}\right).\]
    In the following, when the involved landscape is unequivocal, we will simply write $\tau(x, y)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:09:15.345488+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_310e9c812e3a2ed30299b8dd1ce6dda790f6b3ff95f5f84b8dd905179fe3974e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem of arXiv:2411.05534, 'Inverse problems for stochastic partial differential equations'] Let $ f, g \in L^{2}_{\mathbb{F}}(0, T; H) $ and $ a, b \in L^{2}_{\mathcal{F}_{s}} (\Omega) $, $ 0 \leq s  < t \leq T $. Then 
    \begin{enumerate}[(i)]
        \item $ \displaystyle \int_s^t f d W \in L_{\mathbb{F}}^2(\Omega ; C([s, t] ; H)) $;
        \item $ \displaystyle \int_s^t(a f+b g) d W=a \int_s^t f d W+b \int_s^t g d W, \text { a.s. } $;
        \item $ \displaystyle \mathbb{E}\Big(\int_s^t f d W\Big)=0 $;
        \item $ \displaystyle \mathbb{E}\Big(\Big\langle\int_s^t f d W, \int_s^t g d W\Big\rangle_H\Big)=\mathbb{E}\Big(\int_s^t\langle f(\tau, \cdot), g(\tau, \cdot)\rangle_H d \tau\Big) $.
    \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:28:53.687536+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3117e7528c4c2d883d7c706dd029b41ac69cdea651e7e3cbc16bdb7bb771dbd6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 25 (minorisation on interior) of arXiv:2605.13648, 'Sticky CIR process with potential: invariant measure and exact sampling'] \label[lemma]{lem:scheme-density}
  Let $I,[a,b]\subset(0,\infty)$ be compact and let $T_\star>0$; assume \eqref{eq:nonconvex-hyp}. There
  are thresholds $\theta,T_0>0$, depending only on $\delta,\lambda,\beta$ and the position of
  $I\cup[a,b]$, such that if
  \begin{equation}
    \operatorname{diam}(I\cup[a,b])\ \le\ \theta
    \qquad\text{and}\qquad
