{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:13:18.508046+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_32b8e7a930fd9058bb6b6b8a65ac852653549d0375bae367168e6f753b9b48a0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 17 of arXiv:2608.30589, 'Vector-Valued Wavelet Bases as Hilbert $\mathbb{M}_m(\mathbb{R})$-Module Bases: A Construc'] Consider the following classes of wavelet bases:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item A wavelet basis of \(L^2(\mathbb{R})\) associated with an MRA.
    \item A vector-valued wavelet basis of \(L^2(\mathbb{R}, \mathbb{R}^m)\) (\(m \ge 2\)) associated with a VMRA.
    \item An \(m\)-multiwavelet basis of \(L^2(\mathbb{R})\) associated with an MRA.
