{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.852996+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_33fffdd02146bb06bf4b9eb6b9b1ca3d6184d00935f011b050dce0f01ad5783a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:CMF of arXiv:2606.11951, 'On Skorokhod Problems for Reflected and Singular Stochastic Heat Equations'] (Version of the Cameron--Martin Formula) Let $h \in H_0^1~\cap~H^2$. Then, the measure $T_{+h}(\mu^{\beta})$ is absolutely continuous w.r.t.\ $\mu^{\beta}$, and its Radon--Nikodym density is given by
