{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:32:23.561945+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_34c21c03497985b7c62be0836f096a0d9679b539eae114c724028ed4257cc5ee","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 3.3* of arXiv:2603.13873, '{Solvability of BSDEs with possibly unbounded stochastic coefficients \\ on a general weig'] Let $P(\tau<+\infty)=1$ and let $\rho,\mu\in{\mathbb R}$ and $\nu\in{\mathbb R}_+$ be three given constants satisfying
