{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:33:06.543247+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_34dd08af8fbf7a6e25f3d2d3e81f25dc564e71686148cc03e06d938e298b14ef","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 20 (Necks) of arXiv:2608.25971, 'Positive \texorpdfstring{$\tau$}{tau}-bi-Ricci curvature and Mean curvature flow with surg'] A point $p\in M$ is the center of an $(\eps,k,L)$-neck of radius $r$ if
