{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:45.028703+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_355385f4e0f8b982cac7f11adcebd67474fce23d5c24b43d00309665b8cd4bb6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2606.07096, 'Non-Selection of Lagrangian Trajectories in the Zero-Noise Limit for a Class of Stochastic'] Let $W$ satisfy Assumption~\ref{ass:noise} and $\alpha_W$ be given by~\eqref{eq:noise_regularity_threshold}.
