{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.976112+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3559201d6d1e18d7b70c6953f2bdad4a3da4807edbd14c28db716759273a7a61","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:expdecay of arXiv:2411.07157, 'Rough differential equations in the flow approach'] Fix $t_0\in[0,1]$, $N\in\N$, and consider $\lambda\in C^\infty(\R)$ with $\mathrm{supp} \,\lambda\subset[t_0-c\mu,t_0]$ for some universal constant $c>0$. Then, the following holds uniformly in $t_0\in[0,1]$ and $\mu\in[0,1]$:
