{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.749926+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_363a6e7d6e71e932274bfc2bec8fd2159abb2a4efa572e9b975509591e6ec2bc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:ladder-estimate-paper of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] Fix \(q\in(1,2)\) with \(\rho(q)<1\), let
\(0<\beta<\beta_X(q)\), and fix \(\alpha_{\mathrm{gr}}>1\).  Then there exist
constants
\[
    C_{\mathrm{lad}}<\infty,\qquad
    \tau_{\mathrm{lad}}<\infty,\qquad
