{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:12:20.543233+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_36a1ce552156b3869ba3f66eaddc73397ab2d3d1774f5bcb09ad898fe56ff375","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma expansions of arXiv:2603.27906, 'Marked GUE-corners process in doubly periodic dimer models'] Let~$z_k=1+\frac{Z_k}{N^\frac{1}{2}}$,~$k=1,2$, with $|Z_k|< N^{\frac{1}{2}}$ (on the canonical local chart in this text, at a neighbourhood of $q_{\infty}$). Then, as~$N\to \infty$, we have that
