\end{equation}
that is, $\mathcal{F}$ is $1$-convex along free Wasserstein geodesics.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.115614+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_370dd367a9139cd09df09e7fcac73ca4d0458d2dbc97757ebc8f0571a9433781","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm THM61-2 of arXiv:2608.16170, '\bf On hitting time distributions of Markov processes with sub-Gaussian heat kernel bounds'] Assume that  the volume growth condition (equation eq:41 of the paper) holds  with some constant $\alpha>0$, and the transition density function of $X$ satisfies 
