{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:32:11.126616+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_383f7857b580be989c34153ad67d280985b2aea9218a3f60a46c517a93a06d9b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:int-2 of arXiv:2510.06891, 'Multivariate CLT for L\'evy processes: convergence rates without moment assumptions'] Let $\bm{X}$ and $\bm{Z}$ be as in Theorem~(thm:int-0 of the paper) and assume $\mathds{E}[|\bm{X}_1|^2]<\infty$. Suppose $\mathscr{A}\subset\mathscr{C}$ and that
