{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:42.313769+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3930c3028194d7a65677ae978b36a8c36bcc9e2c55c443b4cf28b26c806b567a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 39 of arXiv:2608.05931, 'Effective Lagrangian regularity and the uniqueness threshold for random H\"older velocity '] Let $\alpha \in (0,1)$ with $\alpha + \beta>1$ and $\alpha + \beta/2 <1$. Suppose for all $p \geq 1,$ there exists $K(p)>0$ such that for all $j \in \N$ and $n \in \{0,1,2\}$,
