{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:32:23.641948+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3b58b5bb10a5cf7ff7fd2add5e3ecda84bdc5f4cfaf1a339c6c57035cfcd916e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop LLN of arXiv:2603.16824, 'Age-dependent random connection models with arc reciprocity: clustering and connectivity'] Let \((F_t:t>0)\) be a a family of non-negative functionals, where \(F_t\) acts translationally invariant on rooted vertex-edge markings on \(\mathbb{T}^d_t\times(0,1)\) and let \(F_\infty\) be a translation invariant functional for a rooted vertex-edge marking on \(\mathbb{R}^d\times(0,1)\). Let us assume that
