{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:26:20.567530+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3be5974e46454a24d65c9c931ba887c0245741577dcf0d9dd1c2733db16a3af3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop ximoments of arXiv:2411.12003, 'Central Limit Theorem for non-stationary random products of $\SL(2, \R)$ matrices'] Assume that the family $\widetilde{\xi}_{a;n}$ satisfies the assumptions ((a:center of the paper))--((a:difference of the paper)) above. Then, there exists a constant $C_{2}$ such that for all $a$ and $n$,
