{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.331645+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d94c0eb031b665611515efe07870953ab1d51c0d761f819db8ad6016faf42f2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma thm:equivs for Schervish of arXiv:2412.06420, 'Accuracy, Estimates, and Representation Results'] The following are equivalent:
		\begin{enumerate}
		\item Schervish form: for $v\in\set{0,1}$ and any $x\in[0,1]$, 
		\begin{align}
		&			\mathsf{acc}_v(v)-\mathsf{acc}_v(x)=\int_{x}^{v}{v-t}\;\;\lambda(\dd{t}).&&\text{(eq:Scherv of the paper)}\nonumber
		\end{align}
		\item For all $x,y\in[0,1]$, (i.e., replacing $v\in\set{0,1}$ by a general $y\in[0,1]$)
				\begin{align}
						&			\mathsf{acc}_v(y)-\mathsf{acc}_v(x)=\int_{x}^{y}{v-t}\;\;\lambda(\dd{t}).
				\end{align}
		\item For all $x,p\in[0,1]$,
				\begin{align}
				&\mathrm{Exp}_p\mathsf{acc}(p)-\mathrm{Exp}_p\mathsf{acc}(x)=\int_x^p (p-t)\;\lambda(\dd{t})
				\end{align}
		\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:36:31.233752+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d96cc7b30582b38a35bc85a1fb826991f4f437efafae7e0b716c10c9f015e09","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 9 of arXiv:2609.00567, 'Hodge--Tate splitting and Akizuki--Nakano vanishing in positive characteristic'] Let \(\mcalG\) be a flat affine group scheme over an fpqc algebraic stack \(\mcalX\). A morphism \(f\colon\mcalY\to\mcalX\) of stacks is called a \emph{\(B\mcalG\)-torsor} if there exists a representable fpqc cover \(U\to\mcalX\) by a scheme and an equivalence
  \begin{equation*}
    \mcalY\times_{\mcalX}U\simeq B_U\mcalG_U
  \end{equation*}
  of stacks over \(U\), where \(\mcalG_U\defeq\mcalG\times_{\mcalX}U\). We use the expression \(B\mcalG\)-torsor only in this sense.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:08.954003+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3d9f9a77d74085e9ab2cd1fe34458a9939071e550165c0264b41f84b3994fdaf","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:Lambda of arXiv:2609.01581, 'Concentration of additive functionals of Stratonovich-type'] For $A \in \{\rho, J\}$ and $k \in \mathbb{R}$ define
