where the supremum is over the real Hilbert space $L^2(\mu)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:57:28.726474+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3dc23fa18b93b834a40104051a508ed7c4002954c8b7848251e01a5e9895fd7c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 31 of arXiv:2609.01190, 'Rough differential equations on manifolds via natural bundles'] There exist constants $\delta\in (0,1)$ and $L\in (0,\infty)$ such that for every interval $[U,V]\subseteq [S,T]$, we have 
