{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:22:59.732918+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e01419b0cd62bfef823b24ce09a1d1ef521e5a84e9c16864ba1cf7a5294c49a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thmintro slippery of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] Suppose $\Phi$ is LBSF and $\bm{s}$ is a strongly $\aleph$-unobstructed slippery point of $\overline{\mathcal{Z}(\Phi)}$. Then at least one of the following happens:
        \begin{itemize}
            \item Some of the $s_i$'s are rational and the corresponding Dehn filling yields a flow with a transverse sphere. In particular, the filling has an $S^1\times S^2$ summand.
            \item Two of the $s_i$'s are irrational and Dehn filling some subset of the rational ones yields a flow with a transverse $\mathbb{T}^2$-type planar lamination. In particular, the filling has a $\mathbb{T}^2 \times I$ summand and is a limit of fillings with $S^1\times S^2$ summands.
        \end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.755669+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3e04b01f644bc1c8fc3529d1b74dc6b65634fefdc501eb1db0d39608256bde54","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:abstract-simple-response of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] If $\Lambda_n^\mu$ is simple, then for every $f\inH_{\mathrm{reg}}$ the two one-sided
derivatives agree and
