{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:07:35.023222+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3ec9b79c071e8898fe7e34aaedfe2ffca97e03f80a90b6bcce6e2dda9f7805b9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Pro 4 (\protect{\cite[Theorem 1.2) of arXiv:2609.02879, 'On the cut locus of Hamilton--Jacobi equations I: structure and propagation via the touchi'] {Azagra2023}}]
	Let $\Omega \subset \R^n$ be an open and convex set, and let $\phi \in \operatorname{SCL}(\Omega)$.
	Then for any $x \in \operatorname{Diff}(\phi)$ and any symmetric real $n \times n$ matrix $A$,
	we have
	\begin{align*}
		\lim_{y \to x} \frac{\bigl|\phi(y) - \phi(x) - \langle D\phi(x), y-x \rangle
			- \tfrac{1}{2} \langle A(y-x), y-x \rangle\bigr|}{|y-x|^2} = 0
	\end{align*}
	if and only if
	\begin{align*}
		\lim_{y \to x} \sup_{p \in D^{+}\phi(y)} \frac{|p - D\phi(x) - A(y-x)|}{|y-x|} = 0.
	\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:07:48.561355+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3ecd505ebcf17fbb6ca064baa0dca0592f331b02bdc3be57c5d2249d3b8f2d4f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 3 of arXiv:2609.01460, 'On cost-induced Santal\'o-type inequalities \\ in Polish measure spaces'] Let $m\in \N$. Let $a,b\in \R\cup\{\pm \infty\}$, with $a<b$, and let $F:(a,b]\to \R_+$ be a continuous, non-decreasing function such that $\lim_{r\to a^+}F(r)=0$. Let $\lambda_i\in (0,1)$ satisfy $\sum_{i=1}^m\lambda_i=1$ and set $\lambda=(\lambda_1,\dots,\lambda_m)$. 

    We say Polish measure spaces $(X_1,\mu_1),\dots,(X_m,\mu_m)$ satisfy the cost-Santal\'o inequality associated with $(\lambda,c,F)$, with domain $(\mathcal{C}_{x_1},\dots, \mathcal{C}_{X_m})$, where $\mathcal{C}_{X_i}\subset 2^{X_i}$, if they satisfy the equivalent inequalities in Lemma~\ref{l:transfer} with these parameters.

    If a single space $(X,\mu)$ is repeated $m$-times, we mention this space just once; the amount of occurrences is dictated by the length of $\lambda$. If $m=2$, we may list $\lambda$ just once, since $\lambda_1=\lambda$ and $\lambda_2=1-\lambda$ in this case.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.212025+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3ed22e64d1021b7aedc58a194ad9bfe171e6f6e6f28161df521a34e4baf618fa","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma exponential_bound_Nt of arXiv:2512.06640, 'Existence and sharpness of the phase transition for the frog model on transitive graphs'] Let $S \subset V$ be a finite set containing the origin. For $x \in S$ define $D_x := d_{\vec{G}}(x, S^c).$ We have that for any $t > 0$ and $x\in S:$
\begin{equation}
