{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.898444+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_3fc41ceaff7dfc840b023f47cf2093ee46d5b9bd4c4a6ec6c14c98186825223d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:sublinearCorrector_martingaleFCLT of arXiv:2411.06861, 'Quenched invariance principle for random walks in random environments admitting a cycle de'] Suppose $d\geq 2$, Assumption ~(ass:P of the paper)-(i) and Assumption ~(ass:p-q-moment of the paper) hold. Let $\chi, \Phi$ be as constructed in Lemma (lem:corrector_construction of the paper). Then 
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
    \item $\chi$ is sublinear on a large scale, i.e. for $\mathbb{P}$-a.e. $\omega$,  and all $i=1, \dots, d,$
    \begin{align}

    \lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{1}{n}\norm{\chi^i(\omega, \cdot)}_{\infty, B(n)}=0; 
    \end{align}
    \item  $M:= (\Phi(\cdot, X_t))_{t\geq 0}$ satisfies the quenched invariance principle, i.e. QFCLT holds for $M$ with a deterministic nondegenerate covariance matrix $\Sigma^2$ given by 
