    Then, for all $z\in \C$, $t\geq 0$, 
    \begin{equation}
        \mathrm{L}\pr{\acc{\xi \in \T\m ;\m \bb{p(\xi)-z}^2\leq t}}\leq 14d \pr{\frac{\sqrt{\Xi}}{m}\sqrt{t}}^{\frac{1}{S}}.
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.385910+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_403022d4eab21a4e6d09f84103241c6183cbee89bb3e649724560b55f3a0e332","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq_new_hopcount of arXiv:2411.02046, 'Speed of Convergence and Moderate Deviations of FPP on Random Geometric Graphs'] There exists~$c > 0$ such that, for any~$x \in \R^d$ with~$\|x\|$ large enough and~$t$ large enough (not depending on~$x$) with~$t \le \|x\|$, we have
