{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.786712+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_415d65bc4ec7808a329b1f62ca10597d0793e216b9385cb5510308ceee75ab16","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:maximal-fluctuation-bound of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] There exists $C$ such that for all $\beta>\beta_0$, as long as $\ell \ge b-a\ge e^{\beta/5}$, one has for all $h$ that  
