{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.502745+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_42cb738cb0883d6a8685327d1bee42bfcfeef88ff1fe2a2f9582265c7426e6ee","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition eq:mu-mixture of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[proposition]{prop:moment-law}
Fix an integer \(q\ge1\) and \(\sigma>1\).  There exists \(\varepsilon_0>0\) such that, for every \(0<\varepsilon<\varepsilon_0\), one can find a symmetric compactly supported \(C^\infty\) density \(\nu\) for which
\begin{equation}
 \mu=\varepsilon\mathcal N(0,\sigma^2)+(1-\varepsilon)\nu
\end{equation}
has the same moments as \(\mathcal N(0,1)\) through order \(2q\).  The density of \(\mu\) is strictly positive and \(C^\infty\), and \(\mu\) is sub-Gaussian.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:44:28.004257+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_42d3918fb5d41c2e600e7bb7f0de307a4994a8b84e54ea35cce11780efe3283c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2607.13308, 'No infinite clusters at criticality for two-dimensional dependent percolation under abstra'] Assume~\eqref{h2},~\eqref{h3},~\eqref{h4}, and $\theta(\lambda)>0$. There exist $\uc{c:circ}>0$ and $\alpha>0$ such that, for any $m \leq n$,
    \begin{equation}
        \P_{\lambda}\big( \Circ(m,n)^{c} \big) \leq \uc{c:circ} \Big( \Big(\frac{n}{m} \Big)^{-\alpha} + r_{m}\log \frac{n}{m} \Big).
    \end{equation}
    In particular,
    \begin{equation}
