{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:25:40.277717+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_43027c7dbf181a0258c2b0db26f4662a1eac53debf7e128e2a55f7081b83879f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Main 2 of arXiv:2609.02871, 'Estimating the number of real zeros of linear combinations of radicals of polynomials'] Let $a_k, b_k$ and $c_k$ be real numbers.  Let $\alpha \in (-\infty, -1/2]$. If the function
