{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.327546+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_43084f6a1d86d86ce3612570222dfd4977f8a16e500490732c0f7cd88e39d682","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition e.Stratification of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] We say that ${\mathbb G}$ is a \emph{Carnot group} of step $k$ if ${\mathbb G}$  is a connected and simply connected Lie group whose Lie algebra $\mathfrak{g}$ is \emph{stratified}, that is, there are non-trivial linear subspaces $V_1,\ldots, V_k$ of $\mathfrak{g}$ such that
\begin{align*}
\mathfrak{g}=V_{1}\oplus\cdots\oplus V_{k},
\end{align*}
and
\begin{align}
& \left[V_{1}, V_{i-1}\right]=V_{i},\hskip0.1in  V_{i} \neq \{0\}, \hskip0.1in 2 \leqslant i \leqslant k,
\notag
\\
& [ V_{1}, V_{k} ]=\left\{ 0 \right\}.
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.301380+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4313134e151945e67dd1e8d9eb727bf4e622d08446be427d707228c2ba1e1e9f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:resultunknownmask of arXiv:2602.11129, 'Information-Theoretic Thresholds for Bipartite Latent-Space Graphs Under Noisy Observation'] Consider any fixed $p \in (0,1)$. Then, the following holds whenever $d \gg \log(n)^3$.

