{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:39:12.320454+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_43f66941c0edb768f6907fc363b3e10d25a68f7b0aa2e5c9dacf9ab5c35e3ee8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:results:Tn2 of arXiv:2412.07710, 'An H-theorem for a conditional McKean-Vlasov process related to interacting diffusions on '] For $n \in \ensuremath{\mathbb{N}}$, define the \emph{truncated 2-tree} $\mathbb{T}_2^n := (V_n, E_n)$  with
    \begin{align*}
        V_n &:= \{-n, \ldots, n\}, \quad E_n := \{(v, v+1) : v = -n, \ldots, n-1\}.
    \end{align*}Here, we have $\mathbf{x} = (x_{-1}, x_0, x_1) \in (\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)^3$, and we let $\mathbf{x}^{(n)} := (x_{-n}, \ldots, x_n)$ denote a vector in $(\ensuremath{\mathbb{R}}^d)^{V_n}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:48:35.821804+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_43fb817a9d4d76a57390655587fa8b7253a9c094fd111db6e5fcfa758cc79937","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm: moment lb of arXiv:2411.09614, 'Moment estimates for the stochastic heat equation on Cartan-Hadamard manifolds'] Fix $\alpha>\frac{n-2}{4},\beta>0$. Let $p\geq 2$ be an integer. For any $x\in M,R>0$ if $u_0$ is bounded, $u_0\geq \varepsilon>0$ in $B(x,R)$ and $\sec_M\geq -K_2>-\infty$, we have for $0<r\leq R$ \begin{equation}
        \mathbb{E}[\abs{u(t,x)}^p]\geq C \varepsilon^p\exp\left\{\max \left[\left(Q(r),C\right)\right]pt\right\}
    \end{equation}
    where $Q(r):=\beta^2(p-1)\overline{G}_{2\alpha}(r)-\frac{c}{r^2}-C$, $c,C>0$ depend on $\alpha,n,K_2$ and $R$, and $\overline{G}_\alpha(\cdot)$ is the function defined in Lemma (Lower Bound for correlation of the paper). In particular, if $R=+\infty$, we have 
    \begin{equation}
        \liminf_{t\uparrow+\infty,x\in M} \frac{\ln \mathbb{E}[\abs{u(t,x)}^p]}{t}\geq p\max\left(\sup_{0<r<+\infty}Q(r),C\right).
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:43.681893+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_44027ead73a2e572e2426cc8715a7b5970d91f9505bd78d263e8727bdfd0278d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition c:cltsharp of arXiv:2605.28430, 'Limit theory for Lipschitz-localized statistics in random geometric models'] Let \(\mathcal{P}\) be a simple, stationary point process on \(\mathbb{R}^d\) with summable exponential mixing correlations as in Definition (def.A2 of the paper), and assume that the (reduced) Palm intensity function of the ground process \(\mathcal{P}\) is bounded at all orders, as specified at (equation bdedreduced of the paper). Let \(\Psi = \Psi(\cdot)\) be a stabilizing interaction graph on finite windows with respect to \(\mathcal{P}\) as per Definition~(d:stabilizing-graph of the paper),
with the  critical probability $q_c$ as in Definition~(d:sharp-dperc of the paper).
Assume that for some $\epsilon>0$, the maximum influence \( q(\Psi(\mathcal{P}_n)) \) defined in~(equation defq of the paper) of the Gibbs specification~(equation eqn:gibbs of the paper) with finite spin space $\mathbb{K}$ satisfies the inequality

\begin{equation} 
q(\Psi(\mathcal{P}_n)) <q_c-\epsilon,
\end{equation}

almost surely for all  $\mathcal{P}_n$, for all large enough $n\in\mathbb{N}$.  Then the system of spins \( \{V_x(\Psi(\mathcal{P}_n))\}_{x \in \mathcal{P}_n} \) satisfies the CLT as stated in Theorem~(spinmain of the paper), provided the variance condition there is also met. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:39:41.439277+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_44066e605a3fb9a0c6a01734f7988162630c49ab7e6cd95306e99b0df5ab71c9","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 18 of arXiv:2604.07370, 'Probabilistic Weyl law for twisted Toeplitz matrices with rough symbols'] Let $f\in \mathscr{C}^{\infty}(\mc{T}_{\A{1},\A{2}})$ and recall that $c_{n,m}(f)$ is defined by \eqref{Coeffs de Fourier en les deux variables}. Then, for all $k\in \N$, $n,m\in \Z^d$,
    \begin{equation}
        c_{n,m}(f)=\mc{O}_k(1)(\A{1}\A{2})^{d/2}\jap{(n,m)}^{-k}\sum_{\bb{\beta}+\bb{\gamma}\leq k}\A{1}^{-\bb{\beta}/2}\A{2}^{-\bb{\gamma}/2}\norme{\partial_x^\beta\partial_\xi^\gamma f}_{L^1(\mc{T}_{\A{1},\A{2}})}.
    \end{equation}
    In particular, if $0<\A{1}\leq\A{2}\leq 1$, then \eqref{Estimation des coeffs de Fourier en les deux variables - 1} becomes
    \begin{equation}
        c_{n,m}(f)=\mc{O}_k(1)\A{1}^{(d-k)/2}\A{2}^{d/2}\jap{(n,m)}^{-k}\sum_{\bb{\beta}+\bb{\gamma}\leq k}\norme{\partial_x^\beta\partial_\xi^\gamma f}_{L^1(\mc{T}_{\A{1},\A{2}})}.
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:06:07.094911+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4406d4c79307d59490836e1495a435f87635754b1317e1072750cec9fa68ec5c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 42 of arXiv:2608.28148, 'Flows and homotopies of Banach Lie algebroids'] Consider a manifold $M$ and a subset $\mathcal{S} \subseteq C^0(M,\R)$ of continuous functions. We say that $M$ 
\begin{enumerate}
\item admits $\mathcal{S}$-bump functions or is ($\mathcal{S}$ -regular) if for every $x\in M$ and every open $x-$neighborhood $U \subseteq M$ there exists $\chi \in \mathcal{S}$ such that $\chi (M) \subseteq [0,1], U = \chi^{-1} (]0, 1])$ and $\chi (x) = 1$.
\item is $\mathcal{S}$-paracompact if every open cover $(U_i)_{i \in I}$ of $M$ admits a subordinate partition
of unity $(\chi_i)_{i\in I}$ of functions $\chi_i \in \mathcal{S}, i \in I$.
\end{enumerate}
If $\mathcal{S} = C^k(M, \R)$ for some $k\in \N_0 \cup \{\infty\}$, we shorten the notation and say that $M$ admits $C^k$-bump functions or is $C^k$
-paracompact. Note that $C^0$-paracompactness is equivalent to the usual topological notion of paracompactness.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:29:08.520818+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_440fe90a4f23351096c566c187cc0ed5eed76c71c1abd4a9e3566687864d9318","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:height-difference-radial of arXiv:2411.19810, 'Radial conformal welding in Liouville quantum gravity'] Let $h_{\alpha\beta}$ be as in Theorem~(thm:radial-ig of the paper), and let $\eta_1$ and $\eta_2$ be two flow lines of $h_{\alpha\beta}$ with angle $\theta_1$ and $\theta_2$ started at $x_1,x_2\in\partial\mathbb{D}$. On the event $E$ where $\eta_1$ hits $\eta_2$ on its right side, 
	    we have $\mathcal{D}_{12}\in(-\pi\chi,2\lambda-\pi\chi)$. Furthermore,
	    \begin{enumerate}[(i)]
	        \item If $\mathcal{D}_{12}\in(-\pi\chi,0)$, then $\eta_1$ crosses $\eta_2$ upon intersecting and does not subsequently
	cross back;
	\item If $\mathcal{D}_{12} = 0$, then $\eta_1$ merges with and does not subsequently separate from $\eta_2$ upon intersecting;
	\item If $\mathcal{D}_{12}\in(0,2\lambda-\pi\chi)$, then $\eta_1$ bounces off but does not cross $\eta_2$.
	    \end{enumerate}
	    Finally, if $\eta_1$ hits $\eta_2$ on its left, then the same result holds with $\mathcal{D}_{21} := -\mathcal{D}_{12}$ replaced with $\mathcal{D}_{12}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:09:23.966766+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_441aef049ae44d9158d09a191d9437637bd548b4066537307ee385357d126e46","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 3 of arXiv:2607.22416, 'A multi-player optimal stopping game based on a spider Brownian bridge'] We say that $(\tau^{*},\sigma^{*}) \in \sT^\TT \times \sT^\TT$ is a subgame perfect Nash equilibrium of threshold-type if for all $t\in[0,1)$ and $x=X_{t}\in\mathbb{R}$, the stopping times $\tau^{*}_t$ and $\sigma^{*}_{t}$ satisfy  
    \begin{equation*}
        \begin{split}
            R_{1}(t,x;\tau_{t}^{*},\sigma_{t}^{*})=\sup_{\rho \in \sT_t} R_{1}(t,x;\rho,\sigma^{*}_{t}),  \\
            R_{2}(t,x;\tau^{*}_{t},\sigma^{*}_{t})=\sup_{\rho \in \sT_t} R_{2}(t,x;\tau^{*}_{t},\rho).
        \end{split}
    \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:30.013253+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_441fe45a9aa810b55b8ae956c87d4447605b5cf1103d4527fa3df60c0064b597","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 23 of arXiv:2605.04359, 'Well-posedness of reflected BSDEs with default time and irregular barrier: An application '] Let $(Y^j,Z^j,U^j)$ be the unique solution of the RBSDE \eqref{basic equation lower} associated
	with data $(\xi^j,f^j)$ for $j \in \{1,2\}$ satisfying assumptions \textbf{(H1)}, \textbf{(H2)}. Then, for any $\beta >2$, there exists a constant $\mathfrak{c}_{\beta}>0$ such that, $s \in [0,T]$,
