{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:44:17.352545+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_451c663ea4def864a5fe6e3dc2383712e320998fa2241560ab629d6b99aea76d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:contraction of arXiv:2608.22765, 'Learning to Control Coupled-Dynamics Environments with Joint Markov Decision Processes'] Every deterministic stationary policy $\pi$ induces a map $\mathcal T^\pi:\mathcal E_p\to\mathcal E_p$. For all $\eta,\zeta\in\mathcal E_p$,
