{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:14:57.713342+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_456c2672146504cccf374c58c8402baaa3a5267d511108db712950ea18754192","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:TLCF_C of arXiv:2605.30999, 'Functional central limit theorems for $U$-statistics of $\beta$-mixing data'] Let $h\colon S^m\to\mathbb R$ be a symmetric kernel, where $\pr{S,\mathcal{S}}$ is a measurable space, let $\left(X_i\right)_{i\geqslant 1}$ be a strictly stationary sequence. Let $h_1\colon S\to \mathbb R$ be defined  in 
(equation eq:definition_de_h1 of the paper).

Suppose that  conditions (equation eq:TLC_DMR of the paper), (equation eq:condition_sur_beta of the paper) are satisfied, and that  
\begin{equation}
 \exists a>1/2\mbox{ such that }   \max_{k\in \llbracket 1,m\rrbracket}\sup_{\bm{i}\in\operatorname{Inc}^ k}\E{H_{\bm{i},k}^2\pr{\log\pr{1+\abs{H_{\bm{i},k}}} }^a }<+\infty. 
