{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:50:30.569173+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_457e8ab1796fdbe8a1b3659686645959e07c758cfbd8abce3aac7adad26e9294","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 13 of arXiv:2605.30779, '2605.30779'] Let \(U\subset\mathbb C\) be an open set, let \(x_0\in U\cap\mathbb R\), and assume that \(\{f_N\}_{N=1}^\infty\xrightarrow{\mathrm{mer}} f\) on \(U\). Suppose that \(x_0\) is not a pole of \(f\), and
  \begin{align*}
