\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:48:17.116976+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4599365147536ca0367fcc01a3a5c3ec705f21f59e46e20506b335b242b6cacb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 145 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] Fix $h>0$ and a base point ${\hat x}_0\ge 0$. Let ${\hat x}_1={\hat x}_1^{[M]}$ be chosen so that
	\begin{align*}
		U_{h;M,Q}'({\hat x}_0)=U_{h;0,0}'({\hat x}_1)
	\end{align*}
	(suppressing from the notation the dependence of $\hat{x}_1$ on $\hat{x}_0$ and $Q$.)
		The choice $M=-2{\hat x}_0-\eta$, for sufficiently small $\eta>0$, has the following property: for each fixed $h'\in(0,h]$, there is a constant
		$c=c(h',h,{\hat x}_0)>0$, such that
		\begin{align}
			\partial_hU_{h';M,Q}({\hat x}_0)-\partial_hU_{h';0,0}({\hat x}_1^{[-2 {\hat x}_0-\eta]})
			\ge cQ\eta.

