                For $0<\varepsilon<h$ one has $\inf\{ c(h',h,{\hat x}_0):h'\in [\varepsilon,h]\}>0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.571668+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_459a68ff3cb0deecba52af2be5cd345507f600f381de91b9b9efbf22eb698022","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 7 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d\geq6$. There exist $c,C>0$ such that, for every $n\geq 2$,  
