{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.056386+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_45c354abbbe46359cb61e9746f359d01fd059107cf0b59af8150a2a83c18f96e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:positive-time-local-density-equivalence of arXiv:2608.16119, 'Fully nonlinear parabolic equations under a fixed reference diffusion: weighted \texorpdfs'] Under Assumption~(ass:reference-diffusion of the paper), there is a function
$\varrho\in C((0,T]\times\mathbb R^d)$, locally H\"older continuous on $Q$, such
that
\begin{equation*}
 \mu_t(\,\mathrm d x)=\varrho(t,x)\,\mathrm d x,
 \qquad \varrho(t,x)>0,
 \qquad (t,x)\in(0,T]\times\mathbb R^d.
\end{equation*}
For every $0<\varepsilon<T$ and $K\Subset\mathbb R^d$,
\begin{equation}
 0<\inf_{(t,x)\in[\varepsilon,T]\times K}\varrho(t,x)
 \leq\sup_{(t,x)\in[\varepsilon,T]\times K}\varrho(t,x)<\infty.

