{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:13:49.976710+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_464eb71fad0e3c8befd374e7d5f1b127380057fa9630f245c9582a6517fc7fec","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:1052a of arXiv:2411.07157, 'Rough differential equations in the flow approach'] For any $N\in\N$, $p\in[1,\infty]$ and $\mu\in(0,1]$, we denote by $\mathcal{W}^p_{N,\mu}$ the set of all time weights $u_\mu\in \mathcal{D}(\R)$ verifying
\begin{equs}
  \max_{i\leqslant N} 
    \mu^{-1/p+i}
    {\| \d^i_t u_\mu 
    \|}_{L^p((-\infty,1])}< \infty\,.
\end{equs}
Then, for every $\psi\in \mathcal{D}(\R)$, $M\geqslant N$ and $q\in[1,\infty]$, uniform in $\mu\in(0,1]$ we have
    \begin{equs}      \norm{K_{M,\mu}\big(u_\mu\psi)}_{L^{q}}&\lesssim \norm{K_{M,\mu}\psi}_{L^{q}}\,,\;\text{provided} \; u_\mu \in\mathcal{W}^\infty_{N,\mu}\,,\\
          \norm{K_{M,\mu}\big(u_\mu\psi)}_{L^{1}}&\lesssim\mu \norm{K_{M,\mu}\psi}_{L^\infty}\,,\;\text{provided} \; u_\mu \in\mathcal{W}^1_{N,\mu}\,.
    \end{equs}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:06:21.713187+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_465b64ec4c977ae648880fcb5b09df14bd760c7ba9d07e3734ac1cfa11171d31","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 of arXiv:2607.21374, 'Local structure at the maximum and sharp persistence asymptotics of rough fractional Brown'] For the grids of Proposition~\ref{prop:dyadic-grid-diagonal}, define
\begin{equation}
  \Lambda_{n,k}:=\{h_n(j-k):0\leq j\leq M_n\},
  \qquad 0\leq k\leq M_n,

\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
  Q_{n,k}:=\mathcal L\left(
    B\,\middle|\, B_t\leq0\text{ for every }t\in\Lambda_{n,k}
  \right),
  \qquad
  p_{n,k}:=\PP(B_t\leq0:t\in\Lambda_{n,k}).

\end{equation}
Then
\(p_{n,k}=\PP(K_n=k)>0\),
\(\sum_{k=0}^{M_n}p_{n,k}=1\), and
\begin{equation}
  \mathcal L(\Xi_n^{\mathrm{grid}})
  =\sum_{k=0}^{M_n}p_{n,k}Q_{n,k}.

\end{equation}
Write
\begin{equation}
  L_{n,k}^-=h_nk,
  \qquad L_{n,k}^+=h_n(M_n-k).

\end{equation}
For \(0<k<M_n\), the component \(Q_{n,k}\) is
\(Q_{h_n,L_{n,k}^-,L_{n,k}^+}\) from \eqref{eq:pure-wall-law}.  The endpoint
components \(k=0,M_n\) retain their direct conditional definitions in
\eqref{eq:mixture-components}; they are full-path laws constrained on only
one side of the pin and are not covered by the positive-two-horizon
definition \eqref{eq:pure-wall-law}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.773596+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_46648d7ad2f4dd02b11416ff4c819d72839c91835e101a4200cfc84ca7a6a81b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 68 of arXiv:2603.24616, 'Pinning in non-critical half-space geometric last passage percolation'] Fix $p \in (0, \infty)$ and set $\sigma = \sqrt{p(1+p)}$. For any $\epsilon, A > 0$ we can find $N_0$ large enough, depending on $p, \epsilon, A $, such that the following holds. For any $n \geq N_0$ and $z \in \mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}$ such that $|z - pn| \leq A n^{1/2}$ we can find a probability space that supports a Brownian bridge $B^{\sigma}$ with variance $\sigma^2$ and a random increasing path $\ell^{(n,z)}$ with law $\mathbb{P}_{\operatorname{Geom}}^{0, n, 0,z}$ such that 
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P} \left( \Delta(n,z) \geq n^{1/4} \right) < \epsilon, \mbox{ where $\Delta(n,z):=  \sup_{0 \leq t \leq n} \left| n^{1/2} B^\sigma_{t/n} + \frac{t}{n} \cdot z - \ell^{(n,z)}(t) \right|.$}
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.721090+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_46742da3e147e1bba4bd94d1539e7327fabf19271b0fd1ec3b217af1a89f057d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi finite action of arXiv:2411.04157, 'Stochastic homogenization of dynamical discrete optimal transport'] Let $(\rho,j)\in \mathcal{M}((0,T)\times \mathbb{R}^n;[0,\infty)\times \mathbb{R}^n)$ be a finite Radon measure. We say that $(\rho,j)$ is a \emph{finite action curve} if
    \begin{enumerate}
    \item $(\rho,j)$ solve the continuity equation 
    \begin{align*}
\partial_t\rho+\dive j=0 \text{ in }\mathcal D'((0,T)\times \mathbb{R}^n).
\end{align*}
        \item $j\ll \rho$ and 
        \begin{align*}
            \int_{(0,T)\times \mathbb{R}^n}\left|\frac{dj}{d\rho}\right|^2\, d\rho<\infty;
        \end{align*}
    \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:40.985035+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4679abe52e10560483c2fe00de653062a4aabfe238dfc79baf3cab2751bfdd30","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem_2 of arXiv:2412.03774, '{ Refining Concentration for \\Gaussian Quadratic Chaos with\\ Applications in Sonar and C'] Let $m\geq 1$ be an integer. For every $\frac{m+1}{m+2}< a<1$, the inequality 
 \begin{eqnarray}

