where $\eta^{(k)}_{i,j}(\gamma)$ can be determined as in ((eq:H0-ij1 of the paper)) and  ((eq:H0-ij2 of the paper)) for $j<i\in [n]$ and $k\in \{1,2\}$ and $\Lambda_{i, j}^{(k)}= 4\lambda_i\lambda_jv_iv_j\,\eta^{(k)}_{i,j}(0)$, for $k=1,2$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.832014+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4746f3510879915ebe150c2b5a3dba245ff50b6ba80fe62ab41639e5955bbc46","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:fs_uppertail_interval of arXiv:2608.05089, 'Correlation decay in area-tilted line ensembles'] There exist constants $C,c > 0$ such that for all $S \geqslant 1$ and $y > 0$ we have
