{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:51.762626+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4803d81338691859dce3f6f78c1d3ec1ef78710fc61d786dcc16e2451b3d0f1c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:MSlin_gen of arXiv:2604.28068, 'Mean-square Stability and Bifurcations for Dissipative SDEs'] Let ${\widetilde{Y}}$ be the solution of (equation eq:sdeLinMult of the paper), $M$ be as defined in Lemma (lem:arnold of the paper) and let $P$ be the solution of (equation eq:Pode of the paper). 
