{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:29:35.077924+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_486ac06026edc1c7d0096bc2c7afbf230d09cd275cc61d4ca299079b204b2814","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 7 of arXiv:2609.03793, 'Typical martingale diverges on a co-$\sigma$-porous set'] Let $(X,\psi)$ be a metric space and let $A\subset X$. Let also $s_n>0$, $\beta_n\in(0,1)$, $n\in\N$ be such that $\beta_n\ra0$ and $s_n\ra0$. Then $A$ is $\sigma$-porous if and only if $A=\bigcup_{n\in\N}A_n$, where each $A_n$ satisfies:
