{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:41:54.342250+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4a0397475dd2efe2cd6898161fd4c0fa7ec9c67a6ecfbc40bd2de67c198edf27","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:apriori of arXiv:2412.01381, 'Ergodicity and mixing for locally monotone stochastic evolution equations'] Assume that Hypotheses~(hyp:hemicont of the paper),~(hyp:coerc of the paper),~(hyp:coerc-g of the paper),~(hyp:monotonicity of the paper), (hyp:monotonicity-g of the paper), (hyp:growth of the paper), (hyp:regularity of the paper) are valid. Let $T>0$ be fixed.
Let $\alpha\ge 2$, $\alpha-2\ge\beta\ge 0$ be as in Hypotheses (hyp:coerc of the paper) and (hyp:monotonicity of the paper).
If $\alpha=\beta+2$, we assume additionally that
\[\|B\|_{L_2(U,H)}^2\le\lambda_3\frac{1}{\alpha}\delta_1 c_0^\alpha,\]
where $\lambda_3$ is as in Hypothesis~(hyp:quant of the paper), and $\delta_1>0$ is as in 
Hypothesis~(hyp:coerc of the paper).
Then for any initial datum $X_0=x$ such that $\exp(\|x\|^{\beta+2}_H)\in L^{1}(\Omega,{\mathcal F}_0,\mathbb{P};H)$, and every $0\le s\le t\le T$, and for any $n\in\mathbb{N}$, the solution $(X_t^{(n),x_n})_{t\in [0,T]}$ to~(equation eq:finitedim0new of the paper) satisfies
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
&\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(\|X_t^{(n),x_n}\|^{\beta+2}_H+\lambda_0\delta_1\frac{\beta+2}{2}\int_s^{t} \|X_r^{(n),x_n}\|^\beta_H \|X_r^{(n),x_n}\|^\alpha_V\,\mathrm{d} r\right)\right]\\
\le&\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(\|X_s^{(n),x_n}\|_H^{\beta+2}+(t-s)(c_1+c_2+c_3)\right)\right],
\end{split}
\end{equation}
for every $0\le s\le t\le T$ in the locally monotone case, and similarly with $\mathbb{E}$ replaced by $\tilde{\mathbb{E}}$ in the fully locally monotone case.
Here, $\lambda_0\in (0,1)$ and $c_i\ge 0$, $i=1,2,3$, are as in 
Hypothesis~(hyp:quant of the paper).

In particular, for $x_n:=Q_n x$, where $Q_n$ is defined as in (equation eq:Qn of the paper), and for any $n\in\mathbb{N}$,
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
&\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(\|X_t^{(n),x_n}\|^{\beta+2}_H+\lambda_0\delta_1\frac{\beta+2}{2}\int_0^{t} \|X_r^{(n),x_n}\|^\beta_H \|X_r^{(n),x_n}\|^\alpha_V\,\mathrm{d} r\right)\right]\\
\le&\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(\|x_n\|_H^{\beta+2}+t(c_1+c_2+c_3)\right)\right],
\end{split}
\end{equation}
for every $0\le t\le T$ in the locally monotone case, and similarly with $\mathbb{E}$ replaced by $\tilde{\mathbb{E}}$ in the fully locally monotone case.

Furthermore, we obtain,
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
&\mathbb{E}\left[\|X_t\|^{\beta+2}_H\right]+\lambda_0\delta_1 c_0^\alpha\frac{\beta+2}{2}\mathbb{E}\int_0^{t} \|X_r\|^{\alpha+\beta}_H\,\mathrm{d} r\\
\le&\mathbb{E}\left[\|x\|_H^{\beta+2}\right]+t(c_1+c_2),
\end{split}
\end{equation}
for every $0\le t\le T$, and similarly with $\mathbb{E}$ replaced by $\tilde{\mathbb{E}}$ in the fully locally monotone case.

Also,
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
&\mathbb{E}\left[\|X_t\|^{2}_H\right]+\delta_1\mathbb{E}\int_0^{t} \|X_r\|^{\alpha}_V\,\mathrm{d} r\\
\le&\mathbb{E}\left[\|x\|_H^{2}\right]+t\|B\|^2_{L_2(U,H)},
\end{split}
\end{equation}
for every $0\le t\le T$, and similarly with $\mathbb{E}$ replaced by $\tilde{\mathbb{E}}$ in the fully locally monotone case.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:45:05.588497+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4a0ae1fd23327b091e0302a6ae45004bf8ca03e24b541ef552e78ca92b99b144","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2608.05842, 'Asymptotic Expansion of the Kallianpur–Striebel Formula under Perturbations of Linear Mode'] For any $0\leq t\leq T$, it holds
