{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:26:02.532956+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4a910530606fe120065dcac206aa8d56be5026090e31756ad353e36b811710fe","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] A \textbf{generalized coarse slope} is an element of $\mathbb{R} \cup \{\pm \infty,\aleph\}$. A \textbf{generalized fine slope} is a coarse slope, plus a type in $\{\natural, \dagger, \sharp, \flat\}$. The meaning of $s^\heartsuit$ for $\heartsuit \in \{\natural, \dagger, \sharp, \flat\}$ remains the same as in \zcref{sec:T2foliations}, and we define the generalized fine slope of a $\Phi$-horizontal foliation $\mathcal{G}$ with a Reeb annulus as follows:

    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $\aleph^\natural$ if $\mathcal{G}$ has neither $+\infty^\sharp$ nor $-\infty^\flat$ annuli. This class was simply called $\aleph$ in the body of the article.
        \item $\aleph^\sharp$ if $\mathcal{G}$ has a $+\infty^\sharp$ annulus, but no $-\infty ^\flat$ annuli.

        \item $\aleph^\flat$ if $\mathcal{G}$ has a $-\infty^\flat$ annulus, but no $+\infty^\sharp$ annuli.

        \item $\aleph^\dagger$ if $\mathcal{G}$ has both $+\infty^\sharp$ and $-\infty^\flat$ annuli.
    \end{enumerate}
    We write $\mathscr{S}$ for the space of real fine slopes $\mathbb{R} \times \{\natural, \dagger, \sharp, \flat\}$, and $\widehat{\mathscr{S}}$ for the space of generalized fine slopes $(\mathbb{R} \cup \{-\infty, +\infty, \aleph\}) \times \{\natural, \dagger, \sharp, \flat\}$.\footnote{If preferred, $+\infty^{\sharp/\natural}$ and $-\infty^{\flat/\natural}$ may be excluded from $\widehat{\mathscr{S}}$ as they do not occur as fine slopes of $\Phi$-horizontal foliations.}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:15:34.386022+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4a983c7f5f20520f0b0c916955e5171c73a8de0c039ba4cddc41de17cefa967f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 4 (\cite{keel1992}) of arXiv:2609.03268, 'Poincare Polynomials of Heavy-Light Hassett Spaces'] Let $R=\Z[x_I: 2\le |I| \le n-2]$ be the polynomial ring over $\Z$ on $2^n-2n-2$ variables. Then there is a quotient map $R\onto A(\DMumford{n})$ given by $x_I\mapsto [D_I]$. Furthermore, the kernel of this quotient map is the ideal generated by the following elements:
            \begin{enumerate}
                \item $x_I-x_{I^c}$ for all $I$;
                \item $x_I x_J$ for each pair $I,J$ such that $\varnothing\notin \{I\cap J, I \cap J^c, I^c\cap J, I^c \cap J^c\};$
                \item (WDVV relations) for $\{a,b,c,d\}\in {[n]\choose 4}$, 
                $$\sum_{I: I\cap\{a,b,c,d\}=\{a,b\}} x_I - \sum_{I: I\cap\{a,b,c,d\}=\{a,c\}} x_I.$$
            \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

