{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:53.445147+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ae61ccdec7d1cb1966d798bd124e4ec05bd07a831c762b22716303f071e88b4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 24 of arXiv:2606.15432, 'A Concavity Theorem for the Parisi PDE'] Fix $0\leq s< \sigma\leq 1$. Then, the following are true. 
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $A^{\gamma,s,\sigma,0}(s)\geq 0$.
    \item For all $x\in \R$ and $\rho\in (s,\sigma)$, $\partial_\rho A^{\gamma,s,\sigma,x}(\rho)\geq 0$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:35:59.919432+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4af2bc0361f44a12c392b65bb0050da234bc53ec5782431255154b5d0f506051","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 5 of arXiv:2608.26084, 'Localic Esakia Duality\\via Conic Frames'] A frame~$L$ is called:
	\begin{itemize}
		\item \emph{algebraic} if~$K(L)$ forms a join-basis for~$L$;
		\item \emph{coherent} if it is algebraic and~$K(L)$ is a bounded sublattice~of~$L$;
		\item \emph{compact} if~$\top\in L$ is a compact element;
		\item \emph{zero-dimensional} if its complemented elements form a join-basis;
		\item \emph{Stone} if it is compact and zero-dimensional.
	\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:44:28.068235+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4afa9434eab5275504c03ab80892159a4bf56b4bf7693b633ee7eda5736427b4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2607.13401, 'Total variation cutoff for Kac's walk on the sphere'] For every \(\varepsilon>0\), there are constants
\(n_0=n_0(\varepsilon)\) and \(C_\varepsilon<\infty\) such that, for all
\(n\ge n_0\) and all \(t\ge0\),
\begin{equation}
        \mb E W_t^2
        \le
        C_\varepsilon
        \exp\left\{-\left(\frac{29}{32}-\varepsilon\right)\frac{t}{n}\right\}.
\end{equation}
Consequently, for every \(2<p<4\) and every \(\varepsilon>0\), with
\begin{equation}
        \sigma_p
        :=
        \left(2-\frac p2\right)\frac12
        +
        \left(\frac p2-1\right)\frac{29}{32}
        =
        \frac{6+13p}{64},
\end{equation}
there are constants \(n_0=n_0(p,\varepsilon)\) and
\(C_{p,\varepsilon}<\infty\) such that, for all \(n\ge n_0\) and all
\(t\ge0\),
\begin{equation}
        \mb E W_t^{p/2}
        \le
        C_{p,\varepsilon}
        \exp\left\{-\left(\sigma_p-\varepsilon\right)\frac{t}{n}\right\}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:52:08.663403+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4afb12b2b942157e482860f197f030c2c4113f60918e37b507b598b2e112d18b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 13 (\bf Energy Estimate) of arXiv:2608.29984, 'On Cauchy Problems for Parabolic Equations with Rough Coefficients'] Let $u^{\epsilon}$ be the classical solution of \eqref{approxnondiv}, then we have
