{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.415583+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4bad70354cdeb856ed2a776acb9763ebba7be15ae4ec43766378e35f0fefe5b1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 96 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Take two variational data satisfying Assumptions~\ref{Assumption_A} and \ref{Assumption_B} with $\iota_h^{-,\textnormal{I}}=\iota_h^{-,\textnormal{II}}=2$, differing by their segment endpoints $\hat{a}_{h}^{\prime\,\textnormal{I}}$ and $\hat{a}_{h}^{\prime\,\textnormal{II}}$ for a single $h \in [H]$, and by the potentials
