{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.590413+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c153acfd635f62c34ffdbe5cfd186817c50111398510950391dbcbba820250f","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:pseudo-deriv of arXiv:2606.02003, 'Higher-Order Multifractional Stable Motion:\\ Definition and Fundamental Properties'] Under Assumption~(ass:params of the paper) with $\beta > 1$, for
$k \in \{0,1,\ldots,n-1\}$ and $t \in \mathbb{R}$, define the
\emph{$k$-th pseudo-derivative} of $X^{(n)}_H$ at $t$ by
\begin{equation}

X^{(n,k)}_H(t)
:= \int_\mathbb{R}
\frac{\partial^k f_n}{\partial t^k}(t,u;H,\alpha)\,dM_\alpha(u).
