{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:53:30.651777+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4c3cfba1aaadb63508a54b407b79c062ba32c3651fe33cd2200df619ded47855","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn eq:defVoro of arXiv:2506.01746, '\bf Optimal Bregman quantization: existence and uniqueness of optimal quantizers revisited'] A Borel partition of $\mathbb{R}^d$ $(C_a(\Gamma))_{a\in \Gamma}$ is called a {\em Voronoi partition of $\mathbb{R}^d$ induced by $\Gamma$} if
