{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:57:20.674542+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4cd2d344b0b67e67e80b36cf3a13fb22f9a5fe35b32205a2f5f42f4a3ba592c5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:single-concentration-stable of arXiv:2411.10113, 'Long-range one-dimensional\\ internal diffusion-limited aggregation'] Suppose that~(equation ass:irreducible of the paper) holds and that~(equation ass:stable-alpha of the paper) holds with $\alpha \in (1,2)$. Take $u,s \in {\mathbb R}$, such that $1<u<s$ and let $q: = {\underline{q}_\alpha}(u,s)$ as given in equation~(equation eq:q-lower-bound of the paper).
Then, there exist $\varepsilon_0 \in (0,1)$, $K>0$, and $x_0 >0$ such that the following holds. 
For all $x>x_0$, every $\varepsilon \in (0,\varepsilon_0)$, 
with $k_x : = \lceil (q^{-1} + K\varepsilon) (s-1)x \rceil$, there is $c >0$ for which
    \begin{equation}

    \max_{t \in {\mathbb Z} \cap [ x,ux]} \Pr\left(K^+_{\sigma_x,k_x}(t,x,s)<(s-1)x\right)  \leq {\mathrm{e}}^{-c(s-1)x},
    \end{equation}
    and 
    \begin{equation}
        \max_{t \in {\mathbb Z} \cap [ x,ux]} \Pr \left( K^-_{\sigma_x,k_x}(-t,x,s)< (s-1)x\right)\leq {\mathrm{e}}^{-c(s-1)x}. 
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:38:08.415658+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4cd72ea422dbc57087a6c3783425f23b6852e27ffd2731dd06c1e385811c3f5f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Delta z on C=0 of arXiv:2609.02073, 'Existence of closed non-planar $p$-elasticae'] The following holds.
