{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:59:24.051831+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4cda0cd570aa1b90c2b291041786040de9f4e979b570b7ad4821b8349364457f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor blowup of arXiv:2608.30847, 'An Almgren-type formula for planar $p$-harmonic functions'] Let $u$, $x_0$, and $\lambda=N_*(x_0,0+)$ be as in Theorem (thm:main of the paper).  If $u$ is not locally constant near $x_0$, then there exists a nonzero homogeneous $p$-harmonic function $P$ of degree $\lambda$ such that
$$
