{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.736025+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4da369584aef852902894fbac23cd34f5d25155e483563c69d6fc382bdae8636","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem-Ward of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] Let $\mathcal A$ be a Hermitian matrix. Define its resolvent as $R(z):=(\mathcal A-z)^{-1}$ for any $z= E+ \mathrm{i} \eta\in \mathbb{C}_+$. Then, we have 
