{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:10.025909+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4e911280dbfa607723b024d9c30e2279feb52f6a23781bfab8cb86fab2354dac","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 20 (Metric comparison on the Stiefel manifold) of arXiv:2608.17374, '\textbf{On the Pseudo-Mixing of Kac's Walk}'] Let $D$ be the Riemannian distance on $\mathrm{St}(n,k)$ induced by the Frobenius
inner product from the embedding $\mathrm{St}(n,k)\subset \mathbb{R}^{n\times k}$.
Then, for all $X,Y\in \mathrm{St}(n,k)$,
