{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:29:08.521675+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ea94eb72f9ff6719495d672285c59b11c0edceba6e5b1ba0e3f0006399bb18e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:lcft-H-conf-infty of arXiv:2411.19810, 'Radial conformal welding in Liouville quantum gravity'] Suppose $\beta_1,\beta_2,\beta_3\in\mathbb{R}$ and $f:\mathbb{H}\to\mathbb{H}$ is the conformal map with $f(0) = 1$, $f(1)=\infty$ and $f(\infty) = 0$. Then 
		\begin{equation}
		\textup{LF}_{\mathbb{H}}^{(\beta_1, 0), (\beta_2, 1), (\beta_3, \infty)} = f_*\textup{LF}_{\mathbb{H}}^{(\beta_1, \infty), (\beta_2, 0), (\beta_3, 1)}.
		\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:48:45.311974+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4ead01faa3b2d2446c7bb78e8bf9de3e4e12166c4725f7c70c0422b4d051e4a1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:sep of arXiv:2411.14921, 'A boundary Harnack principle and its application to analyticity of 3D Brownian intersectio'] For $\mathbb{P}_{\vec x}$-almost  every $\mathcal{W}$, there exist $\delta_1(\mathcal{W})$, $\delta_2(\mathcal{W})>0$ such that for any closed subset $\mathcal{A}\subseteq\mathcal{W}$ and all $x\in B(0,1/2)\setminus \mathcal{A}$, we have 
    \begin{equation}
\mathbf{P}_x\left(\mathrm{dist}(W(\tau),\mathcal{A})>\delta_1 \,\Big |\,  W[0,\tau]\cap \mathcal{A}=\varnothing\right)>\delta_2,
    \end{equation}
    where $\tau$ is the first hitting time of $\partial B(0,1)$ by $W$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:35:10.799279+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4eb70664d74b78aaef536077e8faffa6a02a9535c3f9c94ee0309cd4262d6670","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 66 of arXiv:2604.00635, 'Large deviations of the periodic Toda chain'] Let $\boldsymbol{\lambda}^+_N \in \mathbb{R}^N_{<}$. Then the following are equivalent.
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $\boldsymbol{\lambda}^+_N \in \mathcal{A}_N$.
    \item There exists a vector $\boldsymbol{\eta}_N \in \mathbb{R}^N_{<}$ such that the following holds. Let

$$P(x) := \prod_{k=1}^N ( x - \eta_k)$$ and let $\zeta_1, \dots, \zeta_{N-1} \in \mathbb{R}$ be the roots of $P^\prime$. Then $|P(\zeta_k)| > 2\veps_N$ for all $k \in \intn{1}{N-1}$ and $\lambda_1^+, \dots, \lambda_N^+$ are the roots of $P - 2\veps_N$.
