{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.082733+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4eebd23d8813fb5ac26ad72bfce0e6bbd92a1de7a819e4fe385da8ee92832d75","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition GrowthBoundCond of arXiv:2411.12522, 'Canonical insurance models: stochastic equations and comparison theorems'] Let $\mathbb{Y}^+$ denote the set of all $\mathcal{F}$-adapted, nonnegative, nondecreasing, univariate  càdlàg processes
	$Y$ for which there exists a growth bound  
