Moreover, for any $t\ge 1$, let $P_{n}^{*t}$ be the $t$-fold convolution of $P_n$, viewed $P_{n}^{*t}$ as a random variable in $\mathfrak{S}_n$. Given $n=ml$ with $l\ge 2$, the random variable $\sim_l\backslash P_{n}^{*t}\in\sim_l\backslash\mathfrak{S}_n$ is induced from (defi: quotient of space of the paper) in the obvious way.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:34:09.924490+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4f10d153d233cc96cfcefbfd4e0266a744c79fc9a7af15ca85c19d467066b428","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 7 of arXiv:2603.27433, 'The $k$-cycle shuffling with repeated cards'] Let $r:=n-\l_1$. Suppose that one of the following holds:
\begin{enumerate}
