\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:12:20.543124+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_4f677935e74e26569a07824ccb028724bbd1297bd60d104de203ca48289c1bc6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma local_action_function of arXiv:2603.27906, 'Marked GUE-corners process in doubly periodic dimer models'] Let~$z_k=1+\frac{Z_k}{N^\frac{1}{2}}$,~$k=1,2$. Then, as~$N\to \infty$, for $(z_1,w_1)$,  $(z_2,w_2)$ in the neighbourhood of $q_{\infty}$, we have that
\begin{multline} 
\exp\left({N(G(z_2,w_2)-G(z_1,w_1))}\right)
\frac{w_1^{r_1}}{w_2^{r_2}}
 \frac{z_1^{\mu_1\sqrt{N}}}{z_2^{\mu_2\sqrt{N}}}
 \frac{1}{z_2(z_2-z_1)}
\\= N^{\frac{1}{2}} \frac{\left(1+\mathcal{O}\left( \frac{|Z_1|^3+|Z_2|^3}{N^{\frac{1}{2}}} \right)\right)}{Z_2-Z_1} 
 N^{\frac{\ell r_1}{2}-\frac{\ell r_2}{2}} 
B^{ r_1- r_2} 
