{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:12:46.873594+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_521e75ccd8bed547bbb1e3dfd6a1b2569ddf28af8c97626ce486cf87d780e4c7","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:unravel of arXiv:2608.08375, 'Algebraic formulas for first-passage times of Markov processes in the linear framework: ge'] Let $G$ be a strongly connected graph, and let $v \in \mathcal{V}(G)$. Then the unravelling of $G$ at vertex $v$, denoted $\mathcal{U}_v[G]$, has vertices $\mathcal{V}(\mathcal{U}_v[G]) = \mathcal{V}(G) \cup \{v^+\}$. The edges and labels of $\mathcal{U}_v[G]$ are acquired from those of $G$ through the following rules. Choose $j, k \in \mathcal{V}(G)$. 
\begin{enumerate}
    \item If $j \to_G k$ with $k \neq v$, then $j \to_{\mathcal{U}_v[G]} k$ and $\ell(j \to_{\mathcal{U}_v[G]} k) = \ell(j \to_G k)$.
    \item If $j \to_G v$, then $j \to_{\mathcal{U}_v[G]} v^+$ and $\ell(j \to_{\mathcal{U}_v[G]} v^+) = \ell(j \to_G v)$.
\end{enumerate}
There are no other edges in $\mathcal{U}_v[G]$.","status":"unverified"}

