{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:52:57.732309+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_52ba0e0ebe090400201ba4c2898a930eecf77ce39d0fd99a541453dc570d5380","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2609.02755, 'The Sharp Rate of Probabilistically Strong Convergence to the KPZ Equation'] Suppose that $(\Hb, \Hp, \bar{\mathcal{W}})$ is a solution of the system
	\begin{align*}
