{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:33:12.356218+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_535bd33535d43127f9e00fcb3538d9fa0b4e2602c8f7c0506f787af555c83cbf","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Dfn 231 (row-spliced matrix) of arXiv:2608.29416, 'Algorithmic threshold for high-dimensional projection pursuit I: general theory'] For $S\subseteq [M]$ and matrices $\bG, \hbG \in \R^{M\times N}$ with rows $(\bg^a : a\in [M])$ and $(\hat\bg^a : a\in [M])$, let $\tbG = \tbG(\bG,\hbG;S) \in \R^{M\times N}$ be the matrix with rows $(\tbg^a : a\in [M])$, where 
