{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.424185+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_556273b59a1e0cb15a3672b1d5c4efbcae6934ec2ca8ab6532e061a66f95cbea","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem eq:theta-logpotential of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[theorem]{thm:theta}
Let
\begin{equation}
 \theta_p(u)=\frac12-\frac12\log p-\frac{u^2}{2}
 +\int\log\abs{\sqrt{2p(p-1)}\lambda-pu}\,\rho_{\mathrm{sc}}(\,\mathrm d\lambda).
\end{equation}
Then
\begin{equation}
 \theta_p(u)=\frac12\log(p-1)
 -\frac{p-2}{4(p-1)}u^2-\mathcal I_p(u).
\end{equation}
For every continuous \(V\) bounded below,
\begin{equation}
 \Phi_p^{\rm bulk}(V)
 :=\sup_{u\in\mathbb R}\{\theta_p(u)-V(u)\}
\end{equation}
is the iterated determinant/delta de-regularization of the Gaussian pressure in (thm:gaussian-variational of the paper); see (thm:dereg-variational of the paper).  Moreover,
\begin{equation}
 \theta_p(u)=\inf_{V\in\mathcal V_\infty}
 \{\Phi_p^{\rm bulk}(V)+V(u)\},
\end{equation}
where \(\mathcal V_\infty=\bigcap_{m\ge2}\mathcal V_m\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

