{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.187856+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5592bee63a9e24111c9de86e245fee2ca546754f19180fefbfecf7c6586bcbac","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:Ising-phase-transition of arXiv:2603.01322, 'Gibbs conditioning, atypical consensus and splitting Gibbs measures on random regular grap'] Fix $0\neq c\in [-\k,\k],$ and recall the definition of $\smref$ from (equation eqn:smref of the paper). Then the following statements hold:

