{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:30:14.228633+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56c6866993a36d681af7a6fb6bf6292cad08c9b84c4594392a5fda0f92e53e29","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Lemma Ratio 1 of arXiv:2608.23202, 'Locally finite Fixed points of Branching Brownian Motion'] Let $K>0$ and $E_t=E_t^1 \text{ or } E_t^2$. Then, there exists some $u \ge 0$ \textcolor{black}{(depending on $t$)} such that
