{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:51.762312+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56c860d9cb7e1eb7592573fb86fa001e5624e01e2ba6f197fa98e997e2d0d26a","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Def:linear-m-s-stability of arXiv:2604.28068, 'Mean-square Stability and Bifurcations for Dissipative SDEs'] Let ${\widetilde{Y}}$ be the solution of (equation eq:lin_gen of the paper) with initial data ${\widetilde{Y}}(0)\in\mathbb{R}^d$. 
