{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:10.022835+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56e8e97633b7bde35b9fba5b0668384095f1c18c3d9bdf39607c41786b0cda69","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 9 (Global Multi-Step Contraction) of arXiv:2608.17374, '\textbf{On the Pseudo-Mixing of Kac's Walk}'] Fix $n \in \mathbb{N}$ and $k \in \mathbb{N}$ with $1\leq k < n$. Let $P$ be the one-step transition kernel of the $k$-column walk on $\mathrm{St}(n,k)$, let $D$ be the Riemannian distance on $\mathrm{St}(n,k)$, and let $W_D$ be Wasserstein distance with cost $D$. Then there exists a constant $C > 0$ such that, for every $T\geq0$ and every $X_0,Y_0\in\mathrm{St}(n,k)$,
\[
W_D\left(P^T(X_0,\cdot),P^T(Y_0,\cdot)\right)
\;\le\;
n^{-\left\lfloor \frac{T}{C n (k+\log(n))\log(n)} \right\rfloor}\,D(X_0,Y_0).
\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:01:22.597578+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56f1aee4220f72de5618df50a363e2d0400b25cc4c53d34a794e90c5cdb4fab0","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:DCM of arXiv:2606.10257, 'Downward conditional monotonicity gives survival and extinction for contact processes in r'] Consider MMPPs $(B,X),(B',X')$ with possibly different initial distributions for $B$ and $B'$ but with the same arrival rate vector $\alpha$ and generator matrix $T$. The MMPP with $\alpha,T$ is called \emph{downward conditionally monotone} if $v^*\preceq \mathcal{L}(B_0)\preceq\mathcal{L}(B'_0)$ implies, for all $t>0$,
