{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:30:14.229013+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_571eaa8610bef287c26ab2bee016b7cc0403ddaa364fe32652fe6481df7dd8aa","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma Main_contribution in sec3 of arXiv:2608.23202, 'Locally finite Fixed points of Branching Brownian Motion'] Let $(p_{i})_{i\in I}$ be the atoms of a Poisson point process $\mathcal P$ with intensity measure $e^{-\mu x}dx$. For any choice of $z\in \mathbb R$ and $\epsilon>0$, there exist $t_{0}>0, \delta >0$ such that for all $t > t_{0}$, 
