{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:22:01.670972+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_572df849f641557be4ff6cab179636849c23c63ddc95d275bcbbee9baf24395d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2605.02226, 'Finitely Dependent Processes on Subshifts'] For $ m \in \mathbb{N}$, an element $x \in \{ 0,1\}^{G}$ is called an $ \mathbf{m}$-\textbf{net} (with respect to distance $d$ on $G$) if the set $ \{ g \in G: x_g =1\}$ is a maximal $m$-separated set. In other words, it is
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $m$-covering i.e. for every $ g \in G$ there exists $h\in G$ such that $ d(g,h) \leq m$ and $x_h= 1$, and
    \item $ m$-separated i.e. for every $ g $ with $x_g = 1 $ and $ h $ such that $ d(g, h) \leq m$ we have $ x_{h}=0$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:14:57.718782+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_57333469eb272560ba4f37fc1ef676c73deaf800a61e038d9fe93f17ec1bd0e6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:covariance_inequality of arXiv:2605.30999, 'Functional central limit theorems for $U$-statistics of $\beta$-mixing data'] For each $m\geqslant 2$, there exists a constant $C_m$ such that if  $\pr{S,\mathcal{S}}$ is a measurable space, $\left(X_i\right)_{i\in\mathbb Z}$ is a strictly stationary sequence taking   $h\colon S^m\to \mathbb R$ is a canonical kernel such that $\sup_{x_1,\dots,x_m\in S}\left|h\left(x_1,\dots,x_m\right)\right|\leqslant R$ and $N\geqslant m$, then 
 \begin{align}
     \E{\pr{U_{m,N+a}\left(h\right)-U_{m,a}\left(h\right)}^2}&
     \leqslant C_{m} \left(N+a\right)^{ m-1 } N\pr{1+\sum_{k=1}^{N+a}k^{m-1} 
      \beta\left(k\right) }R^2,\\
     \E{\max_{m\leqslant n\leqslant N}\pr{U_{m,n}\left(h\right)   }^2    }
     &\leqslant C_mN^{m }\left(\log  N\right)^2\pr{1+\sum_{k=1}^Nk^{m-1}
      \beta\left(k\right) }R^2.
 \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:58.358456+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5739f1a2e02518d576461f8bd0fec717706adb9092d487e3135623544e863d3f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 11 of arXiv:2506.18834, '\large\bf On the random-time and finite-time ruin probability for widely dependent claim s'] In a nonstandard renewal risk model,
let $Z_i,\ i\ge1$ be WLOD random variables with dominating coefficients $g_{L,H}(n),\ n\ge1$.
