\end{eqnarray} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:58:01.571057+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_573adf5acbc0836a3788666d18eac20b3a2473db0ae023f50260686821b0cb1a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2608.27307, '2608.27307'] Under Assumption~\ref{ass:basic}, there exists a constant $c_1>0$ such that, uniformly for $z\in\mb D(\tau,\eta_0)$, the following estimates hold.
