{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.365066+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_57538ef538647c470c4fe61e9c8749134b03cbb2c353cbed95eea1fd5c95eea4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:sep2 of arXiv:2606.02472, 'Correlated uniform attachment trees'] If $\bclr{T_n^{1}, T_n^{2} }_{n\in \N}$ is distributed according to the measure $\alpha{\text -}\mathrm{CUA}$, then for all $\varepsilon>0$ there exist $m,K,\ell \in \N$ such that for all $n \geq m$
