{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.745513+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_580c10ce2c263b576fd196f296b435a2f2fa3850561bab9342e0ef92b008172e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main-vector-exact-fourier-dimension of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] Assume that the dyadic vector-weight law is energy-admissible. Let \(\mu\) be the limiting dyadic vector-weight cascade measure on \([0,1]\), and set \(M=\mu([0,1])\). Then, almost surely on \(\{M>0\}\),
