{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:31:49.843915+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58a82a350a57fe2a166c1d3e85d91c951dddfad82f5332894d9a189298c5df90","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conjecture conj:transition of arXiv:2608.23742, 'Second-order fusion asymptotics for $\Sine_\beta$ correlation functions'] Let $R_{\beta,m}(\varepsilon;a)$ denote the bracketed normalized fusion factor in (equation eq:main of the paper). Then the first correction changes type at $m\beta=1$:
