{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:28:53.671855+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58a884e230bb0e598bb79744346abad305775da4d438954f7a867cbe3da92300","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 (sticky resolvent kernel) of arXiv:2605.13648, 'Sticky CIR process with potential: invariant measure and exact sampling'] \label[lemma]{lem:sticky-resolvent}
The fundamental solutions of $(\alpha-\mathcal{L})f=0$ satisfying the
boundary condition~\eqref{eq:wentzell} are $f_\infty(x) = U(a,b,z_x)$
and
\begin{equation}
  f_0^{\rm sticky}(x) = M(a,b,z_x) + c_\mu\,U(a,b,z_x),
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}
  c_\mu = \frac{-\alpha}{\mu\,|\mathcal{W}| + \alpha U_0}.
\end{equation}
The sticky resolvent kernel is
\[
  G^{\rm sticky}_\alpha(x,y) =
  \frac{f_0^{\rm sticky}(x\wedge y)\,f_\infty(x\vee y)}{|\mathcal{W}|},
\]
with the same normalisation constant $|\mathcal{W}|$ as the reflecting
resolvent kernel.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:23:05.283631+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58b3d7e27e17276434dfb57c764cffd450397ed0f20ad276b315e9ea426cab18","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 8 (Information maximality of the complete low-width prefix) of arXiv:2608.21496, '2608.21496'] Consider any finite family of reliability-mean audits whose kernels are randomized mixtures of widths at most $m$,
\begin{equation}
a_\ell=\sum_{n=1}^m q_{\ell n}k_n,
\qquad q_{\ell n}\ge0,
\quad \sum_{n=1}^m q_{\ell n}=1,

\end{equation}
and let $S_A=\Span\{a_\ell\}$. Its worst-case ambiguity at width $N>m$ is
\begin{equation}
\dist_{L^1}(k_N,S_A)\ge B_{m,N}.

\end{equation}
Equality is attained by the complete prefix $k_1,\ldots,k_m$. The same lower bound holds for a sequential schedule that chooses each such mean audit after earlier audit means are observed. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:19:56.677587+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58ba256641e285e3cfad360761596ac39a507bfa2dc6386abd2572cc07649c85","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 24 of arXiv:2608.30875, 'A Decomposition Theorem for Topological Semi-small Maps'] Let $A \xrightarrow{\alpha} D \xrightarrow{\beta} C \xrightarrow{h} A[1]$ be a distinguished triangle in the derived category $\mathcal{D}$ of an abelian category $\mathcal{A}$. Let $n \in \mathbb{Z}$ and suppose:
       	\begin{enumerate}
       		\item $\mathcal{H}^i(A) = 0$ for all $i \le n-1$ (hence $A \in \mathcal{D}^{\ge n}$);
       		\item The induced morphism on cohomology $h^{n-1} : \mathcal{H}^{n-1}(C) \longrightarrow \mathcal{H}^{n}(A)$ is zero, and the morphism $h^n:\mathcal{H}^{n}(C) \longrightarrow \mathcal{H}^{n+1}(A)$ is an isomorphism;
       		\item $\mathcal{H}^i(D) = 0$ for all $i > n$ (hence $D \in \mathcal{D}^{\le n}$).
       	\end{enumerate}
       	Then there is an isomorphism in the derived category
       	\begin{align*}
         D \simeq \tau_{\le n}A \;\oplus\; \tau_{\le n-1}C .
       \end{align*}
       	In particular $\tau_{\le n}A \simeq \mathcal{H}^n(A)[-n]$, so $D \simeq \mathcal{H}^n(A)[-n] \oplus \tau_{\le n-1}C.$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:42:55.312927+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58bbc65d0d23b2c3c56309581065005d8e2bff7c14f77409006bfd882980c063","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 5 of arXiv:2609.02398, '\textbf{Convex Order Comparisons for Sub-Gamma Random Variables}'] Let $p \in (0,1)$ and $\nu > 0$, and suppose that the two-point variable $Y$ with law $p\,\delta_{(1-p)\nu} + (1-p)\,\delta_{-p\nu}$ belongs to $\SE(\sigma^2,\alpha)$. Then
