{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:53.184576+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58d99a3734f54e80d87cc8ceaa146359c9bd22281dbe0c9a9639acfab0e9ed13","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2606.30349, 'Attenuated Poisson Dirichlet approximations for divisibility configurations'] Let $J_n$ be uniformly distributed on $\{1,\dots,n\}$ and let
\begin{align*}
P_1(J_n) \ge P_2(J_n) \ge \cdots \ge P_{K_n}(J_n)
\end{align*}
denote the prime factors of $J_n$, counted with multiplicity and arranged in decreasing order, where $K_n$ is the number of prime factors of $J_n$ counted with multiplicity. Define the random measure
\begin{align*}
\mathcal{X}_n
:=
\sum_{k=1}^{K_n}\delta_{\log P_k(J_n)/\log n}.
\end{align*}
Then $\mathcal{X}_n$ converges in law to a Poisson-Dirichlet distribution. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:06:07.089948+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58db880284c6a4ee12783c2cf5a2c078c055f7b0654e80418c91c200df79fb06","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 19 of arXiv:2608.28148, 'Flows and homotopies of Banach Lie algebroids'] For a bundle morphism $\Psi\colon A\to A'$ between Banach Lie algebroids over $\psi\colon M\to M'$ denote by $\psi^\ast A'$ the pull-back of $A'$ over $M$,
