{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:04:40.950423+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_58fb08f6bc9136537fcd9f7f47d1461a3ba3902b1bda05db57a706d3d305cf2a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem T:biane of arXiv:2412.03521, 'On ergodic properties of stochastic PDEs'] {biane:86:relations}}]
    Let $e = \{e_{\tau}; \tau \in [0,1]\}$ be a 3-$d$ Bessel bridge, and let
    $\zeta$ be a random variable uniformly distributed on $[0,1]$ and
    independent of $e$. Consider a process $\beta = \{\beta_{\tau} ; \tau \in
    [0,1]\}$ defined by
    \begin{align*}
      \beta_{\tau} \coloneqq e_{\tau \oplus \zeta} - e_{\zeta}, \quad \text{with $\tau \oplus \zeta \coloneqq \tau + \zeta\; ({\rm mod}\ 1)$.}
    \end{align*}
    Then $\beta $ is a 1-$d$ Brownian bridge. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:07.257653+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5911cf24d661726940551152bcda76d6b22642a6865c4eee02779755087129d1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2604.19308, '\textbf{On McKean--Vlasov SDEs with polynomial drifts for SIS epidemic models}'] Let~\eqref{co:6} and~\eqref{eq:integrability condition} hold for $\rho > 0$ and $I$ be a positive solution to~\eqref{eq:SIS epidemic model} that admits a measurable locally integrable function $u\colon\R_{+}\rightarrow\R$ such that
