{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.246117+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_59b1ada6cb18178650fa17de7a777ef492acae2f68893e0d6c31404f7388f359","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 22 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] Let $D$ be an open bounded subset of $\mathbb R^2$ with piecewise smooth boundary, let  $f_1,f_2:\partial D\mapsto \mathbb R$ be such that $\Adm(D;f_1),\Adm(D;f_2)\ne\emptyset$ and let $\phi_1,\phi_2$ be the associated limit shapes. Then, it holds:
