{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.989434+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5acadb6fd1dee35881b12c4f95db9d0eb72d4a29b84735fd2f38ac6e0aec6235","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm cokernel distribution theorem 1 of arXiv:2505.11700, 'Distribution of the cokernels of determinantal row-sparse matrices'] Let $G$ be a finite abelian group and $\mathcal{P}$ be a finite set of primes including those dividing $|G|$. 
Assume that a sequence $(k_n)_{n=1}^{\infty}$ satisfies the following:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item for every prime $p$ in $\mathcal{P}$, $p \nmid k_n$ for all sufficiently large $n$;
    \item for every $\epsilon>0$, $k_n < n^{\epsilon}$ for all sufficiently large $n$;
    \item if $2 \in \mathcal{P}$, then for every $\delta>0$, $\delta \log\log n < k_n$ for all sufficiently large $n$.
\end{enumerate}
Then
$$
\lim_{n\to \infty} \mathbb{P}\left(\bigoplus_{p \in \mathcal{P}} \mathrm{cok}(A_n)_p \cong G\right) = \frac{1}{|\mathrm{Aut}(G)|}\prod_{p\in \mathcal{P}} \prod_{i=1}^\infty (1-p^{-i})
= \prod_{p \in \mathcal{P}} \nu_{\mathrm{CL}, p}(G_p).
$$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:42.312101+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5ad4b3a85e357ce9ca530a9874fac7756a97663d29ee3909acf5fe4e2bd519eb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 18 of arXiv:2608.05931, 'Effective Lagrangian regularity and the uniqueness threshold for random H\"older velocity '] Fix $\alpha\in(0,1)$, $\lambda>0$, and $p\geq 1$, and let, for all $j\geq 0$, $u^j$ be defined by~\eqref{eq:autonomous poisson}. Suppose there exists $M\geq 1$ such that for all $j\geq 0$, $n\in\{0,1,2\}$, and $y\in\T^d,$
\[\|\nabla^n f^j_y\|_{L^p_\omega C^0_x}\leq M 2^{(n-\alpha-d/p)j}.\]
Then 
\begin{enumerate}
    \item the $u^j$ are mutually independent with $\E u^j =0$,
\item for each $j\geq 1$, $u^j$ has a finite spatial range of dependence $2^{-j}$,
\item and there exists a constant $C(d)>0$ such that for all $j\geq 0$ and $n\in\{0,1,2\}$,
\[\|\nabla^n u^j\|_{L^p_\omega C^0_x}\leq CM(\lambda+p)2^{(n-\alpha)j}.\]
\end{enumerate}
Letting $U:=\sum_{j= 0}^\infty u^j$, we further have that
\begin{enumerate}
    \item[(i)] if for all $j\geq 0$ and $y\in\T^d$, $\nabla\cdot f^j_y=0$, then $\nabla\cdot U=0$,
    \item[(ii)] if there exists $r\in(0,1)$ and $C>0$ such that for all $j\geq 0$
    \begin{equation}
    \sup_{\substack{x,y\in\T^d\\d_{\T^d}(x,y)\leq 2^{-(j+2)}}}\bigg\|\frac{d\mu^j_{y,x}(z)}{dz}\bigg\|_{L^\infty(\R^d)}\leq Cr^j e^{\lambda j},
    \end{equation}
    then it almost surely holds that for all $\alpha'<\alpha$
    \[\lim_{\eps\rightarrow 0} \eps^{-\alpha'd}|Z_\eps|=0,\]
    where $Z_\eps$ is defined as in~\eqref{eq:zero sets}.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.413119+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5ae1ddbf907d95279024b24836e700d4a8704f8d21d26d477d1e82bb82f1b490","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 64 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Let $\nu^1,\nu^2$ be two nonnegative measures that are absolutely continuous of bounded density on $\amsmathbb{A}$, and as before, $\boldsymbol{\nu}^{1},\boldsymbol{\nu}^{2}$ the corresponding $H$-tuple of measures. We introduce
