{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:52:57.740818+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5aeb79ed735c95d5d02444e1b3c579e6ae241657124361eb811edab1f3fd6bc3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 48 of arXiv:2609.02755, 'The Sharp Rate of Probabilistically Strong Convergence to the KPZ Equation'] One has that $f \in \mcB_{2,2}^0$ if and only if $f \in L_\mathrm{loc}^2$. Furthemore, for every compact set $\mfK$, 
