for all sufficiently small $\lambda>0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:03:39.772352+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5b4d049b9734ced30c43e3da09155eb5130767ce2d9540b5e9b0fcaa2a18bc2a","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:recursion-fnk-new of arXiv:2411.03065, 'Growing conditioned BGW trees with\\ log-concave offspring distributions'] The arrays $(F^s_{n,k})_{n,k\geq0}$ corresponding to adjacent values of $s\in\{0,\dots,d-1\}$ are linked by the following relations:
	\begin{align}
	F^s_{n,k}
	&=\sum_{j\geq 0}W_{j} \,F^{s-1}_{n,k+j},
	\qquad &&s\in\{1,\dots,d-1\},\\
	F^0_{n,k}
	&=\sum_{j\geq 0}W_{j} \,F^{d-1}_{n-1,k+j-1},
	\qquad &&s=0,
	\end{align}
	for all $s,n,k$ such that $nd+s\geq 2$ and $kd+s\geq1$.
	To give sense to (equation eq:relation-fnk-different-s-new of the paper) when $s=1$ and $k=0$, we make the convention that $F^0_{n,0}=0$ for all $n\geq1$.","status":"unverified"}

