{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:09:43.681571+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5c2390ea9f12ebaa8d11e3f42ca4615653391aabe8411c30b732faa7b49ab1c4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma p:ssmsingle-wsm of arXiv:2605.28430, 'Limit theory for Lipschitz-localized statistics in random geometric models'] If  the function \(\mathcal{A}'_{\Psi({\cal X })}\) satisfies
