where $ y(\cdot) $ is the solution to  (eqInversPParabolicPartialBoudaryeqNew of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.454819+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5c5a892a45ed8e611502374ae48516462d2954e6bd37ad634db7f39d78701787","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 4 of arXiv:2609.02516, 'Power convexity of the torsion function on horo-convex domains in hyperbolic space'] Let $n\geq 2$, and let $\Omega\subset\mathbb{H}^n$ be contained in a geodesic ball $B_R$ of radius $R>0$. If $u_\Omega$ is the torsion function of $\Omega$ and $v_\Omega=-\sqrt{u_\Omega}$, then $$-\frac{R}{\sqrt{n}}<v_\Omega<0\quad\mathrm{in}\ \Omega.$$ In particular, if $R\leq 1/(2\sqrt{n})$, then
\begin{equation}
-\frac{1}{2n}<v_\Omega<0\quad\mathrm{in}\ \Omega.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.763932+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5c6454be73ce29f4ae27087879d94cabd89a67f2a61be222687abc8b8b181006","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma l5.1 of arXiv:2411.19255, 'Moderate, large and super large deviations principles for Poisson process with uniform cat'] For any $x,y\in \mathbb{Z}^+$ there exist random processes $\tilde{\xi}(t)$ and $\hat{\xi}(t)$
such that $\tilde{\xi}(t)\stackrel{d}{=}\xi_x(t)$, $\hat{\xi}(t)\stackrel{d}{=}\xi_y(t)$, and the following equality holds
\begin{equation} 
 \mathbf{P}\left(\sup\limits_{t\geq 0}|\tilde{\xi}(t)-\hat{\xi}(t)|\leq|x-y|\right)=1.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:31:02.824024+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5c668b49e63dbfb41e091b4abb61852c4bbcb230bd183d16ace62a4117c80535","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:farey-sixth-order of arXiv:2609.01690, 'Iterated-sumset spectra: The complete exponent law and its rank geometry'] For each integer $N\geq1$, let $\mathrm{FV}(N)$ be the number of distinct
intersections of Farey lines of order $(N,N)$, and let $\mathrm{FR}(N)$ be
the number of connected regions into which those lines cut the open unit
square.  Then, as $N\to\infty$,
\begin{equation}
 \mathrm{FV}(N)=\Theta(N^6),\qquad
 \mathrm{FR}(N)=\Theta(N^6).
\end{equation}
The lower bound for $\mathrm{FV}(N)$ already comes from intersections in
the open triangle $0<x<y<1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:29:14.964956+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5c68d17f71bace26094e3a5d8b34fae3531ea6dea1b1ba5da6982afb9bd268e0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:com_tim of arXiv:2606.14895, 'Effective Resistances and Commute Times in Sparse Random Geometric Graphs'] For any $u,v\in V$, the commute time $C_{uv}$ between $u$ and $v$ satisfies
\begin{equation*}
C_{uv} = \mathrm{Vol}(G) (\vec{\mathbf{1}}_u-\vec{\mathbf{1}}_v)^\top \mathbf{L}^+(\vec{\mathbf{1}}_u-\vec{\mathbf{1}}_v) = \mathrm{Vol}(G) \left({L}^+_{uu} + {L}^+_{vv} - 2{L}^+_{uv}\right) \,.
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.778943+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5c82de37e2f27477f9b10e02cd7e0668294400c69b379d83b13fce1a16b49c1f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2603.25615, 'Fourier dimension of Mandelbrot cascades on planar curves'] For some $p >4$, let $\Phi(t)\lesssim t^{-p}$ when $t \geq 1$. Let $X_1,\ldots, X_N$ be independent random variables with zero expectation such that
\begin{equation}
\PP(X_k>t)\le\Phi(t)    
\end{equation}
for all $1\le k\le N$. Then, for all $a_1,a_2,\ldots a_N\ge 0$, $M>1$, and $t>0$,
\[\PP\left(\sum_{k=1}^N a_k X_k>t\right)=N\Phi(M)+\exp\left(-\lambda t+O(\lambda^2)\sum_{k=1}^N a_k^2\right)\,,\]
where 
\begin{equation}
    \lambda=\frac{q\log M}{M\max_{1\le k\le N}a_k}\,.
\end{equation}
and $q\leq p/2-1$. The $O$-constant only depends on $p$ and $\Phi$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:09.856448+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5c8cfe2d48036f25afaa0c88de485380d978db0722fee8ba412ca39e58948640","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 16 of arXiv:2605.20115, 'Moment bounds on correctors for the degenerate random conductance model'] There exist $C_0,C_1,C_2\ge1$ depending only on $\Lambda$, such that for $C_2\le p\le C_1^{-1}\gamma$, the (stationary) corrector gradient satisfies
\begin{equation}
\expecb{\Big((\nabla\phi+e)\cdot A(\nabla\phi+e)\Big)^p}^\frac1p\,\lesssim_{\Lambda}\, (p\gamma\Gamma)^{C_0}.
