{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:55:27.268692+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5cdc0f6380a4b819620593c0479d28833c78a02e432997af1785e8b56479ac82","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition S62P of arXiv:2410.23899, 'Tightness for interlacing geometric random walk bridges'] As $N \rightarrow \infty$, the sequence $\mathcal{L}^N$ converges weakly to some $\mathbb{N}$-indexed line ensemble $\mathcal{L}^{\infty}$ on $\mathbb{R}$, which satisfies the partial Brownian Gibbs property from [DM21]. Moreover, if $\mathcal{L}^{a,b,c}$ is as in [ED24a] for $\{a_i^+\}_{i \geq 1}, \{b_i^+\}_{i \geq 1}$ and $c^+$ as in the present statement, and $J_a^- = J_b^- = c^- = 0$, then
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{L}^{a,b,c} = \{f_q^{1/2} \cdot \mathcal{L}_i^{\infty}(f_q^{-1}t): i \in \mathbb{N}, t \in \mathbb{R}\},
\end{equation}
where the equality is in distribution as random elements in $C(\mathbb{N} \times \mathbb{R})$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:37:08.954752+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5cdee02f8478233652c932aa06eca3bc9691024d9af44e43ef823207307c7839","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:db_subgaussian of arXiv:2609.01581, 'Concentration of additive functionals of Stratonovich-type'] Let assumptions of Theorem~(thm:conc_current of the paper) hold
