{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.573811+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5d66d549e3d236304cb44ed996aaa31da6881fe10b0bfe77c3894da4323cbfaf","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 33 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d\geq 2$.
	There exists a  constant $K=K(d)>0$ such that the following holds. For every  $\Lambda\subset \mathbb Z^d$ finite containing $0$, and every $1-e^{-\beta_c}\leq p'<p \leq p_c$,
