{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:32:23.686970+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5f57b7a7f59a9514cd1555fd8177fc88e4abfbb0e2c89214e9be240f98110986","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop SSMestimateFixedk of arXiv:2603.17858, 'Decay of correlations and zeros for the hard-core model'] Let $\lambda^\star>0$. For each $k\in\mathbb{N}$, there exists
