{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:35:04.215016+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5fd2bdc97ac87f9e2ae6cb9a2762603239b3a28073206a09454249d4171fbdba","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 23 of arXiv:2608.03956, 'From Triangular Array Progression\\ to Near-Log-Concave State Transitions'] Let $n^*$ be defined as in (\ref{smallestnsatisfy}) for every $n\geq 1$. For any $\mathbf{\lambda} = [\lambda_1,\lambda_2,...] \in \mathcal{Q}$, define $\T^{(1)}(\mathbf{\lambda})$ as follows:
\begin{equation}

\T^{(1)}_{n,j}(\lambda_n) =
\begin{cases}
