{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:46:36.095946+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_5ff6b3f29a4abe4920cf915ae0fe9082b8f6d1e5e02c09f647bdf746eb31d666","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem133 of arXiv:2609.02795, 'Global smooth behavior in Kuznetsov and Westervelt type\\ viscous wave equations:\\ A unif'] Assume ((h of the paper)), ((f0 of the paper)) and ((f1 of the paper)) with some $\lambda>1$, let $p\ge 2$ be such that $p>n$, 
  and let $r\ge p$ be such that $r\ge\lambda$.
  Then there exist $\Gamma_8=\Gamma_8(p,r,a,h,f)>0$ as well as
  $\mu_1=\mu_1(f)>1$ and $\mu_2=\mu_2(h,f)>1$
  such that if ((init of the paper)) holds and ((uut of the paper)) is valid with some $T\in (0,T_{max}]$, then
  \begin{eqnarray}\label{133.1}
	& & \hspace*{-30mm}
	\bigg\{ \int_\Omega |u|\cdot |f(u,u_t,\nabla u,\nabla u_t)| \bigg\}^\frac{p}{2}
