\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.718446+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_607da47b4aea1576b10a83260c3865c6b35507c95bf4a23ca1bfd3dd2c8ac8e8","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem intersection.twodifferent of arXiv:2411.19145, 'On the intersection of critical percolation clusters and other tree-like random graphs'] Let $\mathcal G$ and $\widetilde{\mathcal G}$ two random graphs on the same metric space $(V,d_V)$, satisfying both the BK inequality, and respectively~(equation Halpha of the paper) and $(\mathcal H_\beta)$, for some $\alpha,\beta \in(\frac{d}{2},d)$, with $\alpha\le \beta$, and $2\alpha + 2\beta > 3d$. Let $\mathcal C_0$ and $\widetilde{\mathcal C}_0$ the clusters of the origin in $\mathcal G$ and $\widetilde{\mathcal G}$ respectively. There exsits a constant $\kappa>0$, such that 
\begin{equation}
\mathbb E\Big[\exp\big(\kappa\cdot  |\mathcal C_0\cap \widetilde{\mathcal C}_0|^\gamma\big)\Big]<\infty, \quad \textrm{with}\  
\gamma = \frac{2\alpha - d}{d+ 2\alpha - 2\beta}.
