If \eqref{eq:diag.criterion} holds with the opposite inequality, then \eqref{eq:diag.criterion.forms} also holds with the opposite inequality.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:34:20.714741+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_60867c6ab684de620ff84696f1a30f6ec2f93c60465c970088ac7fe59c45cf1c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 13 (CondSOC Gibbs identity) of arXiv:2609.02196, 'Schr\"odinger Bridges on Lie Group Manifolds for Probabilistic Intrinsic Generation'] For a controlled law \(P^{z,\bm v}\) started at \(x_0\),
\begin{equation*}
\mathcal J_{z,\varepsilon}(\bm v)
=\E_{P^{z,\bm v}}\left[
\frac12\int_0^T\norm{\bm v_t}^2\,\dd t
+\ell_{\varepsilon,y}(X_T)\right]
\end{equation*}
satisfies
\begin{equation}
\mathcal J_{z,\varepsilon}(\bm v)+\log Z_{z,\varepsilon}
=\KL(P^{z,\bm v}\|Q^{z,\varepsilon}).
\end{equation}
If \(\bm v^{z,\varepsilon}\) is the Doob control of \(Q^{z,\varepsilon}\), then
\begin{equation}
\mathcal J_{z,\varepsilon}(\bm v)-\mathcal J_{z,\varepsilon}(\bm v^{z,\varepsilon})
=\frac12\E_{P^{z,\bm v}}\int_0^T
\norm{\bm v_t-\bm v_t^{z,\varepsilon}(X_t)}^2\,\dd t.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:39:41.441323+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6088d73735b3a69d107d628a33a030687d1e8d2cebc4c639fe642805f9e3c713","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2604.07478, 'Mixing Times and Cutoff for the Rook's Walk'] Let $t_\text{mix}(\epsilon)$ with $\epsilon >0$ be the mixing time of the Rook's Walk with dimension $d$ and board-length $n$. Then,
      \begin{multline*}
