{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:48:00.184472+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_60da6528d34a5e323ab88a07f3fa1be155d146ed5da4a4976fcf3ef1aeef8c82","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Pro FourierHilbert of arXiv:2609.02882, 'A new proof that more than $2/3$ of the zeros of the Riemann zeta function are simple and '] Let $\lambda>0$ be a real number and $\eta\in L^2(\mathbb{R})$ be a real valued even function with $\textup{supp} (\eta) \subset (-\lambda, \lambda) $, such that $\widehat{\eta^2}(0)=1$. Let $\mathcal{Z}$ be a non-empty finite multiset of complex numbers which is invariant under complex
conjugation. For $z\in \mathcal{Z}$ we let $m_z$ be its multiplicity in $\mathcal{Z}$.  Then we have 
\begin{equation}
