{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.093541+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_610af49d99dbc34986c2a9206041e93015a77bc58c70f20a0a43605683f86a73","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop manytoone-lebesgue-Addi of arXiv:2411.12717, 'Excursion theory for Markov processes indexed by Lévy trees'] Fix $r \geq 0$. For every non-negative measurable function $\Phi$ on $\mathcal{M}^2_f(\mathbb{R}_+) \times \mathcal{W}_{\overline{E}}$, we have:
\begin{align}
     & \mathbb{N}_{x,r}^{ \bullet, A } \big(  \Phi\big( \rho_U,\eta_U, \overline{W}_U\big)  \big)  
  =   E^0 \otimes \Pi_{x,r} \Big(   \int_r^\infty {\mathrm{d}} a \, \exp\big(- \alpha \tau_{a}\big)\Phi( \mathcal{J}_{\tau_{a}}, \widecheck{\mathcal{J}}_{\tau_{a}} , \bar{\xi}^{\tau_{a}} )  \Big).
