Furthermore, under $\mathbb{N}_{x,r}^{ \bullet, A }$, conditionally on $(\rho_U,\eta_U, \overline{W}_U)$, the
processes $(\rho,W)^{U,\leftarrow}$ and  $(\rho,W)^{U,\rightarrow}$ are independent and their  conditional laws are as follows:
