{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.748735+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_61a554551eae23f0bad37b71633cf7efa673d6f3277e3aa2b135cb89730f206d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:sol_gen_MKV of arXiv:2608.30493, '\bf McKean-Vlasov Differential Equations:\\ {An introduction and a focus on some kinetic m'] A (general) solution to MKV$({\bf b},{\boldsymbol\sigma})$ is a triple $( W, (\mathcal{F}_t)_t, X)$ which is a (general) solution to SDE$({\bf b}_{\boldsymbol\mu},{\boldsymbol\sigma}_{\boldsymbol\mu};0)$ (see Definition (def:sol_gen_SDE of the paper)), where ${\bf b}_{\boldsymbol\mu},{\boldsymbol\sigma}_{\boldsymbol\mu}$ are as in (equation eq:def_frozen_coeff of the paper) with
