{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.614774+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_61c5613955f1f7bdeaa7b69b10b9399ebfd104e7181ed0d5a91fa9d27b603f1e","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 11 (Transition rate) of arXiv:2506.09462, 'Transition Path Theory For L\'{e}vy-Type Processes: SDE Representation and Statistics'] The \textbf{$AB$ transition rate} \(k_{AB}\) is defined as:  
    \begin{equation*}
        k_{AB} = \lim_{T \to \infty} \frac{\mathrm{N}_T}{T},
    \end{equation*}
    which quantifies the rate of transitions from \(A\) to \(B\). Additionally, the limits:  
    \begin{equation*}
        T_{AB} := \lim_{\mathrm{N} \to \infty} \frac{1}{\mathrm{N}} \sum_{n=0}^{\mathrm{N}-1} (\tau_{B,n+1}^+ - \tau_{A,n}^+),
    \end{equation*}
    and  
    \begin{equation*}
        T_{BA} := \lim_{\mathrm{N} \to \infty} \frac{1}{\mathrm{N}} \sum_{n=0}^{\mathrm{N}-1} (\tau_{A,n+1}^+ - \tau_{B,n}^+),
    \end{equation*}
    are called the \textbf{expected transition times} from \(A \to B\) and \(B \to A\), respectively.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.285531+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_61d4b464737861b18a4335e455b26f7331cc98b4bda8fda4b6e68149c6251cc9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conjecture conj:quenched formula of arXiv:2604.20660, 'The Legendre structure of the TAP complexity\\ for the Ising spin glass'] Define
