{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.578651+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6223e15502de4f1aa5a298a6e39b8971efe0609cd66d12d875d66f7e841b9a6c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 51 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] There exists $K_1>0$ such that, for every $n\geq 1$,
