{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.440805+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_631d9c2cfd5ce509f31cafe299e786b554a78423f8be2e99b5c01f46b63688ea","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:F=tildeF of arXiv:2508.17838, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices'] Given  any fixed diagram $\Gamma$ with or without open edges, if all $n_j \gg t_N$ for $j=1,\ldots, s$,    and $\| A_N\|_{\mathrm{op}} \le 1+\tau n^{-1}$ with  $n=\sum_{j=1}^s n_j$,  for any fixed integer $s\geq 1$  and     constant   $\tau >0$,  then  
