{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.714120+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_634b026550d39516962ad38e93085d43beabaa26f49e3195265d9577af896eaa","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem thinning of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] For each $n \geq 1$, let ${\rm Y}_n$ be a random subset of ${\rm D}_n$ which is $L_{t^A_n}({\rm D}_n)$-measurable. Given $u \geq 0$, define the sets ${\rm Z}_n(u):={\rm W}_n(u) \cap {\rm Y}_n$, ${\rm X}_n(u+1):={\rm S}_n(u+1) \cap {\rm Y}_n$ and 
	\begin{equation}
		\mathbb{Z}_n(u):=\{ z \in \mathbb{X}_{n-r_n} : {\rm Z}_n(u) \cap {\rm Q}(z;n-r_n) \neq \emptyset\}.
