{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:09:23.956746+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_63d6a42ab1db564ce30403415f0cdd8a5a22d8ef57dbabcc4850f52fcba3b5e9","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 1 of arXiv:2607.21931, 'Lorenz and convex ordering of parasite burden distributions with density-dependent deaths'] The {\em Lorenz curve} $L: [0,1] \to [0,1] $ for the distribution $F$ on $[0,\infty)$ with finite mean $ \mu$ is given by
    \begin{equation*}
