{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:42:16.238646+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_64d68950c2d3f3a810c546c091602130e9300d2e4646a2f83a7007b933828eee","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem subcritical case theo 2 of arXiv:2607.00731, 'Sharp Asymptotics for the Largest Component in the Subcritical Regime of Preferential Atta'] Assume that \(\alpha=\alpha(n)\to a\in(0,\infty]\), and set $m_c=\frac{\alpha n}{2(\alpha+1)}.$ If \(m=\lfloor m_c(1-\varepsilon)\rfloor\), \(\varepsilon=\varepsilon(n)=o(1)\), and
