 for all $n\in\mathbb{N}$, $x_1,\ldots,x_n\in I$ and $t_1,\ldots,t_n\in[0,1]$ satisfying $t_1+\cdots +t_n=1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.752554+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_657fbf01cc6df4d56c58c2a92622688317f6fe6129545a13ed4e5ba3cd6ef866","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:local-mass-good-events-paper of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] There exist constants \(C<\infty\) and \(c>0\) such that, for all \(n\ge1\),
