{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:03:39.775009+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_65861f2aa08b72c5bef31646412629bd6d997cc1b3f73a769824012f6db5323d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor TP2-forests-partition-function of arXiv:2411.03065, 'Growing conditioned BGW trees with\\ log-concave offspring distributions'] If ${\mathbf{w}}$ is log-concave, then the array $(\PFforests{{\mathbf{w}}}{n,k})_{n,k\geq1}$ is TP2, that is
