{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:38:23.573776+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_65be4187dff1b11d87784982a9d9d9f5749f48a1c611b43c925e6f929cb97339","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:sharpness-local of arXiv:2511.01851, 'Percolation on graphs of polynomial growth is local:\\analyticity, supercritical sharpness'] Let $\mathscr{G}\in\mathfrak{G}$ and $p_0\in (p_c(\mathscr{G}),1]$. Then, there is a constant $c>0$ such that the set of all $\mathscr{H}\in\mathfrak{G}$ satisfying $p_c(\mathscr{H})<p_0$ and the following condition is a neighbourhood of $\mathscr{G}$:
