{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:33:43.749276+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_66b6077fd5ed6c51733f722cf39e011af792e312f6862c069b3ad315f7f5fbfc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:equivalence_nonlinear_mp_weak_sol of arXiv:2608.30493, '\bf McKean-Vlasov Differential Equations:\\ {An introduction and a focus on some kinetic m'] Let $\nu\in\mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^d)$, and let $\mathbb{P}_{\nu}$ be a probability measure on $(C_{\infty}, \mathcal{B} )$, such that
