\end{align*}
and satisfies
\begin{align*}
&&
    \E[\Lap] &= 0, &
    \E[|\Lap|] &= 1, &
    \E\left[e^{\lambda \Lap}\right] &= \frac{1}{1 - \lambda^2}
    \quad (|\lambda| < 1). &
&\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:59:53.381942+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_66cf0416be9f923d15a361b3c04a5e99b1da850ca9887265085d08385b680058","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:largest-fragment-collision-proof of arXiv:2608.18320, 'Asymptotics for Beta-Splitting Trees via Homogeneous Fragmentations and Meromorphic Potent'] For every fixed $x\in\mathbb R$, put
