{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:26:02.534204+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_66dcbac7ee4da928fde1bfc8b8fee076d487e10e9bd618a3adb5f483654bc955","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn Order on fine slopes of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] We define a partial relation $\prec$ on generalized fine slopes generated by the following inequalities. First, for $s,t\in \mathbb{R} \cup \{\pm\infty\}$ we impose
    \begin{equation}
        s^\heartsuit \prec t^\diamondsuit
    \end{equation}
   when $s < t$ and $\heartsuit, \diamondsuit \in \{\natural, \flat, \sharp, \dagger\}$, and
    \begin{equation}
        s^\flat \prec s^\dagger \prec s^\sharp, \quad \text{and} \quad s^\dagger \prec s^\dagger.
    \end{equation}
    Second, we have 
    \begin{equation}
        -\infty^\dagger \prec \aleph^\natural, \aleph^\sharp \quad \mathrm{and} \quad
        \aleph^\natural, \aleph^\flat \prec +\infty^\dagger.
    \end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.714238+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_66e6fef4def5dbb41acf377ed884b8051a3576662c367127f11243d283e247fc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop rest3 of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] If $\gamma$ is chosen small enough, then, given any $0 < \eta' < \eta < \frac{1}{2}$ small enough \mbox{(depending only on $\gamma$),} for any fixed $u \geq 0$ we have
