{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.659265+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_67013fd8f5e6d8dea9bb9db6ada3314e444e14b14d7ba9bf968de8c5d0523c9e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 24 (Moment convergence) of arXiv:2607.24561, 'Range convergence and sharp one-arm asymptotics\\for the critical percolation cluster in h'] Assume \eqref{eq:2pt} and \eqref{eq:guiding-kp}. Then for every
$m\ge1$ and $\phi_1,\dots,\phi_m\in\Cc$,
