{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.328077+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_68450c6de5069250039fc0b93be8c46a5222f395f4fbe9271e73b055ed9ed444","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:fract_horiz_per of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] For $\alpha\in (0,1)$, the $\alpha$-\emph{fractional horizontal perimeter} of a measurable set $\Omega$ is defined as 
 \begin{align*}
     \operatorname{Per}^{(\alpha)}_\mathcal{H}(\Omega)=\int_{\Omega}\int_{\Omega^c} \frac{1}{\|x^{-1}y\|_\alpha}dx dy,
 \end{align*}
 where $\|\cdot\|_\alpha$ is a homogeneous quasi-norm defined by
 \begin{align}
    \|x\|_\alpha=(\widetilde{R}_\alpha(x))^{-\frac{1}{\alpha+Q}}, \quad \widetilde{R}_\alpha(x)=\frac{\alpha}{2\Gamma\left(1-\frac\alpha 2\right)}\int_0^\infty t^{-\frac{\alpha}{2}-1} p(t,x) dt
\end{align}
with $p(t,\cdot)$ being the hypoelliptic heat kernel defined in (equation eq:heat_kernel of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.989535+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6845dee3e0b64d8daea5909882e2f4e8cf77c6af31935406f9ad06d834cecec1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor of arXiv:2505.11700, 'Distribution of the cokernels of determinantal row-sparse matrices'] Suppose that the following hold: 
