Combining this with (equation t_eta of the paper), (equation im_m_t_sim_through_evolution of the paper), (equation largG_3G_1 of the paper), and (equation largG_3G_2 of the paper), we obtain that for all $t\in\left[{t_0,t_m}\right]$,
    \begin{equation}
        \begin{aligned}
            \left\|L_{(1,2,3), t}-K_{(1,2,3), t}\right\|_2 \prec \frac{N^{\varepsilon_g}}{N\left(t_c-t\right)^3\left(\operatorname{Im} m_t\right)^3} \ .
        \end{aligned}
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:46:36.095085+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6964d33ffb53e3b438562484adac51597e446c93f9f14a72aa1769f1ec51f8df","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lem3 of arXiv:2609.02795, 'Global smooth behavior in Kuznetsov and Westervelt type\\ viscous wave equations:\\ A unif'] Let $p\ge 2$ and $q\in [p,\frac{(n+2)p}{n}]$. Then there exists $C(p,q)>0$ such that
