{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:31:02.824498+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6979a73fc0fcc8778e3ec5a378f7bfd81f52326c0fed998d8bb079e83e1ad5de","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:rank-defect-frontier of arXiv:2609.01690, 'Iterated-sumset spectra: The complete exponent law and its rank geometry'] For $h\geq2$, $k\geq3$, and $0\leq r\leq k-2$,
