{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:07:56.710986+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6985ec8dd2da410d0e43d2c7bb973111f581795539abfcff1cec8794eb6663bb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition p:V adapted of arXiv:2411.04773, 'Meeting of squared Bessel flow lines and application to the skew Brownian motion'] (i) Almost surely, for any $r\ge 0$: for any $x \in [V(-r),z)$
