and $K_{\nua }$ is the modified Bessel function of the third kind 
(or Macdonald's function) of order $\nua $. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.300710+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_69c346f39a06511e479ff2d34e2b47690ea40f2a6bcc4bc3aab8154746f69d27","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop proba ineq decoupling map of arXiv:2604.21663, 'Large deviations for non-irreducible Markov chains on Euclidean spaces'] Let $W$ be a measurable set of $\mathcal W_{T_1}\times \mathcal W_{T_2}$ and let 
