{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.869913+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6af534e01a595c96b1a1c4a2b380e37bcd73edd7299508c7d2f65e8b6587ec7b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:te_full_prob_lw_bdd of arXiv:2605.06511, 'Logarithmic Mixing of Random Walks on Dynamical Random Cluster Models'] There exists a constant $C \in (0, 1)$ such that for all $n \in \mathbb{N}$ sufficiently large, with probability $1 - o_n(1)$ over $G \sim \mathcal{G}(d, n)$, for all $\mu \geq \varepsilon \log n $, and for every $S \subseteq V$ and $u \in V$ such that there exists $\alpha_{\min}, \alpha_{\max} \in \mathbb{N}$ and $\zeta \in (0, 1)$ satisfying the following:
		\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
			\item $({1}/{(50 \ p_{\min})}) \log_{d - 1} n \leq \alpha_{\min} < \alpha_{\max} \leq ({4}/{p_{\min}}) \log_{d - 1} n$ and $\alpha_{\max} - \alpha_{\min} \geq \frac{\log_{d-1} n}{100 \ p_{\min}}$
			\item for all $\alpha, h, i \in \mathbb{N}$ such that $\alpha \in [\alpha_{\min}, \alpha_{\max}]$, $h \in \left[\left((d - 2) / d\right) p_{\min} \alpha, \left((d - 2) / d\right) p_{\min} \left(\alpha + \sqrt{\alpha}\right)\right]$ and $i \in \left[(p_{\min} / d) \alpha, (p_{\min} / d) \left(\alpha + \sqrt{\alpha}\right)\right]$, there are at least $\zeta \ \widetilde{\omega}_{h, i}$ walks from $u$ to a vertex in $S$ which are $r$-acyclic and are $(h, i)$-constrained walks
		\end{enumerate}
		then for all $\eta \in \{0, 1\}^E$, $\mathbb{P} \left[X_{C_{\mathrm{burn}} + \frac{\alpha_{\max} + \alpha_{\min}}{2}} \in S \mid \left(\eta_0, X_0\right) = (\eta, u)\right] \geq C \zeta$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:01:39.423832+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6af76bb304bc16c24e89890e193683530bf047f192e5ae5772c6e4c9a94704ff","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:indicators of arXiv:2607.22291, 'Rare subtree patterns in size-conditioned Bienaymé trees: Poisson approximation and declum'] Let $G$ be a $ \{0,1\}$-valued function defined on the set of all finite plane trees. 
