{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:58:01.570365+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6b4788dc1db8b7c7a948bc619131c165fb9f63408d6b5a85db9eaed1d44863a0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 8 of arXiv:2608.27307, '2608.27307'] Under Assumptions~\ref{ass:basic} and~\ref{ass:rand_ent}, suppose that $E_+$ is a regular right edge in the sense of Definition~\ref{def:reg_r_edge}. Then, for every $x\in\R$,
