{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:32:29.000172+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6c122731b4f28e10e2b025db61cfb7284b828e14a253cb15df7cef57ff86b462","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop CT UB UT of arXiv:2608.25471, 'Exact Hausdorff measures and fine geometry of collisions of independent Markov processes'] For any $t \in (0, \infty)$ and $\lambda \in (0, \infty)$,
