{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:36:12.192488+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6cb0c157336484cde4cd42131b232ac9b434e4e66b00ee68a67a18410ba63144","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 (Gauss divisible case) of arXiv:2609.03924, 'Beyond normal fluctuations in local laws for Wigner matrices'] Assume the set-up \eqref{eq:OU_flow}--\eqref{eq:char_flow} and denote $X_t:=N\eta_t\langle G_t-m_t\rangle$ for $t\in [0,T]$. For any fixed $p,q\in\N\cup\{0\}$ with $p+q\ge 3$ it holds that
