{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.822563+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6cb87619b47dfe0310b0a65eb2f475a6e359d9bcd6e78f90e8eb03b818073d78","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor: duality of arXiv:2504.04792, 'Uniqueness and Longtime Behavior of the Completely Positively Correlated Symbiotic Branchi'] Let $\dot{W}$ and $\dot{W_0}$ be two independent white noises on $\mathbb{R}_+ \times \mathbb{R}$. Let $\psi \in C_{\text{tem}}^+$ and $\phi \in C_{\text{rap}}^+$. Define $(V_t)_{t \geq 0}$ and $(\Tilde{V}_t)_{t \geq 0}$ as the unique solutions with values in $C_{\text{tem}}^+$ and $C_{\text{rap}}^+$, respectively, of equation $((eq: dual of the paper))$, driven by $\dot{W}$ and $\dot{W_0}$, respectively, with initial conditions $V_0 = \psi$  and $\Tilde{V}_0 = \phi$. Then, for each $T > 0$, the following self-duality formula holds:
