{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.590932+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6cdb207ba7e05a0d0f96043f986050e56f250f010435a8d24ffd97f022d0ffba","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conjecture thm:convergence of arXiv:2606.03079, 'Mean Field Limits for Stochastic, Underdamped Reactive Langevin Dynamics Models'] The sequence of measure-valued processes $\{\mu^{\gamma, \ell}_t\}_{t\in [0, T]}\in \mathbb{D}_{M_F(\mathbb{R}^{d\times d})}[0, T]$, converge in law to $\{\bar{\mu}^\ell_t\}_{t\in [0, T]} \in C_{M_F(\mathbb{R}^{d\times d})}([0, T])$ for $\ell=1,2,3$, satisfying
{\small
\begin{align}
