{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.413081+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_6d9c2b1642c69c74f53dc5665dccd1072033b67868b24f896a642447d9fb9753","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:waterfall_LLN_intro of arXiv:2507.22011, 'Random Lozenge Waterfall:\\Dimensional Collapse of Gibbs Measures'] Assume that the side lengths of the hexagon, $a,b,c$,
