{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.083566+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_70557e4ea815dde9aace46c20df6bc8cecf655c1d40ac365e5a326b23c9e2149","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem DefStatewiseCondExpect0 of arXiv:2411.12522, 'Canonical insurance models: stochastic equations and comparison theorems'] For  $Y \in \mathbb{Y}$, let  $Y^i$, $i \in \mathcal{Z}$, be defined by (equation DefOfYi of the paper). 
