{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:26:02.395133+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_71a69f80ff51a0c1d690f88869be2f0f240c531cd17586e3fc0ef717154057d7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm fineET of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a cooriented $C^0$-foliation on $M$ transverse to $\partial M$ with finitely many compact planar leaves. Let $L_1, \dots, L_m$ denote its unstable compact planar leaves, and let $\Lambda_1, \dots, \Lambda_k$ denote its unstable $\mathbb{T}^2$-type planar minimal sets. For each of those, choose a boundary point $p_i \in \partial L_i \subset \partial M$ and $q_j \in \partial \Lambda_j \subset \partial M$.

    Then $\mathcal{F}$ can be $C^0$-approximated by positive (resp.~negative) contact structures which dominate some foliation $\mathcal{G}$ on $\partial M$, obtained from $\partial \mathcal{F}$ by the following operations only:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Isotopies,
        \item Blowdowns and blowups of type $\natural/\sharp$ (resp.~$\natural/ \flat$) away from the boundaries of the aforementioned minimal sets,
        \item $\flat$ (resp.~$\sharp$) modifications near $p_1, \dots, p_m, q_1, \dots, q_k$.
    \end{itemize}
    Moreover, all of these operations can be made arbitrarily small, so that $\mathcal{G}$ is tangentially $C^0$-close to $\partial \mathcal{F}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.366054+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_71ae308398fa2ca00b730c245c97db39d0b581222641142e2f2f12f2dcd1a68b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition claim:moment expansion of arXiv:2606.02472, 'Correlated uniform attachment trees'] Let $X_1,\ldots,X_n$ be Bernoulli random variables and let $X=\sum_{i=1}^{n} X_i$. Suppose that for any subset of indices $S\subseteq\{1,\ldots,n\}$ with $\abs{S}\leq 4$, there is a constant $\widetilde C$ such that

