    \end{align*}
    Constants $C_{\lambda,\mu,n}'$, $C_{\lambda,\mu,n}''$ and $A_{\lambda,\mu,n}$ are defined in (equation eq: subexpo L-p norm JSQ of the paper) and (equation eq: MGF upper bound JSQ of the paper), respectively. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:25:40.220923+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7264a885fb057dbf2a7ee247302bf1c5dfd03a003d6488a0a52892c2bab5213d","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:D12 of arXiv:2609.02544, 'A finiteness theorem for geodesic Leech wheels'] If $m\ge40$ and there are two large spokes, then
