{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:14:37.646667+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_72a5902867feb4b286aa249a989998ab6689815637ee638047da2d2bae1b1d02","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 2 of arXiv:2608.19560, '\textbf{Computing transient probabilities in Markovian queues with balking conditional on '] $\bm{q}(u,K)$ is determined by the following linear equation 

\begin{align}
q_{k,\ell,s}(0,K)
&=
\left\{
\begin{aligned}
&1, && k=K,\ \ell=0,1,\ldots,K,\ s\in\mathcal{S},\\
&0, && \text{otherwise},
\end{aligned}
\right.

\\
\frac{\partial \bm{q}(u,K)}{\partial u}
&=
\bm{Q}(T-u)\bm{q}(u,K).

