{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:55:37.870282+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_72efd0bb1799289407013d59d4a3ae803576b6abe8c5b031d835ebc88551b2a5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:path_prob of arXiv:2605.06511, 'Logarithmic Mixing of Random Walks on Dynamical Random Cluster Models'] Let $n \in \mathbb{N}$ be sufficiently large and $G = (V, E)$ a $d$-regular graph on $n$ vertices. For all $\mu > 0$, $t \geq 0$, $x > 0$, $e = \{u, u'\} \in E$ such that $B_R(u)$ has at most one cycle, and $(\eta, v) \in \{0, 1\}^E \times V$, then
		\begin{align*}
			& \mathbb{P}\left[\xi_{u, e}^{\mathrm{path}}\left(t, t + x\right) \mid \left(\eta_t, X_t\right) = \left(\eta, v\right)\right] \\
			\geq&\ \left(1 - 2K \left(p + (1-p)e^{-\mu x}\right)^{{R}/{2}}\right) \mathbb{P}\left[S_{t+x} \left(R, K\right) \mid \left(\eta_t, X_t\right) = \left(\eta, v\right)\right].
