{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:09:23.952198+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_72f167a07b9cb3c608fc043778a40108bfcf78b0e89e5f04bbd4cb6355b8a4b0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 4 of arXiv:2607.21759, 'Marchenko--Pastur law for tensor powers of exchangeable unconditional vectors'] Let $d$ be fixed, and let $\mathbf X = (X_1,\dotsc,X_n)$ be the exchangeable unconditional base vector. If 
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $\E X_1^2 \to 1$, 
        \item  $\E(X_1^2X_2^2) - \E(X_1^2)\E(X_2^2) \to 0$, and
        \item  there exists some $\epsilon > 0$ such that $\sup_n \E(\abs{X_1}^{4d + \epsilon}) < \infty$,
    \end{enumerate} then the three conditions in \cref{thm:main} are satisfied, and we have with probability $1$ that \[\ESD(K_{\PrincipalT}) \wkconv \mu_{\MP(c)}.\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:30.018981+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_72fa1a01341cd67a1d1f44b4b67b83095b96bebd8475bfa547b816bac1213472","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 6 (Markov setting) of arXiv:2605.05986, '\bf Convergence rate of the occupation measure of { classes of ergodic processes toward th'] Let $(P_t)_{t\ge0}$ denote a  Markov transition semi-group defined on bounded $\R$-valued Borel functions defined on $\R^d$. Let $\mu_0\!\in {\cal P}_q(\R^d)$ for some $q> 1$ 
and 

let $\psi:\ER\rightarrow[0, +\infty)$ and $\ee\!\in \mathbb{L}^1([0, +\infty))$  be  Borel functions such that,
\begin{equation}
