{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:37:51.459972+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7475d75cdd8ab65e1b4b725ae2d67d1d4a3a2a54f353c041ff5825f7f1a45e88","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 47 of arXiv:2604.03777, 'Equilibrium fluctuations for a multi-species particle system with long jumps'] Let $(\alpha^{(i)}_n)_{n \in \mathbb{N}_+}$, $i=1,2$, be two sequences of 
diverging sequence of constants such that~\eqref{e:seqConst} holds. 
Let $T>0$ and let $\{\mcb P^n_s\colon s\in[0,T]\}$ be a 
real--valued stochastic processes on $[0,T]$.  
Assume that there exist $\alpha\in(0,1)$ and $C=C(T)>0$, such that uniformly in $n$,
\begin{align}
\sup_{0\leq s\leq T}\E\left[ |\mcb P_s^{n}|\right]&\leq C\,,\\
\E\left[|\mcb P_t^{n}-\mcb P_s^{n}|\right]&\leq C(t-s)^{\alpha}\,,\qquad \text{for all $s,t\in[0,T]$.}
\end{align}
Then, for any $t\in[0,T]$, and Lebesgue-a.e. $k_1,k_2\in\R$
we have
\begin{equation}
\lim_{n\to\infty} \E\left[\left| \int_0^t\mcb P_s^{n} e^{-2\pi \iota  \frac{k_1\alpha_n^{(1)}+k_2\alpha_n^{(2)}}{n}}\dd s\right|\right]=0\,. 
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.684617+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_747c7c53d0734b3ede6f36c4c67f5b1698210d28235d72f21f02afe78f59cf29","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 (Finite-dimensional spectral-growth theorem) of arXiv:2607.26377, '\textbf{Entire Logarithmic Signatures\\ of Bounded-Variation Paths in Finite Dimensions}'] Let $q\geq1$ and let $A:\C\to M_q(\C)$ be entire, with $A(0)=0$, and suppose
\begin{equation}
\norm{\e^{A(z)}}\leq C\e^{\tau\abs{z}}
\qquad (z\in\C)
\end{equation}
for constants $C\geq1$ and $\tau\geq0$, where $\norm{\cdot}$ is an operator norm. Then $z\mapsto\sigma_k(A(z))$ is a polynomial of degree at most $k$ for $1\leq k\leq q$.

If, in addition, $A(z)=zH+O(z^2)$ as $z\to0$ for some $H\in M_q(\C)$, then
\begin{equation}
\det(\zeta I-A(z))=\det(\zeta I-zH)
\end{equation}
for all $z,\zeta\in\C$. Consequently,
\begin{equation}
\tr(A(z)^p)=z^p\tr(H^p)
\qquad (p\geq1).
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:36:12.192360+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_747cc8c07b6561b4fcad68b186e3b57bf7732f76a56988d6ce51527f694b74f1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 5 of arXiv:2609.03924, 'Beyond normal fluctuations in local laws for Wigner matrices'] Let $W$ be an $N\times N$ GUE matrix. For any $n_1,n_2\in\N\cup\{0\}$ and multi-indices $\bm{k}\in\N^{n_1},\bm{l}\in\N^{n_2}$ it holds that    
\begin{equation}
\E(\bm{k},\bm{l}):=\E \left[\eta^{|\bm{k}|+|\bm{l}|}\Delta(\bm{k}) \overline{\Delta(\bm{l})}\right] = \Phi_0(\bm{k},\bm{l}) + \mathcal{O}(\eta),

\end{equation}
uniformly in $z\in \mathcal{D}$. Here $\Phi_0$ is an explicit function of $\bm{k}$ and $\bm{l}$ given later in \eqref{eq:Phi_0_expl} which does not depend on $N$ and $z$. Similarly, the implicit constant in $\mathcal{O}(\eta)$ does not depend on $N$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:38:25.224287+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7496322c24a9324013d72b001c4c17766e3624bf8d81f4fbad9d8cce69e8e631","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem eq:fractionalbubbles of arXiv:2609.00324, 'Quantitative Stability for Fractional Yamabe minimizers'] Let $\gamma\in (0,n/2)$. Then for all $w \in \dot{H}^{\gamma} (\mathbb{R}^n )$ we have
    \begin{equation*}
        \|w \|_{L^{2^{*}}(\mathbb{R}^n )}^2 \leq S(n,\gamma) \|(-\Delta )^{\gamma/2}w \|_{L^{2} (\mathbb{R}^n )}^2 = S(n,\gamma) \int_{\mathbb{R}^n } w (-\Delta )^{\gamma}w  dx,
    \end{equation*}
    where
    \begin{align*}
        S(n,\gamma) = \frac{\Gamma ((n-2\gamma)/2)}{\Gamma ((n+2\gamma)/2)} |\operatorname{vol}(\mathbb{S}^n )|^{-\frac{2\gamma}{n}}.
    \end{align*}
    We have equality if and only if
    \begin{align}
        w(x) = c\left( \frac{\mu}{|x-x_0 |^2 + \mu^2 }  \right)^{\frac{n-2\gamma}{2}} \quad x\in \mathbb{R}^n,
    \end{align}
    for $c\in \mathbb{R}$, $\mu > 0$ and $x_0 \in \mathbb{R}^n$. We denote the set of these functions as $\mathcal{M}_{\mathbb{R}^n} $. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:47:04.945057+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_74990cb5c336cfbd7622006cc8a015ed86332d4b50c10ba1fe15eae8d4a9ac3d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:bicausaltptplanbetweenSDEs of arXiv:2412.02948, 'Causal transport on path space'] $\pi \in \Pi_{bc}\deln{\mu^{\sigma,b}_z, \mu^{\overline{\sigma}, \overline{b}}_{\tilde{z}}}$ if and only if  there exists a stochastic basis $\del{\Omega, \mathcal{G}, \del{\mathcal{G}_t}_{t \in \sbr{0,1}}, \mathbb{P}}$ 
and two $d$-dimensional $\del{\mathcal{G}_t}_{t \in \sbr{0,1}}$-Brownian motions $B = \del{B_t}_{t \in \sbr{0,1}}$ and $\tilde{B} = \deln{\tilde{B}_t}_{t \in \sbr{0,1}}$
        and $\del{\mathcal{G}_t}_{t \in \sbr{0,1}}$-adapted processes $Z = \deln{Z_t}_{t \in \sbr{0,1}}$, $\tilde{Z} = \deln{\tilde{Z}_t}_{t \in \sbr{0,1}}$ such that 
        \begin{itemize}
            \item $\deln{Z,B}$ and  $\deln{\tilde{Z},\tilde{B}}$ satisfy  (equation eqn:firstsde of the paper) and (equation eqn:2ndsde of the paper) respectively, and
            \item $\pi$ is the joint law of  $(Z,\tilde{Z})$: $\pi = \deln{Z,\tilde{Z}}_{\#}\mathbb{P}$.
        \end{itemize}
        In particular, the joint law of $(B,\tilde{B})$ under $\mathbb{P}$ is a bicausal Wiener coupling. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:12:09.045046+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_74a2b48ab43bd5d47d7bb3055453e1e8b5d231e67db393cf4129d9019be2512f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:smoothcycle of arXiv:2608.25279, 'Provable Non-Acceleration of Standard Strang\\ Splittings of Kinetic Langevin Dynamics'] Assume the hypotheses of Lemma~(lem:interiorcycle of the paper), and let $m\ge3$ satisfy the strict cycling condition (equation eq:strictPK of the paper). Then there exist distinct points $x_0^\circ,\ldots,x_{m-1}^\circ\in\mathbb R^2$ on the unit circle, a potential $U\in\mathcal U_\kappa^2$, and constants $r_0>0$, $b_\ast<\infty$ such that, with indices modulo $m$,
\begin{equation}
 x_{j+1}^\circ=(1+\beta)x_j^\circ-\beta x_{j-1}^\circ-s\nabla U(x_j^\circ),
\end{equation}
\begin{equation}
 \nabla U(x_j^\circ+u)=\nabla U(x_j^\circ)+u,
 \qquad \lvert u\rvert\le r_0,
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
 \nabla U(x)=x+w(x),\qquad \sup_{x\in\mathbb R^2}\lvert w(x)\rvert\le b_\ast.
\end{equation}
Consequently, $\nabla^2U=\mathrm{Id}_2$ on each ball $B(x_j^\circ,r_0)$, and the Jacobian of the deterministic heavy-ball update
\begin{equation*}
 (x,y)\longmapsto
 \bigl((1+\beta)x-\beta y-s\nabla U(x),\;x\bigr)
\end{equation*}
at every cycle state $(x_j^\circ,x_{j-1}^\circ)$ is
\begin{equation}
 \mathsf A_1=
 \begin{pmatrix}(1+\beta-s)\mathrm{Id}_2&\;-\beta\mathrm{Id}_2\\
                 \mathrm{Id}_2&\;0\end{pmatrix}.
\end{equation}
Therefore, the Jacobian of the $m$-step update at each cycle state is $\mathsf M=\mathsf A_1^m$, and
\begin{equation*}
 \rho(\mathsf M)
 =\rho(\mathsf A_1)^m
 \le\rho_{\mathrm q}(s,\beta;\kappa)^m
 <1.
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.591455+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_74a5da7e2b9236fe8aaa87f37736aa686c1a8bfc8336433dc0a778df5131be03","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem lemma_density_wall_influence_times of arXiv:2412.03370, 'TASEP with a general initial condition and a deterministically moving wall'] Suppose $x^f_{\alpha T}(T) \simeq \xi T$ and $f$ fulfils Assumption~(assumpt:2.1.1 of the paper) with parameters $\alpha_0 < \dots < \alpha_n$. Then, it holds
	\begin{equation} 
