{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:32:58.356902+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_76b55a0ada599b67813046f78f63ebd220501a22a2b71a2f67e7f1c3a7d5edda","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 5 of arXiv:2506.18558, '2506.18558'] A class of measures $\{\nu^x_t\}_{t\in\RR}$ is called an evolution system of measures for $\{P^x_{s,t}\}_{t\ge s}$, if
