{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:23:05.298216+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_77181712cc18d8625c2d7aa661d4c70bee53c938d43be67742a13780c52874e6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 15 of arXiv:2608.21701, 'Superdiffusivity of random walks on the three-dimensional randomly oriented Manhattan latt'] We have $\Lambda_1=c_1T_1=0$. For every $m\ge1$,
