{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:48:27.276968+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_771bb2e5d09e8f1f1d0354e044f6f705733b1499d1a476ad3d5d1ba32db05eed","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 3 of arXiv:2604.24664, 'Absolute continuity of Rosenblatt measures'] Let $\alpha \in (0, 1)$ and $f: [0, T] \to \Rbb$. The \emph{left} and \emph{right Riemann--Liouville fractional derivatives of $f$ of order $\alpha$} are defined by
