where $b_n$ is defined by
 \[b_n\frac{F'(b_n)}{F(b_n)}=\frac{k_n}{n-k_n}.\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:47:22.244633+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7724e094f1dc46d773a722e3136b19166c7d89e7ab524e9fe4ecf8dda55f5b52","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 1 of arXiv:2605.26664, 'Mixing times for Glauber dynamics of lozenge tilings of the hexagon'] For any $\delta>0$, there exist constants $\kappa > 0$ and $C = C(\delta)>0$ such that the mixing time of the single-flip Glauber dynamic on tilings of the hexagon $\mX$ satisfies
