{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.320212+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7758f588e93e289f336f9f719d69ea2cbc160d33ebd1057baacd5679f80b8b6f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:estimate-log-IG of arXiv:2411.06195, 'Restrictions of some reinforced processes to subgraphs'] \mbox{}\\
  For $W>0$ and $X_W\sim \operatorname{IG}(W^{-1},1)$, one has 
  \begin{align}

    E[\log X_W]=&-\log W-\int_0^\infty\frac{e^{-u}}{u+2W}\, du
                  =e^{2W}\int_0^{2W}(\log t+\gamma)e^{-t}\, dt+{c_2}
  \end{align}
  with ${c_2}$ and $\gamma$ specified in Theorem (thm:from-r-to-l of the paper).
  Furthermore, the following bounds hold
  \begin{align}

    -\log(W+\tfrac12)\le E[\log X_W]&\le\min\{-\log W,{c_2}\}\quad\text{for }W>0,\\

    {c_2}+4W(\log W+{c_2}-1) \le E[\log X_W]&\le{c_2}\quad\text{for }0<W\le\tfrac12 e^{-\gamma},\\

    \lim_{W\to 0}E[\log X_W]&={c_2}.
  \end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:03:39.776260+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_775d184ab23b0040fd1e86d90a7d616ca4345032026010cab0628013d9817e70","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:unshuffling-lemma of arXiv:2411.03065, 'Growing conditioned BGW trees with\\ log-concave offspring distributions'] Let $\mathbb{X}$ be a set and let $\psi$ be an $\mathbb{X}$-shuffling rule.
	If $\psi$ is $\mathfrak{S}$-equivariant, then for all $T,T'\in\trees$, ${\boldsymbol{x}}\in\mathbb{X}^T$, ${\boldsymbol{x}}'\in\mathbb{X}^{T'}$, ${\boldsymbol{\uppi}}\in\mathfrak{S}_T$, we have the equivalence
	\begin{align}
	\begin{cases}
	T'	= \bigl({\boldsymbol{\sigma}}^\psi_{T,{\boldsymbol{x}}}\bigr)\cdotT\\
	{\boldsymbol{x}}' = \bigl({\boldsymbol{\sigma}}^\psi_{T,{\boldsymbol{x}}}\bigr)_*\,{\boldsymbol{x}}
	\end{cases}
	\quad\iff\quad
	\begin{cases}
	T	=	\bigl(\overline{{\boldsymbol{\sigma}}}^\psi_{T',{\boldsymbol{x}}'}\bigr)\cdotT'\\
	{\boldsymbol{x}} = \bigl(\overline{{\boldsymbol{\sigma}}}^\psi_{T',{\boldsymbol{x}}'}\bigr)_*\,{\boldsymbol{x}}',
	\end{cases}
	\end{align}
	and if one of these equivalent conditions is satisfied then ${\boldsymbol{\sigma}}^\psi_{T',{\boldsymbol{x}}'}=(\overline{\boldsymbol{\sigma}}^\psi_{T,{\boldsymbol{x}}})^{-1}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.764418+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_775d50a8298b968d41af95d113fb9c1ae25c137130e3f2cc51e77cd03d30c334","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:lbm-response-realization of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] For every $\mu\in\mathcal M_{\rm LBM}$ and every $u,v$ in a common
positive eigenspace of $A_\mu$,
\begin{equation}
 \Theta_\mu(u,v)=uv\,\mu\in\mathcal M_{\rm fe}(D).

\end{equation}
The map $U_\mu=U_D$ in (equation eq:lbm-response-space of the paper) is linear and
injective, and
\begin{equation}
 \inner{U_\mu\sigma}{f}_{H}
 =\int_Df\,d\sigma,
 \qquad
 \sigma\in\mathcal M_{\rm fe}(D),\quad f\in C_c^\infty(D).

\end{equation}
Thus the LBM response is faithfully potential-realizable in the sense of
Definition~(def:response-realization of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:07:15.761153+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_776addd64571619276b2f003325a82488caff992784de9103067a041993547f2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:lbm-compact-resolvent of arXiv:2608.02459, 'Response Calculus for Spectral Simplicity\\ and Joint Eigenvalue Densities'] For every $x\in\Omega_{\rm op}$,
