As a consequence, the law of $\omega_N$ on $\D'(\T)$ under the positions' distribution $\nu_{N,\beta}(dx^N)$ weakly converges to $\mu_\beta$ for $\beta<\beta_0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.112573+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7795c20f44d164d0fc704d66bfecacba83dd26dcf4aa553f7eea07f30111632b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:differentiated-linear-estimate of arXiv:2608.16119, 'Fully nonlinear parabolic equations under a fixed reference diffusion: weighted \texorpdfs'] Let $\alpha\geq0$ and assume Assumptions~(ass:reference-diffusion of the paper) and
