{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.736420+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_77b39b5580fb11fe737a24f2f72a413a4fe2d45958d2efe099d4644599e2ae48","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma key_lemma_delocalized_eigenvector of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] Take $z=E+\mathrm{i} \eta\in \mathbf D\left({\tau}\right)$ with $E=\gamma_k\in \qa{E^{-},E^+}$ and $\eta\sim N^{-2/3+\varepsilon_L}k^{-1/3}$ for a small constant $\varepsilon_L>0$ (recall that we assume $k\in[\![{1,DN/2}]\!]$). Under the assumptions of (mix of the paper), there exists a constant $c_L>0$ (depending on $\varepsilon_L,\delta_A,\varepsilon_A$) such that 
\begin{equation}
\max_{z_1,z_2\in\{z,\overline z\}}\max_{a,b\in [\![{D}]\!]}\left|\left(\mathbb{E} L_{(1,2)}- K_{(1,2)}\right)_{ab}\right|
