{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.628585+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_77bbf10e02cc5dcdaa14a3a94af5dbd9f66934a57eb696114c6e1e5ee4a7e7f9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:Lq-J-thin of arXiv:2411.03609, 'Asymptotically optimal Wasserstein couplings for the small-time stable domain of attractio'] Consider the coupling $(\bm{D}^{\bm{X},\kappa},\bm{D}^{\bm{Y},\kappa},\bm{J}^{\bm{X},\kappa},\bm{J}^{\bm{Y},\kappa})$ defined in~(equation eq:comp_Poisson_measures of the paper) and~(equation eq:thining_coupling_defn of the paper). Then
\begin{equation}

\mathds{E}\bigg[\sup_{t\in[0,1]}\big|\bm{J}^{\bm{X},\kappa}_t-\bm{J}^{\bm{Y},\kappa}_t\big|^q\bigg]
\leqslant \int_{\mathbb{R}^d_{\bm{0}}}\1_{\mathbb{R}^d \setminus B_{\bm{0}}(\kappa)}(\bm{w})
    |\bm{w}|^q|f_{\bm{X}}(\bm{w})-f_{\bm{Y}}(\bm{w})|\mu(\mathrm{d}\bm{w}),
\,\text{for any }q\in(0,1].
\end{equation}
In particular, the following inequality holds for any $q\in(0,1]$:
\begin{equation}

\begin{split}
\mathcal{W}_q(\bm{X},\bm{Y})
&\leqslant 
|\bm{\gamma}_{\bm{X},\kappa}-\bm{\gamma}_{\bm{Y},\kappa}|^q
+\bigg(4\int_{\mathbb{R}^d_{\bm{0}}}\1_{B_{\bm{0}}(\kappa)}(\bm{w})
    |\bm{w}|^2|f_{\bm{X}}(\bm{w})-f_{\bm{Y}}(\bm{w})|\mu(\mathrm{d}\bm{w})\bigg)^{q/2}\\
&\qquad + 2^qd^{q/2}|\bm{\Sigma_X}-\bm{\Sigma_Y}|^q
+\int_{\mathbb{R}^d_{\bm{0}}}\1_{\mathbb{R}^d \setminus B_{\bm{0}}(\kappa)}(\bm{w})
    |\bm{w}|^q|f_{\bm{X}}(\bm{w})-f_{\bm{Y}}(\bm{w})|\mu(\mathrm{d}\bm{w}).
    \end{split}
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:33:46.768300+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_77bccccd4de527680e8f40ad82c0305c6bbcd6cfb7b89d84cf89c768c8b549fe","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2603.24616, 'Pinning in non-critical half-space geometric last passage percolation'] Assume the notation from Definition \ref{Def.IGP}. Then, for any $\{ B_i \in \Omega(a, b, x_i , y_i) \}_{i = 1}^k$
