{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:33:12.345445+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_78881c73b577f87fecb57ebc5c07a9e4c1d26a8db9293e8851eec10f8d6dbb71","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 137 of arXiv:2608.29416, 'Algorithmic threshold for high-dimensional projection pursuit I: general theory'] In the setting of Proposition~\ref{prop:graph-AMP-cor}, suppose $\psi$ preserves $\bbW_2$ convergence in the sense that if $\mu_k\to \mu$ in $\bbW_2$ as $k\to\infty$, then $\psi_\#\mu_k\to\psi_\#\mu$ in $\bbW_2$ as $k\to\infty$. Let
  \[
  \boldsymbol{\psi}
  \equiv
  \psi(\bu[[\ell]],\bar{\bg}[\ell], \by[0])
  \equiv
  \Big( \psi
  ( u_n[[\ell]],
  \bar{g}_n[\ell]
  , y_n[0] 
   )\Big)_{n\le N} \in \R^N\,.\]
Then the vector $\boldsymbol{\psi}$ also obeys $\bbW_2$ state evolution, meaning that in $\bbW_2$ distance we have
  \[\frac{1}{N}
    \sum\limits_{n=1}^N
