{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.529487+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_78dc016f8a25e8f8570958c171222e54eeebee8dd5987b2a1241315843d4b11a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition eq:sharp-tail-cost of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[proposition]{prop:sharp-one-spike}
If \(\xi\) is sharp sub-Gaussian, then for every \(a>0\) and \(\eta>0\),
