{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.229025+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_78debffe1f7c5c2d928e5c004b7ce838e60ece8b57c5435fb69fbfaf21083813","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] For each $\varepsilon>0$, define $\mathsf{G}_{\varepsilon}$ to be the event that for all $(x,s;y,t) \in [0,1]^{4}_{\uparrow}$ with $\big|\sl^{-1}(x,s;y,t)\big|\leq \varepsilon^{-\frac{1}{2}}$ and for all $\pi\in \mathfrak{G}_{(x,s),(y,t)}$, the geodesic $\pi$  is $\varepsilon\text{-good}$. There exists $\varepsilon_0>0$ and $c,C>0$ such that for all $\varepsilon\in \big(0,\varepsilon_0\big)$, 
