{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.368485+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_78f80093fadf17d75bda7f36e33a54730820c498f67390f667fb0866b6ea9bf6","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 of arXiv:2606.03534, 'Construction and simulation of a path-valued model of dendrite development'] A solution to the \textit{martingale problem} for a generator $\mathcal{A}: \mathcal{D}(\mathcal{A}) \rightarrow B(\W)$ is a measurable stochastic process $\omega_t$ with state space $\W$, defined on some probability space $(\Omega, \mathcal{F},P)$, such that for all $f \in \mathcal{D}(\mathcal{A})$, 
    \begin{align*}
        f(\omega_t) - f(\omega_0)- \int_0^t \mathcal{A}f(\omega_s) \, ds \,,
    \end{align*}
    is a martingale with respect to its natural filtration. We say the martingale problem for $\mathcal{A}$ is \textit{well-posed} if there exists a unique solution to the martingale problem.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.722509+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_790498f4f1ca84b4653b3cfed2b30efd4eb791351c0c0e028c6e2ea4e9809a02","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm5.1' of arXiv:2606.01944, 'Propagation of Chaos for Mean-field Mean Reflected Backward Stochastic Differential Equati'] The reflected BSDE (equation eq7' of the paper) has a unique solution $(\{Y^i,Z^i\}_{1\leq i\leq N},K^{(N)})$ with $K^{(N)}\in \mathcal{A}^2(\mathbb{F}^{(N)})$, $Y^i\in \mathcal{S}^2(\mathbb{F}^{(N)})$ and $Z^i\in \mathcal{H}^2(\mathbb{F}^{(N)};\mathbb{R}^N)$ for $i=1,\cdots,N$. Moreover, there exists a constant $C$ independent of $N$, such that
