	where the expression for $\tilde \ell_\nu$ is given by \eqref{2.21}  $($or by \eqref{eq:xLaplace}$)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:30.985708+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_791efe7fb3d5067cdfc72f7fd9cf99f41135b5c283cf4a260793c712c8a676c7","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 (Block-pairing principle) of arXiv:2608.12492, 'Weak Limits of Wiener Chaos: Primitive--Fock Classification and Hilbert--Stein Extraction'] Let $k_i=[k_{i,n}]\in\cK_{s_i}$, $1\le i\le m$, and
$\ell_j=[\ell_{j,n}]\in\cK_{t_j}$, $1\le j\le \ell$, with
$\sum_i s_i=\sum_jt_j=q$.  Then
\begin{align}
 &\Ulim q!\ip{\Sym\bigotimes_i k_{i,n}}
                     {\Sym\bigotimes_j\ell_{j,n}}
 \notag\\
 &\qquad=
 \1_{\{m=\ell\}}
 \sum_{\substack{\pi\in\mathfrak S_m\\s_i=t_{\pi(i)}}}
 \prod_{i=1}^m
 \ip{k_i}{\ell_{\pi(i)}}_{\cK_{s_i}}.

\end{align}
Here
\begin{equation}
 \ip{k_i}{\ell_j}_{\cK_s}
 =s!\,\Ulim\ip{k_{i,n}}{\ell_{j,n}},

\end{equation}
so the full multiplicity $\prod_i s_i!$ of the matched internal legs is
already contained in the right-hand side.","status":"unverified"}

