{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:58:09.067781+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_792e4fd20d4f9bae870f760348a6eb2d870a1443c43e484e1a9b46aea4f9addf","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2606.27545, 'A simple proof of rapid mixing on random regular graphs beyond uniqueness'] For all $f,g:\{0,1\}^V\to\mathbb R$,
		\begin{equation}
			-\langle f,Lg\rangle_\mu
			=
			\sum_{v\in V}\E_\mu\left[r_v(\sigmabf)D_v^+f(\sigmabf)\,D_v^+g(\sigmabf)
