{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:33:12.347316+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_793516100caec8c8b153bb0cf185f57c21be3856d72ad4bf9e63e06cccddd2ea","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 152 of arXiv:2608.29416, 'Algorithmic threshold for high-dimensional projection pursuit I: general theory'] Given any $\upp,\eta\in (0,1)$, if $\linit$ is sufficiently large
depending on $\upp,\eta$, then
