\end{equation*}
Then
\begin{equation*}
\liminf_{r\downarrow0}
\frac{\log_2\nu(B(x,r))}{\log_2 r}\ge\beta
\qquad
(x\in\operatorname{spt}\nu).
\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.590865+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a1eafcabefe538cdef6c0cc552f6eb8acfe37eb07b0cbd82431d6ee5b1392f2","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:LRD of arXiv:2606.02003, 'Higher-Order Multifractional Stable Motion:\\ Definition and Fundamental Properties'] Under Assumptions~(ass:params of the paper) and~(ass:limits of the paper), $n$-MFSM
exhibits long-range dependence --- that is,
$\tau(X^{(n)}_H(s), X^{(n)}_H(t)) \to 0$ as $t \to +\infty$
at a polynomial rate $t^{-d}$ with $d > 0$ --- if and only if
\begin{equation}

(\alpha-1)H_+ + H(s) < n,
\end{equation}
in which case the LRD exponent is
