{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:40:26.998748+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a267899995a344f67b6cf853d2319a13dc7e997eca38035f67fc6cad46324c9","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition thm:expectation-variance of arXiv:2604.17253, 'Large Deviations for the Nonlinear Schrödinger Equation with Randomized Quasi-Periodic Ini'] Let randomized field $f(\boldsymbol{x})$ be defined as in (equation eq:randomqp_d of the paper). Then the following properties hold:
\begin{enumerate}
\item[\rm(i)] The field is centered: $\mathbb{E}[f(\boldsymbol{x})] = 0$ for all $\boldsymbol{x} \in \mathbb{R}^d$.
\item[\rm(ii)] If the decay rates satisfy ${\rho_{j,j'} > 1/2}$ for each $j=1,\dots,d$ and $j'=1,\dots,\nu_j$, then the second moment is uniformly bounded: $\mathbb{V}[f(\boldsymbol{x})] < \infty$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:37.362826+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a28c6d6840fb5e5d95ecfdef3185d0854770650620bea10d5735132d235e098","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2606.18047, 'Analysis of the asymmetric shelf shuffle'] Fix $m\geq 1$ and $p\in (0, 1)$. Let $X(\pi; {\bf x})$ be as in~\eqref{eqn:CycleStructurePoly}. Then,
\begin{equation}

Z(u, {\mathbf{x}}):=1+\sum_{n\ge 1}u^n\sum_{\pi\in S_n}\nu^{(p)}_{n,m}(\pi)X(\pi ; \mathbf{x})
=
\prod_{i\ge 1}\exp\left\{\sum_{r\ge 1}\frac{B^{(m,p)}_{i,r}}{ir}\,x_i^r u^{ir}
\right\},
\end{equation}
where 
\begin{equation}

B^{(m,p)}_{i,r}:=
\sum_{d\mid i} \mu(d) m^{\,i/d-ir} \bigl(p^{dr}-(-q)^{dr}\bigr)^{i/d},\qquad i,r\ge 1\;.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:57:07.197270+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a2e7cb6f3d9d7a899fd8dbb10fc62ace701f037bd784a6b1d351832b17036c3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:DKS-polymer-weights of arXiv:2509.04333, 'The limiting law of the Discrete Gaussian level lines'] Fix $\delta > 0$. Let $z$, $z_r$ for $r = 1, \ldots, N$ be complex numbers such that $|\Re z| < 2 - \delta/\beta'$. Let $s$ be a real number in $[0, \delta/3]$. For any interval $I \subset [0, N]$ with integer endpoints, define
		\begin{equation*}
			\hat X_{N, s}(I) := (\prod_{r \in I} Q_{z_r})^{-1} \sum_{\Gamma: J(\Gamma) = I} {\widehat q}^n_z(\Gamma)\exp(s|I|)\,.
		\end{equation*}
		Then, there exists some $\beta_0$ and constant $c$ such that for all $N$, $\beta \geq \beta_0$, $z$, $z_r$, and all such intervals $I$, we have
		\begin{equation*}
			|\hat X_{N, s}(I)| \leq \exp(-(\beta - \beta_0)(|I| - 1))\,.
		\end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:57:51.747886+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a3064d17ed2b8896ec884d6b41e4f1c432c76d8f596d3a79e0eefc79eea2aa4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2608.30138, 'High-frequency wave propagation for the viscoelastic wave equation with singular memory'] For $k=0,1,\dots$, let $F\in C([0,T];H^k(\Omega))$, and
assume that \eqref{m-int-k} holds with $k+1$ in place of $k$. 
Then the Volterra equation 
\begin{equation}   
\Delta_{\sigma_\eps} u (t) -  \eps\nabla \cdot \int_0^t \mathfrak{m}(s,\cdot) \nabla u(t-s)\,\d s=F(t)
\end{equation}
has a unique solution $u\in C([0,T]; \, H^{k+2}(\Omega)\cap H_0^1(\Omega))$. Moreover, the norm of the solution operator $F\mapsto u$ is uniformly bounded in $\eps\in [0,\eps_0]$, for $\eps_0\ll1$ possibly depending on $m$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:35:04.214928+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a3427768b504e08bd366570cf9f5676f86a196d5ad6c52acfba82f41a1029aa","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 22 of arXiv:2608.03956, 'From Triangular Array Progression\\ to Near-Log-Concave State Transitions'] Let $\mathcal{S}^{(y,n)}$ be as in (\ref{shannonsum}). Then,
