{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:40:59.340222+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7a3a457407e2e708644969b2545056a894104c5699a8fbf9f35150bad42d99fa","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 11 of arXiv:2609.03954, 'Galois representations ramified at one prime via relative deformation theory'] There is a finite set $\cE_p\subset\Z$ such that
