{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.414147+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7aa161a9a346a39fc611be932186590f934933d2cd63f944da043ec3428fb777","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:limit_of_kernel of arXiv:2507.22011, 'Random Lozenge Waterfall:\\Dimensional Collapse of Gibbs Measures'] We have the following limits of the correlation kernel $K_t$ on a slice.
	On the center line, that is
	$\mathsf{N}<\mathsf{T}$,
