Then for $U_R(x)=R^2U(x/R)$ and $Q_R=Q_{h,\gamma}^{U_R}$ there are constants $c_0,C_0>0$, independent of $R$, such that $Q_R$ has a unique invariant law $\pi_R$ and, for every $R\ge1$ and every $j\in\mathbb Z$, there exist two initial states $z_R^{(j)},z_R^{(j+1)}\in\mathbb R^{2d}$, constructed explicitly in (equation eq:cyclepair-general of the paper)-(equation eq:cyclevelocity-general of the paper) below from the cycle points with indices $j$ and $j+1$, such that at least one of them, denoted by $z_R$, satisfies
