{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.058176+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c9430743c2865092ff5ee69cbbc73d950f28fa722b799e5891d19fbf5f07b36","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:finite-chaos-brownian-probe of arXiv:2608.16119, 'Fully nonlinear parabolic equations under a fixed reference diffusion: weighted \texorpdfs'] Fix $\alpha\geq0$.  For every $\delta_{\rm pr}>0$ there exist $n\geq2$,
$\varphi_{\rm pr}\in C_c^\infty((0,1))$, and a smooth field $q$ on
$[0,1]\times\mathbb R^d$ with
\begin{equation*}
 h_n(\xi):=\frac{\operatorname{He}_n(\xi_1)}{\sqrt{n!}},
 \qquad
 \Theta_n(s):=s^{n/2}\int_s^1
 \tau^{-n/2}\varphi_{\rm pr}(\tau)\,\mathrm d\tau,
 \qquad
 q(s,y):=\Theta_n(s)h_n(y/\sqrt s),\qquad 0<s\leq1,
\end{equation*}
where $\operatorname{He}_n$ is the probabilists' Hermite polynomial.  The
associated source is
\begin{equation*}
 F_0^{\rm tan}:=-\left(\partial_s+\frac12\Delta_y\right)q
 =\varphi_{\rm pr}(s)h_n(y/\sqrt s)\not\equiv0
\end{equation*}
The corresponding Hessian estimate is
\begin{equation}
 \left\lVert D_y^2q\right\rVert_{L^2(s^\alpha\,\mathrm d s\,\mathrm d\gamma_s)}
 \geq(C_\alpha^{\mathrm{Br}}-\delta_{\rm pr})
 \norm{F_0^{\rm tan}}_{L^2(s^\alpha\,\mathrm d s\,\mathrm d\gamma_s)}.

\end{equation}
The field vanishes on a terminal strip, and all its derivatives are
uniformly of polynomial growth in the spatial variable.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:47:12.031146+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7c9499c4eb4a83b44f542c5294f325ef675b65db8ec483f7639d6ea0e9472401","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:12 of arXiv:2512.09219, 'Strong confluence of geodesics in Liouville quantum gravity'] Suppose that (equation it:geodstar of the paper) in Lemma (lem:geodesic_between_geodesics of the paper) holds. We then have the following:
