{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:51:44.866864+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7d18868325344c9fc6e3c333a77f90ddf37f4b160de9e6b5cdd7566c2282414a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 2 of arXiv:2608.26834, 'Small-time annealed large deviations principle for one-dimensional diffusions in a random '] Under assumptions $H_1$ and $H_2$, for each $n\in\N$ and positive constants $R, \ r_i$, $h_i$, $1\le i\le n$,
