{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:39:11.669208+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7dc10d8d617c06f9ff205110c56c87c8fd42da95ba3761ff2d57a1a57d445844","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 (Exact ordered tuple formula) of arXiv:2608.04799, '2608.04799'] If \(K\le n\) and
\(k_i+r_i-1\le\binom{k_i}{2}\) for every \(i\), then
\begin{equation}
  L_n(\mathbf k,\mathbf r)=\frac{(n)_K}{\prod_{i=1}^q k_i!}\prod_{i=1}^q c(k_i,k_i+r_i-1)\,p_n^{K+R-q}(1-p_n)^{A},
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
  A
  &=K(n-K)
    +\sum_{1\le i<j\le q}k_ik_j
    +\sum_{i=1}^q
      \left\{\binom{k_i}{2}-(k_i+r_i-1)\right\}
  \\
  &=Kn-\frac{K^2}{2}-\frac{3K}{2}-R+q.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
If the feasibility conditions fail, then \(L_n(\mathbf k,\mathbf r)=0\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:10:05.677078+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7dc9ec7bc5f5a0a021d711b415ee5f96913307d258d4eafb466f0fbbf6ac8e65","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 16 (Recurrence relations) of arXiv:2608.16752, 'Absorption Probabilities for Random Convex Hulls: Distribution-Freeness via the Wall-Cross'] For every $d\geq 1$, we have
\begin{align*}
N^{\mathrm{Wend}}_{n,d}&=N^{\mathrm{Wend}}_{n-1,d}+N^{\mathrm{Wend}}_{n-1,d-1}, \qquad n\geq d+1,\\
    N^{\mathrm{walk}}_{n,d}&=(2n-1)N^{\mathrm{walk}}_{n-1,d}+N^{\mathrm{walk}}_{n-1,d-1}, \qquad n\geq d+1,\\
    N^{\mathrm{br}}_{n,d}&=(n-1)N^{\mathrm{br}}_{n-1,d}+N^{\mathrm{br}}_{n-1,d-1}, \qquad n\geq d+2.
