{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:12:20.558652+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7e5b5cbd3bc2fa8c6870139e274ea88f346c21a7f0d34ee417a467cd838fc47b","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Question question-1 of arXiv:2604.04882, 'On a Problem of M. Kac on Laplace Distributions'] For which injective completely monotone functions $L:[0,\infty)\to(0,1]$ does the following hold? Whenever characteristic functions $f_1,f_2$ with values in $I_L\coloneqq L([0,\infty))$ satisfy
