{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.721866+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7e5cfd2c853fdfd1e2278472afa559a788ea0a251c383f95e699b4724257d8d6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop.Green of arXiv:2411.19145, 'On the intersection of critical percolation clusters and other tree-like random graphs'] Assume $d\ge 5$. There exists a constant $C>0$, such that for any $L\ge 1$, any $z,x_1,\dots,x_L\in \mathbb Z^d$, 
