{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.332301+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7f15fba5f5b4af2f4fdb340894247011b5da230495d456e86eb37c06aefdaa0a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem See~\Cref{thm:convergence_nonsimple_cle} for a more detailed statement of arXiv:2609.04138, 'The conformally invariant metric on $\CLE_4$ I:\\ subsequential limits of the non-simple C'] For all $\kappa\in(4,8)$, consider a $\CLE_\kappa$ in the unit disk $\BD$ equipped with the graph distance $D^\kappa$, where two distinct loops are adjacent if and only if they intersect. Then, for every sequence $\kappa_n \downarrow 4$, there exists a sequence $\ka_{\kappa_n} \uparrow \infty$ such that, along a subsequence, 
		\[
		\left( \ka_{\kappa_n}^{-1}D^{\kappa_n} (\SCL^{\kappa_n}(x), \SCL^{\kappa_n}(y))\right)_{x,y \in \BD \cap \BQ^2} \mathop{\longrightarrow}\limits_{n\to \infty}^{(\mathrm{d})}
		\left( D (\SCL(x), \SCL(y))\right)_{x,y \in \BD \cap \BQ^2},
		\]
		for the product topology, where $D$ is a distance on the set of loops of a $\CLE_4$ in $\BD$, and where $\SCL^{\kappa_n}(x)$ (resp.\ $\SCL(x)$) is the loop of the $\CLE_{\kappa_n}$ (resp.\ $\CLE_4$) that surrounds $x$. Moreover, the above convergence also holds for the distances to $\partial \BD$, and the distances $D(\partial \BD, \SCL(x))$ for $x \in \BD \cap \BQ^2$ have the law of the times at which the uniform exploration discovers each loop $\SCL(x)$. Finally, the limiting metric $D$ depends on the $\CLE_4$ in a conformally invariant and local manner. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

