{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.577870+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7facb228d04771e016619a2badcd24e39887a0f99e191349dd49825bef9cad68","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2606.14812, 'Joint convergence in Wiener chaos via transport hierarchy and Malliavin covariances'] Let $p\geq 2$ and let $(X_N=I_p(f_N), N\geq 1)$ 
		satisfy \eqref{c1}. Let $Y_N=I_q(g_N)$ with 
		$ap\leq q<(a+1)p$ for some integer $a\geq 1$, and 
		$\sup_N\|g_N\|_{H^{\otimes q}}<\infty$. Define 
		recursively $h_{0,N}:=g_N$ and, for $r=1,\ldots,a$:
		\begin{equation}
			h_{r,N} := \frac{f_N\otimes_p h_{r-1,N}}
			{\|f_N\|^2_{H^{\otimes p}}}\in H^{\odot(q-rp)},
		\end{equation}
		and
		\begin{equation*}
			g_{r,N}^{(2)} := h_{r-1,N} 
			- \frac{(q-(r-1)p)!}{p!(q-rp)!}
			f_N\widetilde\otimes h_{r,N},
			\qquad
			\varepsilon_{r,N} := I_{q-(r-1)p}(g_{r,N}^{(2)}),
		\end{equation*}
		so that $f_N\otimes_p g_{r,N}^{(2)}=0$ for each 
		$r=1,\ldots,a$. Then for every $N\geq 1$, in the 
		\textbf{non-critical case} $ap<q<(a+1)p$:
		\begin{equation}
			Y_N = \sum_{r=1}^a \frac{X_N^r}{p^r\sigma^{2r}}
			Y_{r,N} + \varepsilon_N + r_N,
		\end{equation}
		and in the \textbf{critical case} $q=ap$:
		\begin{equation}
			Y_N = \sum_{r=1}^{a-1}\frac{X_N^r}{p^r\sigma^{2r}}
			Y_{r,N} + \frac{\rho_a}{p^a\sigma^{2a}}X_N^a 
			+ \varepsilon_N + r_N,
		\end{equation}
		where in both cases $\varepsilon_N$ is asymptotically 
		independent of $X_N$ and $r_N\to 0$ in $L^2(\Omega)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:54:57.568062+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7fc94de46f24c475f003407dca3e6f103ce42f1a8964fe00d0125de3326f7358","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2412.03366, 'Regularity of Weighted Tensorized Fractional Brownian Fields and associated function space'] For  $s\in (0,1)$ and $\alpha \in [0,1]$, we define the  weighted tensorized H\"older space $T^{s, \alpha}C(\mathbb{R}^2)$ as the space of functions $f: \mathbb{R}^2 \to \mathbb{R}$ of $L^{\infty}(\mathbb{R})$ such that there is $c>0$ with
    \begin{align*}
&|f(x_1+h_1,x_2+h_2)- f(x_1, x_2+h_2) - f(x_1+h_1,x_2)+ f(x_1,x_2)| \\
& \hspace{6cm} \leq c \, \min\{|h_1|,|h_2| \}^{(1+\alpha)s} \max\{|h_1|,|h_2| \}^{(1-\alpha)s},
    \end{align*}
    and 
$$|f(x_1+h_1,x_2)- f(x_1,x_2)| \leq c \, |h_1|^{(1+\alpha)s} \quad \text{and} \quad |f(x_1,x_2+h_2)-  f(x_1,x_2)| \leq c \,  |h_2|^{(1+\alpha)s}$$
for all $x_1,x_2,h_1,h_2 \in \mathbb{R}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:02:08.132981+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_7fcee8544cf53d04e7f1a7a1b7e9c6a6df1695676bf9654aff82f68e08da6147","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 2 of arXiv:2608.27569, 'Laplace and Dolbeault operators on Sasakian manifolds'] Let $(M^{2n+1},g,\xi )$ be a compact Sasakian
manifold. For $0\leq r,s\leq n$ and $t\in \{0,1\}$, let $H_{\overline{
