{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:36:23.147856+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8017cffd3e847e172504fac4790f4c561070477650fcfc4cf8c10eb804e4f7d7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:autocorrelation of arXiv:2507.16188, 'The noisy voter model with general initial conditions'] Let $G=(V,E)$ be a connected graph on $n$ vertices. Fix an initial state $\mathsf{x}_0 \in \mathfrak{C}_q^{V}$. Let $\psi_1,\ldots,\psi_{n}$ be an $L^2(\pi_G)$-orthonormal basis of eigenfunctions of the transition matrix $P$ of the discrete-time simple random walk on~$G$, and let $\lambda_1,\ldots,\lambda_{n}$ be their corresponding eigenvalues. Further define
\begin{equation} \gamma_l = 1-(1-\theta)\lambda_l
\qquad\mbox{for $l=1,\ldots,n$}\,.
\end{equation}
Then, for every $t>0$,
\begin{align}
\mathcal{A}^{(2)}_t(\mathsf{x}_0) = \frac1q \sum_{k=1}^{q-1} \sum_{v \in V} \pi_G(v)\big|\mathbb{E}_{\mathsf{x}_0}[X_t(v)^k]\big|^2
&= \frac1q \sum_{k=1}^{q-1} \sum_{l=1}^{n} |\langle \mathsf{x}_0^k, \psi_l\rangle_{\pi_G}|^2 e^{-2 \gamma_l t}\,.

\end{align}
Consequently, for any $s \geq 0$, we have
\begin{align}
e^{-(4-2\theta)s}  \leq &\frac{\mathcal{A}^{(2)}_{t+s}(\mathsf{x}_0)}{\mathcal{A}^{(2)}_t(\mathsf{x}_0)} \leq e^{-2\theta s} \,,
\end{align}
and in particular $\frac{q-1}q e^{-(4-2\theta)t} \leq \mathcal{A}^{(2)}_t (\mathsf{x}_0) \leq \frac{q-1}q e^{-2\theta t}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:37.352116+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_801851c8f4fdf8f56c44de6328388bc3d94072d3b86d8d404a1b8122ca023141","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 8 of arXiv:2606.17472, '2606.17472'] If $B=\{a,b\}$ with $a\neq b$, then 
