{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:33:21.479927+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_81c90520c4eb71fa2c698c75f497c48b1dc3b116e8a53088de34df09ba61e308","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Pro Prop_diff_strongly_convex of arXiv:2606.22183, 'Expected loss of quasi-arithmetic means of exchangeable random variables'] Let $I\subseteq \mathbb{R}$ be a nonempty open interval, $\alpha:(I-I)\to\mathbb{R}_+$ be an even function, and $L:I\to \mathbb{R}$ be a differentiable function.
