{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:20:55.608594+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_828cdacb33810e68b9e6ff62311ff97872c4ae8fcda5de5a816fc97cded54ce0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma zygmund-marcinkiewicz of arXiv:2411.07737, 'On Asymptotic Behavior of Extinction Moment of Critical Bisexual Branching Process in Rand'] Let $\{ \xi_n \}_{n = 1}^{\infty}$ be a sequence of i.i.d. r.v. with $\ER \abs*{\xi_n}^{\alpha} < \infty$, where $1 \leq \alpha \leq 2$, and $\ER \xi_n = 0$ for all $n \in \mathbb{N}$.
