{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:19:00.923778+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_84191a9df649949f5dba35fa47dd18117a527378c8bd43170b6d7641aafe3cb5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 27 of arXiv:2608.20613, 'Random walks on wreath products \\and spectral gaps for coloured interchange processes'] Let $G$ be a finite group.  Then the Wedderburn decomposition~\cite[Section~6.2]{Serre} restricts to an algebra isomorphism
