{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:19:47.212579+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_84bdd1bb675885b6275d1bc677b1c3bbfa4c3a483902d22aa7bbdfa64f7d6cdd","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def: nice_vertex of arXiv:2512.06640, 'Existence and sharpness of the phase transition for the frog model on transitive graphs'] Let $B \subseteq V$ be a finite vertex set and $x \in B$. We say $x$ is a \textbf{good} (or $(B, \lambda, t)$-\textbf{good}) vertex if 
