{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:37.363135+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_84cc6c1c994f773c00cdff4d8938f59c890cabd577f711d81472f0c1009447e4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 8 (Large cycles) of arXiv:2606.18047, 'Analysis of the asymmetric shelf shuffle'] Fix $p\in(0,1)$ and $k\geq 1$. Let $m=m_n$ be any sequence of positive integers, fixed or growing with $n$.  If $\pi_n\sim \nu^{(p)}_{n,m_n}$ and $\sigma_n$ is uniform on $S_n$, then
