\big|\mathbb{E}[g(\tilde{X})]-\mathbb{E}[g(X)]\big|\le C\mathbb{E}\big[\big(\kappa(|x_{0}|)+\kappa(|X|)+\kappa(|\tilde{X}|)\big)(|\tilde{X}-X|^{2}+|X-x_{0}||\tilde{X}-X|)\big].
\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:51.769533+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_84f2c7f9f49332adca68c9159bef23278d61d4d0c6fab432c0945bac56bddbe9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm subcritical regime of arXiv:2605.03151, 'Giants through Higher-Order paths in Random Simplicial Complexes'] Let $X_n \sim \MRSC_d(n; \bm{p})$ satisfying Assumption~(assumption: prob parameters of the paper). Assume that $\lambda < 1/d$. Then, for any positive constants $C > d^2/ I_{\lambda}$ and $c < 1/I_{\lambda/2}$, where $I_{\lambda} := \lambda - 1 - \log \lambda$, it holds that
