{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.188883+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_85266c5e8694f8f56c64ddbf2cc9c6708b442448703e9c720a26e9f58be59c25","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:Gibbs-component-two-spin-uniform of arXiv:2603.01322, 'Gibbs conditioning, atypical consensus and splitting Gibbs measures on random regular grap'] Fix $|\X|=2$,  $\nu=\mathsf{Unif}(\X)$, an edge potential $h$, and let $c\in (\k h_{\min},\k h_{\max})$ be such that $\cc\neq\sref$. Then $U_n$ given $\Conset_n(h,\cc)$ lies in $\Gibbsnondeg(\cc)$ asymptotically, where
