{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:06.329992+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_853d41ed05802628bc5d8c8b18c131759eb3957ea8d97d5a5b6cade1fb79d572","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 18 of arXiv:2607.06428, 'Impact of spinning on the early-warning signs in non-Markovian stochastic systems'] Let $H\in\left(0,1\right)$ and $(\mathbf{x}_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be a solution to \eqref{eq:fast system simplified} in the setting \nameref{S2}. For any $\tau\ge0$, it holds that
\begin{align}
    \begin{split}
    &V_\infty(\tau)\left[ \mathbf{e}_{j_1}^*(\lambda), \mathbf{e}_{j_2}^*(\lambda) \right]\\
    =& \left(-\zeta_{j_1}(\lambda)-\overline{\zeta_{j_2}(\lambda)}\right)^{-1} H \left\langle  \mathbf{e}_{j_2}^*(\lambda), Q \mathbf{e}_{j_1}^*(\lambda)\right\rangle P(\zeta_{j_1}(\lambda),\zeta_{j_2}(\lambda),H,\tau) ,
    \end{split}
