{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.022711+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_856e60565fbd6b9fd1c9781c60068ed2f47a0de0a1e27103f5423700e3e52bcc","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 9 (Free independence \cite{NS2006, mingoFreeProbabilityRandom2017}) of arXiv:2606.31528, 'Well-posedness and stationary distribution of free stochastic differential equations'] Subalgebras $\mathscr{A}_1,\dots,\mathscr{A}_m \subset \mathscr{A}$ are said to be \emph{freely independent} if for every $n\in\mathbb{N}$, every choice of indices $i_1,\dots,i_n \in \{1,\dots,m\}$ with $i_k \neq i_{k+1} \text{ for all } k,$
