{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:53:54.855718+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_85cd471a02b5031caac8e7dba913857e5c6d677f536efcf7ddd50d222c0feb86","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2607.16954, 'Repeated differentiation of deterministic polynomials with asymptotically radial root dist'] Consider positive integers $k,l\leq n$  such that when $n\to\infty$ we have $1-k/n\to \alpha$ and $l/n\to t$. In the case $\Delta<0$, we assume
