{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:59:45.016038+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_87dbbd19dcdc8c00179c6b164cd4306d5c678d1881b42a615d7775b53f5fec0d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:growth_f_implies_assumption of arXiv:2605.15401, 'Noise Tradeoffs, Stationary Information Flow, and Structural Balance in Unit-Birth Network'] Consider the continuous time Markov chain on $S=\mathbb{Z}_{\ge0}^N$ with generator
(equation eq:generator of the paper). Assume there exists $\varepsilon\in(0,1)$ such that
