        x\longmapsto\max\{x,U_x+X_t'\},
\end{equation}
where $U_x$ is uniform on $\{0,\ldots,x\}$ and $X_t'$ is independent of $U_x$ with the law of $X_t$. Null changes are allowed. The process is increasing and is sent to $\infty$ when its graphical range becomes infinite.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:48:17.124202+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_880dab9b7a88c242abf0dfec1bbd928bb0b1001ca7007db3ddc99f347264917f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 3 of arXiv:2605.27742, 'Multidimensional Stein's method for asymptotic independence with invariant measures of dif'] Define, for all $x \in (l, u)$,
