{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.580203+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_88338cce89c1fdab70763a4665d170a21d9dc1d206ded484f93013857debab2b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 29 of arXiv:2606.14876, 'High-Order Talagrand and Eldan--Gross Inequalities via Besov-Type Variance Functionals'] For all $J\subseteq [n]$, $f:\cube^n\to \Rbb$, $p\in [1,2]$ and $q\in [1,2)$,
