{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:42:08.471644+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_88e9f2e501403d7d4d399930f3dabe6b0e6825d525236d85336677faa78b1011","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition Proposition3 of arXiv:2511.19391, 'Central limit theorem for supercritical Crump-Mode-Jagers processes counted with non-indiv'] Suppose that (A1 of the paper)-(A7 of the paper) hold and that $\varphi$ is an $h$-dependent descendant characteristic, for some $h \in \mathbb{N}_{0}$,  satisfying (C1 of the paper)-(C3 of the paper). Then, for every $t \in \mathbb{R}$, 
