{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.232504+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8911ed2b08c43ce5f58863b335e59abdb8859feec63bb153b1eb1df156d09498","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 38 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] Let $\UC$ denote the space of upper semi-continuous functions $f \colon \R \rightarrow \R \cup \{ -\infty\}$ such that for some $x\in \R$, $f(x)\neq -\infty$ and such that there exists some constants $m,C>0$ so that for all $x\in \R$
$f(x) \leq m |x| + C$. For any $\mathfrak{h}_0 \in \UC$ and $\mathcal{L}$ an independent (of $\mathfrak{h}_0$) full-space directed landscape, we define the \textbf{full-space KPZ fixed point} with initial data $\mathfrak{h}_0$ as the random function $(y,t) \mapsto \hfix(\mathfrak{h}_0;y,t)$, where
\begin{equation}
\hfix(\mathfrak{h}_0;y,t) := \sup_{x\in \R} \big(\mathfrak{h}_0(x) + \mathcal{L}(x,0;y,t)\big).
\end{equation} For multiple initial data this provides a coupling of full-space KPZ fixed points.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:26:26.799333+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_891a5b45e6b3b8443b59f0f67daeffba7ac0138ea7b51ed6f52f5878f8c3a709","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:cc-gaussian-flip-probabilities of arXiv:2608.06159, 'Majority Dynamics on Resampled Sparse Erd\H{o}s--R\'enyi Graphs:\\[0.5ex] Gaussian Winner '] Recall \(x_t^{\gR},x_t^{\gB}\) from
    (equation eqn:standardized-degree-difference-definitions of the paper). Fix \(c_0>0\)
    and \(M<\infty\), condition on \(\rvy_t\), and suppose that
    \begin{align}
    |\gR_t|\ge c_0N,
    \qquad
    |\gB_t|\ge c_0N,

    \end{align}
    while $x_t^{\gR}$ and $x_t^{\gB}$ in (equation eqn:standardized-degree-difference-definitions of the paper) satisfy
    \begin{align}
    |x_t^{\gR}|\le M,
    \qquad
    |x_t^{\gB}|\le M.

    \end{align}
    Then, uniformly over such configurations,
    \begin{subequations}
    \begin{align}
    p_t^{\gR}
    &=
    \Phi\left(
    x_t^{\gR}-\frac{1}{2\sqrt{v_t^{\gR}}}
    \right)
    +O\left(\frac1{\log N}\right),
    \\
    p_t^{\gB}
    &=
    \Phi\left(
    x_t^{\gB}-\frac{1}{2\sqrt{v_t^{\gB}}}
    \right)
    +O\left(\frac1{\log N}\right).

    \end{align}
    \end{subequations}
    For \(\Delta_t\ge1\), there are constants \(c,C>0\) such that
    \begin{align}
    c\frac{p\Delta_t}{\sqrt{(N-1)p(1-p)}}
    \le
    p_t^{\gR}-p_t^{\gB}
    \le
    C\frac{p\Delta_t}{\sqrt{(N-1)p(1-p)}}.

    \end{align}
    Furthermore, for every fixed \(C_0<\infty\), when
    \(0\le\Delta_t\le C_0\sqrt{N/\log N}\), we have
    \begin{align}
    p_t^{\gR}-p_t^{\gB}
    =
    \sqrt{\frac{2}{\pi}}
    \frac{p\Delta_t}{\sqrt{(N-1)p(1-p)}}
    +O\left(\frac{p\Delta_t}{\log N}\right).

    \end{align}
