{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:36:23.147371+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_89e282fdeeb06a11719013e31ce8f4793ad90095d24c4d02cb4ac744c924e3ae","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:main of arXiv:2507.16188, 'The noisy voter model with general initial conditions'] Fix $\theta\in(0,1]$ and $q\geq2$. Let $G=(V,E)$ be a connected graph on $n$ vertices satisfying (eq:expansion of the paper) for some $\mathfrak{c}_0>0$ and $\upalpha\in(0,1)$, and let $\mathsf{x}_0$ be an arbitrary initial condition. Then the $q$-state noisy voter model on $G$  
