with $\Phi$ associated to $\varphi$ as in (equation eq:Phidef of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:30:50.728711+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b1238026b2276b29a58b79d939ee33c64677a4b645851b7c47df756628477e0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm moment of arXiv:2503.22334, 'Probabilistic analysis of optimal multi-pivot QuickSort'] Let $K\in {\mathbb N}$. For the number $X_n$ of key comparisons using optimal $K$-pivot QuickSort we have 
  \begin{equation}
    {\mathbb E}\left[X_n\right] = \alpha_K n\ln n + \beta_K n + o(n) \quad (n\to\infty),
  \end{equation}
with a constant $\beta_K \in \mathbb{R}$ and $\alpha_K= \gamma_K/(H_{K+1}-1)$, where $H_n := \sum_{i=1}^n \frac1i$ are the harmonic numbers. In the case of $K≤4$, the error term $o(n)$ can be replaced by $\mathrm{O}(\log n)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:30.968108+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b1802265f700b0cc6dcd4ed2952505634646562652de180a7db6a7ca406af55","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 27 of arXiv:2608.12291, 'When should one stop the most exciting game?\\ {\tiny Sequential Inference for win-marting'] The value function $V_T$ satisfies
