{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.450097+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b476686fdf36ccee5897d33927a544199bda0f8aa53df0f145d9753cc6382fb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary eq:coexistence-ratio of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[corollary]{cor:coexistence}
Fix \(p\ge3\), \(\sigma>1\), and let \(\mu_{p,\sigma}\) be the law from
(thm:counterexample of the paper).  For every fixed \(L,\varepsilon>0\),
\(V\in\mathcal V_{2p}\), and either \(f\in\mathcal F_{2p}\) or
\(f=\ell_\eta\) for fixed \(\eta>0\),
\begin{equation}
 \frac{\mathbb E_{\mu_{p,\sigma}}\mathcal Z_{N,L}^J(V,\varepsilon,f)}
 {\mathbb E\mathcal Z_{N,L}^G(V,\varepsilon,f)}
 \longrightarrow1.
\end{equation}
The same holds for the point-incoherent functional.  Nevertheless, for
the compact interval \(B\) supplied by (thm:counterexample of the paper),
\begin{equation}
 \liminf_{N\to\infty}\frac1N\log
 \mathbb E_{\mu_{p,\sigma}}\operatorname{Crt}_N^J(B)
 >
 \lim_{N\to\infty}\frac1N\log\mathbb E\operatorname{Crt}_N^G(B).
\end{equation}
Both conclusions, as well as the local-maximum and local-minimum
versions of (equation eq:coexistence-exact of the paper), remain valid for the standard
symmetric-coordinate model (equation eq:symmetric-coordinate-model of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.573388+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8b536a0fbf12d7900f5b4d0b354bcb2c55c06d3f0312299640d98060dce4d545","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 27 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d\geq 4$. There exists $C>0$ such that the following holds. For every $n\geq 1$, there exists $S\subset \Lambda_n$ containing $0$ which satisfies the following properties:
