{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:36:23.147622+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8be3f88dc8bc66cf00cb331f42dd644595a56f2c9edd4f150c97f98094555a27","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:rainbow of arXiv:2507.16188, 'The noisy voter model with general initial conditions'] Let $G = \mathbb{Z}_n$. There exists $c>0$ such that, for every $q\geq 3$, every $\theta\in(0,1]$ and every initial state $\mathsf{x}_0$,
