{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:32:18.857309+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8f9ffb99cf45773119f98bfdbb798764759fa94eae05199cb3db409426fa5f3b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 18 of arXiv:2609.03875, 'Measure theory without infinities'] Let $\fm{\Theta}{\Lambda}$ be a family of sets such that $A\cap B\in \Theta(\lambda)\cap\Theta(\lambda')$ for every $\lambda,\lambda'\in \Lambda$, $A\in\Theta(\lambda)$, and $B\in\Theta(\lambda')$. Let $\mathcal Q = \bigcup_{\lambda\in \Lambda} \Theta(\lambda)$.
