{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:01:15.328112+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_8fc58e74cdffb234347570689aad1f785d07e6f535fc07d0cde2a2c33ee014de","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theo 6 of arXiv:2608.30357, 'Mean convergence for Banach space-valued random elements indexed in measure spaces'] Let $\{h(n) : n \ge 1\} \subset [0, \infty)$ and $p \in [1, \infty)$. Assume that $\{X^n_s : s \in S_n, n \ge 1\}$ is $(\nu_n)$-$\UI(p)$ w.r.t. $\{h(n)\}$. If
