{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.371335+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9023b8722e135abfae69e03a94db77063a47de99fb2d439b8f0bb83fd40e53eb","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 14 of arXiv:2606.03661, '2606.03661'] Let $X_{i},i=1,2,...$ be real, independent random variables, under the assumption that $X_{i}$ is independent of $N_{\alpha,\nu}$, for any $i=1,2,...$; then we define the CTRW $\left\{Y_{\alpha, \nu}(t)  \right\}_{t \geq 0},$ where 
