{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:01:15.328395+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9025aa08a475562da26007845ad5bb8f2d6e193caf1cac9780c0ce4a62c39778","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 9 (Diagonal negative dependence) of arXiv:2608.30357, 'Mean convergence for Banach space-valued random elements indexed in measure spaces'] \mbox{ }
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
\item Two $\cX$-valued random elements $X, Y$ are said to be \textit{diagonally negatively dependent} if 
\begin{align}
\bP(X \in A, Y \in A) \le \bP(X \in A)\,\bP(Y \in A), \quad \forall A \in \cB(\cX),
\end{align}
or equivalently,
$\Cov(\1_{\{X \in A\}}, \1_{\{Y \in A\}}) \le 0$ for all $A \in \cB(\cX)$.

\item Let $\varnothing \neq I \subseteq \bR$ and $M \in \bN \cup \{0\}$.
A family $\{Y_i : i \in I\}$ of $\cX$-valued random elements is \textit{$M$-pairwise diagonally negatively dependent} if $Y_i, Y_j$ are diagonally negatively dependent for all $i, j \in I$ with $|i-j|>M$.
When $M=0$, we then simply call $\{Y_i : i \in I\}$ \textit{pairwise diagonally negatively dependent}.

\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:41:28.164798+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9025d47000c413fcaa66fd8c8c41a79c565a41c4b3629eb6a31ec4f4b78da6e2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem T_pc of arXiv:2510.26724, 'Sharp Fuss-Catalan thresholds in graph bootstrap percolation'] Fix $r\geqslant5$. Let $\gamma>0$ be the unique positive root of
\begin{equation}
(r-2)!\gamma^{r-2} = \alpha_{{r\choose2}-2}\,.
\end{equation}
Then, for every $\varepsilon>0$,
\[
\mathbb P(\langle \mathcal G_{n,p}\rangle_{K_r}=K_n) \to \left\{
\begin{matrix}
0,&\text{if }\gamma np^\lambda =1 -\varepsilon;\\
1,&\text{if }\gamma np^\lambda =1+\varepsilon, 
\end{matrix}
\right.
\]
as $n\to\infty$. In particular,
\[
p_c(n,K_r)\sim (\gamma n)^{-1/\lambda}.
\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

