  \end{equation*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:43:16.150767+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9087c79f28c5fb14bd59ce084d4e00717ad29931dd97e0e3dcc8c9fc48dd40f1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2604.13454, 'Invariant and periodic measures in classical spin systems on infinite lattices with highly'] For arbitrary $\epsilon>0$ and $t,\delta\in (0,\infty)\bigcap\mathbb{Q}$, there exists a constant $N(t,\delta,\epsilon)\in\mathbb{N}$ such that 
