{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:52:08.675035+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_90b831db2e4f491727926252927ba4d6141552220605e4cf31bcac4fa6d0618b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 47 (Uniform lifted Ricci--DeTurck continuous dependence) of arXiv:2608.30027, 'Under Ricci flow, a 3-torus goes flat'] Fix \(N\geq2\) and \(\sigma\in(0,1)\).  Let \(s(t)\), \(a\leq t\leq b\),
