{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:33:12.346504+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_917788973670463b18372b7da8d322856f9e865c1d7fe37a974435933ac49507","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 145 of arXiv:2608.29416, 'Algorithmic threshold for high-dimensional projection pursuit I: general theory'] Let $U^k$ be the state evolution limits from \eqref{e:state.evol.U}, and let $Y$ be the solution of the SDE \eqref{e:IAMP.Y.SDE}.  Then, for all $0\le \ell\le\ubl-1$, we have
  \beq
  \bigg|\frac{\E[(U^{\ell+1}-U^\ell)^2
  ]^{1/2}}{\delta^{1/2}}
  - \E w^\ell
    (Y(q_0+\ell\delta)) \bigg|
  \le C\delta^{1/4}
  +C_0\epsilon^{1/2}
  \,,\eeq
where $C=C(L,\alpha)$ while $C_0=C_0(\alpha)$.
As a consequence, for $\gamma$ and $\prxgamma$ as defined by \eqref{eq:proxy-C-ell-delta-def}, we have
  \[\max\bigg\{
  \Big|\gamma(\ell,\delta)-
  \E w^\ell
    (Y(q_0+\ell\delta))\Big|
  ,\Big|\prxgamma(\ell,\delta)-
  \E w^\ell
    (Y(q_0+\ell\delta))\Big|
    \bigg\}
  \le C\delta^{1/4}
  +C_0\epsilon^{1/2}
  \]
for all $0\le\ell\le\ubl-1$.

\begin{proof}
We apply the state evolution recursion \eqref{eq:state-evolution-setup}, where $f_{\ell,k}$ and $a_{i,\ell,k}$ are defined by \eqref{e:u.ellp1.decomp} and \eqref{e:f.l.k.explicit}:
  \begin{align*}
  f_{\ell,k}(V[[\ell]], X[0])
  &= \ind\{k\le\ell\}
  a_k (M^\ell-M^{k-1})
