{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.974868+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_91a042a04ba66a5fb810aae82e97ac03789793acd97d51c90a3de6e84ca8cc7f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 8 of arXiv:2606.11142, 'Strong invariance principles for diffusions, Markov chains and their perturbations.'] (Theorem 1.3 from \cite{KozhinaThesis}). Fix $T > 0$ and let us define a time-grid $\mathbb{T}_N := \{t_i\}_{i=1}^N$ for $N \in \mathbb{N}$. Under assumptions A1, A2, AD3 there exist constants $C \ge 1$ and $c \in (0, 1]$ such that for all $0 < t_i < t_j \le T$ and all $((x, y), (x', y')) \in (\mathbb{R}^{2d})^2$:
\begin{equation*}
|(p^\epsilon_h - p_h)(t_i, t_j, (x, y), (x', y'))| \le C \bar{\Delta}_{\epsilon,\gamma,q} \, p_{c,K}(t_j - t_i, (x, y), (x', y')),
\end{equation*}
where $p_{\epsilon,h}$ and $p_h$ stand for the transition densities of the perturbed and original Euler schemes respectively, starting from $(x, y)$ at time $t_i$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.529253+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_91a48a49a28b29cec580e052c71176d21902078392cfd112b0cb12a192c3d400","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:profile-sharp-subg of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[definition]{def:profile-sharp-subg}
We say that the random field satisfies \(({\rm PSG})_p\) if, for every
\(N\), \(x\in\mathbb S^{N-1}(1)\), and \(s\in\mathbb R\),
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb E e^{s h_N^J(x)}\le e^{s^2/(2N)}.
\end{equation}
This rank-one/profile-direction bound is a convenient finite-\(N\)
sufficient condition for the weaker tail-rate input below.","status":"unverified"}

