{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:16:46.769407+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_92559bc3edd78416577f3005cd30fc2a63a55976f77e8fd6d2c1447941ca1163","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi smooth of arXiv:2411.19543, 'Feller property and convergence for semigroups of time-changed processes'] {Revuz}}}}]
{\rm Let $\nu$ be a $\sigma$-finite Borel measure. We say that $\nu$ is \emph{smooth (in the strict sense)} if:
\begin{enumerate}
\item[\rm(1)] $\nu$ does not charge any semi-polar sets.
\item[\rm(2)] There exists an increasing sequence of Borel sets 
$\{E_n\}$ such that $X=\bigcup_{n=1}^{\infty}E_n$ and 
\begin{enumerate}
\item[\rm(a)] $\nu(E_n)<\infty$ for each $n\in\mathbb{N}$.
\item[\rm(b)] $\int_{E_n}G_1(x,y)d\nu(y)$ is bounded with respect to $x$.
\item[\rm(c)] Let $T_n:=\sigma_{X\setminus E_n}$ and $T:=\lim_{n\to\infty}T_n$. Then, it should hold 
\begin{align*}
\mathbb{P}_x(T\geq\zeta)=1\quad\text{ for any }\quad x\in X.
\end{align*}
\end{enumerate}
\end{enumerate}
}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:08.848853+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_926ad27731f9fc0cd8940e0030dad45ccee07946f5bc2f29eceabb7e790a857b","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defination 7 of arXiv:2511.10814, '\Large \bf \boldmath\ \\ Convergence of the extended Kalman filter with small and state-de'] Let  $(A(t))_{t\ge 0}$  be  a family  of  measurable  locally  bounded processes with  values in the class of  $n \times n $  matrices, let $\zeta $  be  the matrix-valued  solution of \begin{equation}
				\dot{\zeta}(t)= A(t) \zeta(t),~~~\zeta(0)= I.
			\end{equation}

			\noindent	 We will  say  that $(A(t))_{t\ge 0}$  is  \textbf{exponentially  stable} if there  exist  some positive  constants  $C$  and $c$    such  that for $s \leq t$,
			\begin{equation} 
				\vert \zeta(t)\vert\leq C e^{ (- c(t-s))} \vert \zeta(s) \vert.
			\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:34:45.616859+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_927405272840421e0294ef3dd043ebca4c6135450888aefec02a6172c298dfd3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem main_theorem_toric of arXiv:2609.01825, 'On everywhere locally soluble varieties \\ in families over toric bases'] Let $X$ be a smooth, projective, split toric variety over $\mathbb{Q}$ of Picard rank $\rho\ge 2$ with open orbit $U$, and let $\pi\colon Y\to X$ be as in (constr:family-over-toric-base of the paper). Write $\Delta = \sum_{d\in \mathcal{D}} \Delta_d$ and assume (eq:affine-asymp of the paper) for $i\in \mathcal{I}$. If $-\vec \Delta$ is of convergent type, then the number 
	\begin{equation*}
		N(B) = \sharp\{x\in U(\mathbb{Q}) : Y_x(\mathbb{A}_\mathbb{Q})\ne \emptyset,\ H(x)\le B\}
	\end{equation*}
	of everywhere locally soluble fibres satisfies
	\begin{equation*}
		N(B) = c B (\log B)^{\rho-1-\Delta} + O_\pi \!\left(B (\log B)^{\rho-1-\Delta-\varepsilon}\right),
	\end{equation*}
	where
	\begin{equation*}
		c= \frac{\alpha(X)}{2^{n+\rho}}  \omega_\infty \prod_p  \left( 1-\frac{1}{p}\right)^{\rho}\frac{|\mathfrak{X}(\mathbb{F}_p)|}{p^n} \prod_{d\in \mathcal{D}} c_d a_d^{\Delta_d},
	\end{equation*}
    and $\varepsilon >0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.849438+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9288541ad56cd6c88a02113f3523337624e7200a9f95de4f1fb58c8200719277","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:cmf_wna of arXiv:2606.11951, 'On Skorokhod Problems for Reflected and Singular Stochastic Heat Equations'] For any $f \in L^2(\mathbb{R})$, the image measure $T_{+f}^{\mathcal{S}'}(\mu)$ of $\mu$ under the translation $T_{+f}^{\mathcal{S}'}$ is absolutely continuous w.r.t.\ $\mu$, and its Radon--Nikodym derivative is given by
	\begin{equation*}
		\frac{dT_{+f}^{\mathcal{S}'}(\mu)}{d\mu} = \exp\left( \langle f, \cdot \rangle - \frac{1}{2} \| f \|_{L^2(\mathbb{R})} \right).
	\end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:54:34.580039+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_92a4edf2dcfd69e67d3d11b98cf0a7c78cbd9327f8b3dac4bd1134407fd093ac","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 27 of arXiv:2606.14876, 'High-Order Talagrand and Eldan--Gross Inequalities via Besov-Type Variance Functionals'] For all $k\in \Nbb$, $f\in \Sob^k(\Rbb^n,\gamma_n)$, $q\in [1,2)$ and $t\geq 0$,
\begin{equation}
    \Vop^k(\Pop_t f) \leq \upe^{-2kt} \Vop^k(f)^{1-\vartheta} \min\left\{\Vop^k(f),\,\left\|\left|\grad^k f\right|\right\|_{\Leb^q}^{2},\, \sum_{\kappa\in \Nbb^n:|\kappa|=k}\left\|\Dop^\kappa f\right\|_{\Leb^q}^2\right\}^{\vartheta},
\end{equation}
and further for all $\kappa\in \Nbb^n$ with $|\kappa|=k$,
\begin{equation}
    \Vop^\kappa(\Pop_t f) \leq \upe^{-2kt} \Vop^\kappa(f)^{1-\vartheta} \min\left\{\Vop^\kappa(f),\,\left\|\Dop^\kappa f\right\|_{\Leb^q}^2\right\}^{\vartheta},
\end{equation}
where $\vartheta=\vartheta(q,t) := \min\left\{\frac{q}{2-q}\tanh(t), 1\right\}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.083411+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_92a58ebefbeb8013aa3bbffdc15d6115619306b5bcb2406da429e8802724b4bd","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition ContainerTheoremE of arXiv:2411.12522, 'Canonical insurance models: stochastic equations and comparison theorems'] For $Y \in \mathbb{Y}$, the processes  $Y^i$, $i \in \mathcal{Z}$, defined by 
