	\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:52:47.254393+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9329d34565994684dc9f65583475192cca5f7c5e6266cf6976b7c91480df7bd0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 3 of arXiv:2609.01101, '2609.01101'] Let $K$ be a fixed number field, let $L$ be its Galois closure, and set
$$
G=\Gal(L/\Q),\qquad H=\Gal(L/K),\qquad
\rho_K=|H\backslash G/H|.
$$
Assume GRH for $\zeta_L$.  Then, for every fixed real $k>0$ and all
sufficiently large $T$,
