{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:46:09.856093+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_932c68b7f8a4bb64cf52bb46ef5d03084103139097664990853df39d27bc869e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 11 of arXiv:2605.20115, 'Moment bounds on correctors for the degenerate random conductance model'] Under the assumptions of Theorem~\ref{thm.main},  if $\gamma \ge C_2$, the correctors satisfy, for all $x\in \Z^d$,
    \begin{equation}
        \expecb{|(\phi,\sigma)(x)-(\phi,\sigma)(0)|^{\frac\gamma{C_1}}}^\frac{C_1}{\gamma}\lesssim_{ \Lambda }( \gamma\Gamma)^{C_0} \left\{
        \begin{aligned}
            &\sqrt{ |x|},\quad &\text{ if }d=1;\\
            &\log^\frac12(1+|x|),\quad &\text{ if }d=2;\\
            &1,\quad &\text{ if }d\ge3.
        \end{aligned}\right.
    \end{equation}
Hence, if $d\ge3$, there is a unique stationary solution $(\phi,\sigma)$ to the equations \eqref{eq.corrector} and \eqref{eq.flux} such that $\expec{(\phi,\sigma)}=0$. In this case, 
    \begin{equation}
        \expec{|(\phi,\sigma)|^{\frac\gamma{C_1}}}^{\frac{C_1}\gamma}\lesssim_{ \Lambda }( \gamma\Gamma)^{C_0}.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:38:08.414370+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9331d30cfb330b861ce2e198df8aae1a61fb2834eccb7b20070ea727fa97094f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor: approx of A from estimate at p-1 of arXiv:2609.02073, 'Existence of closed non-planar $p$-elasticae'] For every $\gamma \in (1,2)$, there exists $\bar \varepsilon_\gamma>0$ such that for $(\lambda,C^2) \in S^0$ with $|p-1-\lambda|<\bar \varepsilon_\gamma$ 
