 where $\big(\textnormal{\textsf{Gau\ss{}}}(z_i)\big)_{i = 1}^{n}$ is a centered random Gaussian vector with covariance matrix $(\mathcal{F}(z_i,z_j))_{i,j = 1}^{n}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:09:15.297404+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_93b8ff22b202a0421662679fb75d2ff470b2907c67a8dcf768284f48f16e6a11","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem of arXiv:2411.05534, 'Inverse problems for stochastic partial differential equations'] For any $ t_{0} \in (0,T) $,
