{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:23:27.788207+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94114c676ebc6001fb5fadd0d3ebd532f133834bb09340264d989fda17363d92","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor clt:I_n of arXiv:2606.09228, 'On topological indices of random caterpillar graphs'] Let $I^{(n)}:=\left(I_1^{(n)},\dots,I_m^{(n)}\right)\overset{d}{=}M(n;1/m,\dots,1/m)$. Then, with $\mu^{(n)}=(n/m,\ldots,n/m)^t$, we have
