{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.758766+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_947b0da7c1072170d0e19fc24ba5badb6360266b6a9c90957d7562d5e961feb0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma derivative_of_edge of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] In the setting of (def_moving_Lambda of the paper), suppose $\Lambda_t=f\left({t}\right)\Lambda$ for some differentiable function $f\in C^1(\left[{a,b}\right])$. Then, we have    \begin{equation}
