{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:18:19.446396+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_94802180bc515d4f21b514123f1e4d7fd38b849a6be895c79c14d96686f1d4a0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary coro:sign_d_regular of arXiv:2508.17838, '\bf Edge Universality for Inhomogeneous Random Matrices'] Let $G_N$ be the adjacency matrix of a $d$-regular graph on $N$ vertices,   assume $d\gg N^{2/3+\tau}$ for some fixed $\tau>0$ and $|\lambda_2(G_N)|,|\lambda_N(G_N)|=o(d)$.  Then edge universality holds for the extreme eigenvalues of $\sigma\circ G_N$. In particular, the rescaled largest eigenvalue converges weakly to $\mathrm{TW}_1$ which  has  the Tracy-Widom $F_1$ distribution, that is, 
