uniformly in $t\in [0,T]$ and $z=z_T\in\mathcal{D}$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.425999+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_96f06bfd2b3c8d268b4a725548aac38231d4e36f762b5cee110ac6cedd0ada41","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 171 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Fix $\hat{A} > 0$, $\hat{B}=\hat{C}>0$, and suppose that the vertical line at distance $\hat{\mathfrak t} \in (0,\hat{B} + \hat{C})$ from the left border of $\hat{A}\times \hat{B}\times \hat{C}$ hexagon does not pass through any of the tangency point of the inscribed ellipse. There exists $\tilde D_0>0$ such that, for any $\hat{D} \in [0,\hat{D}_0]$ and with the choice of $\hat{\mathfrak{h}}$ making the parameters symmetric, the simplified equilibrium measure $\tilde{\boldsymbol{\mu}}$ for the potential \eqref{eq_x284} has two bands $(\alpha_1,\beta_1)$ and $(\alpha_2,\beta_2)$ satisfying strict inequalities
 \begin{equation}

 \hat a'_1<\alpha_1<\beta_1<\hat b'_1<\hat a'_2<\alpha_2<\beta_2<\hat b'_2.
