then the solution $\{U_t\}_{t\ge 0}$ admits a unique stationary distribution $\mu$. Moreover, for any initial value, the distribution of $U_t$ converges to $\mu$ in $W_2$ as $t \to \infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:34:45.627289+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_976cb6dfc764f6e97cf1f92cd9a845fac73d50847d2455bf6463b8cdb78d2ace","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:FaceIntegralAsymptotic of arXiv:2609.01825, 'On everywhere locally soluble varieties \\ in families over toric bases'] Let $\vec\ell$ be of convergent type for the face $\cal F$ and assume that $\cal F$ is not contained in a coordinate hyperplane. Then there exists $\epsilon >0$ such that we have

