{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.329124+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_981840435c564e114b5bbfc99c6572f30a6dd1313237a2e4003b5651cffdde46","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition eq:cf_tempered of arXiv:2412.06374, 'Stable and tempered stable distributions and processes: an overview toward trajectory simu'] Let $(X_t)_{t\in \mathbb{R}}$ be a CTS Lévy process with Lévy triplet $\left(b_\nu, 0,\nu\right)$ where $\nu$ defined as in (equation eq:levy_measure_tempered_stable of the paper) and $b_\nu=\int_{|x|>1}x \nu(dx)$. For $t\in \mathbb{R}_+$, the characteristic function exponent can be expressed for $u\in \mathbb{R}$ as 
