{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:54:18.299912+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_983c740de20860406affa4457766853bb730610ed846eecc821962beac40f5cc","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma le:neg_mom_1 of arXiv:2608.30382, 'Convergence rates for the RMSprop optimizer with full control of the hyperparameters'] Let $c,q,\rho\in(0,\infty)$, $p\in[1,\infty)$, $\beta \in (0, 1) $, $ n, n_0 \in {\mathbb N} $ satisfy
\begin{align}\begin{split} 
q+p\ln\beta\ge \rho
 \end{split}\end{align}
and $n> n_0$. 
Let $V_n^*$ be a non-negative random variable which satisfies for all $ \lambda \in [0,\infty) $ that
\bas{
  - \ln \mathbb{E}\bigl[ e^{-\lambda V_n^*} \bigr]
  \ge \sum_{k=n_0+1}^n \left( c \frac{1-\beta}{1-\beta^n} \beta^{n-k} \lambda \right) \wedge q + c \frac{1-\beta^{n_0}}{1-\beta^n} \beta^{n-n_0} \lambda.
}
Then \bas{
{\mathbb E}[(V_n^*)^{-p}]&\le \frac1{c^p} D_{\rho,p},
}
where
\bas{

  D_{\rho,p}:=\sum_{r=0}^\infty (r+1)^p e^{-\rho r}<\infty.
}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:29:14.942173+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_985263737fd755f4f39a593e3290f9576291ab0edb3a0a9c2913ca500ec906aa","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma LemmaErgodicity of arXiv:2606.13615, 'Data-Driven Subsampling Rates for Diffusion Parameter Estimation of SDEs'] Let $K$ be a Markov kernel on $(\mathbb{R}^d, \mathcal{B}(\mathbb{R}^d))$ with invariant measure $\mu$ and let $\mathbf{Z} = (\mathbf{Z}_n)_{n \in \mathbb{N}_0}$ be a homogeneous Markov chain with kernel $K$ and initial distribution $\mathbf{Z}_0 \sim \mu$. Then $\mathbf{Z}$ is ergodic if and only if
