{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:57:16.053248+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_98679b5c5be05a8f8dcb020e7b60fa886caa63b96939eb356a4f2d974bb3cb77","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:dimhofintersectionwithsublevelset of arXiv:2506.10448, 'Hitting probabilities and the Ekstr\"om--Persson conjecture'] Let $\mu\in \mathcal{P}(\mathbb{R}^d)$ and $t>0$ with $D_\mu(t) \neq \emptyset$. Then, almost surely, for every $\alpha>0$ with $t-F_\mu(t)<\frac 1\alpha \leq t$, we have that
