{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:32:28.995555+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_98c060f5aa92d412084b69a23e23c089da1759fb0f7e2e3ddffc40dd311b3757","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm T typ gau of arXiv:2608.25471, 'Exact Hausdorff measures and fine geometry of collisions of independent Markov processes'] There exist deterministic constants $c_1,c_2\in(0,\infty)$ such that,
