{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:31:45.388842+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_98c8d69ae48921fa85a22b9936854e3144cddf05839261443919bc5ed7461d9b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:error 1 part of arXiv:2412.06452, 'Time-dependent queue length distribution in queues fed by $K$ customers in a finite interv'] \red{
Suppose that for a given $\epsilon_0 \in (0,1]$,
the truncation points $M_n$ ($n=1,2,\ldots,N$) are chosen such that

\begin{align}
\sum_{m=0}^{M_n-K}
\mathrm{Poi}\bigl(\theta_n(T_n-T_{n-1}),m\bigr)
> 1-\epsilon_0,
\quad 
n = 1,2,\ldots,N.

\end{align}

We then have}

\begin{align}
&
(1-\epsilon_0)^n \Pr[\widehat{A}(t)=k] 
< 
\hat{p}_k^{\mathrm{trunc}}(t) 
\leq
\Pr[\widehat{A}(t)=k],
\nonumber
\\
&\hspace{10em}
k=0,1,\ldots,K,\ t \in (T_{n-1},T_n],\ n=1,2,\ldots,N.

\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

