{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:31:02.828436+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9a0de8527b82a3a12f7768286d8bf575af20fec6251f0c944f7a0261f0640df5","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:group-exponent-dichotomy of arXiv:2609.01690, 'Iterated-sumset spectra: The complete exponent law and its rank geometry'] Let $G$ be an abelian group and fix $k\geq4$.
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\roman*)}]
\item If $G$ has unbounded exponent, then
\begin{equation}
 |\mathcal R_G(h,k)|=h^{k-1+o_k(1)}
 \qquad(h\to\infty).
\end{equation}
\item If $mG=0$ for some positive integer $m$, then
\begin{equation}
 |\mathcal R_G(h,k)|\leq m^{k-1}
 \qquad(h\geq1).
\end{equation}
\end{enumerate}
 Consequently, when $|G|\geq k$, the spectrum sizes are bounded in $h$ if
 and only if $G$ has bounded exponent.  The bounded-exponent case has
 logarithmic growth exponent $0$, while the unbounded-exponent case has
 exponent $k-1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.090981+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9a1c33ce58c82cff2736c06c6850b6dc4ec72875a12a8f6178c4a66019d454d9","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Def1 definition:snaketrajectory of arXiv:2411.12717, 'Excursion theory for Markov processes indexed by Lévy trees'] Fix ${\mathrm{w}} \in \mathcal{W}_E$. A continuous function  $\omega:\mathbb{R}_+ \to \mathcal{W}_E$   started at  $\omega_0 = {\mathrm{w}}$
 and  satisfying for any $s,t \geq 0$,  that 
  \begin{equation}
    \omega_{s}(r) = \omega_{t}(r),  \quad \quad  \text{ for every } \, \,  0 \leq r \leq m_{\zeta(\omega)}(s ,t),
\end{equation}
will be referred to as a snake trajectory started from ${\mathrm{w}}$.  We denote  the collection of snake trajectories started from  ${\mathrm{w}}$ by $\mathcal{S}^\circ_{{\mathrm{w}}}$, and we write  
\begin{equation*}
