{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.618121+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b07c7b28c3807fba35e0a421d19ef82de882b9be9d66ea25d6f058261306e36","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 36 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] Given any~$\sigma\in(0,1/10)$, $a\ge0$ and with $\gamma_{n,a}$ as in \eqref{E:6.34ii}, for $k\le n$ let
