{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:48:30.917895+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b2a1187540fea6197ec0449e21cd6e776b57c23126e6fb09bd6c459c511fc53","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Conj 6 (Algebraic Integrability Conjecture) of arXiv:2609.00974, 'On Algebraic Integrability\\ of Vector Fields \\ with Rational Function Coefficients\\ tha'] Let $K/\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(x_1,\ldots,x_n)$ be an algebraic extension of fields. Let $\F$ be a foliation on $K$, which admits a model over the ring of integers $\cO_L$, where $L$ is a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$.

    The following are equivalent:
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item The foliation $\F$ is algebraically integrable, i.e., it is of the form $\F=\op{Der}_{W}(K)$ for a subfield $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\subset W\subset K$.
        \item For almost all primes $p$ and all maximal ideals $q$ over $p$ in $\cO_L$ the reduction modulo $q$ of $\F$ is $p$-closed, i.e., it defines a $1$-foliation.
    \end{enumerate} (Stated as a conjecture by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)","status":"unverified"}

