{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:51:11.491921+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b926a5112c9bf67fb1ccfc77c946222bf8acddc6f84b2910cce70b6beed26aa","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Mainthm 1 of arXiv:2609.02576, 'Sharp estimates for the Jacobi and trigonometric Dunkl heat kernels'] Let $k_1,k_2\geq 0$ be such that $k_1+k_2>0$. The $W$-invariant Opdam--Cherednik heat kernel satisfies the bound
