	uniformly in $t>0$ and $x,y>0$, where $\rho=k_1/2+k_2$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:22:59.730770+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9b9e0afecee58c769d2c5c7f10a3ca1f178b536fd5c5eeb46ca39d9c3e97ddd2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thmintro rationalfilling of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] Suppose $\bm{s}\in \mathbb{Q}^n$. The multislope $\bm{s}$ is realized by a $\Phi$-horizontal foliation with linear boundary type if and only if one of the following holds:
