{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.328302+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9c4cfc137cd6e7d301e551fd8523778182fc1bab98ee38d3a17543e99f7d67f7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:heat_content of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] Let $\Omega$ be a bounded set in $\mathbb{G}$ whose $C^\infty$ boundary $\partial \Omega$ does contain no characteristic points. Then,  the following holds.
     \begin{enumerate}[leftmargin=*]
     \item For $1<\alpha< 2$,
     \begin{align*}
         \lim_{t\to 0} \frac{\operatorname{Vol}(\Omega) - H^{(\alpha)}_\Omega(t)}{t^{\frac{1}{\alpha}}}=\frac{1}{\pi}\Gamma\left(1-\frac{1}{\alpha}\right)\operatorname{Per}_\mathcal{H}(\Omega).
     \end{align*}
     \item When $\alpha=1$,
     \begin{align*}
         \lim_{t\to 0} \frac{\operatorname{Vol}(\Omega) - H^{(\alpha)}_\Omega(t)}{t\log(1/t)}=\frac{1}{\pi}\operatorname{Per}_\mathcal{H}(\Omega).
     \end{align*}
     \end{enumerate}
    For $0<\alpha<1$ and for any bounded open set $\Omega$ satisfying $\operatorname{Per}^{(\alpha)}_{\mathcal H}(\Omega)<\infty$ we have
    \begin{align*}
        \lim_{t\to 0} \frac{\operatorname{Vol}(\Omega) - H^{(\alpha)}_\Omega(t)}{t}=\operatorname{Per}^{(\alpha)}_{\mathcal H}(\Omega).
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

