{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:00:46.812560+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9c74844758cfe02afaa7a7bba144079ea8cec61def9d3f8fff72f7b6326ff543","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 3 of arXiv:2608.12804, 'Scaling Limits for Ising Models on Inhomogeneous Random Graphs and Applications'] Let $T$ be a trace--class operator with eigenvalues $\lambda_i$, counted with algebraic multiplicity. Then the \emph{Fredholm determinant} of $I+T$ ($I$ being the identity operator) is defined as,
