{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:57:20.658402+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9d4e616cd6ad56d0fe9e49fd181ed8b421f43ababca89558ced1c625d6b5c253","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:idla-heavy-tail of arXiv:2411.10113, 'Long-range one-dimensional\\ internal diffusion-limited aggregation'] Suppose that~(equation ass:irreducible of the paper) holds, 
and that~(equation ass:stable-alpha of the paper) holds with $\alpha \in (1,2)$. Then, there exist
constants $c_\alpha, c'_\alpha$
with $0 < c_\alpha \leq c'_\alpha < 1/2$, such that, 
\begin{equation}

