{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.185613+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9e3fea86967cfd561ac4c103743c87fa0eabca88c239922dbcb47792d86cfe39","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 3 of arXiv:2510.20492, 'Heterochromatic two-arm probabilities for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] Assume that $N,v,v'$ satisfy the conditions in Theorem \ref{thm1}. There exist constants $\cl(d),\cl(d)\in (0,1)$ and $\Cl(d)>1$ such that for any $1\le M\le \cref{const_thm3_volume_1}N$, 
