{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:07.257949+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9ed2f47a10c0ab5287451ae1b6fb80027cb6de06d7c35c559e8f9f4fb6ea017c","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2604.19308, '\textbf{On McKean--Vlasov SDEs with polynomial drifts for SIS epidemic models}'] In the setting of Example~\ref{ex:a representative SIS epidemic model} let~\eqref{a.1} be valid and~\eqref{a.2} be false and suppose that if $\eta_{0} = \frac{1}{2}$, then $g_{1,1} = 0$ or $g_{1,2} = 0$. If $u_{1},u_{2}\in\R$ satisfy~\eqref{eq:extinction in the epidemic models 4} and
