{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.300641+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9f153a1bb1eafd80a01e3a7f792154d0bc9ba5e2dead296e824eff4e725fccc4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop geographic ineq decoupling map of arXiv:2604.21663, 'Large deviations for non-irreducible Markov chains on Euclidean spaces'] Let $u\in \widetilde{\mathcal{W}}_n$ be such that $|u|_\gamma\leqslant (\lambda_\gamma+\varepsilon) n$ for $\gamma\in \{1,2\}$ and set $(u^1,\ldots, u^r)=F_{n}(u)$. For $\gamma\in \{1,2\}$, we denote by $\underline v^{(\gamma)}$ the list $ (u^{j_\gamma(1)},\ldots, u^{j_\gamma(r_\gamma)})$. 
