{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.757042+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9f32e96d8415e894c70bd6a844b2f4a0000d7c7b809b7fe052872a79f0ec2807","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma CVtV of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] Under the assumptions of Theorem (MixEV of the paper), there exists a constant $\mathfrak c>0$ depending on ${\varepsilon}_A$ and $\delta_A$ such that the following holds for ${\mathfrak t}= N^{-1/3+\mathfrak c}$.  
