as $L \to \infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.727941+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_9f83b73910ccf61ce71328c47a57d96cb246a6758506af8489882836d890323d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop quadraticFourier of arXiv:2606.08325, 'Digit Mixing under Polynomial Maps'] Let \(R_2(s)\) be defined by (equation eq:R2def of the paper).  There is an absolute constant \(c_2>0\) such that, for every real \(t\) satisfying \(|2t|\ge1\),
