{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.651057+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a0d55c9693e6a13dfd17af72b16cfc1575049983a1440d1439281284e89f35c8","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] A set $A$ is a thin for the field $\field{e^{i\alpha\phi}}$ if for any continuous, bounded function $f:\mathbb C\to\mathbb R$, 
    \begin{equation*}
