{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.849568+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a1afc15664c502ed23be88edc3ded2abdfabc24658a097041a5b5f5b7d807cc3","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition $U$-Functionals of arXiv:2606.11951, 'On Skorokhod Problems for Reflected and Singular Stochastic Heat Equations'] A function $U: \mathcal{S}(\mathbb{R}) \to \mathbb{C}$ is called a \emph{$U$-functional} iff $U$ meets both of the following two conditions:
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item $U$ is \emph{ray-analytic}, i.e.\ for all $\varphi$, $\psi \in \mathcal{S}(\mathbb{R})$ the function $\mathbb{R} \mathrel{\reflectbox{$\in$}} s \mapsto U(\varphi + s \psi) \in \mathbb{C}$
		is entire analytic and therefore extends to an entire function on $\mathbb{C}$.
		\item $U$ is \emph{uniformly bounded of exponential order 2}, i.e.\ there exist constants $A$, $B\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}$ and $p \in \mathbb{N}_{0}$ s.th.\ for all $z\in\mathbb{C}$, $\varphi \in \mathcal{S}(\mathbb{R})$ it holds
		\begin{equation*}
			|U(z\varphi)| \leq A \exp(B|z|^2\|\varphi\|_{p}^2).
		\end{equation*}
	\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:55:27.256923+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a1b39a9b65ac55d86ae27526e3a9bf72248445813757bc6e8b1321ad2c2cff9b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2609.04101, 'Endpoint Estimates for Stein's Purely Quadratic Carleson Operator'] Let $Q$ be an interval and $x \not \in Q.$ The following estimates hold:

