{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-09T06:55:03+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a2c6768429f320cfc463b28045f2fe74d360457c3ceea1c32b07fec273391018","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 19 of arXiv:2507.06186, '2507.06186'] For any $\ka,\eps,t>0$, we let $\mc K_{\ka,\eps}(t)$ denote the integral operator on $L^2(D)$ with kernel
