{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.727427+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a5276bbdb578291330c8fad5cdfd3beb78391f4d7ed57b837fe6490ee8ada405","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2411.17653, 'Exclusion processes with non-reversible boundary: hydrodynamics and large deviations'] Given $\gamma\in{\mathcalboondox M}_{ac}$, let $\Pi_\gamma$ be the set of paths $\pi(t,dx)=\rho_t(x)dx$ in $\mathcal{D}([0,T],{\mathcalboondox M}_{ac})$ such that
