the set 
$\{ \mu \in \P(\TkaXinf): \pi_\mu = \pi\}$ 
of the functional $H(\cdot\| \eta_1)$ and hence, of 
 $I^{\k}_1 (\cdot)$.  Furthermore, we have   
 \begin{equation}

 \min_{\mu \in \P(\TkaXinf): \pi_\mu = \pi}  I^\k_1 (\mu) =  I^\k_1 (\mup) =  J^\nu_{\k} (\pi), \quad \forall \pi \in \Psym{\X}, \end{equation}
  where $J^\nu_{\k}$ is as defined in (equation eqn:J-nu-k of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:37.363384+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a56c159d36d433f6d4d61629e47a0cbaf27986e1e0c426aeaafa9e3e9faae446","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 11 (First two descent moments) of arXiv:2606.18047, 'Analysis of the asymmetric shelf shuffle'] Let $n,m\geq 1$, let $\pi\sim\nu_{n,m}^{(p)}$, and let $D_n=\des(\pi)$. Put $\dd=2p-1$. Then
\begin{equation}

\E[D_n]
=
\frac{n-1}{2}
+
\dd\left(
 m-\frac{n+1}{2}
 -\frac{n+1}{m^n}S_n(m)
\right).
\end{equation}
Moreover,
\begin{align}

\E[D_n(D_n+1)]
&=
\frac{n(n+1)}{4}-\frac{m}{2}
+\frac{(n+1)mS_n(m)-(n+2)S_{n+1}(m)}{m^n} \notag\\
&
+\dd\left(
 nm-\frac{n(n+1)}{2}
 -\frac{n(n+1)}{m^n}S_n(m)
\right) \notag\\
&
+\dd^2\left(
 m^2-\left(n+\frac12\right)m+\frac{n(n+1)}{4}\right. \notag\\
&\qquad\left.
 +\frac{(n^2-1)mS_n(m)-n(n+2)S_{n+1}(m)}{m^n}
\right).
\end{align}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.422293+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a58105cf27298b13428adf66ca18e93d9dbc12d800100dfd855bb5cbf2c82382","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 142 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Consider a discrete ensemble satisfying Assumptions~\ref{Assumptions_Theta}, \ref{Assumptions_basic}, \ref{Assumptions_offcrit}, \ref{Assumptions_analyticity} and the additional Assumption~\ref{Assumptions_extra}. For any tuple of compact sets $\amsmathbb{K}_h\subset \amsmathbb C\setminus \amsmathbb{A}_h^{\mathfrak{m}}$ indexed by $h \in [H]$, there exists a $\N$-independent sequence of positive constants $(C_n)_{n \geq 1}$ depending on these compacts and the constants in the assumptions, such that, for any $n \in \amsmathbb{Z}_{> 0}$, $h_1,\ldots,h_n \in [H]$ and $(z_1,\ldots,z_n) \in \prod_{i = 1}^{n} \amsmathbb{K}_{h_i}$ we have
