{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:12:09.050754+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a5b83ad390251f3ab413c60e76230c66f670d2acd9089d6cfc9ecb26cc62eabc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:LRPseparation of arXiv:2608.25279, 'Provable Non-Acceleration of Standard Strang\\ Splittings of Kinetic Langevin Dynamics'] For every $R\ge1$ and $n\ge0$,
\begin{equation}
 \norm{\delta_{z_R^{\mathrm{cyc}}}Q_R^n-
       \delta_{z_R^0}Q_R^n}_{\mathrm{TV}}
 \ge1-4n\exp\left(-\frac{R^2}{8000}\right).
\end{equation}
Moreover, there is a constant $C<\infty$, independent of $R$, such
that $Q_R$ has a unique invariant law $\pi_R$ satisfying
\begin{equation*}
 \int(\lvert x\rvert^2+\lvert v\rvert^2)\,\pi_R(dx,dv)\le CR^2,
 \qquad R\ge1.
\end{equation*}
Consequently the bound (equation eq:LRPexplicitbound of the paper) holds, proving Corollary~(cor:LRPexplicit of the paper).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:00:22.780861+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a5b85795e06d3406494a617c6406585577d2869bff22cd09cd24a713f3879905","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm Entry Approximation Thm of arXiv:2411.01633, 'On the Limit of the Tridiagonal Model \\for $\beta$-Dyson Brownian Motion'] For some constants $C_{k,T}$ and $n_0(k,T)$, we almost surely have 
    \begin{gather*}
        \sup_{t \in [0,T]}|a_j(t)-\tilde{a}_j(t)| \leq C(k,T)\frac{\log(n)^j}{\sqrt{n}},\\        
        \sup_{t \in [0,T]}\frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}\left|b_j(t)^2-\tilde{b}_j(t)^2\right| \leq C(k,T)\frac{\log(n)^{2j}}{\sqrt{n}},
    \end{gather*}
    for all $n \geq n_0(k,T)$ and $j \leq k$. In particular, letting 
    \begin{equation*}
    \Tilde{E}_n(t):=\left(\Tilde{a}_1(t),\dots,\Tilde{a}_k(t), \frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}(\Tilde{b}_1(t)^2-n),\dots,\frac{1}{\sqrt{n}}(\Tilde{b}_k(t)^2-n)\right),
    \end{equation*}
    we almost surely have
    \begin{equation}
        \lim_{n \to \infty} \sup_{t \in [0,T]} \|E_n(t)-\Tilde{E}_n(t)\|=0.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:49:49.204071+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a5c9dd1e5b2095a84ceda684b4e1bccd11965a3198e1dc8510907c6bc524f160","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 (Matrix Bernstein) of arXiv:2604.27119, '\Large Applied Random Matrix Theory\relatedversion'] Consider a statistically independent family $(\mtx{X}_1, \dots, \mtx{X}_n)$
of $d_1 \times d_2$ random matrices, real or complex, 
that are centered and uniformly bounded: $\Expect[ \mtx{X}_k ] = \mtx{0}$ and $\norm{ \mtx{X}_k } \leq B$ for each index $k$.
Form the sum, and calculate its matrix variance statistic:
\begin{equation} 
\mtx{S} \coloneqq \sum_{k=1}^n \mtx{X}_k
\quad\text{and}\quad
v(\mtx{S}) \coloneqq \norm{ \Expect[ \mtx{SS}^* ] } \vee \norm{ \Expect[ \mtx{S}^*\mtx{S} ] }.
\end{equation}
Then the spectral norm of the sum satisfies the probability inequalities
\begin{gather} 
\Expect \norm{\mtx{S}} \leq \sqrt{2 v(\mtx{S}) \log(d_1 + d_2)} + \frac{1}{3} B \log(d_1 + d_2); \\

\Prob{ \norm{\mtx{S}} \geq t} \leq (d_1 + d_2) \exp\left( \frac{-t^2/2}{v(\mtx{S}) + Bt/3} \right)
\quad\text{for $t \geq 0$.}

\end{gather} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

