 Moreover, the linear system (\ref{sys}) is nonsingular  if and only if the chain is ergodic. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:35:10.792333+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a5ee5fc9d4f1073639d3839bd962ed53bcaf2a2abd2f226a297deb27dc762344","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 15 of arXiv:2604.00635, 'Large deviations of the periodic Toda chain'] Let $\kappa>0$ and $\gamma >1$. Assume that $\bs{\eta}_N\in \R^N$ is such that

\begin{itemize}

\item[i)] $1- \frac{ \ln|P^\prime(\eta_k)| }{ \ln(2\veps_N) }  \, \geq \,  \kappa$ for all $k \in \intn{1}{N}$;

\item[ii)] $|\eta_a - \eta_b| \, \geq \, N^{-\ga}$ for all $a \neq b \in \intn{1}{N}$;

\item[iii)] $N^{\f{3}{2}} \vartheta_N \to 0$ as $N \to +\infty$.

\end{itemize}

 Let $\op{A}$ be as defined in \eqref{definition matrice A}. Then, there exists $N_0 \in \mathbb{N}$ such that, for all $N \geq N_0$, the following lower bound holds

\bem

\det_{N-1}[ \op{A} ] \, \geq  \,  | \ln(2\veps_N)|^{N-1} (1 - \mathrm{O}( N^{\f{3}{2}}  \vartheta_N)) \\

\times \prod_{j=1}^N  \Big( 1- \frac{ \ln|P^\prime(\eta_j)| }{\ln(2\veps_N)}    - \mathrm{O}\big( \frac{\ln N}{N}\big) - \mathrm{O}\big( N^{\f{3}{2}} \vartheta_N \big) \Big)^{1- \frac{1}{N}} \;.

\end{multline} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:10:08.727191+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a5f54d182c8c4f883284cb53d09e507e741b3a326d43ceb034bd3378ea612411","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem hydrolimit_pertubed_process of arXiv:2411.17653, 'Exclusion processes with non-reversible boundary: hydrodynamics and large deviations'] (Hydrodynamic Limit for the perturbed process)
    Fix a  {measurable }density profile $\gamma:[0,1]\to[0,1]$ and let $\{\mu_N\}_N$ be a sequence of probability measures associated to it. Then, for each $t>0,\;\delta>0$ and $f\in C([0,1])$ we have
