{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.572862+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a60085cb31dee9815e3fdbc49788e38431a30d659dd327b4a3bfdb9314ca2187","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 20 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d\geq 2$, $\beta>0$, $h\geq 0$, and $n\geq 1$. Let $J\in (\mathbb R^+)^{E(\mathbb Z^d)}$ which satisfies $J_e=\beta$, for every $e\in E(\Lambda_n)$. Let $\Lambda$ be a finite subset of $\mathbb Z^d$ containing $\Lambda_{2n}$. Then, for every $S\subset \Lambda_n$, 
