{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:34:45.627457+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a60a1d95ba0a49039ea4d9193b369b5144a9db27f238f1c72d86fd6efca20d26","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:Hoelder of arXiv:2609.01825, 'On everywhere locally soluble varieties \\ in families over toric bases'] Let $\vec \ell$ be of convergent type for the face $\cal F$ and assume that $\cal F$ is not contained in a coordinate hyperplane. Let $\Xi \subset \cal P(\log B)$ be a measurable set. Then there exists a $\epsilon > 0$ such that for all $A'>0$, 
