{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:31.001163+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a682b1c3027b25e7fe77060dc71a0c6c682bd7cbcc33a41b78776ec0ccfcb25b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 51 (Counterexample to simultaneous mixed-degree extraction) of arXiv:2608.12492, 'Weak Limits of Wiener Chaos: Primitive--Fock Classification and Hilbert--Stein Extraction'] Let $Q=2,d=1$, and let $e,h$ be orthonormal in $\cK_1$.  Consider
\begin{equation}
 x_1=\alpha e+h,\qquad x_2=e^{\odot2},\qquad 0<\alpha\ll1.

\end{equation}
Then $\cN_1(F)=\mathbb Re$, so $h$ belongs to the canonical Gaussian
factor.  Nevertheless the first reduced
promotion is made at weight two and its range contains a nonzero $e\odot h$ component.
Consequently
\begin{equation}
 \mathbb U_2^{-1}M_{2,\mathcal U}^{[J]}
 \not\subset\cW_2(\cN(F))

\end{equation}
already after the first promotion.  Moreover the defect is not confined to
the module: for this packet the simultaneous reduced trajectory promotes
$h$ itself after finitely many further steps, so that its terminal residual
at weight one is zero, whereas
$G^{\can}=I_1(h)\ne0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:57:49.854026+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a6872ff7a84e325a2fafb9f8d5e7f112325bdccca6815219f1a0ec4c2d34e7ac","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition lem:uniform-non-fix of arXiv:2410.23944, 'Hitting time mixing for the random transposition walk'] Fix $t$ and $M$ such that $|t'|\le n(\log\log n/4 -2\log\log\log n)$ and $M\le (\log n)^2$. 

