{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:37:51.458609+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_a93d4edf644fac9a1c639af66894c7c4d199ede84b90e2d30ea44c467ffb5b5a","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 40 of arXiv:2604.03777, 'Equilibrium fluctuations for a multi-species particle system with long jumps'] Let $ \gamma >2$ and $0 \leq s \leq t \leq T$. Assume that $K_n \sqrt{n} \leq \widehat{C}$, for every $n \in \mathbb{N}_+$. Then there exists some $\delta_1 \in (0, \;1]$ and some $f: \mathbb{N}_+ \mapsto \mathbb{R}$ satisfying $\lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} f(n)=0$, such that
