{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:02:08.132193+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aab017a038f82ffdf26c8e0d4da38291c1d85adafcde8d2cc96aad457ddd2ff6","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 4 (Bures-Wasserstein Distance, \cite{petric2019got}) of arXiv:2608.27500, 'Optimal Transport for Network Comparison: \\ A Review with Machine Learning Applications'] The Bures-Wasserstein distance between the graph signal distributions $\mu=\mathcal{N}(0,L^\dagger)$ and $\nu=\mathcal{N}(0,(L')^\dagger)$ is
