{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:51:52.051751+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aac5c8de91ce9e4222789d073d28ba35961f350bb5be249230869253cb85217c","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:RT of arXiv:2607.12564, 'Power-law and log-periodic degree tails for a family of probability generating function eq'] There exist $C,c>0$, depending only on $p$ and $j$, such that
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb{P}(D^*_n=k)\le C\lambda^{-n}\exp\!\Bigl\{-c\,\frac{k}{\lambda^{n}}\Bigr\},
  \qquad n\ge0,\ k\ge j .
\end{equation}
Consequently, writing $N_k=\lfloor\log_\lambda k\rfloor$ and $m=n-N_k$,
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb{P}(D^*_n=k)\le\lambda^{-n}\mathcal D_m,\qquad
