\end{equation}
and $\mathcal D_m$ is weighted-summable:
\begin{equation}
  \sum_{m\in\mathbb{Z}}\mathcal D_m\,\lambda^{-(\rho+1)m}<\infty .
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:22:59.729831+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aad065f1664662b720cf7c3b872145db2af33162acebbb0f0a616574c26e8b7e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm Jankins--Neumann~\cite{JankinsNeumann1985}, Naimi~\cite{Naimi1994} of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] Suppose $M=(\text{Pair of pants})\times S^1$, with $\Phi$ the periodic flow in the $S^1$ direction. Then the Jankins--Neumann ziggurat $\mathcal{Z}(\Phi)$ is the subset of $\mathbb{R}^3$ cut out by the following inequality (combined with its sibling obtained by inverting all three coordinates):
