{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.572134+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae0796cbf0fc5844908ae9318dd121b315e2e5445788cd1fbbc8a82a08d12427","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 13 (Griffiths' inequality {\cite{GriffithsCorrelationsIsing1-1967,kelly1968general}}) of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d\geq 2$ and $G=(V,E)$ be a subgraph of $\mathbb Z^d$. Then, for every $J\in (\mathbb R^+)^{E}$, every $\mathsf{h}\in (\mathbb R^+)^{V}$, and every $A,B\subset V$,
