{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:55:18.057223+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae2254051d2106f6ef9772e7487d3b5b9cd5ec623ff550a66969fbe1ca1a74f5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 32 of arXiv:2606.16636, 'Free energy of non-convex multi-species spin glasses with centered Ising spins'] A function $\bar\xi:\R^\D_+\to\R$ is called a \textbf{regularization} of $\xi:\R^\D\to\R$ if the following conditions hold.
