{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:00.620626+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ae35006f7f70166f1336ebdccc4c97a94917024ad41d682a61f24157504cef25","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 12 of arXiv:2511.00764, 'Further Developments on Stochastic Dominance for Convex\\ Combinations of Infinite-Mean Ra'] \

\begin{itemize}
  \item[{\rm (vi)}] Let $X$ and $Y$ be independent.
