{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:47:04.944830+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aece00c32452c82e6ecb035b760013c5ecbb85d603bfce8a13e14858ab848aed","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:equivctdscausality of arXiv:2412.02948, 'Causal transport on path space'] A coupling $\pi \in \Pi\del{\eta,\nu}$ is a causal coupling if and only if the filtrations $\deln{\mathcal{H}^\eta_t \otimes \cbrn{\emptyset, \mathcal{W}^d}}_{t\in \sbr{0,1}}$ and $\del{\del{\mathcal{H}_t \otimes \mathcal{H}_t}^\pi}_{t+ \in \sbr{0,1}}$ on $\deln{\mathcal{W}^d \times \mathcal{W}^d, \mathcal{F}_1 \otimes \mathcal{F}_1, \pi}$ 
