{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:56:17.350515+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_aeda38777b1edeb45f77f2ad9cb9503d63950f3c8ca26c9b70b09b80ab56660c","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop P:KPZFP-marginals of arXiv:2604.10020, 'The directed landscape in half-space'] Take $\rho\in\mathbb{R}\cup\{-\infty\}$, and $\mathcal{Q}^\rho$ a subsequential limit in law of $\mathcal{Q}^\rho_n$ (when $\rho\in\mathbb{R}$) or $\mathcal{Q}^{-c(2n)^{1/3}}_n$ for some $c>0$ (when $\rho=-\infty$).
