{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:28:53.672886+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b00cf08ceb56c0ff8f663a82c836e10c3893ad68e11000190fcce4e70e08cda4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 15 (existence and regularity of the ULA stationary distribution) of arXiv:2605.13648, 'Sticky CIR process with potential: invariant measure and exact sampling'] Suppose that $G' \in C^1_{\mathrm b}([0,\infty))$ and that \cref{ass:moment} holds.

