{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.686053+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b0ebc26edd39b772cb265c32048ea20499bc93ff6d2e1d17376545e7e309cc34","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Mainthm t:1.3i of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] The joint law of $\widecheck{{\mathbf T}}_{\rm D}$, $\widecheck{{\mathbf X}}_{\rm D}$ from Theorem~(t:1.1 of the paper) is given by
\begin{equation}

\big(\widecheck{{\mathbf T}}_{\rm D}, \widecheck{{\mathbf X}}_{\rm D}\big) \,\big|\, \mathcal Z_{\rm D}, \overline{h}_{\rm D}\, \sim  {\rm Gumbel}\,\Big(\frac{1}{2\pi} (\log (C_\star\|\mathcal Z_{\rm D}\|) + 4\sqrt{\pi}\,\overline{h}_{\rm D}\big) \,,\,\, \frac{1}{2\pi} \Big) \otimes \mathcal Z_{\rm D}^\circ \,,
\end{equation}
where $C_\star \in (0,\infty)$ is a universal constant, $\mathcal Z_{\rm D}$ is as in~(equation eq:deflqgm of the paper), $\overline{h}_{\rm D}$ is as in~(equation e:1.7p of the paper) and they are coupled together as in 
