= \mathbb{E}\,{\rm e}^{-C_\star\|\mathcal Z_{\rm D}\| {\rm e}^{-2\pi s + 4\sqrt{\pi} \,\overline{h}_{\rm D}}}\mathcal Z^\circ_{\rm D}({\rm d} x) \,.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:36:49.820275+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b0fc7f51bd6cc24ccd57bfc146155db525f436ecf25f1a854392b15bf96e26d4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:brownian-ball-localization of arXiv:2609.02829, 'Quantitative explosion and percolation of the divisible sandpile'] Assume $d<4$. For every $0<T<\infty$ there are $C=C(d)>0$ and $c=c(d)>0$
