{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.389583+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b1172ed248b829759ea69882bb6e2813bcc66f29f69dc172b308f8d6ee960cee","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:global_subgraph_clt of arXiv:2507.10531, 'Quantitative central limit theorems for exponential random graphs'] Assume that there are sequences $\sigma_n \gtrsim n$ and $\delta_n \to 0$ such that
