{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:18:27.572361+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b142ed05ca69cf1a95b669358d90d4d19536fb833bc3a845b8e578eca25f23d7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 16 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d\geq 2$ and $G$ be a subgraph of $\mathbb Z^d$. Then, for every $\beta\geq 0$, every $\mathsf{h}\in (\mathbb R^+)^{V(G)}$, and every $x,y\in V(G)$, one has
