{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:46:25.371744+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b27d6b9ba8b2598a5219b71da46c0a9cb5d80040f1d3046c011fe2d010133136","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:walk1 of arXiv:2604.15146, 'Renormalised two-point functions of CLE$_4$ gaskets'] Let $\mathbb{P}^W_{n}$ be the probability measure on simple random walks $(S_k)_{k\geq 0}$ starting from $n$. 
\begin{itemize}
\item Consider the infinite measure $\mu^A := \sum_{n \in \mathbb{Z}} \mathbb{P}^W_n$. Then $\mu^A(S_{k} = 0) = 1$ for all $k \geq 0$.
\item Consider the infinite measure $\mu^E := \sum_{n \in 2\mathbb{Z}} \mathbb{P}^W_n$. Then $\mu^E(S_{2k} = 0) = 1$ and $\mu^E(S_{2k+1}=0) = 0$ for all $k \geq 0$ .
\item Consider the infinite measure $\mu^O := \sum_{n \in 2\mathbb{Z}+1} \mathbb{P}^W_n$. Then $\mu^O(S_{2k+1} = 0) = 1$ and $\mu^O(S_{2k}=0) = 0$  for all $k \geq 0$. 
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:30.018115+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b28183fcab158750fb66f5be5b4bcfe4c469dc9df7868fd1422e18550430f089","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 33 of arXiv:2605.05864, 'Classification and Metrization of Classes of Smooth measures'] For any compact set $K\subset E$ and \(\alpha >0\), there exists \(C_\alpha >0\) such that, for any \(\mu \in \mathcal{S}_0\), 
