{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:32:19.939832+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b2a7e9f50dc419409f27843e32be21068138d056beb4834f8f1649722eb8dba1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 30 of arXiv:2608.02927, 'Thinning Operation via the Poisson-F\"ollmer Process'] Let $X$ have density $f$ with respect to $\pi_{T}$ and $H(T_{1-a} (X) | \pi_{(1-a)T} ) < \infty$ for some $a < 1.$ Then 
