{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.661317+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b2accb04ddf71d8a4f41c8c540bc57c48cb2d4b2df90e1a7cac123e5d63b783f","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm conv-fields of arXiv:2602.06011, 'Excursion decomposition of the XOR-Ising model'] Let $D$ be a Jordan domain. For every continuous function $f:D\to\mathbb R$ with compact support in $D$, and any $k\geq1$, 
\begin{enumerate}
    \item[(i)] $\mathbb E_{\delta}^+[(\tau_\delta, f)^k]\to\mathcal{C}^{k}\ 2^{k/2}\ \mathbb E[(\field{\cos(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\phi)}, f)^k]$,
    \item[(ii)] $\mathbb E_{\delta}^\varnothing[(\tau_\delta^\dagger, f)^k]\to\mathcal{C}^{k}\ 2^{k/2}\ \mathbb E[(\field{\sin(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\phi)}, f)^k]$,
\end{enumerate}
as $\delta\to0$, where $\mathcal{C}$ is an explicit (lattice-dependent) constant. In particular, the fields converge in distribution with respect to the topology of the Sobolev space $H^{s}_{loc}(D)$ for any $s<-1$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:17:04.322617+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b2b9d83157398414de0802b2a3d04ec04cb836e07374f30de9e17bb37f91182f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem finite time variance bound by asymptotic variance of arXiv:2606.01683, 'Singular-value gap of nonreversible Markov processes'] In the above setting, 
