{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:38:37.403262+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b2caa6b67aa328f73a8cf201575d960ae5a38ddb758bf2d0fa4e062bcacd7507","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 2 of arXiv:2605.15501, 'Well-posedness of the obstacle problem for generalized Dean--Kawasaki equation\thanks{ The'] Let $(\Omega,\mathcal{F},\mathbb{P})$ be a probability space with a filtration $(\mathcal{F}_{t})_{t\in[0,\infty)}$.
