{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.853323+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b2d0b9eed9e1ef71c30d9a293c547f0db2101da57bb6c736bc22eea2ee462fd7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:ibpf of arXiv:2606.11951, 'On Skorokhod Problems for Reflected and Singular Stochastic Heat Equations'] Let $h\inH_0^1~\cap~H^2$ and $F \in \exp(C^{\infty})$. Then we have the IbPFs
	\begin{align}
		\mathbb{E}_{\rho^a\mu^{\beta}}\left[ \partial_h F \right] + \mathbb{E}_{\rho^a\mu^{\beta}}\left[ F \, (h'',\cdot)_{L} \right] &= - \langle \!\langle F(\beta), \bar{h}_a \delta_0(\beta_a) \rangle \!\rangle\\
		\text{and}\quad\mathbb{E}_{\rho\mu^{\beta}}\left[ \partial_h F \right] + \mathbb{E}_{\rho\mu^{\beta}}\left[ F \, (h'',\cdot)_{L} \right] &= - \Big\langle \mspace{-7mu} \Big\langle F(\beta), \int_{(0,1)}\bar{h}_x \delta_0(\beta_x) \, dx \Big\rangle \mspace{-7mu} \Big\rangle.
	\end{align}
	Further, the linear operators
	\begin{align*}
		\exp(C^{\infty})\mathrel{\reflectbox{$\in$}} F &\mapsto \langle \!\langle F(\beta), \bar{h}_a \delta_0(\beta_a) \rangle \!\rangle \in\mathbb{R}\\
		\text{and}\quad\exp(C^{\infty})\mathrel{\reflectbox{$\in$}} F &\mapsto \Big\langle \mspace{-7mu} \Big\langle F(\beta), \int_{(0,1)}\bar{h}_x \delta_0(\beta_x) \, dx \Big\rangle \mspace{-7mu} \Big\rangle \in\mathbb{R}
	\end{align*}
	extend uniquely to $W^{1,2}(L, \mu^{\beta})$. Identifying these operators with their extensions in $W^{-1,2}(L, \mu^{\beta})$, (equation IbPF:rho_x of the paper) and (equation IbPF:rho of the paper) hold for all $F \in C_b^1(L)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-09-07T12:18:08.279320+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b2d97c696dae76bebbb63464a7aa431fa28e9013ad5aa07ec4b6b39b60e49b5d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 (Example 3 in \cite{Kolesko_SPL}) of arXiv:2505.20799, 'A note on the improved sparse Hanson-Wright inequalities'] In the case $0< \alpha\le 1$, we have  for $r\ge 2$
