{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.693558+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b35e35fd521e38005e8ef8012a293137faf2c90057597db871fb05b64eb3ddfc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop rest of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] If $\gamma$ is chosen small enough, then, given any $0 < \eta' < \eta < \frac{1}{2}$ small enough \mbox{(depending only on $\gamma$),} for any fixed $u \geq 0$ we have  
