{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:57:30.994296+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b376719a42e4dfda29162cdf67a9f9ac7e61247f8126080ba1d07e48c9678cbb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 41 (Intrinsicity of the four-copy functional) of arXiv:2608.12492, 'Weak Limits of Wiener Chaos: Primitive--Fock Classification and Hilbert--Stein Extraction'] The quantity in \eqref{bridge:eq:four-copy-functional} is finite,
nonnegative, and independent of the bounded representative $(f_n)$.
It is continuous on bounded subsets of $\cH_q$.  If
$
 T=\mathbb U_q^{-1}\xi
$
