{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.529378+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b5ea7560569e2f4781c28804b23b2e6129f71d3e7a6b9c5dae80a2e70e3023cd","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition eq:uniform-profile-tail of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[definition]{def:uniform-profile-tail}
We say that the random field satisfies \(({\rm PT})_p\) if, for every
\(a>0\),
\begin{equation}
 \limsup_{N\to\infty}\frac1N\log
 \sup_{x\in\mathbb S^{N-1}(1)}
