{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:26:40.354453+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b641a7e3becca9eae1710929a9c6ff58a0065dd337c1b414375a0ed834af4783","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2511.09280, 'Random Walk conditioned to stay above a non-flat floor: curvature effects'] Let \(X, X_1,X_2,\dots\) be an i.i.d.\ family of \(\Z\)-valued, irreducible, aperiodic random variables satisfying~\eqref{eq:conditions_steps}. Let \(a_*,b_*\) be defined as in~\eqref{eq:dual_allowed_slopes}, and \(a_*<a<b<b_*\). Let \(h\in C^2([0,1])\) be a non-negative concave function with \(h''<0\), \(\mathrm{Image}(h')\subset H_X'([a,b])\), and \(h(0)=0\). Define
    \begin{equation*}
        h_n(k) = nh(k/n),\quad k=0,\dots, n.
    \end{equation*}
    Then, there are \(c_+\geq c_- >0, n_0\geq 1\) such that for any \(n\geq n_0\),
    \begin{equation*}
        e^{-c_+n^{1/3}}
        \leq
        e^{n\int_{0}^1 I(h'(s))ds} P\bigl(S\geq h_n, S_n = \lceil h_n(n)\rceil\bigr)
        \leq
        e^{-c_-n^{1/3}},
    \end{equation*}
    where \(S_0=0\), \(S_k=S_{k-1}+X_k\) and \(I(x) = \sup_{\lambda} \bigl(\lambda x - H(x)\bigr)\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:51:26.589624+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b675103ee2eb1a6f9d7ef1af780e92f11a921748d22ad628867e0723a4670d1c","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:complex-SaS of arXiv:2606.02003, 'Higher-Order Multifractional Stable Motion:\\ Definition and Fundamental Properties'] A \emph{complex isotropic S$\alpha$S random measure}
$\widetilde{M}_\alpha$ on $\mathbb{R}$ with Lebesgue control measure
is a complex random measure such that, for every
$f \in L^\alpha(\mathbb{R},\mathbb{C})$:
\begin{equation}

\mathbb{E}\!\left[\exp\!\left(
i\,\mathrm{Re}\int_\mathbb{R} f(\xi)\,d\widetilde{M}_\alpha(\xi)
\right)\right]
= \exp\!\left(-c_\alpha\int_\mathbb{R}|f(\xi)|^\alpha\,d\xi\right),
\end{equation}
where
\begin{equation}

c_\alpha
:= \frac{1}{2\pi}\int_0^{2\pi}|\cos\theta|^\alpha\,d\theta
= \frac{\Gamma\!\left(\frac{\alpha+1}{2}\right)}
{\sqrt{\pi}\;\Gamma\!\left(\frac{\alpha}{2}+1\right)}.
\end{equation}
The measure $\widetilde{M}_\alpha$ is \emph{isotropic}: for every
$\phi \in \mathbb{R}$, $e^{i\phi}\widetilde{M}_\alpha(\cdot)
\overset{d}{=} \widetilde{M}_\alpha(\cdot)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:24:20.990030+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b6801157c11580e930730ac48ba93c82cd8632a7086d1f29fabc69459ed592a3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:somevsall_tail_conditions of arXiv:2509.02074, 'On the Kolmogorov-Feller weak law of large numbers for the Fr\'{e}chet mean on non-compact'] Let $(M,d)$ be a metric space, and let $(X_i)_{i=1}^\infty$ be a sequence of independent $M$-valued random variables. For an $m \in M$, let $c_1(m)$, $c_2(m)$ and $c_3(m)$ denote the following conditions, respectively: 
\begin{align*}
   c_1(m): & \lim_{n\to\infty} n\mathbb{P}(d(X_1,m) > n) = 0;\\
   c_2(m): & \lim_{n\to\infty} n^{-2}\sum_{i=1}^n\mathbb{E}[d^2\{\overline{X_{n,i}}(m),m\}] = 0;\\
   c_3(m): & \lim_{n\to\infty} \sum_{i=1}^n\mathbb{P}(d(X_i,m) > n) = 0.
\end{align*}
\begin{itemize}
    \item[(i)] For any $m,m' \in M$, $c_1(m)$ holds if and only if $c_1(m')$ holds.
    \item[(ii)] For any $m,m' \in M$, $c_2(m)$ holds if and only if $c_2(m')$ holds.
    \item[(iii)] Additionally assume that $M$ is a symmetric space and,  for a given $\mu \in M$, $\mathbb{P}_{X_i}$ is geodesically symmetric about $\mu$. Then, for any $m \in M$, $c_3(\mu)$ holds if $c_3(m)$ holds.
\end{itemize}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:42:47.764526+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b681292d4bed210ba9d0512740eecba31202fa8cc30e4fbc87523157ee638523","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 1 (Weak formulation) of arXiv:2604.12797, 'A free boundary problem for the mean-field limit of diffusing particles with nonlinear bou'] Let $(v,A)$ be such that (i) $t\mapsto A_t$ is continuous in $t\geq 0$, (ii) $v\geq 0$, (iii)  $(t,x) \mapsto v(t,x)$ is continuous jointly in $t>0$ and $x\geq A_t$, and (iv) $v(t,\cdot)\in L^1([A_t,\infty))$ and $v(\cdot,A_{\cdot})\in L^1([0,t])$ for all $t>0$. Let also $A_0=a_0$ and $v(t,x)\dx \rightarrow P_0$ as $t\downarrow 0$ in the topology of weak convergence of measures. Then, we say that $(v,A)$ is a weak solution of the free boundary problem \eqref{eq:classic_PDE}--\eqref{eq:classic_A_I_rate} with initial condition $(P_0,a_0)$ if 
\begin{align}
	&\int_{A_t}^\infty \!\! \phi(x)v(t,x)\dx - 	\int_{a_0}^\infty \!\! \phi(x) \di P_0(x) = \int_0^t\! \int_{A_s}^\infty \!\! \partial_{xx}\phi(x)\frac{1}{2}\sigma(s,x)^2v(s,x)\dx \ds \nonumber \\
	&+ \int_0^t \!\int_{A_s}^\infty \!\!\partial_{x}\phi(x)b(s,x)v(s,x) \dx \ds + \int_0^t  \bigl( \tfrac{1}{2} \partial_x\phi(A_s)-\gamma(s,C_s)\phi(A_s)\bigr)\sigma(s,A_s)^2v(s,A_s) \ds ,
\end{align}
for all $t\geq 0$ and all $\phi \in C^2_b(\R)$, with
\begin{equation}
	A_t=a_0 + \alpha \! \displaystyle \int_{t-\bar{d}}^{t}\varrho(t-s)I_{s} \ds, \;\;
	C_t = \!\int_{t-\bar{d}}^{t}\varrho(t-s)(I_{s}-I_{s-\bar{d}}) \ds, \;\;  I_t=1-\!\int_{A_t}^\infty \!\!\! v(t,x) \dx,
\end{equation}
for all $t>0$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-09-07T12:18:34.092204+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b68379faa26fdd11090c8efc50ae5847216c2b053569f09a6091f9bc602bf8b3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 32 of arXiv:2507.06186, '2507.06186'] For every $\ka>0$,
there exists a constant $\th_\ka>0$ such that
for every $t\in(0,\th_\ka)$, the following holds:
\begin{align}

\lim_{\eps\to0}\mbf E\big[\msf T_{\ka,\eps}(t)\mr e^{-t\msf c_{\ka,\eps}}\big]
=\frac{\mr e^{\ka^2t\log t/2\pi}}{2\pi t}\int_D\mbf E\Big[\mbf 1_{\{\tau_D(B^{x,x}_t)>t\}}\mr e^{\ka^2\ga_t(B^{x,x}_t)}\Big]\d x;
\end{align}
\begin{align}

\lim_{\eps\to0}\mbf E\big[\msf M_{\ka,\eps}(t)\mr e^{-t\msf c_{\ka,\eps}}\big]
=\mr e^{\ka^2(t\log t-t)/2\pi}\int_D\mbf E\Big[\mbf 1_{\{\tau_D(B^x)>t\}}\mr e^{\ka^2\ga_t(B^x)}\Big]\d x;
\end{align}
\begin{multline}

\lim_{\eps\to0}\mbf{Var}\big[\msf T_{\ka,\eps}(t)\mr e^{-t\msf c_{\ka,\eps}}\big]=\frac{\mr e^{\ka^2t\log t/\pi}}{(2\pi t)^2}\int_{D^2}\mbf E\Bigg[\mbf 1_{\cap_{i\leq2}\{\tau_D({_i}B^{x_i,x_i}_t)>t\}}\\
\cdot\mr e^{\ka^2\sum_{i=1}^2\ga_t({_i}B^{x_i,x_i}_t)}\left(\mr e^{\ka^2\al_t({_1}B^{x_1,x_1}_t,{_2}B^{x_2,x_2}_t)}-1\right)\Bigg]\d x;
\end{multline}
\begin{multline}

\lim_{\eps\to0}\mbf{Var}\big[\msf M_{\ka,\eps}(t)\mr e^{-t\msf c_{\ka,\eps}}\big]=\mr e^{\ka^2(t\log t-t)/\pi}\int_{D^2}\mbf E\Bigg[\mbf 1_{\cap_{i\leq2}\{\tau_D({_i}B^{x_i})>t\}}\\
\cdot\mr e^{\ka^2\sum_{i=1}^2\ga_t({_i}B^{x_i})}\left(\mr e^{\ka^2\al_t({_1}B^{x_1},{_2}B^{x_2})}-1\right)\Bigg]\d x.
\end{multline} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:01:56.363858+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b685f596eadcb2184e3fccddae89ab953ae64fabac5b62624592855fd1729768","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition of arXiv:2609.00794, 'On operators whose adjoints or second adjoints attain their norms'] Let $X$ and $Y$ be Banach spaces. The pair $(X, Y)$ is said to have \textit{property $(P^{\star\star})$} if there is a relatively WOT compact $K \subseteq  \mathcal{L}_{w^*,w^*}^{(2)}(X, Y)$ such that 
