{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:11:11.705419+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b6b61fa6474ec11e167624d6143ca4c96b1b09123bd022bbef602824cb6cbb53","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:sep of arXiv:2609.00672, 'Deciding superellipticity and computing the Weierstrass normal form'] Let $t: C\to\mathbb P^1$ be cyclic of degree $n$ with branch data $(l_1,\dots,l_r)$, the point at infinity included when it is a branch point. Then there is a birational map from $C$ to a curve $v^n=h(u)$ with $k(u)=k(t)$ and $h\in k[u]$ separable if and only if there is $c\in(\mathbb Z/n\mathbb Z)^\times$ such that

