{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.413788+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b7b8c6cdc1962d24a8c9994e505fa709944a8c016539f42091aba418a048c9af","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 72 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Suppose that Assumptions~\ref{Assumptions_Theta}, \ref{Assumptions_basic} and \ref{Assumptions_offcrit}
 hold. Assume that $\mathfrak{b}$ is finite. For any $\zeta_2 \in \big(0,\frac{\mathfrak{b} - \mathfrak{a}}{2}\big)$,
