{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:28:53.670959+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b7b8ec1c1adf43c96774d71a2002936821375fd3814659df2d11f7b84aaae284","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 6 (transition density) of arXiv:2605.13648, 'Sticky CIR process with potential: invariant measure and exact sampling'] On $(0,\infty)$, the Lebesgue density $f$ of the CIR process defined by \cref{eq-CIR4} solves
  \[
