{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:12:46.874052+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_b9814c8f890ad2a09fac7d1568af666468fe052d1c4f1d233dc73bfcde9438ca","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma cor:hill-2 of arXiv:2608.08375, 'Algebraic formulas for first-passage times of Markov processes in the linear framework: ge'] With the assumptions above, choose $z \in Z$. Let $W \subseteq \overline{Z} = \mathcal{V}(\mathcal{H}_u[G])$ be the vertex subset of $\mathcal{H}_u[G]$ given by $W = \mathcal{V}_{\text{out}}(u)$. Then,  
