{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:57:59.849820+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba52067442f60514910b75b819f47ab1b451c70411d7cecba8da946208061b6a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:conv_in_hidaspace of arXiv:2606.11951, 'On Skorokhod Problems for Reflected and Singular Stochastic Heat Equations'] Let $(\Phi_n)_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$ be a sequence in $(\mathcal{S})'$. If the corresponding sequence of $U$-functionals $(U_n)_{n\in\mathbb{N}} \coloneqq (\mathrm{S}^{-1}\Phi_n)_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$ satisfies both of the following two conditions
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item $(U_n(\varphi))_{n\in\mathbb{N}}$ is a Cauchy sequence for all $\varphi \in \mathcal{S}(\mathbb{R})$\text{, and}
		\item there exist $p$, $N\in\mathbb{N}$ and $A$, $B\in\mathbb{R}_{\geq0}$ s.th.\
		\begin{equation*}
			|U_n(z\varphi)| \leq A \exp(B|z|^2\|\varphi\|_p^2)\quad \text{for all $z\in\mathbb{C}$, $\varphi \in \mathcal{S}(\mathbb{R})$ and $n\geq N$}.
		\end{equation*}
	\end{enumerate}
	Then, the point-wise limit $U\coloneqq \lim_{n \to \infty} U_n$ is a $U$-functional, and we have $\Phi_n \to \mathrm{S}^{-1}(U) \eqqcolon \Phi$ strongly in $(\mathcal{S})'$ as $n\to\infty$. The analogous statement holds if the $\mathrm{S}$-transform is exchanged for the $\mathrm{T}$-transform. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:12:46.874261+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba5b6410cc45b516cf82d6e5f1928a95e668611d55fea73366c793e6d5ea15bc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:hill-moment of arXiv:2608.08375, 'Algebraic formulas for first-passage times of Markov processes in the linear framework: ge'] With the same assumptions as at the start of this section, choose $z \in Z$. Let $W$ be as defined in the statement of Lemma~(cor:hill-2 of the paper) and let $\Omega$ be as defined in the statement of Theorem~(thm:hill-moment-Z of the paper). Then the $r$-th moment of the conditional FPT from $u$ to $z$ is given by,
\[
\begin{split}
    \mu^{(r)}_{c,u,z}(G) = r! \sum_{(i_1, \dotsc, i_r) \in \Omega}{\left( \prod_{j=0}^{r-1}{\frac{\psi_{i_{j+1}|i_j,u} \, x_{i_{j+1}}^*(\mathcal{H}_u[G])}{\sum_{z' \in Z}{\sum_{k \in W , k \to_G z'}{\ell(k \to_G z') \, x_k^*(\mathcal{H}_u[G])}}}} \right)} \\
    \times \left( \frac{\sum_{k \in W: k \to_G z}{\ell(k \to_G z) \, \psi_{k|i_r,u} \, x_k^*(\mathcal{H}_u[G])}}{\sum_{k \in W: k \to_G z}{\ell(k \to_G z) \, x_k^*(\mathcal{H}_u[G])}} \right) \,.\qquad\qquad\quad
\end{split}
\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:29:00.757596+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba5de18b4455471d58574341eb191e70be06ff428590b33e521af77d253e54e7","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 5 of arXiv:2512.04297, 'Mixing at the Batchelor Scale for White-In-Time Flows'] The analogous statements of Theorem \ref{thm:lower_bound_low_modes} and its two corollaries hold for the three-dimensional model \eqref{spde:3D}.
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
    \item     For $\kappa\geq 0$ and $f_0\in L_0^2(\tor^3) \setminus \{0\}$, let $f_t$ be the solution to \eqref{spde:3D}. The decay rate of the $L^2$-norm of the six innermost modes is lower bounded by
