{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:20:33.756167+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba72ef2879f7d533698d94907ff607b55bf20e155010c27a55cacd7692944c86","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 54 ({\cite{C70}*{Theorem 2}}) of arXiv:2609.03836, 'Koszul Orlik--Solomon Algebras from Non-supersolvable Arrangements'] A collection $\Fc$ of subsets (called ``blocks'') of the ground set of a matroid $M$ of rank $r$ is the set of rank $r$ flats of an erection of $M$ if and only if 
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item each block spans $M,$
        \item each block is $(r-1)$-closed,
        \item each basis of $M$ is contained in a unique block.
    \end{enumerate}
Here, a subset $S\subseteq M$ is said to be $k$-closed if the closure of any $k$-element subset of $S$ lies in $S$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:10:07.502986+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba7d7894fee0242880ea14cd6cd4258fb121b8b99aa8f680ae651d4ba69e65aa","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma eq:mixture-tail-cost of arXiv:2607.27613, 'Regularized Bulk Universality versus Bounded-Disorder Nonuniversality\\for Annealed Comple'] \label[lemma]{lem:mixture-tail}
