{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.632771+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ba9fbabd8b3c7801865355abf9d1c998b0839d3806f743a50cb5482475162249","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition \cite{lawler80selfavoiding} of arXiv:2411.13505, 'Capacity of loop-erased random walk'] Two-sided LERW $\hat\eta$ satisfies the following properties:
\begin{enumerate}
	\item the law $\hat\eta$ is absolutely continuous with respect to the law of $\eta$;
	\item $T^k\eta$ converges weakly to $\hat\eta$ as $k\rightarrow\infty$;
	\item $\hat\eta$ is stationary with respect to $T$, i.e., $T\hat\eta\stackrel{d}{=}\hat\eta$;
	\item $\eta$ and $\hat\eta$ are ergodic with respect to $T$.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:59:25.038842+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bace5515b827bf76879c2fed34c1293aaa90377eb6cf46cf779a642f9fdf7179","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 18 ({\cite{mingoFreeProbabilityRandom2017}}) of arXiv:2606.31528, 'Well-posedness and stationary distribution of free stochastic differential equations'] If $\{\mu_n\}_{n\in\mathbb N}$ is a sequence of probability measures on $\mathbb R$ such that
