{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:45:27.885542+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bae87428608332fdaa398741ea7c9e7e63d7f38167d48e472eec1b924d592edc","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:lack of detailed balance of arXiv:2607.02367, 'Flux solutions for stochastic chemical systems with sources and sinks'] Assume that $(\Omega, \mathcal R , \mathcal R_s ,  \mathcal K, \mathcal K_s )$ is a chemical system with sources and sinks. Assume that the system $(\Omega , \mathcal R, \mathcal K ) =(\Omega, \mathcal R , \emptyset ,  \mathcal K, \emptyset ) $ without sources and sinks satisfies the detailed balance condition.  Let $\mathcal B_{\mathcal W_r} = \{ w_k \}_{k =1}^{|\mathcal W_r |} $ be a basis for the space of the cycles of $(\Omega , \mathcal R, \mathcal K )$ and let $\mathcal B_{ \mathcal W} =  \{ w_k \}_{k =1}^{|\mathcal W |} $ be a basis of the space of the cycles of  $(\Omega, \mathcal R , \mathcal R_s ,  \mathcal K, \mathcal K_s )$. Assume that 
 \begin{equation} 
 |\mathcal W| >  |\mathcal W_r |. 
 \end{equation}
 Then for every $w \in \mathcal W$ such that $ \pi_{ \mathcal R } w \notin \mathcal W_r $, it holds that 
 \begin{equation} 
 \Delta (w)= (E- D)^T \mathbb S_r \pi_{\mathcal R }  w
 \end{equation}
where $E \in \mathbb R^M $ is a solution to \begin{equation} 
 S_\rho^T  E = \ln \left( \dfrac{ K_{ - \rho} }{ K_{  \rho } }  \right)  \ \forall \rho \in \{ 1, \dots, r \}   
\end{equation} 
and where $D \in \mathbb R^M $ is the vector 
\[
D(k)= \begin{cases} &\log \left( \frac{\alpha_k }{ \beta_k } \right), \quad k \in \{ 1, \dots, |\Omega_c | \}   \\
& 0, \quad   k \in \{|\Omega_c | +1 , \dots , M \}. 
\end{cases}
\]","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.617214+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bae9f45a7c393771f9968119fb42fab21e20f85ebfda0c294bfc52d59ceda408","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 23 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] For all~$\lambda\ge0$,
\begin{equation}

\lim_{k\to\infty}\limsup_{n\to\infty} \wt P\biggl(\,\bigcup_{x\in \BbbL_n}\bigl\{h(x)\ge \wt m_n-\lambda\bigr\}\cap\wt\BB_{n, k}(x)^\cc\biggr) = 0,
\end{equation}
where for $\tilde\sigma:=\frac1{12}$, 
\begin{equation}

\wt \BB_{n,k}(x):=\Bigl\{\wt m_k+k^{\tilde\sigma}\le \wt m_n-h(z)\le \wt m_k+k^{1-\tilde\sigma}\Bigr\}
\end{equation}
with our convention $z:=\frakm^k(x)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:39:41.439532+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_baeb33216ae934d7b811d5f49b6b385e611d967d79c8208d563a9f2036d75922","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 21 of arXiv:2604.07370, 'Probabilistic Weyl law for twisted Toeplitz matrices with rough symbols'] Let $0<\A{1}\leq \A{2}\ll 1$ be such that there exists $\omega\in \hspace{0.1cm} ]0,1[$ such that 
    \begin{equation}
        N^{-\omega}\leq \pr{\alpha_1\alpha_2}^{1/2}.
    \end{equation}
    Let $p\in S(1,\A{1},\A{2})$. Then, as $N\to +\infty$,
    \begin{equation*}
        \norme{p_{N,\A{1},\A{2}}}\leq \sup_{\rho\in \mc{T}_{\A{1},\A{2}}}\bb{p(\rho)}+o(1).
    \end{equation*}
    In particular, there exists a constant $C>0$ independent of $N$, $\alpha_1$ and $\A{2}$ such that 
    \begin{equation*}
        \norme{p_{N,\A{1},\A{2}}}\leq C.
    \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:36:31.234413+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_baedf48550c049a2e377d2bfafe46a2b37da5ea7afca329a1862f8e9bcb305a4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 15 of arXiv:2609.00567, 'Hodge--Tate splitting and Akizuki--Nakano vanishing in positive characteristic'] Let \(\mcalX\) and \(\mcalY\) be fpqc algebraic stacks, let \(G\) be a flat affine commutative group scheme over \(\mcalX\), and let \(\pi \colon \mcalY \to \mcalX\) be a \(B_{\mcalX}G\)-torsor. Let \(q \colon B_{\mcalX}G \to \mcalX\) be the structure morphism of the classifying stack.
  Assume that both \(R\pi_*\mcalO_{\mcalY}\) and \(Rq_*\mcalO_{B_{\mcalX}G}\) are perfect objects of \(\mcalD_{\qcoh}(\mcalX)\).
  Then there is an isomorphism
  \begin{equation*}
    (R\pi_*\mcalO_{\mcalY}) \otimes^L_{\mcalO_{\mcalX}} (R\pi_*\mcalO_{\mcalY}) \simeq (R\pi_*\mcalO_{\mcalY}) \otimes^L_{\mcalO_{\mcalX}} (Rq_*\mcalO_{B_{\mcalX}G})
  \end{equation*}
  in \(\Mod_{R\pi_*\mcalO_{\mcalY}}(\mcalD_{\qcoh}(\mcalX))\), where \(R\pi_*\mcalO_{\mcalY}\) acts through the first tensor factor.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:52:32.332686+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_baf0867d9383415962e5e2338c96e5270e1a9b87c9f210cc370897a43733638e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition eq:whitney-unsigned of arXiv:2609.03959, 'The combinatorial Hopf algebra of signed graphs'] Given a graph $G$, consider the deformation $\zeta_x(G) = x^{rk(G)}$ then 
