{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:57:28.232287+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bd93da758728bde4f8855e88175a671267dae00d628ae9aa95a501fc78e82e40","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 36 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] For all $n\in \N$,  the patched last passage times $\LLpaeps$ converge  to the patched directed landscape $\Lpa$ as $\varepsilon \rightarrow 0$, i.e., there exist events $(\mathcal{A}_n)_{n \in \N}$ with $\mathcal{A}_n=\mathcal{A}_n(N)$ such that 
