{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:07:35.028690+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bd942ebf4876e2c670d00366b2391cde8ec99e290155a7a0cb9ded81dc8efbb3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem 11 of arXiv:2609.02879, 'On the cut locus of Hamilton--Jacobi equations I: structure and propagation via the touchi'] Let \( \Omega \subset \R^n \) be an open convex subset and $\phi\in\text{\rm SCL}\,(\Omega)$. If $x\in\reg(\phi)$, then \( \phi \) is differentiable at \( x \) and there exists an open neighborhood \( V \) of \( x \) and a \( C^\infty \) function
