{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:45:32.108500+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bddc0527c97498faa3d089e635d4bcd3ec3d276669c4990b29286e1eef18459e","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lemma def barriers of arXiv:2411.14350, 'Randomized Geodesic Flow on Hyperbolic Groups'] Let $a\in G$ be such that $d_{{\mathcal G}}(a,o)\geq n$ and fix a point $\xi\in \partial \mathbb{H}^d$ and denote by $\alpha \in[0,\pi]$ the angle between the rays $[0,\xi)$ and $[0,\psi(a)]$. 
For fixed $n\in\mathbb{N},\varepsilon>0$, set $2M = \lfloor\alpha {\rm e} ^{\varepsilon n}\rfloor$ and let $I_{i} = [\frac{2i-1}{{\rm e} ^{\varepsilon n}},\frac{2i}{{\rm e} ^{\varepsilon n}}]$ for $i=1,..,M$.
Then there exist barriers $H_1,..H_M\subset G$ and $C_1>0$ such that
\begin{equation}
\sum_{a_{i} \in H_{i}}{\mathcal G}(a_i,a_{i+1})^2 \leq C_1 {\rm e} ^{-rn} {\mathcal G}(a_{i+1}, a_{i+1}^{n})^2
\end{equation}
for all $a_{i+1}\in H_{i+1}$ and where $a_{i+1}^{n}$ is a point on $[a_{i+1},0]$ such that $\lfloor d_{{\mathcal G}}(a^n_{i+1},o)\rfloor=n$.
In particular this also means that there exists $C_2>0$ such that
\begin{equation}
\sum_{a_{i} \in H_{i},a_{i+1} \in H_{i+1}}{\mathcal G}(a_i,a_{i+1})^2\leq C_2 {\rm e} ^{-rn}.
\end{equation}
These barriers can be defined as 
\begin{equation}
H_i = H(\alpha_i) = \bigcup_{\eta} \bigg\{x \in G: d_{{\mathcal G}}(x,o)\geq n \text{ and } d_{\mathbb{H}}(\psi(x),[0,\eta))<C_0\bigg\}
\end{equation}
where the union is over all $\eta\in \partial\mathbb{H}^d$ such that $\angle ([0,\eta),[0,\xi))=\alpha_i$,
for some choice $\alpha_i\in I_i$ for $i=1,..,M$ and for some $C_0>0$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:55:57.002359+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bde53eb6a366da69d9ea31a127e2f042ef10c7defccb5325184ae3c59dc07010","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2609.02790, 'Full-Model Optimality for Tunable Linear Generative Priors in Compressed Sensing'] Suppose $x^\star \thicksim \mathcal{G}_n$, $\mathcal{G}_n = diag(\sigma_1,\dots,\sigma_n)$ has singular values $\sigma_1 \geq \sigma_2 \geq \dots \geq \sigma_n >0 $. Let $G_k = diag(\sigma_1,\dots,\sigma_k)$. Let $A \in \R ^{m\times n}$, $A_{ij}\stackrel{i.i.d}{\sim} \mathcal{N}(0,1)$. For fixed $A$, for $k \in [m,n]$,  and the MAP estimator from $\eqref{eq2}$ obeys 
\begin{align}
    \mathrm E_{x^\star \sim \mathcal{G}_n} \big\| \hat{x}(k) - x^\star \big\|_2^2 = \Big\| G_k P_{G_k^T A_k^T} - G_k \Big\|_F^2 + \big\| \widetilde{G}_k \big\|_F^2 \nonumber + \Big\| G_k (A_k G_k)^\dagger \widetilde{A}_k \widetilde{G}_k \Big\|_F^2,
\end{align}
furthermore,
\begin{align*}
    \mathrm E(k) &=\mathrm E_A \mathrm E_{x^\star \sim \mathcal{G}_n} \big\| \hat{x}(k) - x^\star \big\|_2^2 \\
    &= \mathrm E_{A_k} \left( \| G_n \|_F^2 - \Big\langle G_k^2, P_{G_k^T A_k^T} \Big\rangle + \Big\| G_k (A_k G_k)^\dagger \Big\|_F^2 \sum_{i = k+1}^n \sigma_i^2 \right)
\end{align*}
where $P_{G_k^T A_k^T} = G_k^T A_k^T (A_k G_k G_k^T A_k^T)^{-1} A_k G_k$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.967186+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_bdf07cca10b1cc1787f3ba704f348f20e62f484114f5e75951940a2f35058830","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 9 of arXiv:2606.09904, 'Non-explosion principles for branched rough differential equations with unbounded coeffici'] For a \(\gamma\)-H\"older rough path \(\mathbf{X}\) and a path \(\mathbf{Y} : [0, T] \to \CH^*_{N - 1}\), 
