{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:57:28.721167+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c0a825471865a259d633f85d121f7c27ede7393adc7ea2222537d6dd1a0fc119","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 of arXiv:2609.01190, 'Rough differential equations on manifolds via natural bundles'] Let $m,n\in\Nsf$, $p\in [1,3)$, $x\in C^{p-\mathrm{var}}([S,T],\Rsf^n)$, and let $f_\alpha^i:\Rsf^m\to\Rsf$ (for $i\in\llbracket 1, m \rrbracket$ and $\alpha\in\llbracket 1,n \rrbracket$) be smooth functions. Let also $Y_S\in\Rsf^m$. Consider the system of controlled differential equations
	\begin{equation}

		\d{Y}^i  = f_{\alpha}^i(Y)\d{x}^\alpha, 
			\quad 
		Y^i(S) = Y_S^i,
	\end{equation}
for $i\in \llbracket 1, m \rrbracket$. Given a rough path lift $(X^\tau)$ of function $x$ (see \autoref{ex:natural-lift}), we say that a function $Y: [S,T]\to\Rsf^m$ is a \emph{Davie solution} to problem~\eqref{eq:ode} if $Y(S) = Y_S$ and if there exists a constant $C\in (0,\infty)$ such that the inequality
	\begin{equation}

		\left|
			Y^i(t) - Y^i(s) 
			- f_\alpha^i(Y(s)) X^{\ta}(s,t) 
			- \left(
				\frac{\partial f_\beta^i}{\partial y^j}f_\alpha^j
			  \right)
			(Y(s)) X^{\tc} (s,t)
		\right| 
		\leq C\omega(s,t)^\frac{3}{p}
	\end{equation}
holds for every $i\in \llbracket 1,m \rrbracket$ and $(s,t)\in \Delta [S,T]$.","status":"unverified"}

