{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:06:06.292244+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c185269e539330303264843119495b0f0634eee34456be158f367cb4e2c1f034","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:beta_perturb of arXiv:2605.21265, 'The non-Hermitian minor process'] Fix a (small) $c_0>0$ and a (large) $L>0$. For $w_j=E_j\pm\mathrm{i}\eta_j$ it holds that 
\begin{equation}
\beta_+\beta_-(w_1,w_2) = \beta_+\beta_-(\mathrm{i}\Im w_1,\mathrm{i}\Im w_2) +\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{|E_1|}{\eta_1}+\frac{|E_2|}{\eta_2}\right),

\end{equation}
uniformly in $x_1,x_2\in [c_0,1]$, $x_1\le x_2$, $|z_j|\le L$ and $w_j=E_j\pm\mathrm{i}\eta_j$ with $-L\le E_j\le L$, $0<\eta_j\le L$, $j=1,2$. Here by $\beta_+\beta_-(w_1,w_2)$ we abbreviated the dependence of $\beta_+\beta_-$ on $w_1,w_2$, while the parameters $z_1,z_2$ are the same for both $\beta_+\beta_-$ terms in (equation eq:beta_perturb of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

