Furthermore, if $\gamma\in(0,1)$ and $R\in E^{\gamma}(\Delta_T^2; B_\alpha)$, then $\Theta_\tau R \in F^{\gamma}(\Delta_\tau^2; B_\alpha)$
and for every $0<\varepsilon<\gamma$,
\[\|\Theta_\tau R\|_{\gamma-\varepsilon,\alpha+\varepsilon;\tau}\le M_{\alpha+\varepsilon,T}\|R\|_{\gamma-\varepsilon,\alpha+\varepsilon};\]
if $R\in E_{\log}^{1}(\Delta_T^2; B_\alpha)$, then $\Theta_\tau R \in F_{\log}^{1}(\Delta_\tau^2; B_\alpha)$ and for every $\varepsilon\in(0,1)$,
