{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:00:46.817144+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c2c589724b48a64fba65d00bfad41a1cde3c1418a2df3aacce13ad6a6e7ccf71","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 25 of arXiv:2608.12804, 'Scaling Limits for Ising Models on Inhomogeneous Random Graphs and Applications'] Let $f: [0,1] \to \R$ be Riemann integrable and $\beta < \frac{1}{\|W\|_{\mathrm{op}}}$. Then for small enough $t$,
