{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.975108+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c388d7214545306075b3084ef7f254337376c622e5d2ff42c9ea069fca6547c6","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 11 of arXiv:2606.11142, 'Strong invariance principles for diffusions, Markov chains and their perturbations.'] (Simplified Proposition 3.3 from \cite{Bitter}). There exists a positive constant $C$ such that for every time-grid $\mathbb{T}_h = \{t_i\}_{i=1}^N$ and every $x, y \in \mathbb{R}^d$, the following holds:
