{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T10:52:57.678004+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c433371869b4a9ae4e4cb186c6b68717c98f4f8f52ac22854ae5faa90655f7fe","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 11 of arXiv:2609.02699, '\vspace{-0.5 cm}Gauge theory and symplectic structures'] In dimension $6$, on a closed K\"ahler $3$-fold, for any $(A,\beta,\phi)$, we have the inequality
    \begin{align*}
        \mathcal E(A,\beta,\phi)\geq -8\pi^2\langle c_1(\mathcal L)^2\cup [\omega],[M]\rangle
    \end{align*}
    with equality if and only if $(A,\beta,\phi)$ solves the equations \eqref{Dirac}, \eqref{Curvature}. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:56:25.272176+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c438c1178690a170b46c18c0f2c95cf6d5124b0c3ea2a033d8963ee87143fabb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2606.21111, 'On Elephant Random Walk with Delayed Amnesia'] For $n\ge a$, let
\begin{equation*}
s_n=\Big(\frac{a(2p-1)}{2a(1-p)-1}\Big)^2\sum_{k=a}^{n}(b_kc_k^{-1})^2.
\end{equation*}
Then,\vspace{.1cm}\\
\noindent{(i)} for $0\le p< (4a-1)/4a$, we have
\begin{equation*}
\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{s_n}{n^{4a(1-p)-1}}=\frac{(\Gamma(a(2p-1)+1))^2}{4a(1-p)-1},
\end{equation*} 
\noindent{(ii)} for $p=(4a-1)/4a$, we have
\begin{equation*}
\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{s_n}{\log n}=\Big(\Gamma\Big(a+\frac{1}{2}\Big)\Big)^2,\ \ \text{and}
\end{equation*}
\noindent{(iii)} for $(4a-1)/4a<p\le 1$, we have $\lim_{n\to\infty}s_n=l$,
where $l$ is some non zero constant. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.114643+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c43ff87d52d6269d8c58c4481c715ef353260dfa7dcd956ac527daf453bd240e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem L:1.1 of arXiv:2608.16170, '\bf On hitting time distributions of Markov processes with sub-Gaussian heat kernel bounds'] Assume that $X$ satisfies (AC), (H1a), and (H1b), and additionally that $({\mathcal{E}},{\mathcal{F}})$ is transient. 

Let $B\subset E$ be a nearly Borel set of finite $0$-order capacity. Then there exists a unique  finite, positive measure $\nu_B$ with $\mathrm{supp}[\nu_B]\subset \overline{B}$ such that 
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P}^x[\sigma_B<\infty]=\int_E u(x,y)\nu_B(\mathrm{d} y),\quad \forall x\in  E,
\end{equation}
where $u(x,y)$ denotes the potential kernel of $X$.
In particular,
\begin{equation}
{\mathbb{P}}^x\left[\sigma_B\le t\right] \ge \emph{Cap}_{(0)}(B)\inf_{y\in \overline B}\int_0^t  p(s, x, y)\mathrm{d} s,\quad \forall t>0,x\in E.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.369917+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c44d72afcbf02656c83f1fc2b3c2f9ecae484311c7c3887b04f22a1af9285366","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 18 of arXiv:2606.03534, 'Construction and simulation of a path-valued model of dendrite development'] Define the processes
    \begin{align*}
        A_t = \int a \, d\mu_t \,, \quad I_t = \int 1-a \, d\mu_t \,,
    \end{align*}
    which count the number of active and inactive branches respectively. 
    Then $A_t$ is equal to the number of dendrite tips and $I_t$ is equal to the number of branch points.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.695285+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c45521ebf11b2711abe78544e0f450160d87b6b38267bcbe7901810242564145","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:marginals of arXiv:2510.22778, 'Free denoising diffusion models'] The unique adapted solution of (equation eq:forward of the paper) is
\begin{equation}
  X_{t}=\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}\,X_{0}
  +\int_{0}^{t}\sqrt{\tfrac{\alpha_{t}}{\alpha_{s}}}\,\sqrt{\beta(s)}\;\mathrm{d} S_{s},
\end{equation}
and its spectral law is
\begin{equation}
  \mu_{t}:=\mu_{X_{t}}=\big(D_{\sqrt{\alpha_{t}}}\mu_{0}\big)\boxplus\gamma_{1-\alpha_{t}},
\end{equation}
where $D_{c}\mu$ denotes the pushforward of $\mu$ under $x\mapsto cx$. In particular
$\int x^{2}\mathrm{d}\mu_{t}=\alpha_{t}\int x^{2}\mathrm{d}\mu_{0}+(1-\alpha_{t})$ and
$\mu_{t}\to\gamma$ in $W_{2}$ as $\Lambda(t)\to\infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:28:53.657239+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c45a434c9540218d1df233199d0735f7487a2f5cd16c64e6be4ce1169c16c38d","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition 2 (diffusion local time) of arXiv:2605.13648, 'Sticky CIR process with potential: invariant measure and exact sampling'] \label[definition]{diffusion-local-time}
  For a diffusion $X$ with speed measure $m$, the \emph{diffusion local time} $\ell_t^a$ at level $a$ is defined by
\[
\ell^a_t(X) = \lim_{\varepsilon \downarrow 0} \frac{1}{m((a-\varepsilon, a+\varepsilon))} \int_0^t \mathbf{1}_{\{|X_s - a| < \varepsilon\}}\,ds.
\]
The following occupation-time formula holds: 
for measurable $f \geq 0$,
\begin{equation}
\int_0^t f(X_s)\,ds = \int f(a)\,\ell^a_t(X)\,m(da).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:31:14.333557+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c4625c44351cf88904e95feae4c222682a82ec91de6c781fcee8ac865bff65c4","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma of arXiv:2606.16609, 'On stability of outliers from the circular law'] Set $Q_N(z):=1+b_N^*\mathbf{R}_{N}(z)\mathbf{R}_{N}(z)^*b_N$ for $z \notin Sp (D_N)$ and denote by $\mu_1,\ldots,\mu_{N-1}$ the eigenvalues of $D_N$. Then 
   \begin{equation*}
       Q_N(z) \overset{}{=} \prod_{k=1}^{N-1}\left(1+\frac{\lvert X_k\lvert^2}{N\lvert z- \mu_k \lvert^2}\right)
   \end{equation*}
   where $X_1,\ldots,X_{N-1}$ are i.i.d. standard complex Gaussian random variables, independent of $\mu_1,\ldots,\mu_{N-1}.$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:01:54.286650+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c4645abc34a7d21a2f214f329e7a39d07666c8b835b4bbb8e3a75ebae9c638ea","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm thm 4.8 of arXiv:2411.01847, 'Well-Posedness of Stochastic Chemotaxis System'] Let $(u, v, \tau_m)$ be a local mild solution of system ((main of the paper)), with $\tau_m$ defined by
    \begin{align*}
        \tau_m = \inf \{ t > 0 \mid \|u\|_{\Upsilon^u_t} \geq m \}.
    \end{align*}
    Then, for $p\geq 2$, the following It\^{o} formula for $\|u(t)\|_{p}^{p}$ holds $\mathbb{P}$-a.s. for all $t \in [0, T]$,
    \begin{align*}
        &\|u(t \wedge \tau_m)\|_{p}^{p} - \|u_0\|_{p}^{p} +p(p - 1)  \int_0^{t\wedge\tau_m}\|\nabla u^{\frac{p}{2}}(s)\|_2^2 \, ds \nonumber \\
        &= p(p - 1) \chi \int_0^{t \wedge \tau_m} \int_\mathcal{O} u^{p - 1}(s) \nabla u(s) \cdot \nabla G * u(s) \, dx \, ds \nonumber \\
        &\quad + p \int_0^{t \wedge \tau_m} \int_\mathcal{O} u^{p - 1}(s) g(u(s)) \, dx \, ds \nonumber \\
        &\quad + p \sum_{k=1}^\infty \int_0^{t \wedge \tau_m} \int_\mathcal{O} \sigma_k(u(s)) u(s) |u(s)|^{p - 2} \, dx \, dW^k_s \nonumber \\
        &\quad + \frac{p(p - 1)}{2} \int_0^{t \wedge \tau_m} \int_\mathcal{O} \sum_{k=1}^\infty |\sigma_k(u(s))|^2 |u(s)|^{p - 2} \, dx \, ds.
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:36:23.126439+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c470701936eb9b6dcb53b7bee94f15c8984117bd692405359e6b3f2733ba7eb6","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem CNFormula of arXiv:2506.18207, 'Cartan's Path Development, the Logarithmic Signature and a Conjecture of Lyons-Sidorova'] For any $\lambda,\mu\in \mathbb{C}$, one has 
