Then \(\sup_kE_k<\infty\) and \(\sup_k\ell_k<\infty\), with a bound depending
only on \(E_0\), \(\ell_0\), \(C_0\), and \(\sum_k b_k\).  If, in addition,
\begin{equation}
        \inf_k\ell_k>0,
\end{equation}
then there is a number \(\ell_\infty>0\) such that
\begin{equation}
        \ell_k\longrightarrow\ell_\infty,
        \qquad E_k\longrightarrow2.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.424973+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c4acb0c505cae2e70606cbeab423579fd163579bde23adccdf632c13b2ab1f5f","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 160 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] The total number of lozenge tilings of the trapezoid of width $N$ and with dents at $\ell_1 < \ell_2 < \dots < \ell_N$ is
