{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-09T06:55:03+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c4dc596a2af45a7744e46448bbb28c5e51deb2abc0ec057f6471cb90dcf17b7d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 9 of arXiv:2507.06186, '2507.06186'] Suppose that the hypotheses in Theorem \ref{Theorem: Main}
hold.
Let $t_1>t_2>\cdots>0$ be a vanishing sequence of positive numbers
such that $t_n\leq\tilde c\mr e^{-cn^{1/2+\eps}}$ for some fixed $\tilde c,c,\eps>0$.
For every $\ka>0$,
\[\lim_{n\to\infty}\tfrac{4\pi^2}{\msf{A}(D)\log t_n}\Big(\msf T_\ka(t_n)-\msf T_0(t_n)\Big)=\ka^2\qquad\text{almost surely}.\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

