{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:09:49.849425+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c7e3986eb32bba89d59a28542e7020b662ebe49f63062864a639c21a95180fb1","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 61 of arXiv:2609.03070, 'Variants of order semicontinuity in Banach lattices'] $F$ is $r$-$\sigma$-semicontinuous if and only if the common $\sigma$-order and $\mathrm{u\sigma o}$ closure of $\Ba_{F}$ is contained in $r\Ba_{F}$. Moreover, the following conditions are equivalent:
