{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:54:12.223233+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_c8c528f85f5509d69e52b76821f7dfef923410c06e16256e84b0428e7f90bb15","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma two-spin-existence-boundary-locmin of arXiv:2603.01322, 'Gibbs conditioning, atypical consensus and splitting Gibbs measures on random regular grap'] Let $\X=\{1,-1\}$ and $\nu=\mathsf{Unif}(\X)$. Given an edge potential $h$ and $\cc\in \cpr{\k h_{\min},\k h_{\max}}$, 
