{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T13:47:12.028089+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cb32788f21d02b4d05bd7f5402fa3339d0f82c5b18098d8d56faf0fdd41f30c9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:5 of arXiv:2512.09219, 'Strong confluence of geodesics in Liouville quantum gravity'] {GM20}}]

  There exists a constant $\eta>0$ for which the following holds. Using $\rho_{\varepsilon}(z)$ to denote $\rho_{\varepsilon}^{\lfloor \eta \log \varepsilon^{-1}\rfloor}(z)$, for each compact set $K\subseteq \mathbb{C}$ and each $\text{\usefont{U}{bboldx}{m}{n}z}\in \mathbb{C}$, it holds with probability $1-O(\varepsilon^2)$ at a rate depending only on $K$ that
