{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:50:48.852932+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ccdec52fb409264b646155ce11b870c72ea7e53c68f5d3aa9d810489b42e5ada","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:stat.dist.alpha=0 of arXiv:2607.10708, 'A class of Markov processes with resetting and applications to cybersecurity'] Let $X=(N,\Lambda,C)$  be a self-exciting PDMP with resetting and $Y=(N,\Lambda)$. Under Assumption (a:finitereset of the paper) holds and with $\alpha=0$, there exists an invariant measure $\Pi$ for $Y$, given by the following, for $\lambda \in ({\lambda^o}, A)$:

\begin{equation} 
    \begin{split}
      \Pi(0, d \lambda) &=\frac{K_0}{{\lambda^o}} \delta_{{\lambda^o}}(d\lambda)\\
      \Pi(1, d \lambda) &=\frac{K_0}{\lambda}\,dG_{\ell}(1, \lambda-{\lambda^o})\\
      \Pi(n, d \lambda) &=\frac{1}{\lambda}  d\overline G_{\ell}(n,\lambda)
    \end{split}

\end{equation}
    with $K_0=\sum_{n=1}^\infty\int_{[{\lambda^o},A)}\lambda \bar{G}_{\ell}(n, (A-\lambda) \textrm{-})\Pi(n-1,d\lambda)$ and
    where $\overline \Pi(n,d\lambda) := \lambda \Pi(n,d\lambda)$
    and $\overline G_{\ell}^\star(n,\cdot) :=G_{\ell}(n,\cdot) \star \overline \Pi(n-1,\cdot)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:41:19.328006+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cce495cc4cfb13e0e8babd393e5fea156609f23e3114ace9a4a2092843833eed","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition Horizontal perimeter of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] For a measurable set $\Omega\subset \mathbb{G}$, its \emph{horizontal perimeter} is defined by
\begin{align*}
    \operatorname{Per}_{\mathcal H}(\Omega)=\sup\left\{\int_{\Omega}\sum_{i=1}^{d} X_i \rho_i: \|\sum_{i=1}^d \rho^2_i\|_\infty\leqslant 1, \rho_i\in C_c^\infty(\mathbb G)\right\},
\end{align*}
where $\{X_1, \ldots, X_{d}\}$ is an orthonormal frame in $V_1$. A measurable set $\Omega\subset \mathbb{G}$ is called a \emph{Caccioppoli set} if $\operatorname{Per}_{\mathcal H}(\Omega)<\infty$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:06:42.720653+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ccfbd206b86f278af6be37ca6f3d971afc8627ee492669f6f213064182de70a5","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi iota of arXiv:2411.04157, 'Stochastic homogenization of dynamical discrete optimal transport'] For $J\in \mathbb{R}^{\mathcal E}_a$ we define $\iota J\in \mathcal{M}(\mathbb{R}^n;\mathbb{R}^n)$ by 
    \begin{align*}
        \iota J=\frac12\sum_{(x,y)\in\mathcal E}J(x,y)\frac{y-x}{|y-x|}\mathcal{H}^1|_{[x,y]}. 
    \end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:52:51.770081+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ccfd683cb53273f5280f60c8fd3bf2d837b39a89edb1b7cb09cae458200c72da","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma forward estimate of arXiv:2605.03151, 'Giants through Higher-Order paths in Random Simplicial Complexes'] Let $k \geq 0$ and let $v$ be a vertex that can create a forward $d$-dimensional simplex with a $(d-1)$-simplex $\sigma_k$ that is being explored at Step $k$. Then, given $\mathcal{X}_{k-1}$, the probability that $\sigma_k \cup \{v\}$ appears at Step $k$ is lower bounded by
\[  \tag{3.2.3}
p_k^F := \left( 1 - (k-1) \frac{\lambda}{n} - \sum_{\ell = 1}^{d-1} \sum_{\rho \subseteq \sigma_k, \dim(\rho) = \ell-1} \deg_{\ell-1, d-1}^{\mathcal{X}_{k-1}} (\rho)  p_{d, \ell}  \right) \left( \frac{\lambda}{n} + o(1) \right).
\]
In particular, if the given MRSC model is the Linial-Meshulam model, the probability is exactly $\lambda/n + o(1)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T20:19:06.751656+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd109099319789de88f331010a4571246605d452ded98f6b127e40f6d8203d0b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:exact-dimension-support-mass-witnesses of arXiv:2606.08683, 'Exact Fourier dimensions of dyadic Mandelbrot cascades under minimal integrability'] Assume the minimal Kahane--Peyri\`ere regime. Let \(\beta>A_{\mathrm{loc}}(W)\), let \(\Lambda\) be the block-count exponent in Lemma~(lem:biggins-chernoff-block-count-exponent of the paper), and let \(C\) be a nonnegative random variable with \(0<C<\infty\) almost surely on \(\mathcal S_\circ\). Then, almost surely on \(\mathcal S_\circ\),
\begin{equation*}
\dim_{\mathrm H} E_{\beta,C}(\mu_\circ)=\Lambda(1-\beta).
\end{equation*}
Equivalently,
\begin{equation*}
\dim_{\mathrm H} E_{\beta,C}(\mu_\circ)
=
\inf_{q\ge0}
\left\{
1+\log_2\mathbb E(W^q)-q(1-\beta)
\right\},
\end{equation*}
where \(W^0=\mathbf 1_{\{W>0\}}\), and the value inside the infimum is interpreted as \(+\infty\) whenever \(\mathbb E(W^q)=+\infty\).","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:36:31.237386+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cd27d6b0f0aca120066b8592547ec8a9640260471497210787c6b2a1ead3dc34","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 39 of arXiv:2609.00567, 'Hodge--Tate splitting and Akizuki--Nakano vanishing in positive characteristic'] Let \(k\) be a perfect field of characteristic \(p\) and let \(T\) be an algebraic fpqc \(k\)-stack.
