{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:19:42.623851+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_cdeacc0421737b5446085099da09c6b9474a784da1b6091ab1f4b0b485ef106e","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 23 of arXiv:2609.03512, ''] Let $g(G)=3$ and $r(G)\in \{2,3,4,5\}$. Then $\gamma(G)=\gamma_t(G)=2$ if and only if $G$ belongs to one of the following classes:
