{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.693937+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d18f74b5c2d87354f0be9c881129f1844da0923b27dccf3d7546aad56e6ab380","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop rest2 of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] If $\gamma$ is chosen small enough, then, given any $0 < \eta' < \eta < \frac{1}{2}$ small enough \mbox{(depending only on $\gamma$),} for any fixed $u \geq 0$ we have
