\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:51:00.244689+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d27096dece176499445dc6a09e911a1a3aa3a8677b664e587e997ff02357aac3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem: fixed point CLT_growing m of arXiv:2604.23890, 'The Cutoff Profile for Random Transpositions on Repeated Cards in the Full Range of Parame'] Let $n=ml$, such that $m=\omega(1)$ and $l=\omega(1)$. Suppose $
