{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.331619+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d66921aac787488b60c92a471f036e8896fa05f7fe07d2c79e9c7cdc9dd344c6","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem Th:Chen-Strichartz of arXiv:2411.06827, 'The Exponential Lie Series and a Chen--Strichartz Formula for L{\'e}vy Processes'] The logarithm of  the flowmap has the following series representation
\begin{enumerate}
\begin{align*}
	\log\varphi_t 
& \,= \log\biggl(\sum\limits_{w\in{\mathbb A}^\ast} J_w(t) V_w\biggr)
\\
 &\,   = \sum\limits_{w\in{\mathbb A}^\ast}J_w(t)\biggl(\sum_{\sigma\in{\mathbb S}(|w|)}
\frac{1}{|\sigma|} c_\sigma 
V_{[\sigma (w)]_{\mathrm L}}\biggr),
\end{align*} 
\end{enumerate}
where 
$$
	c_\sigma:=\frac{(-1)^{d(\sigma)}}{|\sigma|}
	\biggl(\begin{array}{c}
	|\sigma|-1\\
	d(\sigma)
		\end{array}
	\biggr),
$$
and where $d(\sigma)$ denotes the number of descents in the permutation $\sigma \in {\mathbb S}_{|w|}$ and $|\sigma|:=|w|$. In particular, it can be represented as
$$\log\varphi_t = \sum\limits_{w\in{\mathbb A}^\ast} J_w(t) V_{\psi(w)},$$
where
$\psi(w):=\sum\limits_{\sigma\in{\mathbb S}(|w|)} 
\frac{1}{|\sigma|}c_\sigma [\sigma (w)]_{\mathrm L}$ is a Lie series.
Here $[w]_{\mathrm L}$ denotes the left-to-right Lie-bracketing of its letters, i.e., we have 
$
	[a_1\cdots a_n]_{\mathrm L}
	=[a_1, [a_2, \ldots [a_{n-1}, a_n]_{\mathrm L}]_{\mathrm L}\ldots ]_{\mathrm L}.
$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:52.419977+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d671ba8e4a648ea07c32f6ac33cfc3a2b9fd513efdec06f019e1640152c59b10","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 125 of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] In the setting of Theorem~\ref{proposition_FFF_conditioning}, let $\mu^X$ be the equilibrium measure of the ensemble $X$, $\mu^Y$ the equilibrium measure of $Y$. Let $h \in [H]$ and set $\amsmathbb{A}_h^{Y} = \amsmathbb{A}^Y \cap [\hat{a}_h',\hat{b}_h']$. For any $\delta > 0$, there exists constants $C_1,C_2 > 0$ depending only on $\delta$ and the constants in the assumptions such that, for any $z \in \amsmathbb{C}$ at distance at least $\delta$ from $\amsmathbb{A}_h^Y$, we have
\[
\bigg|\int_{\amsmathbb{A}^{Y}_h} \frac{\mu_h^X(x) - \mu^{Y}_h(x)}{z - x} \dd x \bigg| \leq \frac{C_1}{\N}.
\]
The upper bound is actually
\[
\bigg|\int_{\amsmathbb{A}^{Y}_h} \frac{\mu_h^X(x) - \mu^{Y}_h(x)}{z - x} \dd x \bigg| \leq \frac{C_2}{\N^2}.
\]
in case the following three conditions hold simultaneously
\begin{itemize}
\item the endpoints $\hat{a}_h'$ and $\hat{b}'_h$ are in a void, or $\theta_{h,h} = 1$;
\item $\iota_h^{-,X} = 0$, or $\rho_{h,j}^{-,X} = \theta_{h,h}$ for every $j \in [\iota_h^{-,X}]$;
\item $\iota_h^{+,X} = 0$, or $\rho_{h,j}^{+,X} = \theta_{h,h}$ for every $j \in [\iota_h^{+,X}]$.
\end{itemize}
Similar results hold in the setting of Theorem~\ref{proposition_fluct_conditioning}, provided we take $\mu^X$ to be the measure obeying fixed filling fractions constraints and compare it with $\mu^Y$ corresponding to the same constraints. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:47.662425+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d67941876d08ace58a1f53f3435c3b5675173f4b304576328004373b38a24c05","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2605.09372, 'Sharp weighted norm estimates for martingale square functions'] Let  $1<p<\infty$.  If $W\in A_p$, then
