{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:27:25.787795+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d6796eb452f5022d59040740d593ac94a34654c3d6af8ebaf53e3beba9a8389e","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem maximal-vertical-oscillations-with-floor of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] Consider a $2N\times 2N$ box with boundary conditions that are $+$ on the bottom side, and $-$ on the other three sides, for $N\ge e^{\beta/5}$. There exists a $C$ (independent of $\beta$) such that for all $\beta>\beta_0$, for all $h$, 
