\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:16:18.685085+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d6fdfc59764c13fe54af4c34f3000a7751f08188616755b7a4bed3d5eee26009","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 7 (Analytic evaluation lemma) of arXiv:2607.26377, '\textbf{Entire Logarithmic Signatures\\ of Bounded-Variation Paths in Finite Dimensions}'] Let $\gamma:[0,T]\to V$ be continuous and of bounded variation, and put $g=S(\gamma)$ and $l=\log g$.
Assume $R(l)=\infty$.
Define
\[
A_{\Phi}(z)=\sum_{n\geq 1}z^n\Phi^{(n)}(l_n),
\qquad
G_{\Phi}(z)=\sum_{n\geq 0}z^n\Phi^{(n)}(S_n(\gamma)).
\]
Then both functions are entire and
\begin{equation}
G_{\Phi}(z)=\e^{A_{\Phi}(z)}
\qquad (z\in\C).
\end{equation}
Moreover,
\begin{equation}
\norm{G_{\Phi}(z)}
 \leq \exp\!\bigl(\abs{z}\,\norm{\Phi}\,L(\gamma)\bigr).
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:01:39.423126+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d705735866cc02c1cad07c7a10627e2c568d26d013efa63981221490593ecb71","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Definition def:first-second-functionals-fg of arXiv:2607.22156, 'A random matrix approach to lamplighter groups'] Let $x,y\in\mathbb{C}[G]$. The first and second order distributions are defined by
