{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T12:52:05.701171+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d74c5f5488914cc91630ee44d9c46a31bc7158ad7fa15923bd12fd8fe0819452","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem idlaw of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] Given $T \in \mathbb N$, the random walk $\widetilde{X}^{[0,T]}$ satisfies:
\begin{itemize}
\item [\rm{i.}] For any $i=0,\dots,T-1$, $j=i,\dots,T-1$, $v \in \mathcal N_k$ and $m \in \mathbb{N}$, conditional on $T_{\widetilde{v}_k}(T-i)=m$, 

\begin{equation}
T_{\widetilde{v}_k}(T-j) \sim \Bigeo\left(m, \frac{1}{j-i+1},\frac{1}{j-i+1}\right)	.
\end{equation}
 	\item [\rm{ii.}] For any $i=1,\dots,T$ and $v \in \mathcal N_k$, 
	\begin{equation}
	\widetilde{L}_{(v)}(T-i) \sim \Biexp\left(\widetilde{v}_k,\frac{1}{i};\frac{1}{i}\right).
\end{equation}
	\item [\rm{iii.}] For any $i=0,\dots,T-1$, $j=i,\dots,T-1$ and $\theta >0$, conditional on $\sqrt{\widetilde{L}_{(v)}(T-i)}=\theta$, 
\begin{equation}
T_{\widetilde{v}_k}(T-j) \sim \Poigeo\left(\frac{\widetilde{\theta}_k}{j-i+1};\frac{1}{j-i+1}\right).
\end{equation}
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:42:57.241175+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d7556d0caec6798336657c493094f90955c327d39a7217529181f41017395f30","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:oracle-persistence of arXiv:2608.20295, 'Physical-Support Confidence Sets for Highly Coherent Dictionaries'] On the balanced orientation submodel in Equation~(equation eq:balanced-hard-core of the paper),
suppose an oracle reveals the coherent-block identity, the scale $s$, the active
support, equal positive coefficients, the separated atom, the coefficient
law, the noise levels, and all nonorientation nuisance parameters. Over a
fixed injective local orientation path, every uniformly valid confidence
correspondence still satisfies
\begin{equation}
    \inf_{\widehat C}
    \sup_{|h|\le h_0}
    \mathbb E_h
    \operatorname{diam}_{\mathrm{pr}}(\widehat C)
    \ge
    c\left(
        s\wedge\frac{1}{\sqrt N\,s^2}
    \right),

\end{equation}
where the infimum ranges over correspondences with marginal coverage at least
$1-\alpha$, for fixed $\alpha<1/2$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:02:08.142224+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d76129fa8633655ddac1f246958a502d696202e44d86afde8a63ec73d9b91edb","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2608.27630, 'Oriented planar maps and \\ annular mating of trees'] Let $k\in\bN$ and let $\cG_k$ be the set of  maps in $\cG$ with $k$ edges on the outer boundary.  Then 
\begin{enumerate}
    \item For each $k\geq 1$, there exists a   bijection between $\mathcal G_k$ and $\mathcal H_k$ which sends an oriented annular map to the associated pair of height functions and preserves the weights~\eqref{eq: planar map weight} and~\eqref{eq: lattice path weight}.
    \item Fix $b>0$. Let $G$ be sampled from $\mathcal G_{\lfloor b\sqrt{N}\rfloor} $ according to the weights~\eqref{eq: planar map weight} with associated height function $(\sfZ_j)_{0\leq j\leq n}$. Then as $N\to \infty$, the law of $(\frac{1}{\sqrt N}\sfZ_{\lfloor Nt \rfloor })_{0\leq \lfloor Nt \rfloor\leq n}$ converges in distribution to $\int_0^\infty \d a B^{\gamma, \bH}_{0, -a+ib}$ with respect to the metric~\eqref{eq:curve-metric}. The   parameter $\gamma$ is given by
    \begin{equation}

        \cos \ab(\frac{\pi\gamma^2}{4}) = \frac{2b_e + 2\sum_{i,j \in \bZ_{\ge 0}} ijb_{i,j}}{2b_e + \sum_{i,j\in \bZ_{\ge 0}}(i^2+j^2) b_{i,j}}
    \end{equation}
    and by choosing  numbers $\{b_e,b_{i,j}:i,j\in\bZ_{\geq0}\}$ properly, $\gamma$ may take every value in $(0,\sqrt{2})$.
\end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

