{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:57:51.740850+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d95cd25cb4f0946226a60630d75ce24a19f97df1be6f03974cc151f6ddaeaecd","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defi 14 of arXiv:2608.30120, 'Graphs of operators as points in the Grassmann manifold'] Let $P$ be an orthogonal projection in $\j=\j_+\oplus\j_-$. Denote $P_+=P_{\j_+}$ and $P_-=P_{\j_-}$. Then $P$ belongs to the restricted Grassmannian $\p_{res}(\j_+)$  (induced by this decomposition) if and only if
\begin{itemize}
\item
$P_+P\big|_{R(P)}:R(P)\to \j_+ $ is a Fredholm operator;
\item
$P_-P\big|_{R(P)}:R(P)\to\j_-$ is  compact operator.
\end{itemize}
The index of $P$ is the index of the above Fredholm operator, and is given by
$$
{\rm ind}_{\j_+}(P)=\dim R(P)\cap\j_--\dim N(P)\cap\j_+.
$$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:53:31.974638+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d9666e1c06e26f660168f83096f79ed497dcbd89f9784729a64704199f21c40b","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2606.11142, 'Strong invariance principles for diffusions, Markov chains and their perturbations.'] For transition densities $p^h, p^h_\epsilon$ of Markov chains there exists a constant $C_1(q) > 0$ such that for any $t_i < t_j$ and $x \in \mathbb{R}^d$:
\begin{equation} 
\int_{\mathbb{R}^d} |p^h(t_i, t_j, x, y) - p^h_\epsilon(t_i, t_j, x, y)| dy \le C_1 \Delta_{\epsilon,\gamma,q}.
\end{equation}
For transition densities $p, p_\epsilon$ of diffusions there also exists a constant $C_2(q) > 0$ such that:
\begin{equation} 
\int_{\mathbb{R}^d} |p(t_i, t_j, x, y) - p_\epsilon(t_i, t_j, x, y)| dy \le C_2 \Delta_{\epsilon,\gamma,q}.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:57:44.955542+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d9745db31a556371176de74ab9c1900f6e66b038595d563befac79b56f6ed652","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2606.25501, 'An RDT based approach to large deviations of Wishart and Wigner matrices spectral edges'] Consider large $n,m\in\mN$ such that $\lim_{n\rightarrow\infty}\frac{m}{n}\rightarrow\alpha\geq 1$ and let $A_{ij}\sim \cN(0,1)$ be the independent elements of $A\in\mR^{m\times n}$. For a real scalar $c_3\geq 0$ set
  \begin{eqnarray}

 \hat{\gamma}_{1} & = &  \frac{c_3 + \sqrt{c_3^2+4\alpha}}{4}
 \nonumber \\
 \phi_{1}(\gamma_1) & = &  \gamma_{1}c_3 - \frac{\alpha}{2}\log \lp 1 - \frac{c_3}{2 \gamma_{1}}   \rp
 \nonumber \\
 \hat{\gamma}_{2} & = &  \frac{c_3 + \sqrt{c_3^2+4}}{4}
 \nonumber \\
 \phi_{2}(\gamma_2) & = &  \gamma_{2}c_3 - \frac{1}{2}\log \lp 1 - \frac{c_3}{2 \gamma_{2}}   \rp.
 \end{eqnarray}
 Let $\xi^+_{sph}$ be as in (\ref{eq:inteq1ab0}) and for a real scalar $u\geq \mE \xi^+_{sph}$ set
 \begin{eqnarray}

 \nonumber \\
 \phi_u(u) & = & -\frac{c_3^2}{2} + \phi_{1}(\hat{\gamma}_1) + \phi_{2}(\hat{\gamma}_2) -c_3 u .
 \end{eqnarray}
One then has the following LDP with the indicator rate function $\zeta_u(u)$
\begin{eqnarray}

\lim_{n\rightarrow \infty} \frac{\log\lp \mP\lp \xi^+_{sph} \geq u  \rp \rp}{n} \leq \min_{c_3\geq 0}\phi_u(u) \triangleq -\zeta_u(u).
\end{eqnarray}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T15:07:17.279719+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_d975c4522cc1f4746fcdf412bc83e51d08d8c4c5bfe0206b1096825b8663b011","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop eq:lesmom of arXiv:2603.21634, 'Individual-based stochastic model with unbounded growth, birth and death rates: a tightnes'] Let $p \geq 1$, and under the \hyperlink{ren}{renormalized setting}, assume in addition that
\begin{align}
    \underset{K \in \mathbb{N}^{*}}{\mathrm{sup}} \hspace{0.1 cm} \mathbb{E}\left(\left(E_{0}^{K} +N_{0}^{K} + \Omega^{K}_{0}\right)^{p}\right) < + \infty.

    \end{align}
Then, for all $T \geq 0$, we have
\[ \sup_{K \in \mathbb{N}^{*}} \mathbb{E}\left( \sup_{t \in [0,T]}\left(E_{t}^{K} +N_{t}^{K} + \Omega^{K}_{t}\right)^{p} \right) < + \infty. \]
This immediately implies that for every $\varphi \in \mathfrak{B}_{1+\mathrm{Id}+\omega}(\mathbb{R}^{*}_{+})$, we have
\[ \sup_{K \in \mathbb{N}^{*}} \mathbb{E}\left(\underset{t \in [0,T]}{\mathrm{sup}} \left|\langle \mu^{K}_{t}, \varphi \rangle\right|^{p} \right) < + \infty. \] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

