Consequently, for every \(K\Subset M\setminus Z\), there exists
\(C_K>0\), independent of \(t\), such that
\begin{equation}
-C_K\leq u_t\leq0\qquad\text{on }K.
\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:33:12.348029+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dc4bd6aaf4f99ddb3b37089dde84a508225d516280b87b6d00685bfe5caa84b7","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Cor 158 of arXiv:2608.29416, 'Algorithmic threshold for high-dimensional projection pursuit I: general theory'] For all $\ell\leq \ubl$, we have 
