{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T22:55:27.268452+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df05addf3f37d3e51f74fbb2b1c37702533709cc47b93b21d556d5bd20cd0a8f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma S51L of arXiv:2410.23899, 'Tightness for interlacing geometric random walk bridges'] For any $a, b \in \Lambda$ with $a < b$, and $\varepsilon > 0$ we can find $W_1 \in \mathbb{N}$ and $M^{\mathsf{top}} > 0$, depending on $a,b$ and $\varepsilon$, such that for $N \geq W_1$ we have 
