{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:24.617912+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_df3857f993be4c3fed94826e3be21eae14cc2af5e28b5fb50c9b6aa3027feacc","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 33 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] For all~$\lambda>0$, $\sigma\in(0,1/10)$ and~$\delta\in(0,1)$ there exist~$c>0$ and~$a_2\ge0$ such that for all $s\ge 1$, all~$u$ satisfying $s\ge u\ge s-\lambda$ and all~$n$ with~$s\le n^{1-\delta}$,
\begin{equation}

\begin{aligned}
Q_{n,s,u}\Biggl(\biggl(\,\bigcap_{k=1}^n\Bigl\{h(x_k)\le&\frac {n-k}n\wt m_n+s+\gamma_{n,a}(k)\Bigr\}\biggr)^\cc\,\Biggr)
\\
&\le
c\frac{(1+s-u)s}n\sum_{1\le k\le n/2}\bigl[k+\gamma_{n,a}(k)^2\bigr]\texte^{-\frac18 c_2\gamma_{n,a}(k)}
