{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:48:47.300302+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_dfd92eca104792de517de98d49ed78c44a719c5efb1d8e6f4e7305f35cc4cff4","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop geographic ineq coupling map of arXiv:2604.21663, 'Large deviations for non-irreducible Markov chains on Euclidean spaces'] Let $\underline u=(u^1,\ldots ,u ^N)\in \widetilde{\mathcal{W}}_n^N$ be such that $\underline u^i:=F_n(u^i)\neq(e,\ldots,e)$ for all $i$, and $\underline v= (\underline u^1,\ldots, \underline u^N)$. Then, for all $w\in \Psi_{N,n, T}(\underline u)$, we have
