{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T08:02:08.132570+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e49d43346d9c42724873011ab81c2bd2fc0b8fb897b51fccccc7897f57651b34","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 8 of arXiv:2608.27500, 'Optimal Transport for Network Comparison: \\ A Review with Machine Learning Applications'] Let $G'=(V,E')$ be a subgraph of $G=(V,E)$, with $|V|=n$, and $|E'|=|E|-1$. If $\mu_G=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^n \delta_{\lambda_i}$ and $\mu_{G'}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^n \delta_{\lambda_i'}$, then
    \begin{align*}
