{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:28:49.058797+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_e85318f83589c62d1bf95bf5a708a9e4a9d889421f9541205cf7f43a9c0ad497","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem thm:zero-terminal-source-problem of arXiv:2608.16119, 'Fully nonlinear parabolic equations under a fixed reference diffusion: weighted \texorpdfs'] Let $\alpha\geq0$ and let $w$ be a regular weight of order $\alpha$.
Suppose that Assumption~(ass:reference-diffusion of the paper) holds and $C_w(X)<\infty$.
For $F\in L_\alpha^2$, the field
$v=SF$ is the unique order-$\alpha$
occupation Sobolev solution with data $(F,0)$, and
\begin{equation}
 \operatorname{Hess}_gv=\mathsf T_wF
 \quad\text{in }\mathcal K_w.

\end{equation}
For every $\kappa\geq1$,
\begin{align}
 \left\lVert v\right\rVert_{w_\kappa}
 &\leq e^{\operatorname{osc}_\alpha(w)/2}
       \kappa^{-1}\left\lVert F\right\rVert_{w_\kappa},\qquad
 \left\lVert \mathsf Z v\right\rVert_{w_\kappa}
