\end{equation}
Consequently, the quotient class $\bigl(\hat\Lambda_{S,\gamma,\alpha}^{\mathrm q}h\bigr)^\tau$ is independent of both the chosen semigroup increment \(B\) and the dyadic normalization used in Section~\ref{sec:dyadic-frozen}.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:24:30.012605+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eaa4ff258c9e63d56160a61d7cd0beb85ffebb261f1957ffac5d30f4d3bb5cf1","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 14 of arXiv:2605.04359, 'Well-posedness of reflected BSDEs with default time and irregular barrier: An application '] Assume that:
