{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:42:08.473423+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eafa52a259abaf1e553706b591120a7ba296115d0c827be0cb55f8ddfbaab0b9","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary corollary5 of arXiv:2511.19391, 'Central limit theorem for supercritical Crump-Mode-Jagers processes counted with non-indiv'] Suppose that assumptions (A1 of the paper)-(A8 of the paper) hold and that $\mu_{\alpha}$ is spread-out such that there exists a Stone's decomposition of its associated renewal measure $e^{-\alpha x} \nu^{(\infty)}({\rm d}x)$ that satisfies (S1 of the paper). Let $\varphi$ be any non-negative $h$-dependent descendant characteristic that vanishes on the negative half-line (i.e., $\varphi(t)= 0$, for $t<0$) and satisfies (C2 of the paper)-(C3 of the paper) and (C5 of the paper). Suppose further that 
