{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:57:28.719550+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb09c9a8858132169ab9f2c24425c51fc48cbfa395a003260bf914e56f526981","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2609.01166, 'Nonparametric inference for density-dependent McKean--Vlasov diffusions'] For any bounded interval $J$ and $\beta>0$ fixed, there exists a constant $C_{\beta,J}$ such that, for all $F\in L^2(J)\cap\mathcal H^{\beta+1}(J)$,
