\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:32:29.004405+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_eb0acce5e7dc7dd531648219112ba901d41b19958cd7cef9f5c195e88f29c0ae","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem typT poly LB of arXiv:2608.25471, 'Exact Hausdorff measures and fine geometry of collisions of independent Markov processes'] There exists a constant $a_1 \in (0, \infty)$ such that, for all sufficiently large $\ell \in \mathbb{N}$,
