     {where $a_t$ and $b_t$ were introduced in (equation def_a_and_b of the paper) and $R_t$ was introduced at the end of Lemma (operators_with_M of the paper).} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:25:44.586774+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ecb5ca944d926179eed3478a7af034e76ac5f0c27df0018b8b2da234113499f5","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lem superstable_log of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] Let $\varphi(x)=-\log\left\lvertx\right\rvert$  and  $\mathsf{P}\in \mathcal P_{s,1}(\Gamma)$ with $\int \xi(\Lambda_1)^2\mathsf{P}(d\xi)<\infty$. Then for $n\in \IN$
