{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.898570+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ee6eb77401304adbdd3c35c857284eb671e3b5b68ddb7cafe1dffa388807dd2f","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 11 (Solving Nekrasov equations with one band) of arXiv:2601.16377, '2601.16377'] Take four real parameters $\hat{a} <\alpha < \beta <\hat{b}$ and set $\sigma(z)=\sqrt{(z-\alpha)(z-\beta)}$. Assume that we have four functions $F(z)$, $A(z)$ (unknown), $E(z)$ and $s(z)$ (known) such that
