where the contour $\gamma$ surrounds $[\hat{a},\hat{b}]$ but leaves $z$ outside.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:11:09.317628+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ee6f91ecf706e8413391c4e4b4f3aaa4ccaf59a2f87358b862132e69b6f7108d","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem fpcomm of arXiv:2411.06131, 'Non-Markovian dynamics: the memory-dependent probability density evolution equations'] Let $ X=(X_t)_{t\in[0,T]} $ be the solutions of the SDEs ((mSDEscom of the paper)), if $ f, g$ and $ h$ are bounded smooth functions and satisfied the commutativity conditions. Then the memory-dependent PDEE for PDFs $ p(x,t) $ of the solutions $ X_t $, satisfies the following equation
