is asymptotically Gaussian as $\N \rightarrow \infty$, in the sense that its cumulants of order $\geq 3$ tend to $0$ as $\N \rightarrow \infty$. Furthermore, if $\theta_{g,g} = 1$ for every $g \in [H]$, then this Gaussian variable is asymptotically centered: the mean is $O(\frac{1}{\N})$ as $\N \rightarrow \infty$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

