{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:45:05.588648+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f56cb9b5256e08d98b64ddef6f4ca75ea03af73721f0f8b10a9c36d0809954f2","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 6 of arXiv:2608.05842, 'Asymptotic Expansion of the Kallianpur–Striebel Formula under Perturbations of Linear Mode'] For any multidimensional random variable $U$ that is independent of $W$ under $P$, the law of $(U, \{Y_t^\epsilon\}_{0\leq t\leq T})$ under $\hat{P}^\epsilon$ is equivalent to the law of $(U, \{\hat{Y}_t^\epsilon\}_{0\leq t\leq T})$ under $P$, where
