{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:54:15.658769+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5d7dbe991cd9de17df3e5758031098a29654b82d9a3ae881f0d264efc678b51","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem 11 of arXiv:2608.09419, 'Left-tail expansions for Schr\"oder branching processes with explicit convergence rates'] \lb{T4} Suppose that the probability generating function $P(z)$ satisfies $P(0)=0$ and $0<p:=P'(0)<1$. Then, the unique solution of the Shr\"oder functional equation 
\[\lb{118}
 \Phi(P(z))=p\Phi(z),\ \ \ \Phi(0)=0,\ \ \ \Phi'(0)=1
\]
exists in some neighborhood of $z=0$. It can be extended analytically to the open connected component of the filled Julia set $\cJ_P(0)$. For its computation, one may use
\[\lb{118a}
\Phi(z)=\lim_{t\to+\iy}p^{-t}\underbrace{P\circ...\circ P}_{t}(z).
\] (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:39:41.441717+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5e0fad04444ec23b8c3bf8914e4de1b4379b17ff9cde862f4c04bc068e55f18","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2604.07478, 'Mixing Times and Cutoff for the Rook's Walk'] Let $\varphi$ be defined as in Definition \ref{defphi}. Then,
   \[\varphi(i) = {d \choose i}(n-1)^i\]
   \begin{proof}
      Fix $i \in \{0,\dots,d\}$. Now, $\varphi(i)$ counts the number of elements in $\mathbb{Z}_n^d$ with Hamming distance of exactly $i$ from $\hat{1}$. That is, the number of elements with $i$ non-one elements. There are ${d \choose i}$ different choices for which dimensions should be non-one, and $(n-1)$ choices for each of these dimensions. 
   \[\therefore \quad \varphi(i) = {d \choose i}(n-1)^i,\quad \forall i \in \{0,\dots,d\}\]
   \end{proof} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:45:07.258131+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5fa4833af035abd9deede802cc6dcaeba56a2e95ffe432abc152637a6bb39d4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 12 of arXiv:2604.19308, '\textbf{On McKean--Vlasov SDEs with polynomial drifts for SIS epidemic models}'] Let~\eqref{co:6} and~\eqref{eq:integrability condition} hold for $\rho = 1$ and $N_{\infty} := \limsup_{t\uparrow\infty} N(t)$ be positive. Then each positive solution $I$ to~\eqref{eq:SIS epidemic model} satisfies the following two statements:
\begin{enumerate}[(i)]
\item If there is a continuous function $f_{\infty}\colon ]0,N_{\infty}]\cap\R_{+}\rightarrow\R$ that admits at least one zero and satisfies $\liminf_{x\downarrow 0} f_{\infty}(x) > 0$ and
\begin{equation*}
\liminf_{s\uparrow\infty} \inf_{x\in ]0,N(s)]:\,x < x_{0}}h\big(s,x,N(s),\mathcal{L}(I_{s})\big) - f_{\infty}(x) \geq 0
\end{equation*}
for the smallest zero $x_{0}$ of $f_{\infty}$, then $I$ persists above $x_{0}$.

\item If there is a continuous function $g_{\infty}\colon \R_{+}\rightarrow\R$ that has at least one zero in $[0,N_{\infty}[$ and satisfies $\limsup_{x\rightarrow N_{\infty}} g_{\infty}(x) < 0$ and
\begin{equation*}
\limsup_{s\uparrow\infty}\sup_{x\in ]0,N(s)]:\,x > y_{0}} h\big(s,x,N(s),\mathcal{L}(I_{s})\big) - g_{\infty}(x) \leq 0
\end{equation*}
for the largest zero $y_{0}$ of $g_{\infty}$ in $[0,N_{\infty}[$, then $\liminf_{t\uparrow\infty} I_{t} \leq y_{0}$ a.s.
\end{enumerate}
In particular, if the requirements of~(i) and~(ii) are met and $x_{0} = y_{0}$, then persistence~\eqref{eq:persistence around a point} around $x_{0}$ holds for $I$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T18:05:28.100291+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f5fac8bbfcfa2a5dfa6f9688a8365046f268b6bfbeae7483d16bd883ae6d28e4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:subcritical of arXiv:2601.20502, 'Optimal matching under size priority'] Define the families of truncated decorated trees $\left(\mathbb{T}_H,o,(i_{-}^{H},Z_{-}^H),(i_{+}^{H},Z_{+}^H)\right)_{H \geq 0}$ as follows:
    Sample $(\mathbb{T},o)$, set $\mathbb{T}_H=B_H(\mathbb{T},o)$ and   $(i_{-}^{H},Z_{-}^H)(u,v)=(0,0)$ for every edge of $\mathbb{T}_H$ pointing towards the $H-$boundary. Then use Recursion~(equation eq:systemrecursionzoombis of the paper) to define $(i_{-}^{H},Z_{-}^H)$ on the remainder of $\mathbb{T}_H$. We proceed similarly for $(i_{+}^{H},Z_{+}^H)$ by setting $(i_{+}^{H},Z_{+}^H)=(1,+\infty)$ on the boundary instead of $(0,0)$.

    Then under condition~(equation eq:subcriticalcond of the paper), both families $((i_{+}^{H},Z_{+}^H)(o,v))_{v \sim o}$ and $((i_{-}^{H},Z_{-}^H)(o,v))_{v \sim o}$ converge almost surely, as $H$ goes to infinity, to the same family $(i_l,Z_l)_{1 \leq l \leq N}$ where $(i_l,Z_l)$ have i.i.d distribution $\zeta'$ and are independent of $N \sim \pi$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:01:48.650454+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f6075e2bc5cb6915453b48e7f58e709ecf822b1229e160a0e90a20856cc50769","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary cor:bw of arXiv:2607.06249, 'Extreme least singular values of Gaussian row submatrices and a phase retrieval stability '] Let $A_m\in\mathbb{R}^{(2m-1)\times m}$ have independent standard Gaussian entries. Then
\begin{equation}
  \frac{1}{m}\log\omega(A_m)\xrightarrow{P}-\log4,
\end{equation}
with the rate
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb{P}\left\{\left|\frac{1}{m}\log\omega(A_m)+\log4\right|>\varepsilon\right\}=O_\varepsilon(m^{-1})
\end{equation}
for every fixed $\varepsilon>0$. Equivalently, $\omega(A_m)=4^{-m+o_P(m)}$.

Let $R_m=\max_{1\le i\le 2m-1}\|a_i\|$. For every $b>1/4$, $\mathbb{P}\{\omega(A_m)\le R_m b^m\}\to1$. For
every $b<1/4$ and every fixed $C<\infty$, $\mathbb{P}\{\omega(A_m)\le C R_m b^m\}\to0$. Thus the Gaussian
critical base in the Balan--Wang question is $1/4$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:38:58.686915+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f61693da9163467538a99faf40147b50e3443aa1f63db92a28897646403f84d4","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:poiss-approx of arXiv:2510.18856, 'Evolution of recursive trees with limited memory'] Let $D_{j,n}$ be the degree of vertex \textcolor{black}{$j$} at time $n$.
    For any $\epsilon > 1$, there exists $j_0$ such that for all $j_0 \leqslant j \leqslant n$,  \begin{align*}
        &d_{TV}\left(D_{j,n}, \text{Poisson}(1)\right) \\
        &\leqslant \epsilon \left[1-(1+\epsilon j^{\beta-1})^{-\beta}\right] + \epsilon j^{-\beta} + \max(\epsilon-1,j^{-\beta})+ \mathds{1}\left\{N_j\geqslant n-j\right\} \abs{\frac{n-j}{j^\beta}-1}
    \end{align*}where $N_j = \abs{\left\{i\geqslant j:i-i^\beta \leqslant j\right\}}.$ (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T05:44:27.981298+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f619fbdec7b3beda5b4705226889b28b7afa9da60f2cbf710326a68a9cc84f48","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2607.13273, 'Asymptotics of transition densities for L\'evy processes with stochastic resetting'] Let $a, b >0$ and $f(s) = \frac{a}{s} + b s,\, s\in (0,\infty).$ Let $\gamma > 0,$ and a positive
    function $g\in C_b(\R_+)$ be such that for some $\kappa\in [0,\infty),$ and $g_0, g_\infty \in (0,\infty)$ we have
    \begin{equation}
        \lim_{s\to 0^+} \frac{g(s)}{s^{\kappa}} = g_0, \quad \lim_{s \to \infty} g(s) = g_\infty.
    \end{equation}
    Then
    \begin{equation}
       \int_0^\infty s^{-\gamma}e^{-rf(s)}g\left(\frac{t^{2/\alpha}}{rs}\right)\, \dx[s]
       \sim \sqrt{\frac{\pi}{a}}\left(\frac{a}{b}\right)^{\frac34 - \frac{\gamma}{2}} \frac{e^{-2r\sqrt{ab}}}{\sqrt{r}} g\left(\frac{t^{2/\alpha}\sqrt{b}}{r\sqrt{a}}\right).
    \end{equation}
    Furthermore, the above asymptotic equality holds also for
    any positive function $g\in C_b(\R_+)$ such that $\lim_{s\to 0^+} \frac{g(s)}{s^\kappa} = g_0$ 
    (without assuming the existence of a positive limit in infinity) provided $\frac{t}{r^{\alpha/2}} <M$ for some constant $M>0.$","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:16:12.366015+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f61b89d5abd13bee419c047fc9a0d682321a1ff676840e0932cb9a4baa2b0760","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[OPEN PROBLEM - not a proved fact. Stated in arXiv:2608.05931, 'Effective Lagrangian regularity and the uniqueness threshold for random Hölder velocity fields' (problem environment).] Construct for some $d \in \N$, $\alpha > 1/2$ a single $u \in C^\alpha(\T^d)$ such that the ODE
