\end{equation}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:30:52.746953+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f760481953a56fbba1ec5e47283b6f56cce4ba3fecac597855d056e0b3b20d29","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2506.10522, 'On the Law of the Iterated Logarithm for $m$-dependent stationary random variables under s'] Suppose $X,Y\in \mathcal{H}_1$ and $X$ is independent to $Y$ under the sub-liner expectation $\mbE$. If $\bE[X]=\be[X]=0$ and $\bE[|X|]<\infty, \bE[|Y|]<\infty$, then 
