{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T20:52:17.374869+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f7b2222343b414fb7140484179ff1a8c7a8b0eaf7df54519da8fde6afa12e1ed","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn 3 of arXiv:2606.04636, 'A Thomson-type variational principle for diffusion coefficients'] Let $l\in\R^{d}$. The flow of particle current
adjacent to $0$ is defined as
\begin{equation}
\phi_{l}(\eta,\eta^{0,z})=\frac{1}{2}(z\cdot l)\ c(0,z;\eta)\left(\eta(0)-\eta(z)\right),\qquad z\in\Z^{d},
\end{equation}
and the overall current adjacent to $0$ is the function 
\begin{equation}
j_{l}(\eta)=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{z\in\Z^{d}}(z\cdot l)\ c(0,z;\eta)\left(\eta(0)-\eta(z)\right).
\end{equation}
The factor $\frac{1}{2}$ is added due to the convention, that when
a particle jumps between $x$ and $y$ we associate half of the corresponding
current to $x$ and the other half to $y$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:32:18.862369+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f7b5d908a9b172b245c6814c354734ed534a3cf45fc74b07e337f7515c0847b0","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 41 of arXiv:2609.03875, 'Measure theory without infinities'] Let $\mf A$ be an HTM and $\mu$ and $\nu$ be $\mf A$-valued premeasures such that $\q{\mu}=\q{\nu}$.
  \begin{enumerate}
  \item[(i)]  $\q{\mu\dotplus\nu}=\q{\mu\boxplus\nu}=\q{\mu}$.
  \item[(ii)] $\mu\boxplus\nu = \as[\mf A]{\mu}\boxplus\nu = \mu\boxplus\as[\mf A]{\nu} = \as[\mf A]{\mu}\boxplus\as[\mf A]{\nu}$.  
  \end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T07:58:01.574874+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f7b5f1e763d9ef4089ccefee683f227664eae67163c45b1ebf766aa5b96a73f3","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 53 of arXiv:2608.27307, '2608.27307'] Under the assumptions of Theorem~\ref{thm:rand_sc_eq}, for every fixed integer $r\geq1$,
        \begin{align}
