{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:55:42.204812+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f7eafb0b34275d0b7a83be7d09929cb0848534be9c3a80334eb448811f24c800","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm eq:modifzakai of arXiv:2411.16366, 'Connections between sequential Bayesian inference and evolutionary dynamics'] \textbf{(Informal Theorem (theo:limitcrowkimura of the paper):) Limiting process of (equation eq:repmutlin of the paper)} Consider a time discretisation of the interval $[0,T]$ with step size $\delta_d$ such that $d \times \delta_d = T$.  Denote by $\{Z_t^d\}_{0 < t \leq T}$ a piecewise linear approximation with step size $\delta_d$ of an observation path generated by (equation eq:obs of the paper).  Finally, let $\mu_t^d \propto \rho_t^d$ denote the unnormalised form of $\rho_t^d$ satisfying (equation eq:repmutlin of the paper).  Then under some conditions, 
		\begin{align*}
			\mu_t^d \rightarrow q_t \quad \text{as} \quad d \rightarrow \infty, \enskip \forall \enskip  t \in [0, T],
		\end{align*}
		where $q_t$ satisfies the modified Zakai equation,
		\begin{align}

			d q_t(x) = \mathcal{L}^\ast q_t(x) -\frac{s}{2}h(x)^\top \Xi^{-1} h(x) q_t(x)  + (r-s)q_t(x) h(x)^\top \Xi^{-1} dZ_t, 
			\tag{$\textbf{ZK}$}
		\end{align}
		with $\mathcal{L}^\ast$ is as defined in (equation eq:repmutlin of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T21:53:10.210967+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f7f2d63de710c1f4dca03e62fe5f1d4b078c966394f57d5055741d454c32fb1d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm vector-main of arXiv:2608.29018, 'Sharp Restricted Isometry Thresholds for\\ Global Minima of Rank-Restricted Matrix LASSO'] Fix integers $r_{\star}\ge1,$ $k\ge2$, and
set $t\coloneqq k/r_{\star}$. Suppose $\normzero{x_{\star}}\le r_{\star}$
