{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T16:38:11.711425+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f81ae97084d9b8079444b308212727e255f35d99f77d4ed0a6c1b1a703acc7c0","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem mix of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] Under (main_assm of the paper), given any $k\in[\![{1,DN}]\!]$, suppose there exists a constant $\varepsilon_A>0$ such that
\begin{equation}
\|A\|_{\text{\rm{HS}}}\ge N^{1/3+\varepsilon_A}{\mathfrak{r}}\left({k}\right)^{-1/3} .
\end{equation}
Then, there exists a constant $c>0$ such that 
\begin{equation}
\mathbb P\left( \max_{a\in\llbracket D\rrbracket}\left|{\bf v}_k^* E_{a}  {\bf v}_k-D^{-1}\right|\ge N^{-c}\right)\le N^{-c},
\end{equation}
where $E_a\in \mathbb{C}^{DN\times DN}$ denotes the block identity matrix restricted to $\mathcal I_a$, i.e., $(E_{a})_{ij}={\bf 1}(i=j\in {\mathcal I}_a)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:27:08.852417+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f81cb429da3af066abdb38b86ac005d01d14d51fbdb08415b7670b530ca87608","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 12 (Ratio identities and diagonal normalization) of arXiv:2511.12623, 'The eigenvector bead process'] For $g_i,g_j\neq0$ and any $k$,
\begin{equation}
