{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T01:47:04.924230+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_f85a28d5dfbf99058892e7b8e6925c01ce86b8dbe06f7953969b1ac3afc0e94d","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Theorem of arXiv:2412.02160, 'A functional central limit theorem for weighted occupancy processes of the Karlin model'] For functions $f:[0,1)\to {\mathbb R}$ such that $(a_j)_{j\in{\mathbb N}}\equiv (a_j(f))_{j\in{\mathbb N}}$ satisfy the assumptions in Theorem (thm:2 of the paper), 
