{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:21:10.889225+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fa233341a862771b57c31fa1d66e6d9fb7a5e9e7132a1f946a6b70dd46f4cd3a","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 39 (Unimodularity of the embedded Delaunay graph) of arXiv:2504.02435, 'Poisson-Voronoi percolation in higher rank'] Let $G$ be a non-compact connected semisimple real Lie group and $(X,d_X)$ be its symmetric space. Let $\mathbf Y$ be a Poisson point process $Y$ on $X$ with intensity $c \, {\rm vol}$ for some $c>0$ and with iid ${\rm Unif}[0,1]$-marks. Let $Y_0=Y\cup\{o\}$ and $\mathbf Y_0=\mathbf Y \cup \{\mathbf o\}$, where $\mathbf o$ is the origin equipped with an independent ${\rm Unif}[0,1]$-mark. Let $\mathcal G$ denote the Delaunay graph associated to ${\rm Vor}(Y_0)$ and let $\rho$ denote the vertex corresponding to the cell of the origin. Then the following hold:
\begin{itemize}
\item[{\rm(1)}] The Delaunay graph $(\mathcal G,\rho)$ defines a unimodular random graph. 
\item[{\rm(2)}] Let $\psi$ denote the marking of the embedded Delaunay graph. Then $(\mathcal G,\rho,\psi)$ satisfies 
\begin{equation}
\mathbb E \bigg[ \sum_{x\in V(\mathcal G)} f(\mathcal G,\rho,x,\psi) \bigg] = \mathbb E \bigg[ \sum_{x\in V(\mathcal G)} f(\mathcal G,x,\rho,\psi) \bigg]
\end{equation}
for every non-negative measurable function $f$ of bi-rooted embedded graphs $(H,u,v,\varphi)$ with the additional property that
\begin{equation} 
f(H,u,v,\tau \circ \varphi)= f(H,u,v,\varphi)
\end{equation}
for every isometry $\tau$ of $X$ which interchanges $\varphi(u)$ and $\varphi(v)$. 
\item[{\rm(3)}] Let $\Psi$ denote the marking of the embedded Delaunay graph with labels. Then $(\mathcal G,\rho,\Psi)$ satisfies 
\begin{equation}
\mathbb E \bigg[ \sum_{x\in V(\mathcal G)} f(\mathcal G,\rho,x,\Psi) \bigg] = \mathbb E \bigg[ \sum_{x\in V(\mathcal G)} f(\mathcal G,x,\rho,\Psi) \bigg]
\end{equation}
for every non-negative measurable function $f$ of bi-rooted embedded labeled graphs $(H,u,v,\Phi=(\varphi,\varphi'))$ with the additional property that 
\begin{equation} 
f(H,u,v,\tau \circ \Phi)= f(H,u,v,\Phi)
\end{equation} 
for every isometry $\tau$ of $X$ which interchanges $\varphi(u)$ and $\varphi(v)$. 
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T23:05:09.629362+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fa2e4d3e4102eaf376876aa26d39060c5268b238dde74096346962552d6d1628","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:large_jump_comono_coup of arXiv:2411.03609, 'Asymptotically optimal Wasserstein couplings for the small-time stable domain of attractio'] Let $\alpha \in (0,2)\setminus\{1\}$ and $q \in (0,\alpha)\cap(0,1]$ satisfy $\int_{\mathbb{R}^d\setminus B_{\bm{0}}(1)}|\bm{w}|^q\nu_{\bm{X}}(\mathrm{d}\bm{w})<\infty$, where $q\ne\alpha/(p+1)$ and $q\ne\alpha/(\alpha\delta+1)$. Then, under Assumptions~(\nameref{asm:S}) \& (\nameref{asm:C}) we have, as $t \downarrow 0$,
\begin{align*}
\mathcal{W}_q\big(\bm{L}^{\bm{S}^t}, \bm{L}^{\bm{Z}}\big) 
&= \mathcal{O}\big(G_2(t)^q 
    +(1+G_1(t))^qt^{\min\{1-q/\alpha,q\delta\}}     
    +G(t)^{pq}(1+G_1(t))^{q(1+p)}t^{\min\{1-q/\alpha,pq/\alpha\}}\big).
\end{align*}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:25:12.189904+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fa32b9d4d0305b6674eb1b00f68caf7bdb9d34cc75dc87b0527ba9747f799a10","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 35 of arXiv:2510.20492, 'Heterochromatic two-arm probabilities for metric graph Gaussian free fields'] For any $d\ge 3$, $v,w\in \widetilde{\mathbb{Z}}^d$ with $|v-w|\ge d$, and $0\le a,b\le |v-w|^{d-2}$, 
  	\begin{equation}
  	\Big| 	\frac{\mathfrak{p}_{v\leftrightarrow w,a,b}  }{\bar{\mathfrak{p}}_{v\leftrightarrow w,a,b}}   -1 \Big| \lesssim (ab+1) \cdot |v-w|^{2-d}, 
    	\end{equation}
    	where $\bar{\mathfrak{p}}_{v\leftrightarrow w,a,b}:=\mathbb{K}_{\{v,w\}}(v,w)\cdot \mathfrak{q}_v(a)\cdot \mathfrak{q}_w(b)$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T19:17:42.313271+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fa4ba5506ca8a546f0dd53a7615fa627973a89d2a0bfe401cb8cf619c50e60e3","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary 33 of arXiv:2608.05931, 'Effective Lagrangian regularity and the uniqueness threshold for random H\"older velocity '] There exists a universal constant such that for any martingale difference sequence $D_i$ adapted to a filtration $\mathcal{F}_i$---so $D_i$ is $\mathcal{F}_i$ measurable and $\E[D_i \mid \mathcal{F}_{i-1}] =0$---we have for all $p \geq 2, n \geq 1$, the bounds
    \begin{equation}

        \Big\|\sum_{i=1}^n D_i\Big\|_{L^p_\omega} \leq C \sup_{ 2  \lor \frac{p}{n} \leq q \leq p} \frac{p}{q} \Big(\frac{n}{p}\Big)^{1/q} \max_{1 \leq i \leq n} \big\|\E[|D_i|^q \mid \mathcal{F}_{i-1}]^{1/q}\big\|_{L^\infty_\omega}.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T09:24:34.395731+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fa4bef944265977e7645fdb9041fe73fc72c3ee2321af20a48083ff0152a0b53","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition 7 of arXiv:2608.31008, 'Stability of gravitational instantons with a bounded Killing vector field'] Let $(M^4,g)$ be oriented Einstein with scalar curvature $s$.  If
$\alpha^+\in\Omega^2_+(M)$ and $\beta^-\in\Omega^2_-(M)$ are harmonic,
then $h=\alpha^+\circ\beta^-$ is TT, and
\begin{equation}
    \cE_g h=-\frac{s}{2}h-2\sum_a(\nabla_a\alpha^+)\circ(\nabla_a\beta^-),

\end{equation}
which implies from $\big\langle(\nabla_a\alpha^+)\circ(\nabla_a\beta^-),
 \alpha^+\circ\beta^-\big\rangle
 =\langle\nabla_a\alpha^+,\alpha^+\rangle
  \langle\nabla_a\beta^-,\beta^-\rangle,$ that
\begin{equation}
    \langle\cE_g h,h\rangle=-\frac{s}{2}|h|^2-\frac12\langle d|\alpha^+|^2,d|\beta^-|^2\rangle.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-26T21:02:06.326619+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fa68cc8f45ca869caf729fc74ea99ec89f11275029b7598941f7c452d4b31cdb","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Thm 16 of arXiv:2607.06242, 'Exponential mixing and Freidlin--Wentzell large deviation principle for Markov cocycles'] Assume Assumption \ref{a.050201}. For $m$-a.e. $\sigma\in\Sigma$,
