Moreover, there are limiting objects $(\zeta^\tau_{0,\mu})^{\tau\in\mathcal{T}}_{\mu\in(0,1]}$ such that $\zeta^\tau_{\eps,\mu}\rightarrow\zeta^\tau_{0,\mu}$ as $\eps\downarrow0$ in the topology induced by the above norm.

Finally, note that the estimate (equation eq:boundZeta of the paper) combined with (equation eq:boundXi of the paper) implies moment bounds on the non-stationary force coefficients. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:32:56.082059+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fe478c3ba8d4c0f61798849d7d075476129cb064970438c35812e2899f99e29b","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Proposition prop:Markov_LambdaDeterministic of arXiv:2411.12522, 'Canonical insurance models: stochastic equations and comparison theorems'] \leavevmode
