{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T14:45:02.037031+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fe9258a807046dcd61ec815e8af4851b2b6030b6ed1d9d8a4a48769c91d5f529","kind":"definition","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Defn def:tree of arXiv:2601.00119, 'The largest common subtree of two random trees'] A \emph{plane tree} is a (potentially infinite) subset $t$ of $\mathcal{U}$ satisfying the following conditions:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item[(a)] $\varnothing\in t$,
    \item[(b)] for all $u\in t$, if $u\neq\varnothing$ then $\overleftarrow{u}\in t$,
    \item[(c)] for all $u\in t$, there is an integer $\mathrm{k}_u(t)\geq 0$ such that $u * (i)\in t \Leftrightarrow 1\leq i\leq  \mathrm{k}_u(t)$ for all $i \in \mathbb{N}^*$.
\end{enumerate}","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T02:47:21.665885+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_fe9ab897a0ab41702235b62a8cc70add1fd6c7ef39269b37620c7859a6820b77","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:second-summand of arXiv:2412.09145, 'Asymptotic expansions for normal deviations of random walks conditioned to stay positive'] Under the conditions of Theorem (thm:lattice of the paper) it holds, with $z=x/\sigma$,
