{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T19:43:55.604136+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ffb7fb71b84c8767653a2a071d4a93c01e372e4d5b72fd1135baef5bf8b2cc16","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Corollary c:act of arXiv:2604.03979, 'Stationary Distributions in Monotone Markov Models: Theory and Applications'] If $T \colon \mathscr{P}(S) \to \mathscr{P}(S)$ is order-preserving, then the following statements are equivalent:

    \begin{enumerate}
        \item $T$ is globally stable on $\mathscr{P}(S)$.
        \item $T$ is asymptotically contractive and has an order-bounded trajectory in $\mathscr{P}(S)$.
        \item $T$ is asymptotically contractive and has a tight trajectory in $\mathscr{P}(S)$.
    \end{enumerate} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T06:29:21.917625+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ffbc1ec99a181fe6d030c2e3ce11e2a0b7a8c3525584431465d99a50455809f0","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2608.01516, 'Nondegeneracy and regularity of polynomial pushforwards'] Let $\alpha\in(0,1]$ and let $\nu$ be a probability Borel measure on $\mathbb R^k$.
Then the estimate
\begin{equation}
\nu(A)\le C\bigl(\lambda_k(A)\bigr)^\alpha
\end{equation}
for every Borel set $A\subset \mathbb R^k$ is equivalent to the estimate
\begin{equation}
