for every $\psi\in C_0^\infty(\mathbb R^k)$ with $0\le\psi\le 1$.","status":"unverified"}

{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T11:17:33.993590+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ffc52b43a4540eb086836540481422c2e86e99ad37fa50f7d55b912e335fb612","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma 35 of arXiv:2609.03386, 'Twisted Gradient Flow Approach to Vegetation-Rainfall-Bushfire Interactions Model'] There exist a sequence $\{\varepsilon_n\}_{n \in \mathbb{N}} \subset (0,1)$ and a nonnegative function
