{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-28T00:41:11.632965+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ffd25ff06533dd1f582437147a8ab79bce395b5308960141fb5e7b5accbf1ea1","kind":"lemma","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma cuttimes of arXiv:2411.13505, 'Capacity of loop-erased random walk'] We have
\begin{equation}
	\begin{split}
		\lim_{n\rightarrow\infty}\mathbb{E}\left[|n-\rho_{n(\log n)^{-1/3}}|\right]=\lim_{n\rightarrow\infty}\mathbb{E}\left[|(\log n)^{1/3}n-\ell_n|\right]=0.
	\end{split}
\end{equation}
Furthermore, there exists $C>0$ such that for all $n$ and all $m$ such that $|n-m|\geq (\log m)^{-6}m$,
