{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-10-27T17:11:02.388314+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_ffec0802839ca988a43eb9725f94ecee87cd9bb4a3ad5246477cc081f7d41a72","kind":"concept","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Lemma lem:contraction of arXiv:2507.10531, 'Quantitative central limit theorems for exponential random graphs'] For any $p \in U_\beta$, there are some $\varepsilon, \kappa > 0$ such that,
